              "__html": "m. and <strong>afrétt,</strong> f. (now always f.; cp. rótt), [prgbably akin to reka, viz. afrekt, contr. afrétt], <i>compascuum, common pasture;</i> it is now prop. used of mountain pastures, whither the cattle (sheep) are driven in the summer in order to graze during July and August, and again collected and driven down in the autumn (Sept.); in Norway called <i>almenningr.</i>",
