        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ötul, atalt, adj. [at, n.; Ormul. <i>attel</i> = <i>turpis</i>], <i>fierce,</i> Lat. <i>atrox;</i> ötul augu, <i>fierce, piercing eyes,</i> Hkv. i. 3; þetta folk er atalt ok illt, Hkr. iii. 313: ötul, amatlig, <i>fierce and loathsome,</i> used of a witch, Hkv. I. 38: Atli ek heiti, a. skal ek þér vera, where the poet plays on the likeness between the pr. name Atli and the adj. atall, <i>my name is ‘Savage;’ savage shall I prove to thee,</i> Hkv. Hjörv. 15. At the present day, freq. in the changed form ötull, in a good sense, <i>brisk, strenuous.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
