      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/au-kvisi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          au-kvisi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [prop. <strong>auð-kvisi,</strong> from auð, <i>easy</i>, and kveistinn, <i>touchy</i>; cp. kveisa, f. <i>ulcus, dolor</i>]; in old writers it is spelt with <i>au</i> or <i>av,</i> and sometimes with a double <i>k</i>, ökkvisi, Bs. i. 497 vellum MS. A. M. 499; auðkvisi, Ld. 236 C and the vellum MS. A. M. 122 A to Sturl. ii. 8; aukvisi, MS. 122 B; O. H. (Ed. 1853) reads aucvisi; it means <i>a weakly</i>, <i>irritable, touchy person.</i> Used esp. in the proverb, einn er au. ættar hverrar, cp. the Engl. <i>there is a black sheep in every flock,</i> Hkr. ii. 238: mun ek son minn láta heita Gizur; lítt hafa þeir aukvisar verit í Haukdæla ætt er svá hafa heitið hér til, Sturl. ii. 8, at the birth of earl Gizur. [The name Gizur was a famous name in this family, Gizur hviti, Gizur biskup, Gizur Hallsson, etc.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/au-vird"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          au-virð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>auvirði,</strong> mod. <strong>auðvirði,</strong> n. [af, <i>off,</i> and verð, <i>value;</i> the change of letter caused by the following <i>v</i>; a purely Icel. form, the Norse being ‘afv-;’ the mod. Icel. form is auð-v., as if it were to be derived from auð- and verð]:",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/au-virdast"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          au-virðast
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, <i>to become worthless,</i> Eg. 103, Glúm. 377 C.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/au-virdliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
