              "__html": "f. pl. corrupt for ábistir (see p. 481, col. 1), cp. Goth. <i>beist</i>, Engl. <i>beestings;</i> the á- is a gen. pl. from ær, <i>a ewe:</i> the word therefore prop. meant <i>sheep’s beestings,</i> but came to be used as a general term; the word is a household word in Icel., but seems not to be found in ancient poets; Hallgr. Pét. speaks of heitar ‘ábristur.’",
