        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Ulf. <i>banja</i> = πληγή; A. S. <i>bana;</i> Engl. <i>bane;</i> O. H. G. <i>bano;</i> v. ben below]. I. <i>bane, death,</i> natural or violent (properly violent); Egill tók sótt þá er hann leiddi til bana, Eg. 767; lostinn öru til bana, Fms. i. 118; kominn at bana, <i>sinking fast,</i> of a sick person, vii. 166. II. <i>a bane,</i> and so = bana-maðr, <i>a slayer;</i> fjögurra manna b., Nj. 8, Grág. ii. 88, Ld. 326; pl., N. G. L. i. 163: the phrase, verða e-m at bana, <i>to slay one,</i> may refer to I. or II: poët. <i>fire</i> is called bani viðar, <i>the bane of wood,</i> and bani Hálfs, <i>the bane of king Half,</i> Ýt. 6; <i>the winter</i> is bani orma, <i>the bane of worms,</i> etc., Lex. Poët.",
            }
