        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "interj. <i>fie!</i> <strong>bía,</strong> <i>to defile.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjagadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bjagaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>wry, deformed,</i> cp. bagr. <strong>bjag-leitr,</strong> adj. <i>ugly, deformed,</i> Fas. ii. 149.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjalla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bjalla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a bell,</i> certainly an Engl. word imported into Icel. along with Christianity; bjöllu gætir, <i>the keeper of the bell,</i> is a nickname given by the heathen Icel. to a missionary, A. D. 998, Kristni S. (in a verse): hann vígði klukkur ok bjöllur, Bs. i. 65, Fms. i. 233: bjalla is now esp. used of small bells, e. g. on the horns of sheep, but klukka of a church bell; cp. dynbjalla, Grett.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjannak"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bjannak
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. an απ. λεγ.; þat var háttr hans ef hann (viz. Odin) sendi menn sína til orrostu eðr aðrar sendifarar, at hann lagði áðr hendr í höfuð þeim ok gaf þeim bjannak, trúðu þeir at þá mundi vel farast, Ýngl. S. ch. 11; it is commonly interpreted as <i>benedictio,</i> but it is no doubt the Scot. <i>bannock,</i> from Gael, <i>banagh, an oat-cake;</i> cp. Lat. <i>panis.</i> The whole passage in the Hkr. points to Christian rites and ideas brought into the pagan North, but which are here attributed to Odin, (cp. the breaking of bread and the Eucharist.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjarg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bjarg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Ulf. <i>bairgahei</i> = η ορεινή; A. S. <i>beorg;</i> Germ. <i>berg;</i> lost in Engl.], <i>rocks, precipices:</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjarg-aurar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bjarg-aurar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. = bjargálnir, Mag. 160.",
            }
