            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjugr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bjúgr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "s, m., medic., Lat. <i>tumor;</i> in many compds: skyr-bjúgr, <i>scorbuticus,</i> Engl. <i>scorbutic;</i> vind-bjúgr, <i>tumor aereus;</i> vatns-bjúgr, <i>tumor oedematosus,</i> Fél. ix. 197.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjugr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bjúgr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>bowed, hooked, crooked, bent;</i> fætr lágu bjúgir við lendar, Hom. 114; með bjúgum þornum, Sks. 419; hann var b. á baki, <i>he sat bent</i> or <i>bowed</i> (<i>from age</i>) <i>on horseback,</i> Fs. 183; b. í vexti, Eg. 710; með bjúgum hring, Sks. 198, Rb. 344, Band. 9: metaph., hvárt er yðr þykir bjúgt eðr beint (MS. brátt), <i>whether it seems to you crooked or straight,</i> i. e. <i>whether you like it or not,</i> Fms. viii, 436: cp. boginn, baugr, etc.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjorg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          björg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. bjargar [v. bjarga], <i>help, deliverance, out of need</i> or <i>danger,</i> e. g. feeding the hungry, saving one’s life; unlawful ‘björg’ is that of giving help to an outlaw, who is ‘úráðandi öllum bjargráðum,’ one on whom no help must be bestowed, neither food, shelter, nor ferry; Grág. in several passages, and there commonly used in plur. (bjargir) when in this particular sense; it was liable to a heavy punishment, and the case was to be summoned before the Fifth Court, Grág. Þ. Þ. ch. 25, Ld. 42.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjork"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          björk
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. bjarkar, [A. S. <i>beorc;</i> Swed. <i>björk;</i> Dan. and Scot. <i>birk;</i> Engl. <i>birch;</i> Germ. <i>birke;</i> Lat. <i>betula;</i> v. birki], <i>a birch,</i> Edda (Gl.), Bs. ii. 5, Jb. 236. In compds <strong>bjarkar-.</strong>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bjorn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          björn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. bjarnar; dat. birni, pl. n. birnir; acc. björnu, mod. birni, [an enlarged form, cp. Goth, <i>biari,</i> by which word Ulf. renders the Gr. θηρίον, Titus i. 12; A. S. <i>bera</i>; Engl. <i>bear</i>; Germ. <i>bär</i>; but Swed. and Dan. <i>björn</i>]:—<i>a bear;</i> hvíta-björn, <i>the white bear</i> or <i>ice-bear;</i> and skóg-björn, híð-björn, við-björn, <i>the black bear</i> or <i>wood-bear,</i> Germ. <i>wald-bär;</i> the ice-bear was unknown in Europe till the discovery of Iceland at the end of the 9th, and Greenland at the end of the 10th century. The very first ice-bear was brought to Europe by Ingimund the Old as a gift to the king of Norway about A. D. 900, Landn., Fs. (Vd.) 27; Isleif, the first bishop of Iceland, also brought one as a present to the German emperor about A. D. 1050, Bs. i. 61, Hv. ch. 2; cp. the little story of Audun in Fms. vi. 297–307, Sks. 186, Sturl. iii. 82, Grág. ii. 181, Am. 17, where a hvítabjörn is mentioned, Fs. (Flóam. S.) 148; as to the black bear, vide esp. Grett. ch. 23, Finnb. ch. 11, Glúm. ch. 3, Fas. i. 50; cp. an interesting paper, ‘Waldbär und Wasserbär,’ by Konrad Maurer, upon this subject; winter is called <i>‘the bear’s night;’</i> hence the saying, ‘löng er bjarnar-nótt;’ cp. langar eigu þeir bersi nætr, Mkv. Björn and Bjarni are freq. pr. names; also in compd. names, Þorbjörn, Ásbjörn; and as a prefix, Bjarngrímr, Bjarnhéðinn, etc.; vide Landn. (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blad"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blað
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [A. S. <i>bläd;</i> Germ. <i>blatt;</i> Hel. <i>blad.</i> Ulf. renders the Gr. φύλλον by <i>laufs,</i> Engl. <i>leaf,</i> Icel. <i>lauf.</i> The Engl. say <i>a blade of grass</i> or <i>corn, a leaf</i> of a tree; and so, in Icel., herbs or plants have blað, trees lauf]:—<i>a leaf;</i> blöð þess grass er … heitir, Pr. 472; blöð á lauk, Hervar. S. (in a verse): metaph. <i>a veil,</i> svá er mér sem hangi b. fyrir auga, Fms. iii. 126.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bladra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blaðra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> að, prob. an onomatopoëtic word, like Lat. <i>blaterare,</i> Scot. <i>blether,</i> Germ. <i>plaudern,</i> in the phrase, b. tungunni, <i>to talk thick,</i> Hom. 115; tungan var úti ok blaðraði, Fbr. 77 new Ed.; hann blaðraði tungunni ok vildi við leita at mæla, Fms. v. 152: metaph. <i>to utter inarticulate sounds, bleat,</i> as a sheep. <strong>blaðr,</strong> n. <i>nonsense.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blak"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blak
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a slap</i>; fyrir pústr (<i>a buffet</i>) fjórar merkr, fyrir blak (<i>a slap</i>) tvær merkr (as a fine), Gþl. 177, 187.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blaka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blaka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> að, <i>to slap,</i> Ann. 1394.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blakk-fjallr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blakk-fjallr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>black-skinned,</i> epithet of a wood-bear, Akv. 11.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blakkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blakkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> m. (for. word), a <i>sort of measure,</i> N. G. L. i. 324.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blakkr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blakkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [A. S. <i>blac;</i> Engl. <i>black;</i> O. H. G. <i>plak:</i> in Icel. svartr, as in A. S. and other kindred tongues <i>swart,</i> etc., represents the Lat. <i>niger;</i> while blakkr corresponds to the Lat. <i>ater, dead</i> or <i>dusky black</i>], in poetry used as an epithet of wolves, etc., Lex. Poët., in prose it is very rare, Fas. iii. 592; hence blekkja, <i>to defraud:</i> the mod. Icel. blek, n. <i>ink,</i> Swed. <i>blak,</i> Dan. <i>blæk,</i> come from blakkr, corresponding to Lat. <i>atramentum,</i> Str. 63 (blez), Pr. 474.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blakra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blakra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [<i>blakra,</i> Ivar Aasen, <i>to shake,</i> of leaves], <i>to blink;</i> b. augum, Hom. 89; now <strong>blakta,</strong> að, e. g. b. augum, <i>to move the eyes,</i> and also used of <i>the beating of the heart;</i> hón fann að hjartað blaktaði, in the story of the Beauty and the Beast (Skrýmslið Góða), Kvöldv. ii. 176: blakra vængjum = blakta vængjum, <i>to flutter with the wings,</i> Barl. 88; of sails, Úlf. 3. 14.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bland"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bland
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. in the adverbial phrase, í bland, <i>among,</i> Dan. <i>i blandt,</i> Bs. i. 802, Stj. 231, Matth. xiii. 25, (rare in mod. usage.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blanda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blanda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>any mixture of two fluids,</i> Fs. 145 (of watery blood); but esp. <i>a beverage of hot whey</i> mixed up with <i>water,</i> Vm. 60, Fms. ix. 360. Blanda also is the local name of a stream of glacier water in the north of Icel., v. Landn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blanda-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blanda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "in early Icel. poetry and prose a strong verb; pres. 1st pers. blend, Ls. 3; 3rd pers. blendr, Grág. ii. 389; reflex. blendsk, Symb. 30; pret. 1st pers. blétt, Am. 79, Greg. 50; reflex. blézk, Orkn. 104 (in a verse from about A. D. 1046); pl. bléndu, bléndum, Ls. 9, Greg. 60, Edda 47; reflex. bléndusk, Hkm. 8; subj. reflex. bléndisk, Mart. 129; blandinn (freq.), Sdm., Ýt., etc., vide Lex. Poët., Skálda 164; but in the 13th century and later the weak form (blanda, að) prevailed in all tenses except the part. pass., where the old blandinn = blandaðr may still be used, though the weak is more common; imperat. blanda, Pr. 471, 472, N. G. L. i. 12; pres. blandar, 13; part. blandaðr, Sks. 349, Pr. 470, 472 (MS. about A. D. 1250), [Ulf. <i>blandan,</i> a redupl. verb; A. S. <i>bland;</i> Engl. <i>blend;</i> O. H. G. <i>blantan;</i> lost in N. H. G.; Swed. <i>blanda</i>]:—<i>to blend, mix,</i> the beverage in acc., the mixed ingredient in dat.; b. mjöð (drykk), eitri, meini, Greg. l. c.; drottning ok Bárðr blönduðu þá drykkinn ólyfjani, Eg. 210: adding ‘við,’ lítið (acc. instead of dat.) verðr ok við blandit, Skálda 164; maturt blandin við upsa-gall, Pr. l. c.; þar fellr Jórdan í gegnum, ok blendsk eigi (<i>does not blend</i>) við vötnin, Symb. l. c.; tak skógar súru ok blanda (imperat.) við fornt vín, Pr. l. c.; b. með, <i>id.,</i> Rb. 164; b. saman, <i>to mix together,</i> Pr. l. c.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blandan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          blandan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>mixing,</i> N. G. L. i. 153.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/blasa"
