        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Engl. <i>to borrow</i> and <i>bargain;</i> Germ. <i>borgen;</i> related to byrgja and bjarga; O. H. G. <i>porgen</i> only means <i>parcere, spondere,</i> not <i>mutuare.</i> In Icel. the word is of foreign origin; the indigenous expressions are, lána, ljá, <i>to lend;</i> gjalda, <i>to pay;</i> selja, veðja, <i>to bail,</i> etc.; the word only occurs in later and theol. writers]:—<i>to bail;</i> vil ek b. fyrir Árna biskup með mínum peningum, Bs. i. 770 (thrice): now obsolete in this sense.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
