              "__html": "a, m. [Germ. <i>bube, büberl, spitzbube,</i> v. Grimm], <i>a knave, rogue,</i> in Icel. only in a bad sense; cp. the rhyming phrase, þjófar og bófar, <i>thieves and knaves;</i> no reference from old writers is on record (though it is common enough at the present day), except that in Eb. it is used as a nickname, Freysteinn Bófi; in Swed. it occurs as a pr. name, Baut. 1478, 1483.",
