        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>bauðkr,</strong> Art. 7, mod. contr. <strong>baukr,</strong> m. [a for. word derived from Gr. αποθήκη; mid. Lat. <i>apotheca;</i> Ital. <i>bottega;</i> Fr. <i>boutique;</i> O. H. G. <i>buttick;</i> mod. Germ. <i>böttich;</i> hence Germ. <i>böttcher,</i> Dan. <i>bødker,</i> mod. Icel. <i>beykir</i> = <i>a cooper</i>]:—<i>a box,</i> originallv a box to keep herbs and balsams in; tvá buðka með balsamum, Bs. i. 872, Mar. 43: buðkr nokkurr er húsfreyja átti, Glúm. 378, Stj. 215: Bauka-Jón, <i>Pillbox-John,</i> was a nickname given to a bishop in Icel. for having made money by dealing in medicine-boxes; kölluðu óvinir hans hann Bauka-Jón, sögðu hann hafa selt i smá-baukum, þat er hann léti sem væri dýrindi nokkur, Espol. Árb. 1685; hence prob. banka, q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
