        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>búðar-verðr,</strong> m. [verðr = <i>cibus</i>], <i>the cooking and stewardship</i> in a vessel, work which the crew was bound to do in turn day by day; cooking and dairy work was thought unworthy to be the sole business of a man, and therefore the sailors were obliged to take it turn about, cp. Eb. 194, 196, 220:—metaph. <i>meat, meal,</i> eigi hafða ek þina veðra … mér til búðarvarðar, <i>the rams of thy flock I have not eaten,</i> Stj. 181. Gen. xxxi. 38; lofa mér at búa þér búðarvörð, <i>‘let me set a morsel of bread before thee,’</i> in the Engl. V., Stj. 493. 1 Sam. xxviii. 22; ráða til b., <i>to prepare for a meal,</i> Fms. v. 287, viii. 357; honum þótti þar gott til blaut-fisks ok búðarvarðar, Bs. i. 853, D. N. i. 311, ii. 16, Fas. ii. 209.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
