        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/byrr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          byrr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "gen. byrjar, nom. pl. byrir, acc. byri: [Swed.-Dan. <i>bör</i>; cp. usage of Gr. ουριος]:—<i>a fair wind;</i> it is freq. used in pl., esp. in the impers. phrase, e-m gefr vel byri (acc. pl.), <i>one gets a fair wind,</i> rarely, and less correct, byr (acc. sing.), Nj. 10, Vápn. 9, but sing. Nj. 4, Eg. 98; byri gefr hann brögnum, Hdl. 3; með hinum beztuni byrjum, Bs. i. 781; bíða byrjar, Fms. i. 131; liggja til byrjar, <i>to lie by for a fair wind,</i> Eg. 183; byrr rennr á, <i>a fair breeze begins to blow;</i> þá rann á byrr ok sigldu þeir, Nj. 135, Eg. 158; þá féll byrrinn, Eb. 8; þá tók byrr at vaxa, Eg. 390: allit, naut. phrases, blásandi byrr, blíðr byrr, beggja skauta byrr; hagstæðr byrr, fagr byrr. hægr, óðr byrr, Hm. 89; hrað-byri, etc.: also metaph., hafa góðan, mikinn, lítinn byrr, <i>to be well, much, little favoured:</i> in poetry in many compds, byrjar drösull, <i>the horse of the wind, a ship;</i> byr-skíð, byr-rann. <i>a ship;</i> byrr always denotes the wind on the sea. <strong>byrjar-gol,</strong> n. <i>a fair breeze,</i> Fms. ix. 21.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/byrsta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          byrsta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, [bursti], <i>to furnish with bristles</i> or <i>spikes,</i> Sks. 418; gulli byrstr, Fas. i. 184.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
