      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bysn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          býsn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [cp. A. S. <i>bysen, bisen,</i> which means <i>example,</i> whilst the Icel. word means] <i>a wonder, a strange and portentous thing;</i> commonly Used in pl., urðu hverskonar býsn, 625. 42; þar sem þessi býsn (acc. pl.) bar fyrir, Fms. xi. 13; þetta eru stór býsn, 64; slíkt eru banvæn býsn, Fas. iii. 13 (in a verse); sing., Fms. xi. 10, 64: in mod. use fem. sing., Fb. i. 212, Pr. 76, 91; býsna-veðr, <i>portentous weather,</i> Fms. iii. 137; býsna-vetr, <i>a winter of portents,</i> when many ghosts and goblins were about, Bs., Sturl. i. 115; býsna-sumar, in the same sense, Ann. 1203. In mod. use <strong>býsna-</strong> is prefixed to a great many words in the sense of <i>pretty, tolerably,</i> Germ. <i>ziemlich;</i> býsna-vel, b. góðr, langr, fljótr, <i>pretty well, pretty good,</i> etc. in early writers the sense is much stronger.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bysna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          býsna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to portend, bode;</i> þetta býsnar tjón ok sorg, Karl. 492; the proverb, býsna skal til batnaðar, i. e. <i>things must be worse before they are better,</i> Old Engl. ‘when bale is highest, bote is nighest,’ Fms. v. 199, (spelt bisna, O. H. L.); er býsna skal at betr verði, x. 261.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/byta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          býta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "tt, [bútr], <i>to deal out, give,</i> with dat. of the thing; býtti Hrafn silfrinu, Fas. iii. 256: esp. býta út, or út býta, <i>to give alms,</i> Hebr. xiii. 16, Gal. vi. 6.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/byti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          býti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>exchange, barter,</i> Krók. 65; <strong>býting,</strong> f. <i>spending,</i> Ann. 1408.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baedi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "[v. báðir, where in p. 54, col. 2, 1. 7, the words ‘rarely Norse’ should be struck out], used adverbially, <i>both,</i> Scot. <i>‘baithh,’</i> with conjunctions connecting two parts of a sentence:",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baegi-fotr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bægi-fótr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [bágr], ‘<i>lame-foot,’</i> a cognom., Eb.; Egilsson renders αμφιγυήεις (Od. viii. 349) by bægi-fótr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baeging"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæging
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>thwarting,</i> Finnb. 344.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baeginn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæginn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>cross-grained,</i> Fms. iii. 95; <strong>bægni,</strong> f. <i>peevishness;</i> orð-bæginn, q. v.; mein-bæginn, <i>pettish.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baegja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bægja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, (an old pret. bagði, Haustl. 18), [bágr], with dat. <i>to make one give way, push one back;</i> tröll-konan bægir honum til fjallsins, Bs. i. 464; b. skipi ór lægi, <i>to push the ship from her moorings,</i> Fms. vii. 114; b. vist sinni, <i>to change one’s abode, remove,</i> Eb. 252; þeim bægði veðr, of foul wind, Eg. 245; honum bægði veðr, ok bar hann til eyja þeirra er Syllingar heita, <i>the weather drove him from his course, and he was carried to the islands called Scilly,</i> Fms. i. 145.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baeki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "v. beyki; <strong>bæki-skógr,</strong> m. <i>a beech-wood,</i> Fms. xi. 224.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baeklingr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæklingr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [bók], <i>a ‘bookling,’ little book,</i> Lat. <i>libellus,</i> Bs. i. 59.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baela"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d,",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baeli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [ból],",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baen"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>bón,</strong> f. [biðja], <i>prayer, request, boon;</i> these two words are nearly identical in form, and sometimes used indiscriminately as to sense; but in most cases they are different, bæn having a deeper sense, <i>prayer,</i> bón, <i>request, boon;</i> we may say biðja e-n bónar, and biðja e-n bænar, but the sense is different; only bæn can be used of prayer to God; göra e-t at bæn e-s, Fs. 38; er su bæn allra var, at …, <i>we all beg, that…,</i> Eg. 28; skaltú veita mér bæn þó er ek mun biðja þik, Nj. 26; fella bæn at e-m, <i>to pray one earnestly,</i> Ísl. ii. 305.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baen-heyra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæn-heyra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, esp. theol. <i>to hear one’s prayer,</i> N. T.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baen-heyrsla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæn-heyrsla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>the hearing one’s prayers,</i> eccl., N. T., Vídal.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baen-hus"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæn-hús
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= bænahús, Pm. 41, Dipl. iii. 2, iv. 9, Vm. 78.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baen-raekinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæn-rækinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>diligent in prayer,</i> Hkr. ii. 191.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baena"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, <i>to pray, entreat one;</i> bændi hann til at hann skyldi, Fms. x. 387; prestr sá er bændr er. <i>requested,</i> K. Þ. K. 8, 40; því ætla ek at senda hann til keisarans sem hann bændi (<i>asíed</i>) sjálfr, Post. 645. 98, cp. Acts xxv. 25; grát-bæna, <i>to pray ‘greeting,’</i> i. e. <i>with tears.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baena-fullting"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæna-fullting
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>support of prayers,</i> Fms. vi. 114.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baena-hald"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæna-hald
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a holding of prayers,</i> Landn. Hi, Gþl. 41; bænahalds-maðr, <i>a man who prays to God, a religions man,</i> Bs. i. 72, Hom. 154.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baena-hus"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæna-hús
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a chapel,</i> Grág. i. 459, Bs. i. 646; b. tollr, 647: <i>a house of prayer,</i> Matth. xxi. 13.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baena-stadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæna-staðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>entreaty, intercession, prayer;</i> þat er b. minn til allrar alþýðu, Nj. 189; ek ætlaða, at þér munduð láta standa minn b. um einn maun, Fms. vi. 101; göra e-t fyrir bænastað e-s, <i>to do a thing because of one’s intercession</i> or <i>prayer,</i> Lv. 13: <i>supplication,</i> Bs. i. 740; með beztu manna ráði ok b., Gþl. 13.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baenar-bref"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bænar-bréf
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a letter of entreaty,</i> Ann. 1330; bónar-bréf, 1392.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baenar-ord"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bænar-orð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>prayers, entreaties,</i> Fs. 10, Fms. ii. 235, Sks. 515.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baer"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bær
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>bœr,</strong> or <strong>býr,</strong> gen. baejar or býjar; gen. biar also occurs, esp. in Norse MSS. of the 14th century, Fb., but is rare and unclassical; pl. -ir, gen. -ja, dat. -jum. In Icel. people say bær; in Norway <i>bö</i> in Swed. and Dan. (always with <i>y</i>) <i>by</i>; the root word being búa, bú: this word is very freq. in local names of towns and villages throughout the whole of Scandinavia; and wherever the Scandinavian tribes settled the name <i>by</i> or <i>bö</i> went along with them. In the map of Northern England the use of this word marks out the limits and extent of the Norse immigration, e. g. the name Kirkby or Kirby; about twenty or thirty such are found in English maps of the Northern and Midland Counties, denoting churches built by the Norse or Danish settlers, as Whitby, Grimsby, etc., cp. Kirkjubær in Icel. In Denmark and Sweden local names ending in <i>-by</i> are almost numberless.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baera"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, [bera, báru], <i>to move, stir,</i> esp. reflex. <i>to stir a limb,</i> Bb. 3.31; enginn sá hans varir bærast, <i>no one saw his lips move.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baeri-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæri-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>fit, seemly,</i> Stj. 141.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baerr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bærr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>due, entitled to,</i> cp. Germ. <i>gebührend;</i> the proverb, b. er hverr at ráða sínu, <i>every one has a right to dispose of his own property,</i> Ísl. ii. 145; vera b. at dæma um e-t, <i>to be a fit judge in a matter</i> (a proverb); <i>unbecoming,</i> Yt. 11.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baesa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæsa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, [báss], = bása, <i>to drive cattle into stall,</i> Gísl. 20; the saying, fyrr á gömlum uxanum at b. en kálfinum, Fms. vi. 28.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baesingr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæsingr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., prop. <i>one born in a báss</i> (q. v.); hence, as a law term, <i>the child of an outlawed mother;</i> þat barn er ok eigi arfgengt (<i>that child is also not entitled to inheritance</i>), er sú kona getr er sek er orðin skógarmaðr, þó-at hon geti við bónda sínum úsekjum, ok heitir sá maðr bæsingr, Grág. i. 178. Is not the name <i>Bastard,</i> which first occurs as. the surname of the Conqueror, simply a Norman corruption of this Scandin. law term? The son of an outlawed father was called vargdropi, q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baeta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "tt, [bót; Ulf. <i>bôtjan</i> = ωφελειν; Hel. <i>bôtian;</i> A. S. <i>bêtan;</i> O. H. G. <i>bôzau;</i> Germ. <i>büssen</i>]:—<i>to better, improve, amend,</i> also <i>t</i> o <i>restore, repair,</i> Nj. 163, Gþl. 411; b. aptr, <i>to restore,</i> Grág. ii. 336; b. upp, <i>to restore, atone for,</i> Fms. ix. 43; b. at e-u, <i>to repair,</i> 367; bæta ráð sitt, <i>to better one’s condition, to marry,</i> Nj. 2: theol. <i>to better one’s life:</i> Guð bætti honum af þessi sótt, <i>God restored him to health,</i> Fms. ix. 391; with gen. of the sickness, O. H. L. 84.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/baexl"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          bæxl
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "mod. <strong>bæxli,</strong> n. [bógr], <i>the shoulder</i> (Lat. <i>armus</i>) <i>of a dragon, whale, shark,</i> or the like, Fms. vi. 351, Bret. 544.16, Gullþ. 7.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bod-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          böð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. böðvar, [A. S. <i>beadu</i>], <i>a battle,</i> only in poetry, in which it is used in a great many compds; hence come the pr. names Böðvarr, Böðvildr, Böðmóðr, vide Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bodull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          böðull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. böðli, [Dan. <i>böddel;</i> A. S. <i>bydel,</i> Engl. <i>bedel,</i> O. H. G. <i>putil,</i> Germ. <i>büttel</i>], <i>an executioner,</i> (mod. word.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bodvask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          böðvask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, dep. <i>to rave,</i> Hðm. 21.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/boggr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          böggr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. böggvi, an obsol. word, <i>a bag;</i> breiðr b., <i>a big bag,</i> in a metaph. sense, Glúm. (in a verse): the dimin. <strong>böggull,</strong> m. <i>a small bag,</i> is in freq. use as a nickname, Arn. S. Bs. i. <strong>bögla,</strong> að, <i>to shrivel,</i> v. bagla.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/bol-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          böl
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., dat. bölvi, gen. pl. bölva, [cp. Goth. <i>balva-vesei</i> and <i>balveins</i> = βάσανος, κόλασις; A. S. <i>balew;</i> Engl. <i>bale</i>; Hel. <i>balu;</i> O. H. G. <i>balv;</i> lost in mod. Germ. and Dan.]:—<i>bale, misfortune;</i> allit. phrases, böl and bót, <i>‘bale’</i> and <i>‘bote;’</i> bölva bætr, Stor. 22; þegar böl er hæst er bót næst, <i>‘when bale is hest, bote is nest,’</i> Morris, E. Engl. Spec, 100; svá skal böl bæta at bíða annat meira (a proverb), Grett. 123, Fbr. 193; böl er búskapr (a proverb).",
            }
