              "__html": "m., gen. ballar, dat. belli, [Engl. <i>ball</i>; O. H. G. <i>balla</i>]:—<i>a ball, globe: the ball,</i> in the game of cricket, Gísl. 26 (in a verse, A. D. 963), but hardly ever used, knöttr being the common word: <i>a globe,</i> Al. 18; b. jarðar, Sks. 205 B; b. sólar, id., v. 1.: <i>the front</i> of a phalanx, belli svínfylktar fylkingar, 384 B: <i>a small body of men,</i> Lat. <i>globus,</i> Fms. viii. 406, where some MSS. read bjöllr, probably to avoid the ambiguity: <i>a peak, mountain,</i> in the local name Ballar-á, a farm in the west of Iceland, Eb.",
            }
