          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>dawn,</i> Eluc., Sturl. i. 83 C.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/deig"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          deig
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Ulf. <i>daigs,</i> m. = φύραμα; A. S. <i>dâg;</i> Engl. <i>dough;</i> Germ. <i>teig;</i> Swed. <i>deg</i>]:—<i>dough,</i> Ann. 1337, Matth. xiii. 33, I Cor. v. 6–8. Gal. v. 9; the earliest trace of this word is the Goth. <i>deigan,</i> a strong verb by which Ulf. renders the Gr. πλάσσειν<i>,</i> as also οστάκινος by the part. <i>digans,</i> πλάσμα by <i>gadik</i> in Róm. ix. 20, and επλάσθη by <i>gadigans</i> in I Tim. ii. 13: to this family belong the following Icel. words, deigr (<i>moist),</i> deigja, digna, deigla, dígull, the fundamental notion being <i>plasticity:</i> vide the following.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/deigja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          deigja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> u, f. <i>a dairy-maid;</i> this word is the humble mother of the Engl. <i>lady,</i> qs. <i>la-dy</i> (vide p. 76. s. v. brauð). A. S. <i>hlæf-dige</i> = <i>bread-maid;</i> cp. Norse bú-deigja (q. v.). Chaucer’s <i>dey (a maner dey),</i> and West Engl. <i>day-</i> (or <i>dey</i>-) <i>house, a dairy.</i> The deigja in old Norse farms was the chief maid, but still a bondwoman, N. G. L. i. 70, H. E. i. 510; öll ertú d. dritin. Ls. 56, where it is curiously enough addressed to the daughter of Byggvir (bygg = <i>barley</i>), a handmaid of the gods; deigja seems to mean <i>a baker-woman,</i> and the word no doubt is akin to deig, <i>dough,</i> and Goth. deigan, <i>to knead,</i> the same person being originally both <i>dairy-woman</i> and <i>baker</i> to the farm: in Icel. the word is never used, but it survives in the Norse <i>bu-deia, sæter-deia, agtar-deia, reid-deia</i> (Ivar Aasen), and Swed. <i>deja,</i> = <i>a dairy-maid.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/deigla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          deigla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a crucible,</i> Germ. <i>tiegel.</i> v. digull.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/deigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          deigr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>‘doughy,’ damp, wet;</i> Icel. say, vera d. í fætrna, <i>to be wettish,</i> less than vátr, <i>wet,</i> and more than rakr, <i>damp.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/deigull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          deigull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= dígull, m.; <strong>deigul-mór,</strong> m. <i>a sort of clay.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/deila"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          deila
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u. f. <i>disagreement, a contest,</i> often as a law term, <i>law contest</i> (laga-deila, þing-deila), Nj. 90, Fms. i. 68, iv. í 19, 198, vi. 136, viii. 146, Sturl. i. 105, Eg. 367, Rd. 304, Ld. 204.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/deila-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          deila
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, [Goth. <i>dailjan</i> and <i>ga-dailjan</i> = μερίζειν, μεταδιδόναι, διαιρεθν, etc.; A. S. <i>dælan;</i> Engl. <i>to deal;</i> Germ. <i>theilen;</i> O. H. G. <i>tailjan;</i> Swed. <i>dela;</i> Dan. <i>dele.</i>]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
