      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/detta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          detta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. datt, 2nd pers. dazt, pl. duttu; part. dottinn; pres. dett; pret. subj. dytti:—<i>to drop, fall:</i> d. niðr dauðr, <i>to drop down dead,</i> Fms. iii. 132; of a bird when shot, 179; þeir tóku brandana jalhskjótt sem ofan duttu, Nj. 201; spjótið datt ór hendi, El. 91; duttu þær ofan, <i>they tumbled down,</i> Fas. ii. 84; draga þá stundum upp, en láta stundum d., Karl. 161: <i>to drop, die suddenly,</i> sauðfénaðr datt niðr unnvörpum í megrð, Bs. i. 873; þau hafa nú niðr dottið í hor, <i>the cattle dropped down from starvation,</i> 875: <i>to sink,</i> of the heart, Fbr. 108: metaph., líf dettr ór e-m, <i>the life drops out of one,</i> Fms. iii. 214: denoting <i>to come on suddenly,</i> daudinn dettr á, Al. 90; láttu nidr d., engu er nýtt, <i>drop it, it is all false,</i> Fs. 159: the phrases, e-m dettr e-t í hug, <i>a thing drops into one’s mind,</i> i. e. <i>one recollects it suddenly;</i> d. ofan yfir e-n, <i>to be overwhelmed, amazed;</i> d. í stafi, <i>to fall in pieces</i> (as a tub without hoops), <i>to be amazed:</i> cp. datta, dotta.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dettr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
