        >
          digrask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to grow big,</i> of a pregnant woman, Fms. xi. 53; d. í gerðum, <i>id.,</i> Bárð. 173, Fb. i. 157: metaph. <i>to make oneself big,</i> d. ok dramba, Th. 11.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/digrd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          digrð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>bigness, stoutness</i> (cp. lengd, hæð, breidd, þykt), Fms. iii. 209.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dik"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dik
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a run, leap;</i> taka dik (taka undir sig d.), <i>to take a spring,</i> Bs. ii. 143: the word is probably foreign, but root uncertain; hence comes <strong>mið-dik,</strong> n., pronounced <strong>mið-bik,</strong> <i>the middle of a thing;</i> hún (i. e. the Reformation) hefir upphaiit illt og efnislaust, mið-dikið mátalaust, og endann afskaplegan, Bs. ii. 313, a pastoral letter of the old popish bishop Ögmund, A. D. 1539.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dika"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dika
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ad, <i>to run,</i> (mod.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dikt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dikt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>composition in Latin,</i> Látínu-dikt, Fms. iii. 163, Bs. i. 869, ii. 121; þat nýja dikt, 77: söngva-dikt, <i>composition of songs,</i> Sörla R. I. 5.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dikta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dikta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Lat. <i>dictare</i>], <i>to compose in Latin;</i> Gunnlaugr munkr er Látínu söguna diktað hefir, Bs. i. 215, 786; dikta ok skrifa bréf á Látínu; bréf skrifað ok diktað, 798; d. bækr, 79; d. vers, 655 xxxii. 17; d. röksemdir, Bs. i. 786: in old writers dikta is only used of Latin (not Icel.) compositions, but as these compositions were in an affected and artificial style, the word also got the sense of <i>fiction,</i> cp. Germ. <i>dichten, dicbter</i> = <i>a poet, dichtung</i> = <i>poetry;</i> mod. Dan. <i>digter;</i> Engl. ditty; in Icel. mostly with the notion of <i>falsehood,</i> not as in Germ. and mod. Dan. of <i>fancy.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/diktan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          diktan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>composition in Latin,</i> Bs. i. 798.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/diktr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          diktr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a poem</i> (rare), seldom used but as a name of several legendary poems of the 15th and 16th century, Ceciliu-d., etc.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dilk-fe"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dilk-fé
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>ewes together with their lambs,</i> Bs. i. 719.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dilk-saudr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dilk-sauðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a <i>sheep with a lamb,</i> Grág. i. 418.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dilk-aer"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dilk-ær
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a ewe with a lamb,</i> Grág. ii. 304.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dilkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dilkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a sucking lamb,</i> Grett. 137, Þorst. St. 51, Grág. i. 417, ii. 307, in the last passage also of <i>sucking pigs, calves</i> or <i>kids;</i> kvíga (<i>a ‘quey’</i> or <i>young cow</i>) með tvá dilka, Ísl. ii. 401; in Icel. households the lambs are separated from the mother in June, this is called ‘færa frá,’ the time ‘fráfærur,’ the lamb ‘fráfæru-lamb;’ the lambs that are left with the mother all the summer are called ‘dilkar’ as opp. to ‘fráfæru-lamb.’",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dilla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dilla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, with dat. <i>to trill, lull;</i> dillandi rödd, <i>a sweet voice:</i> <strong>dillindo,</strong> interj. <i>lullaby:</i> <strong>dillari,</strong> a, m. <i>a triller,</i> of the nightingale; hjartans danspípu dillarinn, Jón Þorl. i. 131.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dimm-hljodr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dimm-hljóðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. = dimmraddaðr, Fas. ii. 231.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dimm-raddadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dimm-raddaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>deep-voiced,</i> Grett. 111.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dimm-vidri"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dimm-viðri
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>dark, cloudy weather.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dimma"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dimma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> d, (but dinimaðisk, Fb. i. 91; dimmat, part., Mar.):—<i>to become dim;</i> neut. or impers., um kveldit er d. tók, <i>when it began to grow dark,</i> Fms. viii. 305; dimmir af nótt, <i>the night darkens,</i> iii. 135: also of clouds, <i>to grow dark</i> (of a gale, storm); þá hvesti ok dimdi í fjörðinn, Espol. Árb. 1768.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dimmr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dimmr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [A. S. and Engl. <i>dim</i>], <i>dim, dark, dusky;</i> d. ok dökt ský, <i>a dim and dark sky,</i> Fms. xi. 136; verða dimt fyrir augum, <i>to see dimly,</i> esp. of sudden changes from darkness to light, iii. 217; var dimt hit neðra, <i>dark below,</i> Háv. 40; d. himin, Matth. xvi. 3; harla dimt var af nótt, Pass. II. 1; dimm nótt, <i>a dark night;</i> d. stigr, a <i>dim path</i>, Fms. i. 140; dimt él, <i>a dark storm,</i> Úlf. 7. 63; d. regn, Lex. Poët.; d. dreki, <i>the dusky dragon,</i> Vsp. 66.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dindill"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dindill
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the tail</i> of a seal.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dingla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dingla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to dangle;</i> <strong>dingull,</strong> m. <i>a small spider,</i> cp. dor-dingull.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dirfa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dirfa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, (vide djarfr), <i>to dare,</i> always with the reflex. pronoun separated or suffixed, dirfask or d. sik, with infin. <i>to dare,</i> Fms. xi. 54, Ísl. ii. 331; d. sik til e-s, <i>to take a thing to heart,</i> Al. 88, 656 A. I. 36: reflex., dirfask, <i>to dare;</i> bændr dirfðusk mjök við Birkibeina, <i>became bold, impudent,</i> Fms. ix. 408; er þeir dirfðusk at hafa með höndum hans píslar-mark, vii. 195; engi maðr dirfðisk at kveðja þess, i. 83, K. Á. 114; dirfask í e-u, þá dirfðumk ek í ræðu ok spurningum, <i>I grew more bold in speech,</i> Sks. 5.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dirfd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dirfð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>boldness,</i> often with the notion of <i>impudence, arrogance,</i> Eg. 47, Glúm. 309, Fms. iv. 161, xi. 54, Post. 645. 71; of-dirfð, <i>impudence.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dirfska"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dirfska
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = dirfð; of-dirfska, <i>temerity.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dirokkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dirokkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a drudge</i> (Dan. <i>drog</i>), a word of abuse, Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dirrindi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dirrindi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "onomatopoetic. <i>the lark’s note,</i> see p. xxxii, col. 1, bottom.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/diskr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          diskr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [a for. word: from Gr. δίσκος; Lat. <i>discus;</i> A. S. and Hel. <i>disc;</i> Engl. <i>d</i>es<i>k</i> and <i>disk;</i> Germ. <i>tisch</i>]:—<i>a plate;</i> þá vóru öngir diskar, Ísl. (Heiðarv. S.) ii. 337, O. H. L. 36, Fms. i. 259, Bs. i. 475; silfr-d., gull-d., <i>silver</i> and <i>gold plate</i> are mentioned as a present given to a king, O. H. 154, cp. Fb. iii. 332; both the words used in this sense, diskr and skutill (Lat. <i>scutellum,</i> Germ. <i>schüssel</i>) are of for. origin; cp. also Rm. 4, 39: in the earliest times small movable tables also served as plates.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dispensera"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dispensera
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to dispense</i> (Lat. word), H. E. i. 510.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dispenseran"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dispenseran
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>dispensing,</i> Stj., Bs.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/disputa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          disputa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>disputera,</strong> að, <i>to dispute</i> (Lat. word), Stj.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/diametr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          díametr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>diameter</i> (Gr. word), 732. 7.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/diar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          díar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. [the Icel. has two words, but both of them poetical and obsolete, viz. díar answering, by the law of Interchange, to Gr. θεός (Icel. <i>d</i> = Gr. θ), and tívar, by the same law, to Lat. <i>deus</i> (Icel. <i>t</i> = Lat. <i>d</i>); cp. Sansk. <i>devas,</i> Gr. θειος, Lat. <i>dîvus,</i> Ital. <i>dio,</i> Fr. <i>dieu</i>]:—<i>gods</i> or <i>priests;</i> this word occurs only twice, Yngl. S. ch. 2—þat var þar siðr, at tólf hofgoðar vóru æðstir, skyldu þeir ráða fyrir blótum ok dómum manna í milli; þat eru díar kallaðir eðr drottnar,—where diar means not <i>the gods</i> themselves but <i>the priests;</i> and by the old poet Kormak in an obscure periphrasis, in a poem addressed to the staunch heathen earl Sigurd; Snorri (Edda 96), in quoting Kormak, takes the word to mean <i>gods;</i> but the version given in Yngl. S. seems more likely; the díar of the Yngl. S. were probably analogous to the Icel. goði, from goð (<i>deus</i>). The age of Kormak shews that the word was probably not borrowed from the Latin.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/digull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dígull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [deig].",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/diki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          díki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>dík,</strong> n. [Germ. <i>teich</i>], <i>a dike, ditch,</i> Eg. 529–531, Hkr. iii. 154, Jb. 245, Grett. 161, Fms. iii. 187, vi. 406, Ó. H. 21 (in a verse), Orkn. 452; <strong>díkis-bokki,</strong> a, m. <i>an eel</i>, poët., Kormak.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dili"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          díli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a spot, mark;</i> alloðin nema d. undir vinstri hendi, Fms. iii. 125.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dis"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dís
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., pl. disir, and an older but obsolete form <strong>jó-dís,</strong> which remains in the earliest poems, jódís (<i>the sister of</i>) úlfs ok Nara = <i>Hela,</i> Ýt. 7; but Loga dís, <i>the sister of Logi,</i> 9; cp. Edda 109: it also remains in the Icel. fem. pr. name Jódís,—the explanation given in Skálda 183 (from jór, <i>equus,</i> and dís) has no philological value, being only the poet’s fancy: [Hel. <i>idis</i> = <i>virgo;</i> A. S. <i>ides;</i> Grimm ingeniously suggests that the Idistaviso in Tacitus may be corrupt for Idisiaviso, <i>the virgin-mead,</i> from <i>idis</i> and <i>viso</i> = Germ. <i>wiese.</i>]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/disa-blot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dísa-blót
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a sacrifice to the</i> disir, Eg. 205, Yngl. S. ch. 33; þar var veizla búin at vetr-nóttum ok gört disablót, Glúm. 336. In early Swed. laws occur <i>disa-þing, a general assembly,</i> held in February, and <i>disa-þings dagher</i> = <i>the day when the d. sat; disn-þings fridher</i> = <i>the peace, sanctity of the d.,</i> Schlyter.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
