        >
          dogg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a pillow</i> (?), in the phrase, að sitja upp við dogg, <i>to lie half erect in bed,</i> leaning the head upon a high pillow.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dokk"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dokk
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>dokka,</strong> u, f. <i>a windlass,</i> Fms. x. 53.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/doparr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          doparr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., and <strong>doppa,</strong> u, f. <i>a boss</i> of metal, Þiðr. 111, Karl, 550 (in a saddle); of earrings, D. N. i. 321: (the last word is freq.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dor-digull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dor-dígull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(<strong>dordingull</strong>), m. <i>a small spider; araneus tolas ater splendens, filo demissorio,</i> Eggert Itin. 609; also called fiski-karl, <i>fisher-carle;</i> the word is no doubt to be spelt <strong>dorg-dígull,</strong> i. e. <i>angling spider;</i> for popular lore as to the dordígull vide Ísl. Þjóðs. ii. 547, 548: the small spider’s web is called hégómi, q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dorg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dorg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>an angler’s tackle,</i> rod and line, etc., for trout or small fish; þeir réru tveir á báti með dorgar sínar at smá-fiski, Sæm. Gm. (introd.), p. 32; land-dorgar, <i>the land of</i> dorg, <i>the sea,</i> Edda 66; dorgar-skot, <i>a kind of fishing implement,</i> D. N. iii. 201; cp. dorga.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dorga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dorga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to fish with a</i> dorg: in mod. use dorg is only used of fishing through holes in the ice; metaph. Icel. also say, d. við e-t, <i>to go angling for a thing, go dangling after it.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dorma"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dorma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Lat. <i>dormire</i>], <i>to doze.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dormr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dormr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a dormitory</i> in a convent, Safn i. 82.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dornikar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dornikar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. [from Doornik in Flanders], <i>a kind of water-tight boots,</i> Jón Þorl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dorri"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dorri
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a wether.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dotta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dotta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, (dott, n.), <i>to nod</i> from sleep; <strong>dottr,</strong> m. <i>a nodder,</i> Háv. 44.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dolg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dólg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(<strong>dolg</strong>), n. [A. S. <i>dolg</i> = <i>vidnus,</i> O. H. G. <i>tolg</i>], <i>direful enmity,</i> only in poetry in compds, as dólg-brandr, -eisa, -ljós, <i>the fire, embers, light of the</i> d., = <i>sword;</i> dólg-lið, <i>the ale of the</i> d., i. e. <i>blood;</i> dólg-linnr, <i>the</i> d. <i>snake, i. e. spear;</i> dolg-svala, <i>the battle-swallow,</i> i. e. <i>the shaft;</i> gaping wounds are called dólg-spor, Hkv. 2. 40.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dolg-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dólg-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>fiendish,</i> Finnb. 326.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dolg-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dólg-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = dólgr, Hkv. 2. 49 (Ed. dólgar mær).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dolgr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dólgr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(<strong>dolgr</strong>), m. [Ulf. renders χρεωφειλέτης<i>,</i> Luke vii. 41, by <i>dulgisskula;</i> and δανειστής<i>,</i> id., by <i>dulgahaitja</i>]:—<i>a fiend;</i> dauðir dólgar, <i>ghosts,</i> Hkv. 2. 49—verða öflgari allir á nóttum dauðir dólgar mær, en um daga ljósa—used synonymous to ‘devil,’ djöfull, Fms. iii. 200, vi. 143, x. 172 (of a giant); þar sat dólgr í hásæti, mikill ok illiligr (of witches), Fas. ii. 184; svartir dólgar, Karl. 525; sögðu at sá d. væri kominn í bygðina er þeim þætti eigi dæll viðfangs, Grett. 127; söku-dólgr, <i>a criminal;</i> vide dylgja.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/doli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [<i>dole</i>, Ivar Aasen; cp. Engl. <i>dull</i>], <i>a drudge,</i> Edda. (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dolpr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dólpr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a sort of dress,</i> Edda (Gl.) 232.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dolpungr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dólpungr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the larva</i> of a caterpillar, Björn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-festa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-festa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>submitting to subpoena,</i> N. G. L. i. 22, 221.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-fe"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-fé
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a fee</i> or <i>payment fixed by sentence,</i> D. N.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-flogi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-flogi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. a law term, <i>a runaway from court,</i> used either of the plaintiff or judge if they do not appear in court, or quit the court, or even rise in court, without leave; in which case the judge forfeits his seat, and the plaintiff his case; defined N. G. L. i. 23, 220.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-hringr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-hringr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>‘doom-ring,’ ‘judgment-ring;’</i> (cp. also vé-bönd, <i>the sacred bounds</i> or <i>bar</i>): the courts of heathen times were surrounded by the dómhringr, about a bow-shot from the centre where the benches were placed; no evil-doer might enter this hallowed ring, or commit an act of violence within it; if he did so, he was called a vargr í véum (<i>lupus in sanctii);</i> the Engl. law term ‘bar’ answers to this old word, cp. Gr. δρύφακτοι, Lat. <i>cancelli;</i> the Goth. <i>staua,</i> = <i>court</i> and <i>judge,</i> properly means <i>a staff, bar;</i> the bar was, according to Eg. l. c., a pole of hazel-wood, hesli-stengr: classical passages referring to this,—þar sér enn dómhring þann, er menn vóru dæmdir í til blóts, í þeim hring stendr Þórs steinn, etc., Eb. ch. 10; þar stendr enn Þórs steinn … ok þar ‘hjá’ (better) er sá domhringr er (<i>in which</i>) menn skyldi til blóts dæma, Landn. 98: another classical passage is Eg. ch. 57 beginning; cp. also Fas. iii. Gautr. S. ch. 7, Edda 10, though the ‘ring’ is not expressly mentioned in these last two passages: hann gengr í dómhringinn ok setzk niðr, Band. 6; en þeir eigu at rísa ór dóminum ok sitja í dómhring innan meðan um þá sök er dæmt, Grág. i. 78, cp. 17, 26: in early heathen times this sacred circle was formed by a ring of stones, cp. dóm-steinar: no doubt some of the so-called Celtic or Druidical stone circles are relics of these public courts, e. g. the Stones of Stennis in the Orkneys; cp. Scott’s last note to the Pirate, referring to this subject: even in later times, when the thing was obsolete, the name still remained.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-hus"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-hús
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the ‘house of doom,’ court-bouse,</i> Sks. 784; the idea is foreign, though the word is native: the old courts and meetings were always held in the open air.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-kirkja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-kirkja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [Germ. <i>dom-kirche,</i> from Lat. <i>domus</i>], <i>a cathedral,</i> (mod.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-leggja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-leggja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "lagði, a law term, <i>to lay before a court,</i> Dipl. iii. 13.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-nefna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-nefna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>the nomination of judges</i> in the Icel. court, described in Íb. ch. 5; in parliament the goðar (<i>priests</i>) had the right to appoint the judges, Grág. i. 25; þeir (viz. the priests) skyldu dómnefnur eiga á þingum, Fms. iii. 106.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-rof"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-rof
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>disregard of judgment,</i> Grág. i. 87, cp. Gþl. 21.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-rudning"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-ruðning
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a challenging of judges,</i> Grág. i. 27.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-seta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-seta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>sitting in court, judgment,</i> Sks. 638, 641.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-setning"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-setning
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>opening the court,</i> N. G. L. i. 220.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-stadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-staðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>court, tribunal,</i> Grág. i. 448, ii. 405, Edda 10.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-staurr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-staurr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a court bar,</i> properly <i>court rails,</i> but used in N. G. L. i. 220 of select men <i>who stand outside</i> and pronounce an opinion on the case.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-stefna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-stefna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(<strong>-stemna</strong>), u, f. <i>a citing, summoning,</i> Grág. i. 448.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-steinar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-steinar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. <i>‘court-stones,’ court-ring,</i> Sturl. i. 31, vide dómhringr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-stoll"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-stóll
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the judgment-seat,</i> John xix. 13, Sks. 622, 637, Hom. 46, Fms. x. 443.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-saeti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-sæti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. = dómstóll, Sks. 488, 606.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-saetr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-sætr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., in the phrases, vera d., N. G. L. i. 84; eiga dómsætt, <i>to be qualified to sit in a court, a lawful judge,</i> Grág. i. 64.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dom-varzla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóm-varzla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>guarding a court,</i> Grág. i. 65. <strong>dómvörzlu-maðr,</strong> m. <i>a man who guards the court, a javelin-man,</i> Grág. l. c.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/domandi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dómandi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m., pl. dómendr, [A. S. <i>dêmend</i>], <i>a judge,</i> Fas. ii. 32, Grág. i. 27, 65, 79, Nj., N. G. L. i. ii, Eg. ch. 57, Stj. 378 sqq.; as to the Icel. judges cp. esp. Grág. Þ. Þ. ch. 1, 6, and numberless passages in the laws and Sagas.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/domari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dómari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Dan. <i>dommer;</i> Swed. <i>domare</i>], <i>a judge,</i> this is the common form instead of dómandi, Edda 93, K. Á. 202, Sks. 472 B, Pass. 27. 5, 28. 10; <strong>dómara-sæti,</strong> n. <i>judgment-seat,</i> Sks. 480 B; <strong>Dómara-bók,</strong> f. <i>the Book of Judges:</i> used besides in many compds, lands-dómari, <i>chief judge</i>, of Pilate, Matth. xxvii. 27, Pass. 25. i; yfir-dómari, undir-dómari, etc.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/domr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dómr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Goth. <i>dôms,</i> which occurs once, but not in Ulf., who only uses the word in compds, and renders κρίσις and κριτής by <i>siaua;</i> A. S. <i>dôm;</i> Engl. <i>doom</i> and the termin. <i>-dom;</i> O. H. G. <i>tom;</i> known in Germ. only from the termin. <i>-tum (-thum)</i>].",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/doni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dóni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. (and compds <strong>dóna-legr, -skapr, -háttr</strong>); this is a college word, by which the students of the old colleges at Skalholt and Hólar called outsiders as opposed to collegians, like the <i>Philister</i> of Germ. universities: it is still used: from Span. <i>don,</i> through the E. Engl. <i>done</i>, (<i>‘In þi dysch sette not þi spone, noþer on þe brynke, as unlernyd done,’</i> = einsog ólærðr dóni, <i>as an illiterate clown</i> (used mockingly), Bodl. Ashm. MSS. no. 61, about A. D. 1500, Boke of Curtesy, E. Engl. Text Society, 1868.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
