              "__html": "m., dimin., dat. dregli, a <i>ribbon,</i> Nj. 214, Hkr. i. 320, Edda 20, O. H. L. 65, H. E. ii. 113; dregla-lið = dreglat lið, <i>soldiery decorated with ribbons,</i> Fb. ii. 337,—a reference to the custom of neophytes after baptism wearing a white ribbon round their heads.",
            }
