      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreka-merki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreka-merki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the sign of a dragon,</i> Karl. 35 1; the constellation <i>Scorpio</i> is also called Sporð-dreka-merki. The language distinguishes between flug-dreki, <i>the flying dragon</i> of the tales, and sporð-dreki, <i>a tailed dragon,</i> i. e. <i>a scorpion.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [from the Gr. δράκων; Lat. <i>draco;</i> A. S. <i>draca;</i> Germ. <i>drache;</i> Engl. <i>dragon;</i> Swed. <i>drake;</i> Dan. <i>drage</i>]:<i>—a dragon,</i> Al. 160, 656 A, Gullþ. ch. 4; this word, which undoubtedly is of foreign origin, is however very old; it occurs in Vsp. 65 (there is no reason to suspect the genuineness of this verse); it is most freq. used by poets of the 10th and 11th centuries, and is especially used of ships of war bearing a dragon’s head as beaks. Fms. ii. 179, 182, 217, 303, iv. 354, v. 311, vi. 314, 360, vii. 51, 109, 248, x. 36, 77, 204–206, xi. 45, 375.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drekk-hladinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drekk-hlaðinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>‘drench-loaden,’ a ship laden till she sinks.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drekka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drekka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>drink, beverage,</i> Edda 48: <i>a banquet,</i> N. G. L. i. 91, Og. 13; cp. Ægis-drekka, <i>the banquet at Ægir,</i> Edda.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drekka-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drekka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. drakk, pl. drukku; sup. drukkit; pres. drekk; pret. subj. drykki; [Ulf. <i>drigkan;</i> A. S. <i>drinkan;</i> Engl. <i>drink;</i> O. H. G. <i>trinkan;</i> M. H. G. <i>trinken;</i> Dan. <i>drikke;</i> Swed. <i>dricka</i>]:—<i>to drink</i>, the beverage or feast in acc.; d. mjöð, Hm. 18; mungát, el, Fms. viii. 166, Hm. 82; d. full, minni (<i>a toast</i>), Eg. 552, Fms. vi. 442; d. horn, <i>to drain, drink off a horn, a cup,</i> Hkr. i. 35; síðan tók Kolskeggr justu eina af miði fulla ok drakk, Nj. 43; d. drykk, <i>to drink a draught,</i> Fms. xi. 233; eptir þat tók Þórir kalkann ok drakk af tvá drykki, Gullþ. 7; þú skalt d. af tvá drykki, id.; d. brjóst (acc.), <i>to suck</i> (v. brjóst-drekkr), Mar. 656 A. 23, cp. Gþl. 504.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drekkja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drekkja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t and ð, [Ulf. <i>dragkjan;</i> Engl. <i>drench</i>], <i>to drown,</i> with dat., Edda (pref.) 144, Fms. iii. 28, Fas. ii. 35: metaph. <i>to swamp,</i> Fms. x. 395: with acc., Hom. 154 (rarely): reflex, <i>to be submerged,</i> Fms. xi. 66.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drembi-liga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drembi-liga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. (<strong>-ligr,</strong> adj.), <i>haughtily,</i> Fms. vi. 155, x. 237, Nj. 78, Fas. i. 39; cp. rembiligr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreng-leysi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreng-leysi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>want of generosity, unmanliness,</i> Stj. 396.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreng-lundadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreng-lundaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>-lyndr,</strong> adj. <i>noble-minded,</i> Hkr. i. 327, Nj. 30, Fms. ii. 220; hógværr ok drenglyndr, <i>gentle-minded and high-minded,</i> Nj. 30 (of Njal).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreng-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreng-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a bachelor,</i> opp. to bóndi, N. G. L. i. 31, 98: <i>a stout doughty man,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreng-mannliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreng-mannliga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <strong>(-ligr,</strong> adj.), <i>bravely, doughtily,</i> Nj. 78, v. l.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreng-menska"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreng-menska
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>boldness,</i> Fas. i. 404.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreng-skapr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreng-skapr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. ar, <i>courage, high-mindedness;</i> the phrase, falla með drengskap, <i>to fall sword in hand,</i> Fms. ii. 42; vit ok d., xi. 112; deyja með drengskap, opp. to lifa með skömm, v. 136; þínum drengskap (<i>manliness</i>) skal ek við bregða, Nj. 13: allit., dáð ok d.; með litlum drengskap, <i>cowardly,</i> Fms. viii. 29; má þat verða til drengskapar, Ísl. ii. 366; drengskapar-raun, <i>trial of</i> d., Sturl. ii. 62.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drengi-liga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
