          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drep-sótt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a plague, pest,</i> Yer. 21, Kb. 478.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drep-sottr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drep-sóttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>plague-stricken,</i> Bs. ii. 33.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drepa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drepa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. drap, 2nd pers. drapt, mod. drapst, pl. drápu; pret. subj. dræpi; part. drepit; pres. drep; with the suff. neg. pret. drap-a. Orkn.: [A. S. <i>drepan;</i> Dan. <i>dræbe;</i> Swed. <i>drapa;</i> O. H. G. <i>trefan;</i> mod. Germ. <i>treffen,</i> whence the mod. Dan. <i>treffe,</i> in the sense <i>to hit;</i> Ulf. uses <i>slahan</i> and <i>stautjan,</i> but never <i>dripan;</i> in Engl. the word is lost.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drepill"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drepill
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., in knatt-drepill, <i>a bat,</i> in the game of cricket.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drettingr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drettingr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [dratta], <i>a loiterer,</i> a cognom., Sturl. i. 89.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreyma"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreyma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d and ð, poët. obsol. pret. reflex. dreymdumk; [draumr; A. S. <i>dryman</i> = <i>psallere;</i> Hel. <i>drômian</i> = <i>jubilari;</i> Engl. <i>dream;</i> Germ. <i>träumen;</i> Dan. <i>drömme;</i> Swed. <i>drömma</i>]:<i>—to dream;</i> in Icel. impers. and with a double acc., that of the dreamer and the dream or person appearing; thus, mik dreyindi draum, mik dreymdi mann, etc.; þat dreymdi mik, Nj. 95; hvat hefir þik dreymt, id.; hinn veg d. mik þó, 53; hann kvað sik dreymt hafa Hákon jarl (acc.), 122; dreymt hefir mik mart í vetr, Ld. 126; enn dreymdi hann enn þriðja draum, Fms. xi. 8; or poët., draum dreymdumk = draum dreymdi mik, <i>I dreamt a dream,</i> Bjarn. 49; or with ‘at’ with subj., hann (acc.) dreymði þat, at hann væri at lögbergi, Íb. ch. 4, cp. 385: konung dreymdi aldri, <i>the king never had a dream,</i> Hkr. i. 171; the phrase, at dreyma fyrir daglátunum, esp. of light merry dreams at daybreak, which people in Icel. consider a sign of good health, Fél. ix.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreypa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreypa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t and ð, [drjúpa, draup], <i>to drop, put a drop of fluid,</i> wine, medicine, etc., into the mouth of one sick, fainting, and the like, the fluid in dat.; d. e-u á e-t, or í munn em; hann dreypir vígðu vatni í munn henni, Bs. i. 199; at hann dreypi vatni á tungu mína, Greg. 23, Luke xvi. 24; d. víni á e-n (of fainting), Fas. iii. 508, 571; hann dreypti á konuna þar til at hon raknaði við, ii. 151: <i>to dip</i>, at hann dreypi í vatn enum minsta fingri sínum, Greg. 22, Luke xvi. 24, where the N. T. of 1540 sqq. has, at hann ‘drepi’ hinu fremsta síns fingrs í vatn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreyr-blandinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreyr-blandinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>blent, mixed with blood,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dreyr-fadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dreyr-fáðr
