        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dros-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drós
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [cp. Ital. <i>druda</i> = <i>a sweetheart</i>], poët. <i>a girl;</i> drósir heita þær er kyrlátar eru, Edda 108, Fas. iii. 618, Al. 70, 152.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drott"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drótt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drott-kvaedr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drótt-kvæðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (<strong>-kvæði,</strong> n.), <i>in the heroic metre,</i> the metre used in the drápas (q. v.) or poems which were recited before a king and the king’s men (drótt), whence the name probably comes; dróttkvæðr is opp. to kviðu-háttr, <i>the epic, narrative metre,</i> and ljóða-háttr, <i>the metre of didactic poems</i> or <i>poems in the form of dialogues,</i> Edda (Ht.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drott-lat"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drótt-lát
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. adj. <i>beloved by the household, gentle,</i> epithet of a queen, Am. 10.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drott-megir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drótt-megir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. <i>men, people,</i> Vþm. 11, 12.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drott-seti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drótt-seti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a steward at the king’s table;</i> this word occurs in various forms throughout the Saxon parts of Germany, Holland, Belgium, Friesland, Brabant, etc. Du Cange records a ‘drossardus Brabantiae;’ it is in mid. Lat. spelt <i>drossatus,</i> Germ. and Saxon <i>drost, land-drost, reichs-drost (drozerus regni),</i> Fris. <i>drusta,</i> vide Grimm; the Dutch prefer the form <i>drossardus:</i> in the court of the king of Norway the office of dróttseti is not heard of before the beginning of the 12th century (the passage Bs. i. 37 is monkish and of late composition), and is there a kind of <i>head-cook</i> or <i>steward at the king’s table,</i> who was to be elected from the king’s skutilsveinar; d. spurði hvat til matar skyldi búa, <i>the</i> d. <i>asked the king what meat they should dress,</i> Fms. vii. 159 (about A. D. 1125), ix. 249, x. 147; d. ok skenkjari, N. G. L. ii. 413, 415; cp. also Hirðskrá (N. G. L. l. c.) ch. 26, Fms. x. 100 refers to the drost of the German emperor. In the 14th century the dróttseti became a high officer in Sweden and Denmark. The derivation from drótt and seti (seti can only mean <i>a sitter,</i> not <i>one who makes to sit,</i> cp. land-seti, <i>a land-sitter, a tenant</i>) is dubious; the Norse word may be an etymologising imitation of the mid. Lat. <i>drossatus.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drotta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drótta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, d. e-u at e-m, <i>to bring to one’s door-post,</i> i. e. <i>impute to one.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drottin-hollr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dróttin-hollr
