          drykkju-skáli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a banquet hall,</i> Orkn. 244, Fms. i. 299.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drykkju-stofa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drykkju-stofa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = drykkjuskáli. Fms. vii. 147, Eg. 553.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drykkju-stutr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drykkju-stútr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a drinking-can,</i> Bs. i. 877.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drykkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drykkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "jar, m., pl. ir, [A. S. <i>drinc</i>; Engl. <i>drink</i>; Germ. <i>trunk;</i> Dan. <i>drik</i>]:<i>—drink, beverage,</i> Fms. xi. 108, 233; eiga drykk ok sess við e-n, Eg. 95: <i>a draught,</i> Edda 32, 48; hvat hafa Einherjar at drykk? 24; vatns-d., <i>a draught of water,</i> id.; svala-d., þorsta-d., <i>a thirst-draught;</i> muntu nú eigi sparask til eins drykkjar, <i>one draught more,</i> 32; þreyta á drykkinn, <i>to take a deep draught,</i> id.; drekka í tveimr, þremr … drykkjum, <i>to drain in two, three … draughts,</i> id.; undarliga mundi mér þykkja ef þvílíkir drykkir væri svá litlir kallaðir, id.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dryllr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dryllr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a nickname, Fms. i; <strong>drylla,</strong> u, f., Snót 184; also spelt with <i>u, proluvies alvi,</i> (vulgar.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drymba"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drymba
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a kind of stockings</i> (?), Art. (Parcevals S.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dryn-rann"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dryn-rann
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., poet. <i>‘the roaring inn of drink,’ a drinking-horn,</i> Fas. l. c.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drynja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drynja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "drundi, pres. dryn, <i>to roar.</i> This root word is common to Goth., Scandin., Fris., and Dutch; for Ulf. <i>drunjus</i> = φθόγγος, Róm. x. 18, is a sufficient proof; in Swed. we have <i>dröna,</i> and <i>drön</i> neut.; Dan. <i>dröne</i> and <i>drön;</i> Dutch <i>dreunen;</i> North. E. <i>to drone,</i> as a cow; Fris. <i>dröne;</i> the mod. High Germ. <i>dröhnen</i> was, in the 17th century, borrowed from Low Germ. In old Icel. no instance happens to be on record, except dryn-rann in Gsp. 23, Fas. i. 480; in mod. usage it is freq. enough, and the absence in old writers seems to be accidental; draugr dimmr og magr, drundi í björgum undir, Snót 226, a ditty by Stefan Olafsson; drynja and dynja are different in sense, drynja denotes <i>roaring,</i> dynja <i>crushing;</i> þá heyrði hilmir hátt við kletta drafnar drynja dunur þungar, <i>of the roaring surf,</i> Od. (poët.) v. 401.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drynr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drynr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. [Dan. and Swed. <i>drön</i>], <i>roaring;</i> <strong>drunur,</strong> f., vide above.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drysil"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drysil-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>dusil-,</strong> a term of contempt, <i>paltry,</i> in the COMPDS <strong>drysil-djöfull,</strong> m. <i>a petty, paltry devil, devilkin,</i> Fms. iii. 201, in the amusing ghost story, opp. to the big inmates of hell. <strong>drysil-hross</strong> (spelt dusil-), n. <i>n paltry horse,</i> Ísl. iii. 333. <strong>drysil-menni,</strong> n. <i>a paltry, petty man,</i> Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/drygja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drýgja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, [drjúgr; A. S. <i>dreógan</i> = <i>to endure;</i> North. E. and Scot. <i>to dree</i> = <i>to endure, suffer</i>]:<i>—to commit, perpetrate,</i> mostly in a bad sense; d. synd, <i>to commit a sin,</i> K. Á. 202; d. glæp, <i>id</i>.; d. hórdóm, <i>to commit whoredom,</i> Sks. 340; þú skalt ekki hórdóm d., <i>thou shall not commit whoredom;</i> d. misræðu við konu, <i>id.,</i> Grág. i. 338; d. hernað, <i>to pirate,</i> ii. 70; d. ílsku, Orkn. 32: it is a standing phrase in eccl. or sacred writers, N. T., Pass., Vidal.: in a good sense only in a few phrases as the allit., d. dáð, Sturl. iii. 7; or in poets or bad old prose; orlög d., A. S. <i>orlig dreogan</i> (cp. the North. E. <i>to dree one’s weird</i> = <i>to abide one’s fate</i>), <i>to try one’s luck,</i> Vkv. i, cp. also the Germ. tales, <i>in die welt gehen;</i> d. hlýðni, Sks. 675; d. mannliga náttúru, <i>to pay the debt of nature,</i> 447; d. e-s vilja, <i>to comply with one’s wishes,</i> Bær. 14,—the last three passages are bad prose.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/draegr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          drægr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>that which can be pulled against.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/draemt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dræmt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. adj. [from draumr ?], <i>slowly,</i> Ósv.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/draeplingr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
