      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dubla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dubla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>dufla,</strong> að, [dubla = <i>a coin</i>, Du Cange], <i>to gamble,</i> Gþl. 521; <strong>dublari,</strong> a, m. <i>a gambler,</i> Róm. 161.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dug-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dug-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (<strong>-leysi,</strong> n.), <i>good for nothing,</i> Þórð. 47 (Ed, 1847).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/duga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          duga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. dugði; pres. dugi; sup. dugat; imperat. dugi þú, mod. dugðu; [A. S. <i>dugan;</i> Scot. and North. E. <i>to dow;</i> O. H. G. <i>tûgan;</i> Germ. <i>taugen:</i> Dan. <i>due;</i> Swed. <i>duga;</i> Engl. <i>do,</i> in phrases such as, that will <i>do</i>]:—<i>to help, aid,</i> with dat.; dugi þú mér Hvíta-Kristr, Fs. 101; d. frændum sínum, Post. 658 C. 19; ok vill eigi d. henni, <i>will not support her,</i> Grág. i. 368; hann dugði heiðnum mönnum, 655 iii. 4: with the notion <i>to do, suffice,</i> þat er þér man d., <i>which will do for thee,</i> Nj. 13; hefir oss þó dugat þessi átrúnaðr, <i>this faith has done well for us,</i> Fms. i. 34; mun þat d. mínum hesti, <i>it will do for my horse,</i> Mag.: the proverb, fátt er svá illt at einu-gi dugi, cp. the Engl. ‘’tis an ill wind that blows nobody good,’ Al. 46, Hm. 134; mun þér eigi þat d. at sofa hér, <i>it will not do (is not safe) for thee to sleep here,</i> Fms. v. 307: adding prepp. við, at, til, <i>to succour, lend help,</i> en Gísli fór at d. þeim við, Gísl. 22; d. þeir nú at þeim mönnum er lífs var van, Finnb. 316, cp. at-dugnaðr; hón dugir eigi verr til enn einhverr karlmaðr, Fb. i. 533: impers., e-m dugir e-t, <i>it does well, beseems, becomes;</i> hón dugir mér illa (vel), Mar. (Fr.), Hkv. I. 45; þó myndi mér enn vel d. (<i>it would do well for me</i>), ef ek fengja at drekka, Ísl. ii. 369.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dugan-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dugan-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>doughty,</i> Ýt. 15.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/dugandi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          dugandi-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>dugandis-,</strong> as a prefix to nouns, denoting <i>doughty;</i> d. maðr (<strong>dugand-maðr,</strong> Fms. viii. 104), a <i>doughty man,</i> Dipl. i. 3, Orkn. 456, Rd. 260, Róm. 137.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
