        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. átti; pret. subj. ætti, pres. eigi; pres. ind. á, 2nd pers. átt (irreg. eigr, Dipl. v. 24), pl. eigum, 3rd pers. pl. old form eigu, mod. eiga; imperat. eig and eigðu; sup. átt; with suffixed neg. pres. ind. 1st pers. á’k-at, 2nd pers. átt-attu; pret. subj. ættim-a: [Gr. ἔχω; Goth. <i>aigan;</i> A. S. <i>âgan;</i> Hel. <i>êgan;</i> O. H. G. <i>eigan;</i> Swed. <i>äga;</i> Dan. <i>eje;</i> Engl. <i>to owe</i> and <i>own</i>, of which the former etymologically answers to ‘eiga,’ the latter to ‘eigna’]:—<i>to have, possess.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
