          href="/word/einga-vinr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          einga-vinr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>an only friend, bosom friend,</i> Nj. 77. In mod. usage einka- (q. v.) is used instead of einga-, which is an obsolete form; and even in old MSS. both forms occur, e. g. Stj. (l. c.), v. l.: Þiðr. 130 spells ‘einka-,’ and it even occurs in old vellums as 623, p. 41; einka-sonr, Luke vii. 12.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/eingi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          eingi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>einginn,</strong> in old writers more freq. spelt ‘eng’ (which accords with the mod. pronunciation), <strong>engi, enginn,</strong> qs. einn-gi from einn, <i>one,</i> and the negative suffix -gi:—<i>none.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/einigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
