              "__html": "f. indecl. [Dan. <i>ælde</i>], <i>‘eld,’ old age;</i> the saying, öllum hefir elli á kné komit, <i>old age has brought all on their knees,</i> cp. the tale in Edda 33, 34, where the old giantess Elli wrestles with Thor, whence in poetry she is called ‘<i>the antagonist</i> of Thor,’ Eg. (in a verse); engi hefir sá orðit …, at eigi komi ellin öllum til falls, Edda 34; fyrir elli sakar, Eg. 107; eigi er þat síðr en elli …, Nj. 171.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
