        >
          elsku-váttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a love token.</i> Elska never occurs as a verb or noun in old heathen poets; Arnor is the first poet on record who uses it; old writers prefer using ást; with Christianity, and esp. since the Reformation, it gained ground; ἀγαπαν of the N. T. is usually rendered by elska (<i>to love</i>) and ἀγάπη by elska (<i>love</i>) or kærleiki (<i>chanty</i>); so, mann-elska, <i>humanity, kindness.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
