        >
          ey-vit
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>ey-fit, ey-fvit, ey-vitar,</strong> adv. [ey = <i>not</i>, and vit = <i>wight</i>], <i>naught;</i> used as subst. eyvitar, gen., Hm. 93; eyvitu, dat., 27; but else used as adv., blandask eyvitar (<i>blend not</i>) við aðra ísa, Sks. 40 new Ed.: the proverb, eyfit týr (<i>it boots not</i>) þótt skyndi seinn, Mkv.; eyfit hef ek fé, <i>I have no money,</i> Fbr. 49 new Ed.; en biskup hafði þó eyfvit at sök við þenna mann, <i>the bishop could do nothing with this man,</i> Bs. i. 170; hón matti eyfit mæla eðr sofa, <i>she could neither speak nor sleep,</i> 180; hón mátti ok eyfit sofa, 195.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
