          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          feti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> a, m. <i>a stepper, pacer,</i> in compds, há-feti, létt-feti, mál-feti, <i>a high-stepper, light-stepper,</i> etc., poët. names of a race-horse.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/fetill"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          fetill
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. fetli, pl. fetlar; an older dat. form fatli (cp. katli) seems to be left in the phrase, bera hönd í fatla (qs. fatli), <i>to carry the arm in a sling:</i> [Germ. <i>fessel</i>]:—<i>the strap by which a bag is hung on the shoulder,</i> N. G. L. i. 349: <i>the strap</i> or <i>belt</i> of a shield or sword (skjaldar-fetill, sverds-f., Gr. τελαμών), umgörð ok fetlar, Fas. i. 414, El. 22, 33, Edda 123, N. G. L. ii. 422; hence the sword is in poetry called <strong>fetil-stingi,</strong> a, m. <i>a ‘belt-pin,’</i> etc. <strong>fetla-byrðr,</strong> f. <i>a burthen carried by straps,</i> N. G. L. i. 143.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
