        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. (mod. <strong>firni</strong>), [Ulf. <i>fairina</i> = αἰτία], <i>an abomination, shocking thing;</i> mæltu margir at slíkt væri mikil firn, Nj. 156, Fs. 62, Sturl. i. 12, Fms. vi. 38, Gullþ. 13; svá miklum firnum, Eg. 765; f. ok endemi, or heyr á firn, <i>what a monstrous thing!</i> Fms. vii. 21, 25: the saying, firnum nýtr þess er firnum fær, cp. the Lat. ‘male parta male dilabuntur,’ Fbr. 28, Grett. 16 new Ed.: gen. pl. <strong>firna-,</strong> used as a prefix to adjectives and nouns, <i>shockingly.</i>",
            }
