        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [fjá], <i>hatred;</i> an obsolete word, occurs in old prose in the phrase, reka e-n fjónum, <i>to persecute,</i> Ver. 29, Rb. 388; or else in poetry, leggja fjón á e-n, <i>to hate one</i>, Hallfred: in pl., konungs f., <i>the king’s wrath,</i> Ad. 11; vekja f., <i>to stir up quarrels,</i> Sl. 76, vide Lex. Poët.; guð-fjón, <i>an abomination, that which drives the gods away,</i> Fbr. (in a verse): mod. poets use a verb <strong>fjóna,</strong> að, <i>to hate</i> (Bjarn. 67, 122), probably misled by the corrupt passage in Sl. 27.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
