        >
          fóðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Engl. <i>fodder;</i> Germ. <i>futter;</i> Dan. and Swed. <i>foder</i>], <i>fodder</i> for cattle, (but fæði or fæða of human food), Ísl. ii. 138, Gþl. 503, Fbr. 156: <i>a certain quantity of fodder</i> or <i>hay</i>, a stack thus contains so many kýr-fóðr or lambs-fóðr:—<i>a foddering of lambs</i> for the parson in the winter, hence a parish has so and so many lambs-fóðr; skila úr fóðrum, <i>to return lambs</i> in the spring. <strong>fóðr-birgðir,</strong> f. pl. (<strong>-birgr,</strong> adj.), <i>stores of hay.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
