          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, mod. að, <i>to rush, run frantically;</i> hann spurði hví hann gandi svá, Sturl. ii. 177; ganaði hann langt undan hernum, Fas. iii. 422; ganir at honum ok höggr, Jómsv. 49; þótt þú ganir galinn, Skáld H. 2. 57: of wildfire, Skálda 202 (in a verse); in Fbr. 162 (in a verse) it has the notion <i>to glare in one’s face;</i> akin is góna (q. v.), <i>to stare.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gand-alfr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gand-álfr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a pr. name, <i>a wizard, bewitched demon.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gand-fluga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gand-fluga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = galdrafluga, <i>a ‘gand’ fly, gad-fly,</i> a kind of tipula, Eggert Itin. 604.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gand-reid"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gand-reið
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the ‘witches’ ride;’</i> in nursery tales a witch is said to ride on a broomstick, Germ. <i>besenstiel;</i> in old lore they were said to ride by night on wolves, which are hence in poetry called ‘the steeds of witches;’ fá þú mér út krókstaf minn ok bandvetlinga því at ek vil á gandreið fara, Fms. iii. 176; ekki skorti gandreiðir í eynni um nóttina, Fas. ii. 131; hann kvað hann séð hafa gandreið, ok er þat jafnan fyrir stórtíðindum, Nj. 195; cp. also on this subject Ísl. Þjóðs. i. 440 sqq.; renna göndum, <i>to slide on ‘gands,’ ride a witch-ride;</i> víða hefi ek göndum rennt í nótt, of a witch in Fbr. 124; víta ganda, <i>to bewitch ‘gands,’</i> i. e. <i>to deal in sorcery,</i> Vsp. 25, cp. the passage in Þiðr. S., fór Ostracia út ok rœrði gand sinn, <i>then O.</i> (a witch) <i>went out</i> (cp. útiseta) <i>and reared her ‘gands,’</i> i. e. <i>raised ghosts,</i> or gener. <i>exercised her black art,</i>—the MSS. have here even neut. gannd (gönd) sín. The compd spá-gandar in Vsp. seems to mean <i>‘spae-ghosts’</i> or <i>spirits of divination.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gand-rekr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gand-rekr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a gale brought about by witchcraft,</i> Bs. i. 647 (in a verse), Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gand-vik"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gand-vík
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>‘Gand’ bay</i>, i. e. <i>Magic bay,</i> the old name of the <i>White Sea,</i> for the Lapps were famous sorcerers.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gandr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gandr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m.:—the exact sense of this word is somewhat dubious; it is mostly used in poetry and in compds, and denotes <i>anything enchanted</i> or <i>an object used by sorcerers,</i> almost like <i>zauber</i> in Germ., and hence <i>a monster, fiend;</i> thus the Leviathan of northern mythology is called Jörmun-gandr, <i>the great ‘gand;’</i> or Storðar-gandr, <i>the ‘gand’ of the earth:</i> a snake or serpent is by Kormak called gandr or gandir, Korm. ch. 8: wildfire is hallar g., <i>a worrier of halls,</i> and selju g., <i>a willow-worrier,</i> Lex. Poët.: the wolf Fenrir is called Vonar-gandr, <i>the monster of the river Von,</i> vide Edda.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-dagr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-dagr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "freq. spelt by metath. <strong>Gagn-dagr,</strong> m. [A. S. <i>Gang-däg</i>], <i>the Rogation-days,</i> called <i>‘Ganging days’</i> from the practice of going in procession round the boundaries on those days, K. Þ. K., Rb., N. G. L. passim: the 25th of April is called Gangdagrinn eini, <i>the minor Rogation-day,</i> K. Þ. K. 106, Rb. 46, 544; in pl., Grág. i. 325, Fms. vii. 228, N. G. L. i. 24, 348, K. Þ. K. 102, vide Bs. ii. 247.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-fagr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-fagr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>with a graceful gait,</i> Eb. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-fasta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-fasta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(<strong>Gagn-f.</strong>), u, f. <i>the Rogation-fast,</i> in the Rogation-week, Vm. 94, N. G. L. i. 17.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-faeri"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-færi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Dan. <i>före</i> or <i>gangföre</i>], <i>the condition of a road;</i> íllt (gott) g., <i>bad</i> (<i>good</i>) <i>walking,</i> Fms. viii. 400.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-faerr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-færr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>able to walk,</i> Hom. 152.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-lati"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-lati
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a ‘lazy goer,’ an idler;</i> and <strong>gang-löt,</strong> f. <i>id.,</i> pr. names of the servants in the hall of Hela, Edda.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-leri"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-leri
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. obsolete, except as a pr. name of the mythical wanderer Edda; in Scot. still found as an appell. in the true sense, <i>a gangrel</i> = <i>stroller, vagabond.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-limir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-limir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. <i>‘gang-limbs,’ shanks.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-mikit"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-mikit
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. adj. <i>a great crowd, tumult.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-prudr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-prúðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>with stately gait,</i> Sks. 291.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-rum"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-rúm
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a passage-room, lobby,</i> Grett. 99 B.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-silfr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-silfr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>current money,</i> Sturl. iii. 307, Fms. ix. 470, Jb. 157, Grág., N. G. L. passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-skor"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-skör
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., in the phrase, göra g. at e-u, <i>to make steps in a thing.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-stigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-stigr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a footpath,</i> Sks. 4, Greg. 59.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-tamr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-tamr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>pacing</i> (of a horse), Hðm. 3.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-vari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-vari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. (<strong>gang-ari, gang-verja,</strong> u, f.), collect. <i>a suit of clothes,</i> Grág. i. 299, Sks. 288, Bs. i. 876, Ann. 1330.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gang-verja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gang-verja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = gangvari, Stj. 367, 616.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ganga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ganga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a walking,</i> Bs. i. 225, Vþm. 8; tóku heyrn daufir, göngu haltir, 625. 82, cp. Matth. xv. 31; nema sýn eðr göngu frá mönnum, Post. 645. 70: <i>the act of walking,</i> Korm. 182, Fms. vi. 325; ganga göngu, <i>to take a walk,</i> Korm. (in a verse):—<i>a course,</i> ganga tungls, <i>the course of the moon,</i> Edda 7; hvata göngunni, id.; ganga vinds, <i>the course of the wind,</i> 15, Rb. 112, 476:—<i>a procession,</i> Fms. x. 15, Fs. 85, Ísl. ii. 251; vera sarnan í göngu, <i>to march together,</i> Band, 11; lögbergis-g., <i>the procession to the hill of laws,</i> Grág. Þ. Þ. ch. 5, Eg. 703; kirkju-g., <i>a going to church;</i> her-g., <i>a war-march;</i> hólm-g., <i>a duel,</i> q. v.; fjall-g., <i>a walk to the fell</i> (<i>to fetch sheep</i>):—of animals, hrossa-g., <i>grazing, pasture for horses,</i> Dipl. v. 14; sauð-g., <i>sheep-pasture:</i> esp. in pl. <i>fetching sheep from the fell-pastures</i> in autumn (fjall-ganga), Grág. ii. 310, cp. Korm. ch. 3, Vd. ch. 44, Vápn. 22; ó-göngur, <i>straits.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ganga-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ganga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. gekk or gékk, 2nd pers. gékkt, mod. gékst; pl. gengu, geingu, or géngu, and an old poët. gingu; gengengu in Vsp. 12 is a mere misspelling (vide Sæm. Möb. 258); pres. geng, pl. göngum; pret. subj. gengi (geingi); imperat. gakk and gakktú; with the neg. suffix geng-at, gengr-at, gékk-at, gakk-attu, passim; a middle form göngumk firr, <i>go from me,</i> Gm. 1: a contracted form gá occurs now and then in mod. hymns; it is not vernacular but borrowed from Germ. and Dan.: [cp. Ulf. <i>gaggan;</i> A. S. and Hel. <i>gangan;</i> Scot. and North. E. <i>gang,</i> mod. Engl. <i>go;</i> Dan.-Swed. <i>gange</i> or <i>gå;</i> Germ. <i>gehen;</i> Ivar Aasen <i>ganga:</i> Icel., Scots, and Norsemen have preserved the old <i>ng,</i> which in Germ. and Swed.-Dan. only remains in poetry or in a special sense, e. g. in Germ. compds.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gangari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gangari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Dan. and Scot. <i>ganger,</i> a transl. of the mid. Lat. <i>ambulator</i>]:—<i>an ambling nag, a palfrey,</i> Sturl. iii. 117; spelt gangvari in Þiðr. 16, 23; passim in the romances.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gangdaga-helgr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gangdaga-helgr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>Rogation-holidays,</i> N. G. L. i. 10.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gangdaga-vika"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gangdaga-vika
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>Rogation-week,</i> K. Þ. K. 100, 102, Rb. 544, 558.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gangdaga-thing"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gangdaga-þing
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a meeting during Rogation-week,</i> Fms. vii. 217, 347. In all these compds spelt variously ‘gagn-’ or ‘gang-.’ The word Gangdagar is undoubtedly borrowed from the A. S.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gangr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gangr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [A. S. <i>gong;</i> Scot. <i>gang</i> = <i>a walk, journey;</i> Dan. <i>gang;</i> Swed. <i>gång;</i> cp. Germ. <i>gehen</i>]:—<i>a going, walking,</i> Sks. 370; vera á gangi, <i>to be walking to and fro,</i> Grett. 153: metaph., röng eru mál á gangi, <i>bad reports are going about,</i> Bs. i. (in a verse); vápn á gangi, <i>weapons clashing</i> (vide II. 2. below), Grág. ii. 8; þá var hvert járn á gangi, Fb. i. 212:—gefit mér gang, <i>give me way, passage, let me go,</i> Fms. xi. 275, 347:—<i>pace,</i> a horseman’s term, engan (hest) hafa þeir slíkan séð bæði sakir gangs ok vaxtar, Róm. 422: Icel. say, það er enginn g. í honum, <i>he has no pacing</i> or <i>ambling in him;</i> or <strong>gang-lauss,</strong> adj. <i>not pacing</i>:—<i>grazing,</i> úti-g., útigangs-hestr, opp. to a stall-fed horse:—<i>course,</i> of the sun, stars, moon, gangr himin-tungla, Edda (pref.), hence sólar-g., <i>the course of the sun</i> above the horizon = <i>day;</i> stuttr, lítill, langr sólar-g., <i>a short, long day</i>:—<i>course,</i> of money.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ganti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ganti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Dan. <i>gante</i>], <i>a coxcomb,</i> (mod.) <strong>ganta-skapr,</strong> n., Vídal.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gap"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gap
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [A. S. <i>geap;</i> Engl. <i>gap;</i> Dan. <i>gab;</i> cp. gapa], prop. <i>a gap, empty space,</i> whence Ginnunga-gap, <i>the Chaos</i> of the Scandin. mythol., Edda, Vsp.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gap-lyndi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gap-lyndi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>bluster,</i> Karl. 493.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gap-ripur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gap-ripur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl., or <strong>gap-riplar,</strong> m. pl. an απ. λεγ., for the reading vide Johnson. Nj. Lat. l. c., <i>gaping, staring with open mouth,</i> Nj. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gap-uxi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gap-uxi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a blusterer, a bully,</i> Fs. 71.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gap-throsnir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gap-þrosnir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = gapi, Edda (Gl.), an απ. λεγ.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gapa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gapa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. gapði, Edda 20, Mart. 118; and gapti, pres. gapi, Bs. i. 647; sup. gapat, imperat. gapi, Skm. 28: [Dan. <i>gabe;</i> Germ. <i>gaffen</i>]:—<i>to gape, open the mouth wide,</i> Edda l. c.; með gapanda munn, of a wolf, 41, Fms. iv. 57; með gapandi höfðum, Þórð. 94 new Ed.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gapa-legr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gapa-legr
        </a>
        <p
