            {
              "__html": "m. [Ulf. <i>gaurs</i> = <i>sad</i>], <i>a rough, a ‘sad fellow,’</i> used in Kormak 240, but esp. freq. in old romances translated from French; seldom used in genuine old writers; in exclamations, gaurr! vándr g! etc., Flóv., Art., Str. passim, Fas. iii. 6. <strong>gaura-gangr,</strong> m. a <i>gang of ruffians,</i> Gísl. 53.",
            }
          }
        />
