        >
          gizki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. a kind of <i>kerchief</i> (<i>of goal-skin</i>?); hón horfði upp í fjallit ok veifði gizka eðr dúki, Fs. 59; síðan veifði hann gizka til fjalls ok tók þá af veðrit, 78:—mod. <i>a scarecrow.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gifr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gífr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. [A. S. <i>gîfre</i> = <i>rapacious,</i> used as an epithet of the devil, wildfire, etc., and as noun, <i>a glutton,</i> vide Grein]:—<i>witches, fiends,</i> = Germ. <i>unhold,</i> Vsp. 52, Hkv. Hjörv. 15; freq. in poetry, al-gífri, <i>pandemonium,</i> Bragi; gífrs grand, <i>‘witch-bane’</i> = <i>the god Thor,</i> Eb. (in a verse); wolves are gífrs hestar, <i>‘witch-horses,’</i> Jd., and hræ-gífr, <i>carrion beasts,</i> Gkv. 2. 29, Lex. Poët.: the simple word is never used in prose, but in compds; it however remains in prose in the following adv.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gifr-liga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gífr-liga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>savagely;</i> láta gífrliga, Sturl. ii. 238, Fas. ii. 424 (of a dog): mod. <i>exorbitantly.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gifr-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gífr-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., prop. <i>savage:</i> mod. <i>immoderate, exorbitant.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gigja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gígja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to fiddle</i> (Germ. <i>geigen</i>), Str. 82.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gigja-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gígja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [Germ. <i>geige;</i> mid. H. G. <i>gîge;</i> old Fr. <i>gigue;</i> and <i>to jig</i> in Scot. means <i>to play the fiddle,</i> while in Engl. <i>a jig</i> is <i>a lively dance</i>]:—<i>a fiddle,</i> Stj. 181, Hkr. ii. 136, cp. Yngl. S. ch. 25, Fms. vii. 97 (in a verse); this instrument was known at an early age, as a lawyer in Icel. in the first part of the 10th century was called gígja, prob. because of his eloquent pleading or his clear voice, Nj., Landn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gigjari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gígjari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a fiddler,</i> Hkr. i. 30.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gima"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gíma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a vast opening,</i> Fb. i. 210; in mod. usage also <strong>gímald,</strong> n. <i>id</i>.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gina"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gína
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. gein, pl. ginu; pres. gín (Edda 101); sup. ginit; in old poems a weak pret. gínði also occurs, Arnór, Orkn. 90; pl. gíndu, Geisli 29, Fms. iii. 4 (in a verse); [A. S. <i>gînan;</i> Engl. <i>to yawn;</i> Germ. <i>gähnen;</i> Gr. χαίνω]:<i>—to gape, yawn,</i> esp. of wild beasts; gínandi úlfr, Hm. 84; hann brá líndúk um hödduna ok gein yfir, Fms. i. 36: of wounds, en er gína tóku sár hans, Bjarn. 10; gína við agni, <i>to snap at the bait,</i> Hým. 22; gína við flugu, <i>to snap at a fly;</i> þóttisk Sigmundr nú yfir flugu ginit hafa, Ísl. ii. 25; Miðgorðs-ormr gein yfir oxa-höfuðit, Edda 36; vide fluga.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gisl"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gísl
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [A. S. <i>gîsel;</i> lost in Engl.; Germ. <i>geissel;</i> Swed. <i>gislan;</i> Dan. <i>gidsel;</i> to be distinguished from geisl; mod. Germ. and Dan. confound the two forms, one of which has <i>ei</i> and the other <i>î</i> as root vowel; mid. H. G. retained a distinction]:—<i>a hostage,</i> Ls. 39, Fms. v. 171, ix. 359, passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gisla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gísla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to give as hostage,</i> Edda 15, Fms. ix. 447, N. G. L. i. 103; menn höfðu gíslat Knúti konungi sonu sína, Hkr. ii. 385; hann hafði verit gíslaðr (<i>taken as hostage</i>) af Skota-konungi, Orkn. 418 old Ed.; gilstir = gíslaðir, N. G. L. i. 103; gísla sér land, <i>to take possession of the land as a hostage,</i> Fagrsk. 158.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gislar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gíslar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>sureties, securities;</i> hann tók gíslar af honum ok bóndum, Eg. 589; hann tók gíslir (v. 1. gíslar, gísla) af bóndum, Fms. ix. 313, 409, passim; gísla (<i>the persons</i>) and gíslar (<i>the things</i>) are often used indiscriminately.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/gisling"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          gísling
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>hostage,</i> Gþl. 81, Fms. ii. 43, vi. 240, ix. 447, passim: <i>guard,</i> setja gíslingar fyrir = <i>to guard</i> (vide gíslar); setti Þórir þá gíslingar fyrir Gretti (an outlaw) hvar hann kæmi fram, Grett. 139 C: in the old Swed. law gislunga-lagh = <i>the section of law respecting bail and mainprise,</i> Verel.",
            }
