        >
          gjafa-skipti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>gjafa-víxl,</strong> n. <i>exchange of gifts,</i> Gísl. 13, 96, Bs. i. 82:—in a technical sense, brúð-gjöf (q. v.), bekkjar-gjöf (q. v.), morgun-gjöf, <i>a bride-gift, bench-gift, morning-gift,</i> cp. N. G. L. i. 27, 29, 51, passim: til-gjöf, <i>a dowry,</i>—all referring to a wedding: með-gjöf—fúlga, q. v.; á-gjöf, q. v.; milli-gjöf, <i>discount;</i> líf-gjöf, <i>pardon;</i> ofaní-gjöf, <i>rebuke:</i> Icel. also give the name to <i>foddering,</i> setja á gjöf, hence <strong>gjafar-mál,</strong> n. <i>foddering hour,</i> Gþl. 442.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
