              "__html": "f., pl. gjarðar, mod. gjarðir, [Ulf. <i>gairda</i> = ζωνή; Engl. <i>girth, girdle;</i> Dan. <i>gjord</i>]:—<i>a girdle,</i> Ísl. ii. 340, Sks. 403, freq.; söðul-g., <i>a saddle-girth;</i> megin-g., <i>main girdle,</i> the belt of Thor, vide Edda: poët. the sea is called jarðar-g., <i>earth-girdle</i>:—<i>a hoop</i> on tubs, botn-g., <i>a bottom hoop</i>:—a kind <i>of lady’s head-gear,</i> in western Icel. a kerchief wrapped round the head.",
