        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [A. S. <i>glôf</i> occurs as early as Beowulf], <i>a glove,</i> Nj. 46, Fms. i. 246, Dipl. v. 18, Bs. i. 342, Gullþ. 6, 8, Fb. i. 529. <strong>glófaðr,</strong> part. <i>gloved,</i> Karl. 288. The word is no doubt borrowed from the English, and is used in the Sagas chiefly of costly embroidered gloves; another word is handski = <i>‘hand-shoe,’</i> prob. from the Germ. <i>handschuhe;</i> the popular words are vöttr and vetlingr.",
            }
