              "__html": "f. indecl., always so in old writers, (<strong>gœ,</strong> i. e. góe, Bs. i. 9, v. 1.), mod. <strong>góa,</strong> u, f.; the month Gói has thirty days, from the middle of February to the middle of March; for the mythical origin of this word vide Fb. i. 22, Edda 103, Landn. 154, 225, Rb. 48, 50, Ann. 1276, 1340, Bs. i. 9, Ó. H. 64:—in Icel. the names of the winter months Þorri and Góa are still very common.",
