        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a storm, sleet;</i> grund var grápi hrundin, Haustl. 15; Egils hryn-gráp, <i>the hail of Egil,</i> poët. <i>arrows;</i> Egil, brother of Völund, is the Tell of the northern mythology, vide Lex. Poët.; in prose this word seems not to occur, whereas krap, n. <i>sleet</i> (q. v.), and krapi, a, m. id., are common words; cp, the mod. <i>grape-shot.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
