      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-farir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-farir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. a mythical word, <i>the ‘faring’</i> or <i>travelling</i> in the assumed shape of an animal, fowl or deer, fish or serpent, with magical speed over land and sea, the wizard’s own body meantime lying lifeless and motionless; graphically depicted in Yngl. S. ch. 7, Vd. ch. 12, Hkr. (O. T.) ch. 37; hann sendi Finna tvá í hamförum til Íslands, Landn. 174; Haraldr konungr bauð kunngum manni at fara í hamförum til Íslands, sá fór í hvals-líki, etc., Hkr. i. 228.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-fraer"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-frær
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl., from hamfrú (?), <i>witches,</i> an απ. λεγ.; leirblót gört í manns-líki af leiri eðr deigi, eðr hamfrær, N. G. L. i. 383, v. l.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-fong"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-föng
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>frenzy, fury,</i> Sturl. ii. 137.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-hleypa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-hleypa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a ‘ham-leaper,’ a witch that travels in</i> hamfarir, Eg. 421, Fas. ii. 80, 390, Gullþ. 64: in mod. usage Icel. say, hann er mesta hamhleypa, <i>he is a great</i> h., <i>works like a giant,</i> of one who does great work in little time; hann er hamhleypa að skrifa, hamhleypa að vinna, etc.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-ledr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-leðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the shank leather of a hide;</i> cp. höm.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-ljotr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-ljótr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>scraggy, ugly,</i> Haustl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-ramadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-ramaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. = hamramr, Fas. iii. 424, (bad.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-ramr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-ramr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. a mythical term, <i>able to change one’s shape;</i> in the Sagas it is esp. used of berserkers,—men gifted with supernatural strength or seized with fits of warlike fury (berserks-gangr), vide hamask; but also, though less frequently, referring to hamfarir; hann var h. mjök, <i>he was a great wizard who changed his shape,</i> Landn. 87, 289; hann var h. mjök svá at hann gékk heiman ór Hraunhöfn um kveldit en kom um morgininn eptir í Þjórsár-dal, Landn. 236, 285, 306, Gullþ. 30; þat var mál manna at hann væri mjök h., Eg. 3; allir hinir sterkustu menn ok margir hamramir, 109; þeim mönnum er hamramir vóru eðr þeim er berserks-gangr er á, 125; eigi var þat einmælt at hann væri eigi h., 514:—as a nickname, Vékell hinn hamrami, Landn. 191; Vigi hinn h., Korm. 58; Tanni er kallaðr var hinn hamrami, Ísl. ii. 360,—the MS. has handrami, which is no doubt wrong, as also in the name of the mythical king Hávarðr handrami, Fb. i. 26; cp. hinn Rammi and ramaukinn, Landn. 107, 249, 277, Hdl. 34.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-remi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-remi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the state of being</i> hamramr, Eg. 125.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-skarpr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-skarpr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [höm], <i>thin in the flank,</i> of a horse: the name of a horse, Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-skiptask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-skiptask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, dep. = skipta hömum, Str. 30.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-stoli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-stoli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "mod. <strong>ham-stola,</strong> adj. <i>‘ham-stolen,’</i> prop. <i>a wizard whose skin has been stolen,</i> and hence metaph. <i>frantic, furious,</i> Eg. 565, Fms. vi. 198, Barl. 56, Karl. passim, cp. Völs. S. Fas. i. 130.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-stolinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-stolinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. = hamstoli, Karl. 243, 352, El.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ham-vatr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ham-vátr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>skin-wet,</i> i. e. <i>drowned,</i> Landn. (in a verse): freq. in foreign, Saxon, and Germ. pr. names and local names;",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hama"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hama
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [cp. höm = <i>shanks</i> in animals, whence Engl. <i>ham</i>], of cattle or horses in a storm, <i>to stand and turn tail to wind,</i> leaving off grazing.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamal-kyrni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamal-kyrni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. a kind of <i>seed,</i> N. G. L. i. 385, 401.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamall"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamall
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> m. a pr. name, Landn., Hkv.; see the following word.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamalt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamalt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. adj., only in the old phrase, fylkja hamalt, synonymous with svínfylkja, <i>to draw up a wedge-shaped column</i> in the form of a hog’s snout; thus defined, hann hefir svínfylkt her sínum—Hverr man Hringi hafa kennt hamalt at fylkja? (<i>who has taught king Ring to draw up the phalanx of</i> hamalt?) … Hringr hafði svínfylkt öllu liði sínu, þá þótti þó svá þykk fylkingin yfir at sjá, at rani var í brjósti, <i>Ring had drawn all his troops up in a hog-shaped column, so that the ranks looked all the deeper for the snout-formed shape of the front,</i> Fas. i. 380; hildingr fylkti hamalt, a paraphrase from hann fylkti liði sínu svá, at rani var framan á fylkingar-brjóstinu, Fms. xi. 304: used of <i>a column of ships</i> in a sea-fight, vi. 314 (in a verse), cp. also Skv. 2. 23, Fas. ii. 40 (in a verse); a description of the cuneiform column is given in Sks. 384; in Skjöld. S. its invention is attributed to Odin himself, and it was a favourite battle array with the men of old.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamar-gangr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamar-gangr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>hammer-clash,</i> Stj. 45.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamar-skalli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamar-skalli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>the thick end of a hammer,</i> Fms. viii. 138.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamar-skapt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamar-skapt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the shaft</i> or <i>handle of a hammer,</i> Edda 28.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamar-spor"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamar-spor
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a hammer’s print,</i> Edda 34.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamarr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamarr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. hamri, pl. hamrar, [A. S. <i>hamor;</i> Engl. <i>hammer;</i> O. H. G. <i>hamar;</i> Germ. and Dan. <i>hammer;</i> Swed. <i>hammare</i>]:—<i>a hammer;</i> h. töng, steði, Edda 9, Vkv. 18, Landn. 212 (in a verse); the thunderbolt was in the northern mythology represented as a hammer,—the hammer Mjölnir, Edda (Sksm.) 15, 26, 28–30, 58, 70, passim, Þkv. passim, Hbl. 47; hann (the idol) var merkðr eptir Þór ok hefir hamar í hendi, Ó. H. 108, O. T. 44; Þrúð-hamarr, <i>the mighty hammer,</i> Ls. 57, 59, 61, 63: the hammer was the holy sign with the heathens, answering to the cross of the Christians, hann görði hamar yfir, <i>he made the sign of the hammer over it,</i> Fms. i. 35; Þórr tók hamarinn Mjölni ok brá upp ok vígði hafr-stökurnar, Edda 28, cp. also Þkv. 30, where the bride and bridegroom were to be marked with the holy sign; hence Þórs-hamarr = the character RUNE which occurs on a few of the earliest heathen Runic stones (e. g. Thorsen, pp. 17, 329), cp. also Ísl. Þjóðs. i. 446; this RUNE is evidently an imitation of the thunderbolt.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamars-hogg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamars-högg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a hammer stroke,</i> Stj. 563.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamars-mudr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamars-muðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(<strong>-munnr, -munni</strong>), m. <i>the ‘mouth’</i> or <i>thin end of a hammer,</i> Edda 30.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, dep. <i>to rage, to be taken by a fit of fury</i> in a fight, synonymous to ganga berserks-gang (see p. 6l): the word is derived from hamr, prob. owing to a belief that such persons were possessed by a strange spirit or demon; cp. hamr, hamstoli, hamramr, all of them words referring to a change of shape:—svá er sagt, at þá hamaðisk hann, ok fleiri vóru þeir föru-nautar hans er þá hömuðusk, Eg. 122; hamask þú nú, Skallagrímr, at syni þínum, 192; Þórir hljóp þá af baki, ok er svá sagt, at hann hamaðisk þá it fyrsta sinn, Gullþ. 30, Fas. iii. 343, Landn. 119; Fránmarr jarl hafði hamask í arnar líki, Sæm. 95: the word is still used, <i>to work as hard as a giant.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamdir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamðir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a pr. name, qs. Ham-þér, cp. A. S. <i>Hama-þeow.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamingja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamingja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>luck, fortune;</i> prop. in a personal sense, <i>a guardian spirit,</i> answering to the guardian angel of Christians; derived from hamr, for the guardian spirits of men—and every man had his hamingja—were believed to take the shape sometimes of animals, sometimes and more commonly of human beings, esp. that of women; but they were themselves supernatural beings; that the hamingjur were giant-females proceeding from the great Norns—who were the hamingjur of the world—is borne out by the passage in Vþm. 48, 49. Hamingja and fylgja or fylgju-kona (Hallfred S. ch. 11) seem to be nearly synonymous, as also gæfa, gipta, auðna, heill; but hamingja is the most personal word, and was almost symbolical of family relationship. At the hour of death the hamingja left the dying person and passed into a dear son, daughter, or beloved kinsman; cp. Hallfr. S. ch. 11, and esp. the charming tale in Glúm. ch. 9. One might also impart one’s own good luck to another, hence the phrase leggja sína hamingju með e-m, almost answering to the Christian, ‘to give one’s blessing to another.’ Examples: sögðusk mundu leggja til með honum hamingju sína, Ld. 74; h. ok gæfa, Fms. vi. 165; þú en ústöðuga h., Al. 23; h. konungsins, 22; ok mun kona sjá hans h. vera er fjöllum hærra gékk, Glúm. 345; etja hamingju við e-n, Fb. ii. 65; ok reyna hvat hamingjan vill unna þér, Fs. 4; vilnask (<i>hope</i>) at h. mun fylgja, 23; vera má at þat sé til h. várrar ættar, 11; langæligar nytjar munu menn hafa hans hamingju, Bs. i. 229; forlög ekki forðumst ill | fram kemr það hamingjan vill, Úlf. 3. 69; meiri í hreysti en hamingju, Gullþ. 21; sigri eðr hamingju manns þessa, Fs. 10. It is still used in Icel. almost as <i>Heaven, Providence;</i> það má Hamingjan vita, <i>God knows;</i> eg vildi Hamingjan gæfi, <i>would to Heaven!</i> Guð og Hamingjan, <i>God and Good Luck;</i> treysta Guði og Hamingjunni; eiga undir Hamingjunni, <i>to run the risk;</i> and in similar phrases.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamingju-drjugr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamingju-drjúgr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>lucky,</i> Fs. 34.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamingju-hjol"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamingju-hjól
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the wheel of fortune,</i> Fas. iii. 470.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamingju-hlutr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamingju-hlutr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a lucky chance,</i> Fms. x. 180.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamingju-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamingju-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>luckless, hapless,</i> Stj. 464, Fms. viii. 93.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamingju-leysi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamingju-leysi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>want of luck,</i> Fms. i. 286.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hamingju-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hamingju-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a lucky man,</i> Fms. xi. 205, Fs. 21.",
