        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. hékk, 2nd pers. hékkt, mod. hékst, pl. héngu; pret. subj. héngja, mod. héngi; part. hanginn; pres. indic. irreg. hangi; a provincial weak pret. hangði also occurs a few times in old writers, e. g. Edda 76, which form is still heard in southern Icel. (in and about Reykjavík): [Ulf. <i>hahan;</i> A. S. <i>hæn;</i> Engl. <i>hang;</i> O. H. G. <i>hahan;</i> Germ. <i>hangen;</i> Dan. <i>hænge;</i> Swed. <i>hänge</i>]:—to hang, Lat. <i>pendere:</i>",
