              "__html": "n. [cp. Engl. <i>hap, happy</i>], <i>good luck,</i> but with the notion of <i>hap, chance,</i> as is well said in the ditty, hamingjan býr í hjarta manns | höpp eru ytri gæði, Núm. 2. 87; þá varð minna happit en ek vilda, Fms. i. 182; happa fullting, <i>‘hap-help,’ Deus ex machina,</i> vi. 165; happ sótti þik nú en brátt mun annat, gættu at þér verði þat eigi at úhappi, Landn. 146; til happs ok heilla sátta (allit.), <i>for good hap and health,</i> Grág. ii. 21: in the saying, sá skal hafa happ er hlotið hefir, Eb. 24; úhapp, <i>mishap.</i>",
