        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n.; that this word was originally masc. (as vetr, sumarr) is seen from the other Teut. idioms, as also the Norse form <strong>haustar-</strong> (for haust-), which occurs in <strong>haustar-tími,</strong> Stj. 14, and <strong>haustar-dagr,</strong> D. N. (Fr.), = haust-tími, haust-dagr; [A. S. <i>hærfest;</i> Engl. <i>harvest;</i> O. H. G. <i>herbist;</i> Germ. <i>herbst;</i> Dan. <i>höst</i> = <i>harvest;</i> Swed. <i>höst:</i> haust is in Icel. only used in a metaph. sense]:—<i>autumn</i> (<i>harvest season</i>), for the extension of that season see Edda 103, Nj. 9, 168, Fb. ii. 185, passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
