          heilagr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., usually contracted before a vowel, whereby the root vowel becomes short, thus helgan, helgir, helgum, helgar, and the definite helgi, helga; but also uncontractcd, esp. in mod. usage, heilagir, heilagan, heilögum, definite heilagi; [Ulf. seems not to have known the word, and renders αγιος etc. by <i>veihs;</i> so also in Dan. and Swed. local names, holy places and temples are marked by a prefixed or suffixed <i>vi-,</i> e. g. <i>Vi-borg, Odens-e</i> (= Óðins-vé): heilagr is derived in a metaph. sense from heill, <i>whole,</i> and is consequently not so old as the primitive <i>vé, veihs;</i> so A. S. <i>hâlag;</i> Engl. <i>holy;</i> Hel. <i>hêlag;</i> Germ. <i>heilig;</i> Dan. <i>hellig;</i> Swed. <i>helig</i>]:",
