      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/heipt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          heipt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "better <strong>heift,</strong> f. [Ulf. <i>haifsts</i> = ἔρις, ἐριθεία, ἀγών, cp. <i>haifstjan</i> = ἀγωνίζεσθαι; akin is Germ. <i>heftig,</i> whence mod. Dan. <i>hæftig</i>]:—the earliest sense is <i>feud, deadly war;</i> vinna e-m heipt, <i>to wage war</i> (<i>do battle</i>) <i>against one,</i> Vkv. 10; deila heiptir, <i>to wage deadly feud,</i> Hkv. 1. 44; senda e-m heiptar-boð, <i>to challenge one to combat,</i> Fas. iii. 27 (in a verse): hereto belong such poët. epithets as, <strong>heiptar-nýtr, heiptar-strangr, heipt-bráðr, heipt-fíkinn, heipt-glaðr, heipt-mildr, heipt-minnigr, heipt-móðr, heipt-örr, heipt-snarr,</strong> = <i>mighty in war, warlike,</i> all of them used as ‘ornamental’ epithets of praise, vide Lex. Poët.: as also <strong>heiptar-hvessir,</strong> m. <i>a war kindler,</i> id.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/heipt-gjarn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
