              "__html": "f., gen. heljar, dat. helju or hel (less correct); a nom. helja never occurs in old writers, although a gen. helju is used in the mod. phrase, milli heims ok helju (old and better heljar); [Ulf. <i>halja</i> = αδης, Matth. xi. 23, Luke xvi. 23, 1 Cor. xv. 55; A. S. and Engl. <i>hell;</i> Hel. and O. H. G. <i>hellia;</i> Germ. <i>hölle;</i> cp. Dan. <i>i hjel</i>]:—<i>the abode of the dead:</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
