              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> u, f., gen. hellna, Bs. i. 204, [hallr, m.; Swed. <i>häll</i>], <i>a flat stone, slate,</i> Þórð. 36 new Ed., Fs. 66, Fms. viii. 9, xi. 241, Orkn. 246: <i>a table-land of rocks,</i> leiddum síðan skipit upp á hellurnar, Fms. xi. 241; þar ól Þóra barn uppi á hellunni, Hkr. i. 118, (Hákonar-hella, the name of a place); sumt féll á hellu ok þornaði, Hom. Matth. xiii. 5; hjálpar-h., <i>rock of salvation;</i> hneyxlunar-h., <i>rock of offence,</i> Rom. ix. 33; þvíat þat var grundvallat á hellu, Matth. vii. 25: <i>a tablet of stone</i> (= steintafla), Ver. 22; gull-hella, q. v.: a local name, Landn.; also <strong>Hellu-land,</strong> n. the Polar-land north and east of Greenland.",
            }
          }
        />
