        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "also spelt <strong>higat</strong> (Eg. 51, Nj. 227, Fms. i. 189, Stj. 27, 35) and <strong>hegat</strong> (Ísl. ii. 270, Gþl. 272), prob. only by dropping the mark of abbreviation (¯) above the line (hīgat, hēgat), as seen from old rhymes such as h<i>in</i>gat fyrir konu b<i>in</i>g, Eb. 73 new Ed.:—<i>hither,</i> Lat. <i>huc,</i> Íb. 5, Nj. 2, Grág. i. 189, Fms. i. 72, x. 18; hingat ok þangat, <i>hither and thither, to and fro,</i> viii. 39, Stj. 35, 284, Blas. 40; hón vissi löngum ekki hingat, i. e. <i>she was in a senseless state,</i> Bs. i. 384.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
