        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> t, [Engl. <i>to nip, knap</i>], <i>to cut short, curtail;</i> vilja heldr hneppa við sik þann eina búninginn, <i>to curtail oneself in dress,</i> Hom. (St.): also, hneppa e-n undir sik, <i>to keep one under,</i> a wrestler’s term, Fas. iii. 353; h. í þrældóm, <i>to keep bound in thraldom,</i> Sks. 465:—slóðu upp og hnepptu hann út af borginni, <i>thrust him head-foremost out,</i> Luke iv. 29: metric. <i>a monosyllabic end syllable</i> is called hneppt, Edda (Ht.): part. <strong>hnepptr,</strong> <i>crippled.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
