        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [A. S. <i>hol;</i> Engl. <i>hole, hollow;</i> Dan. <i>hule;</i> Swed. <i>håla;</i> Germ. <i>höhle,</i> etc.]:—<i>a hollow, cavity;</i> lýstr vindinum ofan í holit verplanna, Fms. xi. 34, Boll. 340 (of a shield), but esp. <i>a cavity</i> of the body, Bs. i. 385: á hol, (<i>piercing</i>) <i>to the inwards,</i> Nj. 60, Fb. i. 146; ef blóð má falla á hol ór sári, <i>if it bleeds inwardly,</i> Grág. ii. 11, Gullþ. 66, Band. 42 new Ed.; í hol, <i>id.,</i> 91; inn í holit, of the chest, Edda 76, Fs. 65; hit efra, neðra hol, <i>the upper and nether hollow</i> (i. e. the chest and stomach), N. G. L. i. 172, Sturl. iii. 54: <i>a hole,</i> = hola, stór hol, Bs. i. 321, Rb. 440; grafinn með hol, Thom. 468.",
            }
          }
        />
