        >
          horskr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [A. S. <i>horsc</i>], <i>wise;</i> thus in the old Hm., horskr and heimskr, <i>wise</i> and <i>foolish, good</i> and <i>wicked,</i> are opposed, 19, 92, 93; horskr is opp. to ósviðr, Fm. 35, 36, cp. 37; h. ok þögull, <i>the wise and silent</i>, Hm. 6 (cp. σοφός και σιγων of Pythagoras); sá er vill heitinn h., Hm. 61; horskir hugir, <i>wise minds,</i> 90; en horska mær, <i>the wise maiden,</i> 95; it horska man, <i>id.,</i> 101; horskar konur, Hbl. 17; h. halr, Skv. 3; heill ok h., Akv. 12, see Lex. Poët.; hvít ok horsk, of a maid, Rm. 36. This word is almost obsolete in prose, Sks. 207, Str. 31.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
