        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. hróðrar and hróðrs: [A. S. <i>hræð, hrôðer;</i> O. H. G. <i>hruodi;</i> Goth. <i>hrôþ</i> is assumed as the subst. of <i>hrôþeigs,</i> 2 Cor. ii. 14]:—<i>praise,</i> prop. <i>fame, reputation;</i> heyra hróðr sinn, <i>to hear one’s own praise,</i> Fms. v. 174; bera hróðr e-s, 623. 36; hróðrs örverðr, <i>unworthy of praise,</i> Ad. 14, 15; njóta hróðrar, <i>to enjoy one’s praise,</i> Edda (in a verse); mun þinn hróðr (<i>thy honour</i>) ekki at meiri þó at ek mæla berara, Gísl. 16; hróðr varlega góðr, Fas. i. 267 (in a verse); ú-hróðr, <i>disgrace.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
