              "__html": "a, m. = hugr, Hbl. 21, Edda 24, Glúm. 323, Hkr. ii. 243, Stj. 5, and passim, the weak and strong forms being used almost indiscriminately both in old and mod. usage, as also in the compds, huga-góðr, huga-fullr, = hug-góðr, hug-fullr, q. v.; á-hugi, <i>zeal;</i> var-hugi, <i>caution;</i> at-hugi, <i>attention.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
