          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hylda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, [hold], <i>to slash</i>, N. G. L. i. 381, Am. 55; h. hval, Fms. v. 178 (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyldga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyldga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to get flesh.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyldgan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyldgan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>getting flesh;</i> of-hyldgan, medic.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hylja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hylja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. hyl (hylk = hyl ek, Hbl. 11), pl. hyljum; pret. hulði (huldi); part. huliðr, huldr, and hulinn; [Ulf. <i>huljan</i> = καλύπτειν; A. S. <i>helan;</i> Old Engl. <i>to hele, hull;</i> O. H. G. <i>huljan;</i> Germ. <i>hüllen;</i> Swed. <i>hölja;</i> Dan. <i>hylle</i> and <i>hæle</i>]:—<i>to hide, cover;</i> hylja hann allan, Edda 72; hann hulði höfuð sitt, Fms. x. 255; huldi andlit sitt, 361; hón huldi dúk, bjóð, Rm.; hann huldi hræ hans, Nj. 27, Grág. ii. 88; ok svá mikit hárit at hón mátti h. sik með, Nj. 16: <i>to bury,</i> jörðu hulinn, <i>buried in the earth,</i> Magn. 506; hylja auri, Korm. (in a verse); huliðr sandi, Geisli 25: <i>to conceal,</i> limi okkra hyl ekki, Sks. 504: part. <strong>huldr</strong> or <strong>huliðr,</strong> id.; fara huldu höfði, <i>to go with the head covered,</i> i. e. <i>in disguise</i> or <i>by stealth,</i> Eg. 406, Fms. i. 222; cp. huliðshjálmr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyljan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyljan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a covering, hiding,</i> Sturl. iii. 234.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hylki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hylki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a hulk,</i> of an old tub or vessel.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hylla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hylla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, <strong>hylda</strong> in N. G. L. ii. l. c.; [cp. hollr; Germ. <i>huldigen;</i> Dan. <i>hylde</i>]:—<i>to court a person’s friendship;</i> h. sik fjándmönnum e-s, Fms. vi. 174; h. sik svá við menn, Gþl. 25; h. fyrir e-m, <i>to recommend one,</i> Lv. 6; h. ok samþykkja, N. G. L. ii. 65, 220; h. hug með e-m, <i>to consent,</i> 183.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hylli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hylli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>favour, grace,</i> Þkv. 29, Fas. ii. 69; Guðs h., Grág. ii. 167, Ísl. ii. 382, passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hylling"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hylling
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>homage.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hylma"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hylma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, [akin to hylja], <i>to hide, conceal;</i> used only as a law phrase, and with the prep. yfir; yfir h. verk sitt, Stj. 42; nú mundi elligar yfir hylmask mál Odds, Fms. vi. 384; þarf ekki lengr yfir þessu at hylma, vii. 20, Fas. i. 195.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hylming"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hylming
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a concealing,</i> of a sin, Pass. 5. 3.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hylr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hylr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. hyljar, pl. ir, [akin to holr], <i>a hole</i> or <i>deep place</i> in a river, e. g. places where trout and salmon lie hidden, Bs. i. 46, Hrafn. 23, Fs. 48: freq. in local names, Skip-hylr (a dock in a river), Þúfu-h., Hörgs-h., D. I.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyltingr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyltingr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [from holt; cp. <i>hultiggir</i> in the Golden horn], <i>the ‘holt-dwellers,’</i> in compds, Hjarð-hyltingar, etc.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hymni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hymni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>ymni,</strong> proncd. <strong>himni,</strong> a, m. [a for. word], <i>a hymn,</i> Ám. 54, Bs. <strong>hymna-bók, -skrá,</strong> f. <i>a hymn book,</i> B. K. 83, Pm. 24, 29; but out of use except in the word <strong>hymna-lag,</strong> n. <i>a hymn, melody;</i> með hymnalag, Pass. (begin.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyndask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyndask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, [hund = hundrað], <i>to be multiplied,</i> a απ. λεγ.; unz fé hyndisk, <i>till the money increases,</i> N. G. L. i. 23.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyndla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyndla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [hundr], <i>a little dog, doggie,</i> Mar. 494, v. l.: name of <i>a giantess,</i> whence <strong>Hyndlu-ljóð,</strong> n. pl. the name of an old <i>song.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hypja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hypja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> að, [hjúpr], <i>to huddle the clothes on;</i> h. sig í fötin, <i>to dress oneself in a hurry.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyrja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyrja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. name of a giantess, Edda.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyrja-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyrja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. hyrr, [hurr], <i>to knock at;</i> hann hyrr hurðir = <i>impingebat in ostia portae</i> of the Vulgate, Stj. 475 (v. l.), 1 Sam. xxi. 13.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyrna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyrna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n, f. [horn], <i>one of the horns</i> or <i>points</i> of an axe-head, öxar-h., Bjarn. 36, Fms. vii. 191, Nj. 198: of a mountain, <i>a peak,</i> freq.: of a house, Hornklofi: a horned ewe is called hyrna; Mó-hyrna, Grá-h.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyrndr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyrndr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>horned,</i> Rb. 356, Grág. i. 501, Fms. xi. 6, Stj. 314: <i>angular,</i> mathem., þrí-h., fer-h., átt-h., Alg. 195.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyrning"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyrning
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a corner, nook</i> of a house, Skálda 162, Stj. 152, Eg. 91, Fbr. 168, Grett. 57 new Ed., Fas. ii. 427, Thom. 80.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyrningr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyrningr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a horned man,</i> used mockingly of a bishop with his crosier; margt mælir h. hjá, Ó. H.; karp þess hyrnings er ér kallit biskup, id.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyrr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyrr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. hyrjar, [cp. Ulf. <i>hauri</i> = <i>embers,</i> John xviii. 18, Rom. xii. 20]:—<i>embers of fire,</i> but only in poetry, Vþm. 31, Hdl. 45, Ýt. 20, Haustl. 14, Vellekla, passim, as also in a great many compds denoting weapons (= <i>the fire</i> of the battle or of Odin), or gold (= <i>the fire</i> of the sea), see Lex. Poët. pp. 431–433. <strong>Hyrr-okin,</strong> the name of a giantess, from hyrr, and rokinn from rjúka, Edda.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyski"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyski
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [better hýski, from hús], <i>a household, family,</i> cp. hjú, Edda 5, Hkr. 197, Fms. vi. 368, Al. 21, N. G. L. ii. 473, Hom. 152, Stj. 57; but, in mod. usage at least, used almost exclusively in a low sense, of beggars and low people.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hyskinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hyskinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>slothful.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hy"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hý
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
