          className="link"
          href="/word/haeveskr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hæveskr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., also spelt <strong>heyveskr,</strong> Str. 75, or <strong>heyskr,</strong> Art.:—<i>well-mannered, polite,</i> Fms. ii. 133, vi. 1, Sks. 246, 276, 277; h. siðir, <i>polite manners,</i> Sks. 8.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hod"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höd
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [A. S. <i>heaðu-</i> in several poët. compds; cp. Sansk. <i>çatru</i> and <i>çâtayâmi;</i> Lat. <i>caedo;</i> Gr. κότος]:—<i>war, slaughter,</i> but only in compd pr. names, <strong>Höð-broddr,</strong> Fb.; <strong>Höð,</strong> f. the name of a Valkyria (also Geira-höð), Gm.: as also of a woman, but mythical, Fas.: the name of an island in Norway: <strong>Höðr,</strong> m., gen. Haðar, dat. Heði, the name of the blind brother and ‘slayer’ of Baldr, the ‘fratricide’ or ‘Cain’ of the Edda, Vsp. 37, Vtkv. 9, Edda 17, 56: also the name of a mythol. king, whence <strong>Heðir,</strong> pl. a Norse people; and <strong>Haða-land,</strong> the county, Fb. iii. <strong>Haðar-lag,</strong> n. <i>the metre of</i> Höd, a kind of <i>metre,</i> Edda.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hodnu-kid"
