        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-jarn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-járn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a ‘hewing iron,’ chopper,</i> Ld. 38, K. Þ. K. 112: <i>a chisel.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-ormr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-ormr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [North. E. <i>hagworm;</i> Swed. <i>huggorm</i>], <i>a viper,</i> 623. 26, Skálda 176, Edda 37, Stj. 28, passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-orrosta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-orrosta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a close fight,</i> Eg. 231, Fms. vi. 78, passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-ro"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-ró
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "usually spelt <strong>hugró,</strong> f. <i>a clinch</i> on a sword’s hilt, Edda (Gl.), Fms. i. 177, Hkr. i. 238, Þórð. 75: name of a ship, Fms. viii: in Hkv. Hjörv. the true reading is prob., hugró í hjalti, … önn er í oddi, for the MS. reading ‘hugr er í hjalti’ yields no meaning; hugró and önn (q. v.) were parts of the sword.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-rum"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-rúm
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>room to draw a sword,</i> Þórð. 47, Eg. 492.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-sax"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-sax
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. a kind of <i>hatchet,</i> Fbr. 58.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-skogr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-skógr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Dan. <i>skovhugst</i>], <i>felled trees;</i> þat er h. er menn höggva upp, Grág. ii. 264.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-sledda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-sledda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = höggsax, Safn i. 689.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-spjot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-spjót
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. a kind of <i>halberd,</i> Fms. iv. 338, vi. 113, vii. 143, Fær. 207, Eg. 374, 378, = kesja.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-stadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-staðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a place for a blow,</i> Eg. 507, Fms. vi. 99, vii. 290, viii. 404, Hkr. iii. 165.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-stokkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-stokkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a chopping-block,</i> Ó. H. 117: <i>a block for execution.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogg-vapn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högg-vápn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a cutlass,</i> Eg. 580, Fms. vi. 158.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoggorma-bit"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höggorma-bit
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a viper’s bite.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoggorms-tonn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höggorms-tönn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a viper’s tooth.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoggva"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höggva
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "also spelt heyggva, Sæm. (Kb.); pres. höggr, mod. also heggr; pl. höggum, mod. höggvum; pret. hjó, hjótt, hjó, mod. hjó, hjóst, hjó; pl. hjoggum and hjuggum, mod. only the latter form; a Norse pret. hjoggi = hjó, D. N. ii. 331; pret. subj. hjöggi and heyggi, mod. hjyggi; part. högginn, mod. but less correct, höggvinn, which also is freq. in the Editions; but in the MSS. usually abbreviated, högḡ, höggͭ, = högginn, höggit: [not recorded in Ulf.; A. S. <i>heawan;</i> Engl. <i>hew, hack;</i> Hel. <i>hauwan;</i> O. H. G. <i>houwan;</i> Germ. <i>hauen;</i> Dan. <i>hugge;</i> Swed. <i>hugga</i>]:—höggva denotes <i>to strike</i> with an edged tool, slá and drepa with a blunt one:",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoggvandi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höggvandi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m., part. <i>a hewer,</i> as a nickname, Fms. xi. 115: <i>a headsman,</i> Post. 645. 65.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoggvin-kinni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höggvin-kinni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>cut cheek,</i> a nickname, Landn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogld"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högld
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., pl. hagldir, a kind of <i>buckle</i> (shaped like ∞), commonly made of horn, used to run the rope through with which hay is trussed: hann tekr reip á tíu hesta ok leysir af hagldir, Fb. i. 523: in metaph. phrases, hann þóttisk nú hafa hagldir fengit á sínum málum, Bs. i. 730; and the mod. phrase, hafa bæði töglin ok hagldirnar, <i>to have it all one’s own way.</i> <strong>haglda-brauð,</strong> n. <i>buckle-gingerbread.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogldungr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högldungr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = högld. <strong>högldungs-reip,</strong> n. <i>a rope with buckles;</i> kirkja á tíu högldungsreip, Vm. 177.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hogni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          högni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a tom cat,</i> freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hokta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hökta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, <i>to limp,</i> Bárð. 167; h. kyrr, Fas. ii. 369.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoku"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höku-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "see haka.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoku-bein"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höku-bein
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the chin bone,</i> Sd. 169.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoku-langr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höku-langr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>having a long chin,</i> Bárð. 165.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoku-mikill"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höku-mikill
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>having a large chin,</i> Sd. 147.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoku-nott"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höku-nótt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>mid-winter night,</i> about the time of Epiphany, when the heathen Yule began; a απ. λεγ.: hann setti þat í lögum at hefja Jólahald sem Kristnir menn …, en áðr var Jóla-hald hafit Hökunótt, þat var miðsvetrar-nótt (thus in Fms. i. 32, l. c.), ok haldin þriggja (þrettán?) nátta Jól, Hkr. i. 138 (Hák. S. Aðalst. ch. 15). The Scot. <i>hogmaney,</i> = <i>the last day of the year</i> or a feast given on that day, is a remnant of this ancient word. The heathen Yule seems among the Scandinavians to have been celebrated about three weeks later than Christmas; but the Norse king Hakon, who had been brought up in Christian England, altered the time of the festival, so as to make it correspond with the English Yule or Christmas; and so the heathen hökunótt came to represent our Christmas Eve. The etymology is not known.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoku-skard"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höku-skarð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a cleft in the chin.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoku-skegg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höku-skegg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the beard on the chin,</i> Fas. ii. 434, Hkr. ii. 176.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hokul-braekr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hökul-brækr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl., also by dropping the aspirate, ökul-brækr, Fas. iii. 41:—<i>‘cloak-breeks,’</i> a kind of <i>dress,</i> perhaps like a Highlander’s <i>kilt,</i> prob. derived from hökull, hekla, and not from ökla, <i>an ankle;</i> it is used of beggarly attire, Ísl. (Kjaln. S.) ii. 417, Fas. iii. 41.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hokul-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hökul-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>‘cope-less,’ without a cope,</i> Vm. 22.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hokul-skuadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hökul-skúaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part., prob. <i>wearing a kilt and brogues</i> like a Highlander, Fms. ix. 512; this word is also, in the various MSS. to l. c., spelt with or without the <i>h,</i> see Fb. iii. 151 (ökulskoðr).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hokull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hökull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. hökli, [Ulf. renders by <i>hakul</i> the Gr. φελόνης, i. e. φαινόλης, Lat. <i>paenula, a mantle,</i> 2 Tim. iv. 13; A. S. <i>hacela;</i> O. H. G. <i>hachul;</i> old Fr. <i>hekil;</i> Dan. <i>messe-hagel;</i> akin to hekla, q. v.]:—<i>a priest’s cope;</i> purpura-h., Bs. i. 67; hann hafð ok út pell þat er h. sá er úr görr er Skarbendingr heitir, 77, Vm. 13, 92, Fms. iii. 168, viii. 197, D. I. passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hold-borinn-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höld-borinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>born of a</i> höld (see höldr), <i>enjoying a</i> höld’s <i>right,</i> Hdl. 11, 16, N. G. L. i. 346.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hold-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höld-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = höldr, N. G. L. i. 44, 55, 71, 175.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/holdr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höldr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., in old MSS. spelt hꜹlðr or hꜹlþr, denoting that the <i>d</i> is inflexive, not radical; [the word therefore is not to be derived from halda, but is identical with A. S. <i>hæleð,</i> Germ. <i>held,</i> whence mod. Swed. and Dan. <i>hjälta</i> and <i>helt,</i> see halr]:—a Norse law term, a kind of <i>higher yeoman,</i> like <i>the statesman of</i> Westmorland, i. e. <i>the owner of allodial land,</i> mod. Norse <i>odelsbonde;</i> the höld is to be distinguished from a hersir (q. v.) or a lendr maðr, who held land in fee from the king, see the interesting story in Har. S. Harðr. ch. 62 (Fms. vi. 278); the höld is thus defined, sá er hꜹldr er hann hefir óðöl at erfðum tekit bæði eptir föður ok móður, þau er hans forellrar (<i>forefathers</i>) hafa átt áðr fyrir þeim, N. G. L. ii. 146; hölda tvá eða bændr ina beztu, i. 251. In old Norway the churchyards were divided into four parts; in the first were buried the lendir menn, next them the hölds and their children (hölds-lega), then the freed men (leysingjar), and lastly the thralls (man, q. v.) nearest to the wall; the höld had right to twice as much as the simple franklin, and half as much as the lendr maðr, e. g. bóandi hálvan annan eyri, höldr þrjá aura, lendr maðr sex aura, jarl tólf aura, konungr þrjár merkr, N. G. L. i. 45, cp. 55, 71, 81; þegnar ok hꜹlðar, svá eru búendr kallaðir, Edda 107; haulðar, þat er búendr þeir, er gildir eru af ættum eða réttum fullum, 94; Björn hlaut annan bústað góðan ok virðilegan, görðisk hann ekki handgenginn konungi, því var hann kallaðr Björn hölðr, Eg. 198; lends manns son skal taka hölds rétt ef hann fær eigi lönd, N. G. L. i. 71; hann veltisk ór jarldóminum ok tók hölds rétt, Orkn. 12: for the weregild to be paid for a höld (hölds-gjöld) see N. G. L. i. 81: a law of king St. Olave ordered that Icelanders whilst in Norway should enjoy the right of a höld; Íslendingar eigu at hafa hölds-rétt í Noregi, D. I. i. 65.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/holfa-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hölfa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, see hválfa.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/holgi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hölgi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. a pr. name, in the Hb. spelt <strong>Hœlgi;</strong> this is the old Norse form, whereas the old and mod. Icel. form is <strong>Helgi,</strong> and of a woman, <strong>Helga,</strong> u, f., Landn.; prob. contracted from Hálogi, cp. the Dan. <i>Holger</i> and Russian <i>Olga</i>: Hölgi was the name of a mythol. king, Edda 83, whence <strong>Hölga-brúðr,</strong> f. <i>the bride of</i> Hölgi, or <strong>Hölga-tröll,</strong> n. (Skálda 168, Fms. xi. 134), <i>the giantess of</i> H.: <strong>hölda-brúðr</strong> and <strong>hörga-brúðr</strong> are less correct forms, Nj. 131 (v. l.), Fb. i. 213; for the various readings in different MSS. see Jóms S. ch. 44, Nj. ch. 89: this is the name of two <i>weird sisters</i> worshipped by the earls of Hlaðir; the passage in Skálda l. c. refers to some lost myth concerning these sisters.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/holkn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hölkn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a rough stony field,</i> almost = hraun, q. v.; á hölkni einu, Fas. iii. 625; hann setsk niðr á hölknit fyrir ofan búðirnar, Ld. 290 (v. l. hraunit); þá er undir svá hart sem hölkn, Hrafn. 26; hölkn eða hreysar, N. G. L. i. 38; í fjöru eða á hœlkn, ii. 111, 146, Hým. 24; um hölkn ok skóga, Karl. 243: in local names, <strong>Hölkna-heiðr,</strong> see the map of Icel.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/holkvir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hölkvir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., poët. <i>a horse,</i> Edda (Gl.); h. hvílbeðjar, poët. <i>a clothes’ horse,</i> cp. Dan. <i>sænge-hest</i> (?), Akv. 31; gólf-h., <i>a ‘closet-horse,’</i> poët. <i>a house,</i> Bragi; borð-h., <i>a ‘board-hobby,’ a ship,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/holl-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höll
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. hallar, often spelt <strong>hall</strong> without umlaut, Fb. i. 212, 1. 26, Fas. iii. 42, 87, Fms. viii. 191, v. l.; as also rhymed so in poets, e. g. Geisli 11; [A. S. <i>heal,</i> gen. <i>healle;</i> Engl. <i>hall;</i> Hel. <i>halla;</i> but not found in old and mid. H. G., the mod. Germ. <i>halle</i> being a borrowed word, Grimm’s Gr. iii. 427]:—<i>a hall,</i> but in the Norse only of a king’s or earl’s hall, whereas a private dwelling is called skáli, eldhús, q. v.; and thus ‘hall’ never could be used of an Icel. dwelling. In earlier times it seems to have had a more general sense, which remains in a verse of Kormak, Korm. 42:—in the mythology and old poems ‘hall’ is also used of the hall of gods, giants, Vþm., Hým., Lv.; Val-höll, <i>Valhalla, the hall of the slain,</i> of Odin, Gm., Edda: as also Guðs höll, <i>God’s hall</i> = <i>the heaven,</i> Geisli; dags höll, <i>days’ hall, the sky;</i> höll fjalla, <i>mountain hall, the sky;</i> lífs höll, <i>life’s hall, the breast,</i> Lex. Poët.:—in prose constantly, konungs-höll, <i>a king’s hall,</i> or hall simply, passim. For the building, structure, seats of a hall, see the Sagas passim, Fagrsk. ch. 219, 220, Hrólfs S. Kr. ch. 34, 40, Jómsv. S. ch. 5, 22, Völs. S. ch. 3, Hálfs S. ch. 12, Eg. S. ch. 8, Edda 2, 30–33, 82. As all heathen Scandinavian buildings were of timber, the hall of stone of Nj. ch. 6 is no doubt an anachronism.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/holzti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hölzti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "see heldr B. III.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hom"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höm
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. hamar, [A. S. and Engl. <i>ham</i>], <i>the ham</i> or <i>haunch</i> of a horse; Grettir hljóp undir hömina á hesti sínum, Grett. 108; kom á hömina hestinum, Karl. 124; skjóta þeir upp höminni allir í senn, Od. xiii. 83; standa í höm = hama, q. v., of horses in a tempest.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/homlu-band"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hömlu-band
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>an oar strap</i> (= hamla), Eg. 390, Fbr. 181.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/homlu-bardi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hömlu-barði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. a dub. απ. λεγ.; má þat ríki kalla hömlu-barða eða auðnar óðal, Sks. 333: the word is prob. taken from a ship defeated in a fight and pulling or drifting stern foremost.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/homlu-fall"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hömlu-fall
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>an illegal breaking up of a ship,</i> a Norse law term, no king’s ship might be demolished unless the keel had been laid for a new ship; hömlufall was liable to a fine of three marks for every hamla, N. G. L. i. 101.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/homlu-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hömlu-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a Norse term answering to Icel. há-seti, <i>an oarsman, sailor,</i> N. G. L. i. 99.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/homul-gryti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hömul-grýti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [provinc. Norse <i>humul,</i> Shetl. <i>hammers</i>], <i>heaps of earth-fast stones;</i> í klungri eða humulgrýti, Barl. 19.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/homungr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hömungr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = hemingr (q. v.), N. G. L. ii. 511.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hond"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hönd
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. handar, dat. hendi, acc. hönd, pl. hendr, mod. proncd. höndur, gen. handa; [Goth. <i>handus;</i> A. S. and Engl. <i>hand;</i> O. H. G. <i>hant;</i> Germ. <i>hand;</i> Dan. <i>haand;</i> Swed. <i>hand</i>]:—<i>a hand;</i> beit höndina þar er nú heitir úlfliðr, Edda 17; armleggir, handleggir ok hendr, Anecd. 6; kné eðr hendi, Grág. ii. 8; ganga á höndum, Fms. vi. 5; með hendi sinni, K. Þ. K. 5 new Ed.; taka hendi á e-u, <i>to touch with the hand,</i> Fms. x. 110; taka höndum um háls e-m, Nj. 10; hvítri hendi, Hallfred; hafa e-t í hendi, <i>to hold in hand, wield,</i> Eg. 297, Nj. 84, 97, 255; hrjóta ór hendi e-m, Fms. xi. 141; hafa fingrgull á hendi, Nj. 146; handar-högg, Fms. xi. 126, Fas. ii. 459; sjá ekki handa sinna skil (deili), <i>not to be able to see one’s hands,</i> of a dense fog.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hondla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höndla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, (<strong>handla,</strong> Stj. 22, 47), <i>to handle;</i> h. heiðarliga, Karl. 51; h. úvarliga, Stj. 22: <i>to manage,</i> Gkv. 1. 8; h. e-n ílla, <i>to treat one ill,</i> Stj. 47; h. um e-t, Mar.; h. kaup, <i>to strike a bargain, to handsel</i> (North. E.), Gþl. 493.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hondulega"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höndulega
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>adroitly;</i> honum fórst það hönduliga.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/honk"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hönk
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. hankar, pl. henkr, hankar, Fs. 132, l. 12, mod. hankir; [Engl. <i>hank,</i> cp. Germ. <i>henker</i>]:—<i>a hank, coil, skein;</i> toga hönk, Fms. vi. 312, Fs. 146; þar var hönk í meðalkaflanum, ok dró hann hana á hönd sér, Eg. 378, Grett. 101; henkr tvær af viðjum, Gþl. 413; festa með hönkum, 381; sterkar henkr (<i>clasps</i>), Fs. 132.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hor-hnoda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hör-hnoða
