              "__html": "m. <i>a linen thread,</i> Bs. i. 644.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hordar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörðar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. <i>the Hords, a people of Norway;</i> whence <strong>Hörða-land,</strong> n. <i>the land of the Hords:</i> <strong>Hörða-konungr, -kappi,</strong> m. <i>the king, champion of the Hords,</i> Fms. passim: <strong>Hörðu-ból,</strong> n., <strong>Hörðu-dalr,</strong> m. a local name in Icel.: <strong>Hörð-dælir,</strong> m. pl. <i>the men from H.,</i> Sturl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hordr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., Herði, Hörð, a pr. name, Landn. <strong>Harðar-saga,</strong> u, f. <i>the story of</i> Hörð.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horfa-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörfa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [akin to hvarfa, q. v.], <i>to retire,</i> Fas. iii. 34; h. frá í brott, Nj. 216; hvárt sem þeir h. með ánni norðr eða suðr, 228; h. fyrir, <i>to give way,</i> Grett. 114; h. undan, Sd. 175, Fbr. 41 new Ed., Fs. 45; nú h. þeir innar eptir höllinni, Fas. ii. 261; hann hörfaði at borðinu út, Fms. vii. 264; þá skal ganga á feld þó áðr hafi af hörfat, Korm. 86: <i>to pass round,</i> hefir þat (viz. the moon) hörfat hring sinn, Rb. 116: reflex., láta hörfask undan, Ísl. ii. 447.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horfan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörfan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>retrogression;</i> h. heimsins, Mag. 69.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horg-brjotr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörg-brjótr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a breaker of horgs,</i> of a missionary king, Hallfred.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horgr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörgr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., never f., for the form hörg (Landn. 111) is merely an error; [A. S. <i>hearg;</i> O. H. G. <i>haruc</i>]:—<i>a heathen place of worship.</i> Distinction is to be made between hof (<i>temple</i>) and horg; the hof was a house of timber, whereas the horg was <i>an altar of stone</i> (the hátimbraðr in Vþm. is not literal) erected on high places, or <i>a sacrificial cairn</i> (like haugr), built in open air, and without images, for the horg itself was to be stained with the blood of the sacrifice; hence such phrases as, to ‘break’ the horgs, but ‘burn’ the temples. The horg worship reminds one of the worship in high places of the Bible. The notion of a ‘high place’ still remains in the popular Icel. phrase, það eru ekki uppi nema hæstu hörgar, <i>only the highest horgs jut out,</i> when all lies under a deep snow. In provincial Norse a dome-shaped mountain is called <i>horg</i> (Ivar Aasen). The worship on horgs seems to be older than that in temples, but was in after times retained along with temple worship, and then, it seems, specially reserved for the worship of the goddesses or female guardians (dísir), Hervar. S. ch. 1, Hdl. l. c., Edda l. c., cp. also <strong>Hörga-brúðr,</strong> f. <i>the bride of the horgs,</i> see Hölgi. Many of the old cairns and hows are no doubt horgs or high places of worship of the heathen age. A third way of worshipping is recorded, viz. a portable booth or tabernacle in which the god was carried through the land, mentioned in Tacit. Germ. ch. 40; traces of this ancient worship were still found in Sweden at the close of heathendom, see the interesting tale of Gunnar Helming in Fms. ii. 73–78.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horkla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörkla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [hark and harki], <i>to hobble, go with difficulty,</i> as if walking on rough ground; hann hörklar af heiðinni ofan, Bs. i. 443.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horkn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörkn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. = hölkn, Bs. i. 452, v. l.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horkull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörkull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>roughness;</i> hann segir svá meðr hörðum hörkul, 732. 15; skal ek göra þeim mikinn hörkul, <i>I will work them much annoyance,</i> MS. 4. 16: <i>noise, din,</i> hófsk þá bardaginn með miklum hörkul, Karl. 289; mátti þá heyra mikinn gný ok ógurligan hörkul, 307; þeir heyrðu hörkul ok stór högg Frankismanna, 354: hence comes prob. the mod. <strong>hörgull,</strong> meaning <i>dearth;</i> það er mesti hörgull á því: as also in the phrase, spyrja e-n út í hörgul, or segja e-t út í hörgul, <i>to ask</i> or <i>tell minutely.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hormeitidr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörmeitiðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a απ. λεγ. in Hým. end; may not this word contain a variation or corruption of some month’s name, occurring under various forms in A. S. and Germ., and of which the Scandin. form is not known, such as <i>Horemaent</i> = <i>November</i> or <i>December, Hornunc</i> = <i>February, Hartmonat</i> = <i>January</i> (Dr. Karl Weinhold),—months of great festivals and sacrifices? For an attempt at interpretation of the passage, see véar, p. 687, col. 1, at bottom.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hormugr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörmugr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>afflicted,</i> Gkv. 3.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hormuliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörmuliga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>sadly,</i> 4. 15, Gþl. 45, Stj. 51, Hom. 116, passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hormuligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörmuligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>sad, distressing,</i> Sturl. i. 13, Þiðr. 174; h. tíðendi, Nj. 170; h. villa, Stj. 250; h. hrygð, 494; h. glæpr, Fms. i. 205: neut. <i>a distressing thing,</i> Fms. vii. 160, x. 400: also with the notion of <i>indignation,</i> það er hörmulegt að sjá það!",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hormung"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörmung
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [harmr], <i>grief, affliction,</i> Fms. vi. 94, Str. 24, 453, Fas. iii. 303; hörmungar tala, <i>lamentation,</i> Fms. iv. 165; hörmungar orð, H. E. i. 255; hörmungar víg, Fs. 8; freq. in mod. usage, N. T. = θλιψις, esp. in plur., Mark xiii. 19, Acts vii. 10: in sing. with the notion of <i>indignation,</i> það er hörmung að vita til þess.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horn-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. one of the names of the goddess Freyja, Edda.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horpu"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörpu-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "see harpa.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/horpu-leikr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hörpu-leikr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>playing on a harp,</i> Hkr. iii. 246.",
