            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hos-magi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hös-magi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a sheep with a gray, dusky belly,</i> Grett. 154: the spelling haustmagi is caused by a false pronunciation.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hos-mogottr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hös-mögóttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>gray on the belly,</i> Grett. 148.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hoss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., acc. hösvan, with a characteristic <i>v;</i> [A. S. <i>hasu,</i> gen. <i>hasweg</i> and <i>haswig;</i> Engl. <i>hazy;</i> Lat. <i>caesius</i>]:—<i>gray,</i> of a wolf; úlfr enn hösvi, Em. 6; hösvan serk hrísgrisnis, <i>a gray wolf’s coat,</i> Hl., Edda 86; höss örn, <i>a gray eagle,</i> Fms. vi. 159 (in a verse); and höss sverð, <i>a dusky sword blade</i> (or = hvöss?), Lex. Poët.: in pr. names, <strong>Hös-kollr,</strong> in common pronunciation <strong>Höskuldr,</strong> <i>the gray Coll;</i> the old form is freq. presented in good MSS., e. g. Arna-Magn. 468, as also in the old ditty, trautt man ek trúa þér | <i>troll</i> kvað Hös<i>koll</i>r, Sturl. ii. 136; but that even in the 13th century the name was pronounced as at the present day is shewn by the pun in the words <i>Höskuld</i> and <i>haustskuld,</i> Sturl. iii. 216. The word is quite obsolete, and does not occur elsewhere in prose.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hostugr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          höstugr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [hastr, herstr], <i>harshly,</i> Pass. 40. 4.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/hosvask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          hösvask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
