      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/jokull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          jökull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. jökli, pl. jöklar, prop. a dimin. from jaki, q. v.; [A. S. <i>gicel,</i> i. e. <i>îs-gicel,</i> whence Engl. <i>icicle;</i> Low Germ. <i>jokel</i>]:—<i>an icicle;</i> gékk inn í sal, glumdu jöklar, var karls er kom kinnskógr frörinn, Hým. 10, of the icicles in the giant’s beard; síðan tóku þeir jöklana ok bræddu, Fms. ix. 155: so also in poët. phrases, where <i>silver</i> is called jökull handar or mund-jökull, <i>the icicle of the hand,</i> Hallfred, Lex. Poët.: as also böðvar-j., <i>the war-icicle</i> = <i>the sword,</i> or sár-j., <i>the wound-icicle,</i> see Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/jolstr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          jölstr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Swed. <i>jolster</i>], <i>salix pentandra,</i> a kind of <i>willow,</i> Gkv. 1. 19 (Bugge 419).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/jord"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          jörð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. jarðar; dat. jörðu, mod. also jörð; pl. jarðir; in old writers dat. and acc. are carefully distinguished; in mod. prose and conversation the apocopated dative is mostly used, whereas the poets use either form, as is most convenient for the flow of the verse and the metre, as in the Passion hymns,",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/jorfi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          jörfi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>gravel;</i> hann jós á þá jörfa ok moldu, Stj. 529. 2 Sam. xvi. 13, ‘lapides terramque spargens’ of the Vulgate:—<i>gravel, gravelly soil;</i> þar var þá víða blásit ok jörvi, er þá vóru hlíðir fagrar, Fas. ii. 558; Þorsteinn gékk frá at jörva nökkurum, Þorst. Síðu H. 183: in local names, <strong>Jörfi</strong> (Eb.) in the west, and in the south Klifs-jörfi, also called Klifs-sandr, Bjarn. (in a verse). <strong>Jörva-sund,</strong> n., Hkv. 1. 24 (Bugge), Vídal., Skýr. 302.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/jormun"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          jörmun-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a prefix in a few old mythical words, implying something <i>huge, vast, superhuman:</i> [cp. the A. S. <i>eormen-</i> in <i>eormcn-cyn, -grund, -lâf, -strind, -þeôð;</i> and Hel. <i>irmin-</i> in <i>irmin-got</i> = <i>the great god, irmin-man</i> = <i>the great man, irmin-sul</i> = <i>a sacred column</i> or <i>idol, irmin-thiod</i> = <i>mankind,</i> see Schmeller]:—<i>great;</i> the compds. of this word, which occur in old Scandin. poets only, are, <strong>Jörmun-gandr,</strong> m. <i>the Great Monster,</i> a name of the northern Leviathan, the Midgard Serpent, Vsp. 50, Bragi (Edda i. 254): <strong>Jörmund-grund,</strong> f. = A. S. <i>eormen-grund</i> (Beowulf), = <i>the earth,</i> Gm. 20: <strong>Jörmun-rekr,</strong> m. a pr. name, A. S. <i>Eormenric</i> (the Goth. form would be <i>Airmanariks</i>), Edda, Bragi: <strong>Jörmun-þrjótr,</strong> m. <i>the Great Evil One,</i> of a giant, Haustl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/jormunr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          jörmunr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a name of Odin, Edda (Gl.): name of an ox, id.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/jostr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          jöstr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. jastar, [<i>ister,</i> Ivar Aasen], a kind of <i>willow,</i> Bragi (Edda) twice.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
