              "__html": "að, (older form <strong>kvafna,</strong> Sks. 108), <i>to be suffocated, choked,</i> in water, steam, or the like; kafna af sandfoki, Al. 50; sögðu at Kvásir hefði kafnat í mannviti, Edda 47; k. í stofu-reyk, Grett. 116: of light, <i>to be extinguished,</i> Sks. 208: of a horse, kafna eðr springa, Fas. iii. 74.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
