              "__html": "a, m. [Engl. <i>cag</i> or <i>keg;</i> Swed. <i>kagge;</i> mid. Lat. <i>caga,</i> whence Engl. <i>cage;</i> the Dutch and Low Germ. <i>kaag</i> and <i>kag</i> = <i>a ship</i> used in rivers and canals]:—<i>a keg, cask,</i> Bs. i. 790, freq.: a nickname, Bs.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
