        >
          karl-dyrr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>the men’s door;</i> in ancient dwellings the wings (skot, set) were occupied, the one side by the men, the other by the women; hence the door leading to the men’s side was termed karldyrr, as opp. to the entry leading to the females’ side, Nj. 14, K. Þ. K. 9, 14 new Ed., Grág. ii. 228.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
