      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/karl-fot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          karl-föt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>male attire,</i> Ld. 276, Grág. i. 338.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/karl-gildr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          karl-gildr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., a law term, meaning <i>full, complete;</i> thus karlgildr úmagi means, not <i>a</i> ‘<i>male</i>-úmagi,’ but <i>a ‘complete invalid,’</i> one who can contribute nothing towards his sustenance, e. g. an infant, a sick or aged person, male or female. The word is a standing term in the old church deeds, where the donor charged the gift with the support of a karlgild úmagi for ever, D. I. passim. The old Swedish laws present the same use of the word, e. g. karlgild mark = <i>good money, money of full value,</i> see Verel. s. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/karl-hofdi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          karl-höfði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a carved man’s head, figure head;</i> bað hann Þorgeir reisa þar upp ás, ok skera á karlhöfða á endanum, an effigy ‘in contumeliam,’ Rd. 305; cp. Fs. 56,—Jökull skar karlshöfuð á súlu-endanum ok reist á rúnar; as also Landn. 4, ch. 4: name of a ship with a man’s head carved on her prow, Ó. H.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
