              "__html": "m. [Goth. <i>kalbo</i> = δάμαλις; A. S. <i>cealf;</i> Engl. <i>calf;</i> O. H. G. <i>chalbâ;</i> Germ. <i>kalb;</i> Dan. <i>kalv;</i> Swed. <i>kalf</i>]:—<i>a calf;</i> kýr ok kálfr, Fms. i. 168, vi. 260, 368, Njarð. 374, Gísl. 80, Eb. 316, 318, Fas. iii. 34, Grág. i. 502, N. G. L. i. 25: the phrase, ala öðrum þræl kálfs-eldi, <i>to feed a thrall for another man as a calf,</i> i. e. to feed a person who does nothing but eat, 31; hindar-k., <i>a fawn,</i> Str. 3: <i>a whale-calf.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
