            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ker"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ker
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Goth. <i>kas</i> = σκευος; O. H. G. <i>char;</i> mid. H. G. <i>kar;</i> Dan. <i>kar</i>]:—<i>a tub, vessel,</i> Grág. ii. 339, Fs. 137, Bs. i. 336, 339, 340, Fms. vii. 150; hvert ker kann verða svá fullt at yfir gangi, Sturl. iii. 282: for fishing, göra garða eðr ker, Grág. ii. 350: valit ker, <i>a chosen vessel,</i> 656 C. 13, Matth. xxv. 4, Mark xi. 16, Luke viii. 16, Rom. ix. 21, 22, 1 Thess. iv. 4, 2 Tim. ii. 21, Rev. ii. 27: <i>a goblet,</i> Fms. x. 236, Js. 78, Hm. 18, 51: <i>a chest,</i> Gh. 7; aus-ker, <i>a bucket,</i> cp. Yngl. S. ch. 14; öl-ker, <i>an ale cask,</i> Orkn. 246; vín-ker, <i>a wine cask;</i> sýru-ker, Bs. i. 336; váð-ker = <i>vestiarium;</i> skap-ker = Gr. κρατήρ; gull-ker, leir-ker, silfr-ker, <i>a gold, earthen, silver vessel:</i> poët., vind-ker, <i>the wind basin</i> = <i>the sky,</i> Egil; ker svefna, <i>‘basins of sleep’</i> or <i>‘tear-basins’</i> = <i>the eyes,</i> Gísl. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ker-bad"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ker-bað
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a tub-bath,</i> Fms. x. 147.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ker-ganga"
          onClick={[Function]}
