        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., kröpp, krappt, [see kreppa]:—<i>strait, narrow,</i> of a road or the like; kröpp leið, Skálda 169; komast í krappan stað, <i>to get into straits,</i> a saying, Fb. i. 311: naut., krappr sjór, <i>a short, chopping sea:</i> metaph., kröpp kaup, <i>a scant bargain,</i> Grett. (in a verse): of a person, <i>sharp, crafty,</i> kröpp var Guðrún, Am. 70. <strong>krappa-rúm,</strong> n. <i>the ‘strait-room,’ a place in an ancient ship of war,</i> the third from the stern, Fms. ii. 252, Fb. iii, 219.",
            }
          }
        />
