              "__html": "f. [Dan. <i>kro</i>], <i>a nook, corner;</i> krá eðr hyrning, Stj. 152, Bs. ii. 134, Skáld H. 6. 2, freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kraka-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kráka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [Dan. <i>krage;</i> cp. Engl. <i>to croak</i>], <i>a crow,</i> Lat. <i>cornix,</i> Hom. 69, Fms. vi. 446, Karl. 437, Edda (Gl.), Rm. 44; vinna eina kráku, Fms. vii. (in a verse); galandi kráka, Hm. 84; íllviðris-kráka, <i>a croaking crow,</i> boding ill weather; sumar-k.: the saying, betri er ein k. í hendi en tvær í skógi, <i>a bird in the hand is worth two in the bush,</i> Ld. 96: a nickname, <strong>Kráka,</strong> Fas., whence <strong>Kráku-mál,</strong> n. pl. name of a poem, id.: <strong>kráku-nef,</strong> n. <i>crow nose,</i> a nickname; whence <strong>Krákneflingar,</strong> m. pl., Landn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
