      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kvan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kván
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. (<strong>kvæn,</strong> Ls. 26, 56, Þkv. 8, Am. 6, Gkv. 3. 7), [see kona; Goth. <i>quêns;</i> A. S. <i>cwên;</i> Engl. <i>queen;</i> Scot. <i>quean;</i> Hel. <i>quân</i>]:—<i>a wife,</i> but never used in the general sense = <i>a woman;</i> an obsolete and poetical word, <i>a ‘queen,’ wife,</i> nú færit mér Freyju at kván, Þkv. 22; honum var brúðr at kván of kveðin, Fsm. 42, 46; svá beið hann sinnar kvánar, Vkv. 5; kván frjá sína, Skv. 3. 8; Héðins kván, <i>the queen of Hedin</i> = Hilda, Korm. 4, Ó. H. (in a verse); Óðs kván, <i>the queen of Od,</i> Hkr. i. (in a verse); kván Niðuðar, <i>N.’s queen,</i> Vkv. 28; bróðir hans kvanar = <i>his wife’s brother, brother-in-law,</i> Am. 28; ok kynvið kvánar minnar, Stor. 20: plur. kvánir, Skv. 3. 14; bið kván, <i>a beloved wife,</i> Lex. Poët.; ósk-kván, <i>id.;</i> Viðris kvæn, <i>Odin’s wife,</i> Ls. 26; Byggvis kvæn, 56; kvæn konungs, <i>a king’s queen,</i> Gkv. 3. 7; nema færi mér Freyju at kvæn, Þkv. 8, but kván, 11, 22; kvæn var hón Högna, Am. 6.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kvan-baenir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kván-bænir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>wooing,</i> Ísl. ii. 215, 216, 239 (where it is sing.), Fas. iii. 144, 595.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kvan-fang"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kván-fang
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>‘queen-fetching,’ wife-taking,</i> as also <i>a match, wife;</i> leita e-m kvánfangs, Eg. 22; leita á um k., Nj. 66; fá gott k., Fms. i. 11; virðuligt k., vi. 57; Brynjólfr hafði gefit honum þat k. er hann hafði áðr átt, Eg. 36; Æsir tóku sér kvánföng (<i>married</i>) þar innanlands, Edda 152 (pref.); gefa e-m til kvánfangs, D. N. <strong>kvánfangs-eiðr,</strong> m. <i>a wedding oath,</i> as to the forbidden degrees, Grág. i. 319.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
