        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f., which is the truest and oldest spelling; kongorváfa, Eluc. 23, Barl. 195, v. l.; kavngorváfa and kaungorvofva, Mar. 153; whence köngulváfa, Barl. 195; mod. <strong>könguló:</strong> [the word is derived from an obsolete köngur (<i>a texture</i>), which has been preserved in the Norse-Finnish <i>kankas, kankuri;</i> perhaps also kögurr (above) is akin, if not the same word; O. H. G. <i>kanker;</i> Norse <i>kaangle</i>]:—<i>a spider,</i> passim.",
            }
