          className="link"
          href="/word/kor-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kör
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. karar, <i>a bed in which one lies bedridden;</i> liggja í kör, <i>to lie bedridden,</i> Ld. 82, Hkr. i. 35, Bs. i. 351, Fms. ii. 200, Gkv. 2. 43; leggjask í kör, <i>to lay oneself down bedridden;</i> sagði at allt var annat athæfiligra en at auvirðask ok leggjask í kör, Eg. 103: mythol. the bed of Hel is called kör, Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kor-bedr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kör-beðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = kör, Eg. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kor-leg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kör-leg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the lying in a kör;</i> körlegs-maðr = kararmaðr, Stj. 158.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kor-leginn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kör-leginn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. = körlægr, Post. 40.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kor-laegr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kör-lægr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>bedridden,</i> D. N.; see karlægr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kori"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          köri
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or keri, a, m., medic. <i>a tent, probe;</i> ef köra kennir inn til heila-basta, Grág. ii. 91: poët. <i>a sword</i> is called keri, Hallfr.; as also Val-keri, <i>id.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kortr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          körtr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [karta], <i>short-horn</i> (?): a nickname, Landn., Sturl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/korugr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          körugr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [kar], <i>slimy,</i> (mod.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kos"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kös
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. kasar, <i>a heap, pile,</i> as of stones, blubber, or the like; hvalr lá í kös, Eb. 292; ok er sú kös (<i>a heap of stones</i>) þar enn allt til þessa dags, Stj. 359, v. l.; þeir þrír fella marga riddara ok alla í eina kös, El. 16; sumir lögðusk í kös, Fms. viii. 306.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kostr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          köstr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. kastar, dat. kesti, pl. kestir, acc. köstu; [akin to kös]:—<i>a pile;</i> bera saman í köstu, Grág. ii. 297; þar féll hverr um annan þveran, svá at þar var k. mikill. Fms. ix. 225; hjoggu ok báru saman í einn köst, Sturl. i. 69; val-köstr, <i>a pile of slain;</i> hris-k., <i>a pile of fagots;</i> kastar skurðr, <i>the right of digging peat enough to make a stack,</i> Vm. 64: esp. <i>a pile of fuel,</i> whence poët., lífs köstr, <i>‘life’s-pile’</i> = <i>the body,</i> Eb. (in a verse); kastar hel, <i>‘pile’s-bane’</i> = <i>fire,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kosungr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          kösungr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>kausungr,</strong> m. a kind of <i>jacket,</i> Fms. vi. 422.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/kottr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          köttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., kattar, ketti, pl. kettir, acc. köttu, mod. ketti; [A. S. and Engl. <i>cat;</i> O. H. G. <i>chatza;</i> Germ. <i>katze;</i> Dan. <i>kat;</i> Swed. <i>katt</i>]:—<i>a cat,</i> originally <i>the martin cat</i> or <i>weasel;</i> engi dynr verðr af hlaupi kattarins, Edda 19; hross eigu menn eigi at eta ok köttu, K. Þ. K. 134; mýss svá stórar sem kettir ungir vaeri, Ó. H.; liggja hjá sem köttr í hreysi, Orkn. 104; sér köttrinn músina, Ísl. ii. 309; rífast eins og gráir kettir, <i>to live a cat and dog life,</i> a saying; hvatr, blauðr, breyma k. (q. v.); <i>a tom-cat</i> is called fress, högni, steggr; <i>a she-cat,</i> bleyða; <i>a black tom-cat,</i> kolr; <i>a white tom-cat,</i> mjaldr; the pet name is kisa, kis kis, q. v.; hreysi-k. (q. v.), <i>the ermine cat.</i> It seems that in the Saga time (10th century) the cat was not yet domesticated, for passages such as Vd. ch. 28, Eg. S. Einh. ch. 10, and the story in Edda (Thor lifting the giant’s cat) apply better to the wild cat or the martin cat; and the saying in Ísl. ii. l. c. (<i>sees the cat the mouse?</i>) probably refers to the weasel and the field mouse; but that early in the 12th century the cat was domesticated even in Icel. is shewn by the story of the chess-players and the kittens leaping after a straw on the floor, told in Mork. 204, 205; for a curious legend of the genesis of the cat, see Maurer’s Volks. 190; kattar sonr, <i>a cat’s son</i> (<i>the ermine cat</i>), <i>a bastard,</i> was a term of abuse, Hkv. 1. 18:—a nickname, Landn.; hvers son ertú?—Ek em Kattarson,—Hverr var sá kottrinn? Fms. vi. 390.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/labba"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          labba
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to slouch;</i> labbaðu veginn, Blesi, a ditty.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lad-ord"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lað-orð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>an invitation, bidding;</i> þiggja laðorð at e-m, Bjarn. 53, and perhaps in the corrupt passage Bs. i. 142 instead of leitorð or letorð.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lada"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          laða
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Ulf. <i>laþon</i> = καλειν; A. S. <i>laðjan;</i> Hel. <i>lathjan;</i> O. H. G. <i>ladon;</i> Germ. <i>laden</i>]:—<i>to bid, invite</i> a guest; Geirríðr sparði ekki mat við menn, ok lét göra skála sinn um þjóðbraut þvera, hón sat á stóli ok laðaði úti gesti, en borð stóð inni jafnan, ok matr á, Landn. 100; ok munu menn mæla, at sá laði er ráðin á, Bjarn. 53; Broddhelgi bauð þeim þar at vera … Þorsteinn spurði hví hann laðaði gesti, Þorst. hv. 44; laða hirð í höll, Edda (Ht.); ef hann er kurteisliga laðaðr, Fms. x. 234: metaph., laða menn til sín, <i>to draw one to oneself,</i> Skálda (in a verse), Harms. 65, Líkn. 28; laða menn til eilífrar sælu, Fb. i. 517; ok laðar til hugskota várra Drottinn sjálfan ok Engla hans, Hom. 149: reflex., laðask, <i>to be drawn;</i> ok laðask allir til Broddhelga, Vápn. 19, but perhaps better hlaðask, see hlaða (fine).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ladadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          laðaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>an invitation.</i> <strong>laðaðs-maðr,</strong> m. = laðmaðr; ok beið hann af því sem l. hans jarteina, Bs. i. 303.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ladan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          laðan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>löðun,</strong> f. <i>an invitation.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ladrunn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
