        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Scot. <i>lax;</i> O. H. G. <i>lahs;</i> Germ. <i>lachs;</i> Dan. <i>laks;</i> Swed. <i>lax</i>]:<i>—a salmon,</i> Edda 40, 72, Nj. 69, Fs. 35, 164, Fb. i. 539, passim: the male lax is called hæingr (contr. hængr), cp. goð-lax, q. v. In Lent it was forbidden even to mention meat by name, and hence at that season people called it jestingly klauf-lax, <i>‘cloven-hoofed salmon,’</i> see the story told in Maurer’s Volks. 207, 208.",
            }
          }
        />
