        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/leikari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          leikari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [North. E. <i>laker</i>], <i>a player,</i> esp. <i>a fiddler, jester,</i> MS. 623. 18, Fms. viii. 207, Fagrsk. (in a verse), Hkr. i. 30, Al. 41, Th. 77.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/leikinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          leikinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>playful, gay,</i> Fms. ii. 169, vii. 175, Mar. 280.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/leikn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          leikn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. the name of <i>an ogress,</i> perhaps with reference to the ancient belief that sicknesses arise from the being ‘ridden’ by witches, Edda 54 (in a verse), cp. Edda (Gl.); leiknar hestr, <i>the ‘ogress steed,’</i> poët. <i>the wolf,</i> Hallfred; the <strong>Leikin,</strong> Vsp. 25, is prob. identical, seið hón leikin, <i>she</i> (the prophetess) <i>worshipped witches</i> (<i>trolls</i>) = <i>she was a sorceress.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/leikni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          leikni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>playfulness, curiosity;</i> göra e-ð til leiknis, Ísl. Þjóðs. i. 615.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/leikr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          leikr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. an inflexion or termination, see Gramm. p. xxxiii, col. 1.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/leikr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          leikr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. leiki is freq. in poetry and old prose, but mod. leik; plur. in old usage always leikar, even in late MSS. such as Fb. iii. 405; but in mod. usage leikir, acc. leiki: the phrase ‘á nýja leik’ seems to point to a lost feminine leik: [Ulf. <i>laiks</i> = χορός, Luke xv. 25; A. S. <i>lâc;</i> North. E. <i>laik;</i> O. H. G. <i>leik</i>; Dan. <i>leg;</i> Swed. <i>lek</i>]:—<i>a game, play, sport,</i> including athletics, Eg. 147, Edda 31–33, Fs. 60; ok eigi var sá leikr er nokkurr þyrfti við hann at keppa, Nj. 29; sjá skulum vér leika þína (not leiki), Fb. iii. 405; leika ok gleði, Fagrsk. ch. 26; slá leik, <i>to set up a game</i> (cp. slá danz), Sturl. ii. 190 (of a game of ball): of a dance, Bret. 42; hann hendi gaman at aflraunum ok leikum, … knattleikar vóru þá tiðir, Eg. 187; leikr var lagiðr á Hvítár-völlum allfjölmennr, 188; sveinninn var á leiki með öðrum ungmennum, Fms. i. 78; fara at (með) leik sínum, <i>to roam about,</i> Boll. 336, Fms. x. 159; hverir eiga hér leik svá újafnan? Nj. 125: of a ceremony, Fbr. 7: of capping verses, Bs. i. 237; cp. streng-leikr, <i>a ‘string-play,’ lay.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/leiptr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          leiptr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. leiptrs, a kind of <i>whale</i> or <i>dolphin,</i> Dan. <i>lyft,</i> Edda (Gl.); hnísa … eða leiptr er eigi verðr lengri en sjau álna, Sks. 203, Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
