              "__html": "n., as in leirinu, Stj. 72, 414; með góðu leiri ok seigu, Sks. 417; leirit, Fms. ix. 511, v. l. In mod. usage <strong>leirr,</strong> m., which also occurs in Fms. ix. 511 (leirrinn); grár leirr, Orkn. 374 (in a verse); leirinum, Fb. i. 354, Orkn. 336, but leirinu öllu two lines below; leirnum, Fas. iii. 583; leirinn, Orkn. 374 (Fb.); thus the older vellums prefer the neut., the later the masc.; [Dan. <i>leer;</i> Swed. <i>ler;</i> Scot. <i>lair</i>]:—<i>clay, earth, loam,</i> but also <i>mud,</i> esp. on the beach, passim, see the references above: in plur. leirar = leira (q. v.)",
            }
          }
