          lest
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> f. [cp. Engl. <i>last,</i> as in Orkneys and East Angl. ‘a <i>last</i> of herrings,’ and Old Engl. <i>lastage</i> = <i>freight;</i> Germ. <i>last;</i> Dan. <i>læst</i>], <i>a last, burden,</i> a measure of ship’s burden, reckoned at twelve ‘skippund,’ D. N. iv. 651, Bs. i. 545, Gþl. 371, B, K. 20, 89, MS. 732. 16 (where wrongly ten for twelve); lest gulls, Fms. xi. 351, where = <i>talentum</i> (?); lest járns, harðsteins, D. N.; lest síldar, N. G. L. passim: <i>a cargo,</i> Jb. 386. In mod. usage the tonnage of Dan. and Norse ships is counted by <i>læster.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
