        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, [lauss; Ulf. <i>lausjan</i> = δύειν; A. S. <i>losjan;</i> Engl. <i>loosen;</i> Germ. <i>lösen</i>]:<i>—to loosen, untie,</i> Edda 29, Eg. 223, Fms. vii. 123; leysa skúa, 656. 2: the phrase, þó mun einn endi leystr vera um þetta mál, <i>it will all be untied, end in one way,</i> Gísl. 82, cp. Korm. (in a verse); leysa til sekkja, <i>to untie, open the sacks,</i> Stj. 216; leysa til sárs, <i>to unbind a wound,</i> Bs. ii. 180; leysa sundr, <i>to tear asunder,</i> Grett. 115.",
            }
          }
