              "__html": "n. [Dan. <i>lærred;</i> prob. a compd. qs. lé-ript = <i>soft raiment</i>]:—<i>linen, a linen cloth,</i> K. Þ. K. 20, Grág. i. 213, Sks. 287, Fms. vi. 348, Fs. 147: also in plur., vera at léreptum, <i>to be at one’s linen,</i> of a lady, 161; lérept is opp. to vaðmál, K. Þ. K. (Kb.) 8. <strong>lérepts-dúkr, -hökull,</strong> m. <i>a linen cloth</i> or <i>cope</i>, Vm. 53, 114.",
            }
          }
        />
