              "__html": "n. [Old Engl., Scotland North. E. <i>lowe</i>], <i>a flame;</i> þeir gáfu honum kerti mjök mikit ok log á, Ó. H. 152; ef kerti er látið í vatnið, þá er log er á því, Rb. 352; hræ-log (q. v.), <i>ignis fatuus.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/log-brandr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          log-brandr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a firebrand,</i> Fms. i. 29, 290, Gullþ. 15, Bret. 18.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/loga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          loga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Old Engl. <i>to lowe</i>], <i>burn with a flame;</i> þeim endanum er logaði, Eg. 238; loganda eldi-brand, Nj. 194; hyrr sé ek brenna en hauðr loga, <i>burn in a bright lowe,</i> Hdl. 48; ef ek sé hávan sal loga, Hm. 153; loga ílla skíðin, Finnb. 254; runnr, sá er Moyses sá loga ok eigi brenna, 655 viii. 2; þar til er borgin öll logaði, Fms. vi. 154; ljósið logar, <i>the light lowes;</i> það logar á skíðum or það skíða-logar, <i>the fire lowes brightly.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/loga-blaeda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          loga-blæða
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "dd, [laga], <i>to flow profusely,</i> of blood; það loga-blæðir.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          logi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Germ. <i>lohe</i>; Dan. <i>lue</i>], <i>a lowe, flame;</i> brenna loga (dat.), <i>to stand in a bright lowe,</i> Gm. 29; brennandi logi, hár logi, Hm. 84, Am. 15, Ls. 65; Surta-logi, <i>the flame of Surt,</i> Vþm. 50; fundu eigi fyrr en loginn stóð inn um ræfrit, Eg. 239; svá var at sjá í fjallit upp sem í loga sæi, er roðaði af skjöldunum, Fms. viii. 210; reyk ok loga, Ó. H. 121; þá var enn logi á eldinum, <i>there was still a lowe in the fire,</i> 153.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logmals-ork"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          logmáls-örk
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the ark of the covenant,</i> Rb. 374, Pr. 77.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          logn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Scot. and North. E. <i>loun</i> = <i>calm;</i> Swed. <i>lugn;</i> Ivar Aasen <i>logn</i>]:<i>—calm, tranquil,</i> of weather, Alm. 23; logn veðrs, Ó. H. 36; í logni, Fms. viii. 178; ok er þeir réru í logui ok sækyrru, … er boði féll í logni, Orkn. 164; datt veðrit í logn, Bs. i. 834; hann hastaði á vindinn ok sjóinn, þá varð logn mikit, Matth. viii. 26: plur., logn mikil, Orkn. 358.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logn-alda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          logn-alda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>rolling in a calm,</i> of a ship.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logn-drifa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          logn-drífa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a drift of snow in a calm,</i> Gísl. 28, Njarð. 374.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logn-rett"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          logn-rétt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., in the naut. phrase, liggja í lognrétt, <i>to be becalmed on the sea,</i> Fas. ii, 30.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logn-snjor"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          logn-snjór
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>snow fallen in a calm.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lok"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lok
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Ivar Aasen <i>lok;</i> Dan. <i>laag</i>; the word remains in Engl. <i>hem-lock</i>], a kind of <i>fern</i> or <i>weed;</i> in the phrase, ganga sem lok yfir akr, <i>to spread like weeds over a field;</i> menn hans gengu sem lok yfir akra, Orkn. 4; gengu þeir einir yfir allt sem lok yfir akra, Fbr. 24 new Ed.; the mod. sem logi yfir akra is a corruption of the old phrase.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lok-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lok
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [lúka], <i>a cover, lid</i> of a chest, vessel; hann stakk endanum í lokit þar sem lykillinn gékk at, Mag. 1; ok lok yfir kerinu, Eb. 196; hálfrýmis-kistur þeirra stóðu á skipum, en lyklar vóru settir í lokin, Fms. viii. 85, Mag. 24, 78; kistu-lok, pott-lok: of a ship, <i>a locker</i> or <i>bench</i> in the stem of a boat, mod. stafn-lok, gékk biskup fram í lokit, Bs. ii. 129.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lok-hvila"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lok-hvíla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a ‘lock-bed,’ a locked bed-closet,</i> in ancient dwellings, as a defence against night attacks, Sturl. ii. 217, Nj. 183, Eg. 603, Fms. ii. 64, Fs. 72, 102; lokhvílu-þil, <i>the wainscot of a bed-closet,</i> Sturl. ii. 228.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lok-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lok-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>coverless, uncovered,</i> Vm. 167, Dipl. v. 18.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lok-leysa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lok-leysa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>lok-lausa,</strong> u, f, <i>‘without end,’ nonsense, absurdity,</i> Nj. 214, Sks. 620, Blas. 45, Orkn. 346 (of a promise not fulfilled), Fms. viii. 102, Karl. 50, passim; cp. endi-leysa.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lok-rekkja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lok-rekkja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = lokhvíla, Ísl. ii. 262, Ld. 140, Nj. 35, Eg. 603, Eb. 118, Gísl. 115. <strong>lokrekkju-gólf,</strong> n. <i>a locked bed-closet,</i> Vápn. 4, Gísl. 115.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lok-sveinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lok-sveinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = lokusveinn, Th. 8.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/loka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          loka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a lock</i> (<i>latch</i>); hann rekr aptr hurð ok lætr fyrir loku, Ísl. ii. 135, Fms. vi. 189; lokur ok slagbranda, iv. 299; loka var engi fyrir hurðum, láta lokur frá hurðum, … Auðr lætr loku (lok MS., but loku 114, l. c.) frá hurðu, Gísl. 28–30, Fms. vi. 189, viii. 332, Eg. 601, Lv. 60: the phrase, margr seilisk um hurð til lokunnar, <i>many a man reaches far to catch what is near at hand,</i> (almost answering to the Lat. <i>quod petis hic est</i>), Grett. 107: prop. <i>a peg,</i> Jabel tók búðar-nagla sinn eða loku, ok hamar, Stj. 388, (Judges ii. 21, a nail of the tent.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/loka-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          loka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Engl. <i>to lock</i>], <i>to lock, shut;</i> hann gékk inn í húsit ok lokaði innan hurdina, Fms. ii. 281; loka hús, Þjal. 10:—in mod. usage with dat., loka hurðu, dyrum.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lokarr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lokarr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. lokri, [A. S. <i>locer</i>], <i>a plane,</i> a joiner’s term; lokrar tveir, Pm. 124; kirkjan á þrjá lokra ok felli-stokk, 13: metaph., frekr get ek at þeim þykki lokarr minn til fégjalda, <i>I ween they will think my plane cuts no thin shavings in the matter of fees,</i> Fms. ii. 65: poët., óðar-lokarr, ömun-lokar, <i>the ‘voice-plane’</i> = <i>the tongue,</i> Ad. 16, Edda 85 (in a verse). <strong>lokar-spánn,</strong> <i>m. plane shavings,</i> Fms. vi. 156, xi. 34, Edda 46, Þiðr. 20.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/loki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          loki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> a, m. [perh. akin to lokka], the evil giant-god of the Northern mythol., see Edda passim, Vsp. 39. <strong>Loka-senna,</strong> u, f. <i>the banter of Loki,</i> the name of an old poem: as a nickname, Landn. The name of Loki is preserved in a few words, <strong>Loka-sjóðr,</strong> m., botan. <i>rhinanthus crista galli, Loki’s purse,</i> the name for <i>cockscomb</i> or <i>yellow rattle;</i> and <strong>Loka-sjóðs-bróðir,</strong> m. <i>bartsia alpina,</i> Maurer’s Volks. 1: <strong>Loka-brenna,</strong> u, f. <i>fire, the ‘blazing’ of Loki</i> = <i>Sirius,</i> according to a statement of Finn Magnusson: <strong>Loka-ráð</strong> and <strong>Loka-heilræði,</strong> n. pl. <i>Loki’s advice,</i> i. e. <i>ironical, misanthropic advice,</i> see Snot 192; cp. the Ditmarscher-lügen in Grimm’s Märchen: <strong>Loka-lykt,</strong> f. <i>a close smell,</i> as from an evil spirit haunting the room, Ísl. Þjóðs. ii. 556.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lokka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lokka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Shetl. <i>luck;</i> Germ. <i>locken</i>], <i>to allure, entice,</i> Am. 73, Fms. viii. 23, Barl. 107, Edda 16, Hom. 108; lokka með blíðum orðum, 623. 12; lokka e-t af e-m, Fms. vi. 201: <i>to pull softly and by stealth,</i> hann lokkar þá af henni menit, Fb. i. 276.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lokkadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
