        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logmanns-urskurdr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögmanns-úrskurðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a logman’s decree,</i> Jb. 170.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logmals-bok"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögmáls-bók
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the book of the law,</i> Stj.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logmals-spjold"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögmáls-spjöld
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>the tables of the law,</i> Th. 10.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logmals-stadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögmáls-staðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a law point,</i> Germ. <i>rechtspunkt,</i> Grág. i. 402; hvat viltú þá göra fyrir lögmáls-staðinn? Ísl. ii. 149.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logn-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., pl. lagnir, [leggja], <i>a net</i> laid in the sea, opp. to a drag-net, Gþl. 421; lagnar skip, <i>a boat used in laying down nets,</i> Eg. 4, Ó. H., D. N. ii. 89: in plur., lagnir, <i>the place where the nets are laid;</i> sela-lagnir, <i>nets for catching seals.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. lagar; dat. legi. pl. legir, Lil. 31; acc. lögu, Fb. i. 525 (in a verse); [A. S. <i>lagu;</i> cp. Engl. <i>lake;</i> O. H. G. <i>lagu;</i> Lat. <i>locus</i>]:<i>—the sea;</i> koma um lög, <i>to come by sea,</i> Vsp. 51: in the allit. phrase, lopt ok lög, <i>air and sea,</i> Sks. 47, Skm. 6; lands eða lagar, <i>on land or sea;</i> or á landi eða legi, Grág. ii. 171, Al. 107; hvergi kom ek þar lands né lagar, at …, Bs. i. 721, ii. 5, 122; lagar hjarta, <i>‘sea-heart,’</i> poët. for <i>a stone,</i> Ýt.; lagar stóð, <i>the sea steeds</i> = <i>ships,</i> Lex. Poët.; stíga land af legi, Hkv. Hjörv. 26.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logrettu-skipan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögrettu-skipan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the order, constitution of the</i> l., as to the number of its members, Jb. 9, Nj. 150.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logrettu-fe"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögréttu-fé
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the treasury of the</i> l., from which the lögsögu-maðr was paid, Grág. i. 3.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logrettu-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögréttu-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [<i>lagraetman,</i> Jamieson], <i>a member of the</i> lögrétta, in Icel. sense, Grág. i. 8; in Norse sense, Jb. 1.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logrettu-seta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögréttu-seta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a seat in the</i> l., Grág. i. 4.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logrettu-thattr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögréttu-þáttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the section of law of the</i> l., Grág. i. 4.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logsogu-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögsögu-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the ‘law-speaking man,’ the lagman</i> or <i>law-speaker</i> of the Icel. Commonwealth, see the remarks s. v. lögmaðr; for the office, duties, etc. see Grág., esp. the Lögsögumanns-þáttr or <i>section of the</i> l., the Íb., Kristni S. ch. 11, Nj., etc.; for a list of the Icel. lögsögumenn from 930–1280 A. D. and lögmenn from 1280–1800, when the office and name were abolished, see Safn ii. 1 sqq. The lögsögumaðr was during the first hundred years (930–1030) elected for life, afterwards for a shorter time (three years); his tenure of office formed the groundwork for the chronology of Ari the historian in his work the Icelander Book.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logsogumanns-rum"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögsögumanns-rúm
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the seat of the law-speaker in the</i> lögrétta, Grág. i. 37, (the opening of the courts fixed at the hour when the sun shone on the seat of the l.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logsogumanns-thattr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögsögumanns-þáttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the section of law about the lagman</i> (see lögmaðr), Grág. i. 1–4.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logu-nautr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögu-nautr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., prop. <i>a messmate,</i> Orkn. 442, Fms. vi. 6, Sks. 370, Stj. 436:—<i>a mate, colleague, companion,</i> Fms. vii. 268, Gþl. 20, 518.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/logu-neyti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lögu-neyti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>messmateship,</i> Sks. 293.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lom"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          löm
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., pl. lamar, mod. lamir, [lama], <i>the hinges,</i> esp. <i>of a chest,</i> but hjarir (q. v.) of a door; lamar á bak en hespur fyrir, of a shrine, Fms. v. 120, freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lombungr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lömbungr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [lamb], a nickname, Sturl. iii. 187.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lon-3"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lön
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., pl. lanar, mod. lanir, <i>a small oblong hayrick,</i> freq. in mod. usage: poët., hræs lanar, <i>heaps of corpses,</i> Höfuðl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/longu"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          löngu
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>löngum,</strong> adv., see langr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/longum-ordinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          löngum-orðinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<i>long-talker, long-winded talker,</i> used as a vocative, in king Harald’s parting words to the poet Arnór—kom sja til nakkvars, löngumorðinn, <i>he came for something, that long-talker!</i> Mork. 32; in Fms. vii. 198 the passage is corrupted into kom <i>svá</i> næst til <i>Noregs,</i> by the transcriber who did not understand the king’s banter.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lopp"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          löpp
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. lappar, pl. lappar and lappir, <i>a paw,</i> of dogs and cats.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/loskr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          löskr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., acc. löskvan, [cp. Engl. <i>lazy;</i> in early Swed. <i>loska-mader</i> = <i>a bachelor, loska-kona</i> = <i>a spinster, loska-læghe</i> = <i>stuprum;</i> cp. Swed. <i>losk,</i> Dan. <i>luske,</i> and Icel. lið-leskja]:—<i>weak, idle;</i> löskvan láð-mann, Fas. ii. (in a verse); löskr mun hann æ heitinn, Am. 57; löskvan þátt, <i>the weak side</i> (in a moral sense), Harms. 13.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lostr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          löstr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. lastar, Ó. H, 176, line 3; mod. lösts; dat. lesti, pl. lestir; acc. löstu:—<i>a fault, flaw;</i> en ef lestir eru á, Gþl. 499; sá löstr er vér köllum nykrat eðr finngálknat, Skálda 187; brag-löstr, <i>a metrical fault,</i> Sighvat: allit., kost ok löst, Nj. 23, see kostr; löstu ok kostu, Hm. 134; skap-löstr, <i>fault of temper,</i> Ó. H. 176:—<i>a blunder,</i> af lesti pentarans, Mar.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          löt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., pl. latar, [latr], <i>dissuasion;</i> telja latar á e-u, <i>to tell the drawbacks, dissuade,</i> Sturl. ii. 55; konungr fór mjök undan ok taldi allar latar á um ferð þessa, Fas. iii. 143.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/lotra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          lötra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, = latra, [Engl. <i>loiter</i>]:<i>—to loiter, lag behind carelessly.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/madk-sjor"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maðk-sjór
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a sea full of worms,</i> Þorf. Karl. 438.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/madk-smoginn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maðk-smoginn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>worm-eaten,</i> of drift timber, ships.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/madka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maðka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to become maggoty,</i> Stj. 91: <strong>maðkaðr,</strong> part. <i>maggoty.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/madkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maðkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Ulf. <i>mada</i> = σκώληξ; A. S. <i>madu;</i> O. H. G. <i>mado;</i> Germ. <i>made;</i> an augmented form, Engl. <i>maggot,</i> qs. <i>madog:</i> Dan. <i>madike;</i> Norse <i>makk,</i> Ivar Aasen; Scot. <i>mauch</i>]:<i>—a maggot, grub, worm;</i> dvergarnir höfðu kviknat sem maðkar í holdi Ýmis … ok vóru þá maðkar, Edda 9; vall hann allr möðkum í hel, Rb. 414; mölu ok maðka, Fb. ii. 78; síðan hitti Þorbjörn í maðka-sjó sem liggr nær Vínlandi, … ok maðkr sá smó neðan skipit til úfæru, A. A. 198, 199; þar drógu vér maðka digrari manns læri, Al. 174, Stj. 91, Sks. 50 (improp. of an insect); ámu-maðkr, <i>a rain worm;</i> sjó-maðkr, <i>sea worms,</i> Þorf. Karl. 438; skel-maðkr, <i>worms with shells,</i> id. <strong>maðka-veita,</strong> u, f. <i>a brood of maggots.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., qs. <strong>mann-r,</strong> which form also occurs in old poets, engi ma<i>nn</i>r und ra<i>nn</i>i, Vellekla, (for the change of <i>nn</i> before <i>r</i> into <i>ð</i> see the introduction to letter N); gen. manns, dat. manni, acc. mann, plur. menn, qs. menn-r; with the article, menninir, so always in old writers, but in mod. mennirnir erroneously, as if from mennir: the plur. meðr, answering to the sing. maðr, occurs in old poets—m<i>eð</i>r vituð öðling <i>æð</i>ra, Fms. vii. 87 (in a verse); Norð-m<i>eð</i>r róa n<i>að</i>ri, vi. 309 (in a verse); m<i>eð</i>r fengu mikit v<i>eð</i>r, Edda 102; hirð-m<i>eð</i>r, v<i>eð</i>ja, Rekst., all verses of the 11th and 12th centuries; er meðr Myrkvið kalla, Akv. 5: meðr hlutu sár, Fbr. 75 new Ed. (in a verse): gen. pl. manna, dat. mönnum, acc. menn. In Ballads and Rímur after the 15th century, and hence in eccl. writers of later times, a nom. mann is now and then used, esp. in compds influenced by Germ. and Engl., e. g. hreysti-mann, Skíða R. 58; or for the sake of rhyme, ætla þú ekki, aumr mann | af komast muni strafflaust hann, Pass. 14. 17: [Ulf. <i>manna</i> = ἄνθρωπος; in other Teut. languages spelt <i>man,</i> or better <i>mann.</i>]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/madra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maðra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [A. S. <i>maddere</i>], <i>madder, rubia,</i> a plant, Hjalt.: freq. in local names, <strong>Möðru-dalr, Möðru-fell, Möðru-vellir,</strong> Landn.; <strong>Möðru-vellingar,</strong> <i>the men from M.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mag-all"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mag-áll
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>tripe of sheep, the flesh of the belly,</i> esp. of sheep, Fas. iii. 392, freq. in mod. usage. Norse <i>kviðaal.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mag-fyllr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mag-fyllr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. = maga-fyllr, Barl. 39, Hom. (St.) 11.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/maga-bragd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maga-bragð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a wrestling trick.</i> Fas. iii. 502.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/maga-fyllr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maga-fyllr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a belly full,</i> Fas. iii. 101, K. Á. 78.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/maga-skegg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maga-skegg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>shaggy hair on the belly.</i> Fms. vi. 141.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [A. S. <i>maga;</i> Engl. <i>maw;</i> O. H. G. <i>maho;</i> Germ. <i>magen;</i> Dan. <i>mave</i>]:<i>—the maw, stomach,</i> Nj. 27: þeir báru sinn varning brott í mögum sínum, Þorf. Karl. i. 242, Fbr. 56 new Ed., Fas. iii. 223, v. l.; opt fær hlægis manni heimskum magi … kunna mál síns maga, Hm. 19, 20; grá-magi, rauð-magi.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [cp. megin and mega], <i>main</i> (as in ‘might and <i>main</i>’), <i>strength;</i> hver Guð hafa þér magn gefit? Bær. 9; trúa magni, Fas. i. 438 (in a verse); þótt magnit væri litið, Bs. i; sina-magn, <i>the strength of the houghs,</i> Vkv. 16; fyrir sakir magns munar, <i>by main force,</i> Bs. i. 679; vinds magn, Barl. 63; mátt ok magn, Fb. i. 259; meira magn, Bs. ii. 18; vera e-t um magn, <i>to be beyond one’s power, too strong for one,</i> Stj. 395; bera e-n magni, <i>to overpower by main force,</i> 512; hón segir at máttr skal at magni um liðveizlu við hann, <i>she says that might shall go with main in helping him,</i> Ó. H. 144; af magni, <i>with might and main,</i> Lex. Poët.; eptir öllu magni, id., Fms. viii. 104; er þat við meira magni, at þú gengr við slíkar meiðingar, <i>it is a sorer thing that …,</i> Bs. i. 531; magn flóttans = megin, Fb. ii. 615; magn ríkis síns, Al. 53: plur. goð-mögn (q. v.), see megin.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magn-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magn-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>magn-lítill,</strong> adj. <i>‘main-less,’ weak, feeble.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magn-leysi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magn-leysi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., medic. <i>weakness, palsy.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to empower, strengthen;</i> Guð magnar jöfur, Fms. vi. (in a verse); oss magni goð gagni, <i>may the gods grant us victory!</i> Eb. (in a verse); rögn magna ríki Hákonar, Vellekla; magna þrif e-s, <i>to give health and wealth to a person,</i> Bs. i. 138 (in a verse); drengr magnar lof þengils, <i>the poet magnifies the king’s praise,</i> Sighvat.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magnadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magnaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>mögnuðr,</strong> m. <i>a strengthener;</i> in poët. compds, hjaldr-m., <i>a war-maker, warrior;</i> sigr-m., <i>a victor,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. a son of Thor, Edda, Ls.: a pr. name, Fms. xii.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magnuss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magnúss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a pr. name; for the origin of this Norse name from Charlemagne see Ó. H. ch. 111,—hví létztu sveininn Magnús heita, ekki er þat várt ættnafn? Sighvatr svarar, ek hét hann eptir Karla-magnúsi konungi (<i>king Charlemagne</i>), þann vissa ek mann beztan í heimi. From this Magnús (king Magnús the Good, born 1024) the name afterwards spread to all countries in which Norsemen settled.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., fem. mögr, neut. magrt, compar. megri, megrstr or magrari, -astr; [A. S. <i>mæger;</i> Engl. <i>meagre;</i> Dan.-Swed. <i>mager;</i> Lat. <i>macer</i>]:—<i>meagre, lean;</i> magran mar, Hm.; mögr kýr, Eb. 316; magr ok máttdreginn, Fms. vi. 302; hón var mögr, Róm. 216:—<i>lean,</i> þvílík slátr er svá eru mögr, Fms. x. 303; tvá hesta aðra feita en aðra magra, Nj. 32; verði þau mögr, Rb. 344:—as a nickname, þá var hann sveltr svá at þau kenndu hann eigi, þau höfðu hann brottu með sér ok kölluðu Helga enn Magra, Landn. 205.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/magrligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          magrligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>lean-looking, pinched,</i> Fas. iii. 178.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mak"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mak
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Dan. <i>mag</i>], <i>irksomeness;</i> ó-mak, <i>troubles,</i> (rare.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mak-radr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mak-ráðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>leisurely,</i> Fas. i. 325.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/maka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a female mate,</i> Art.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/maka-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, [Engl. <i>make;</i> Germ. <i>machen;</i> a root word quite alien from the Northern languages, for of the three references below, two seem to be put into the month of foreigners trying to speak Norse]:—<i>to make;</i> in the phrase, ek ska1 maka honum háðung, <i>I will ‘make shame’ to him,</i> O. H. L. 45 (the persons in the story were prob. foreigners); maki enginn sukk, <i>let none ‘make’ a disturbance,</i> the words of John the Fleming in Bs. i. 801; byrjar oss at maka þessar þjóðir í várri dvöl með nokkurri venju, <i>we ought to put them to some shame,</i> Al. 119.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/maki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Dan. <i>mage, ægte-mage</i> = <i>husband;</i> Old Engl. <i>make</i>]:<i>—a match</i> (prob. originally <i>a customer, partner,</i> cp. mak II), Nj. 35, Ld. 64, Eb. 86, Ó. H. 112, Bs. i. 765, Karl. 296; maki bólstrs, <i>the ‘bolster-mate,’</i> poët. <i>the head,</i> Ad. 6; tveggja, fjögurra manna maki, <i>a match</i> (in strength) <i>for two, four:—a mate,</i> esp. of animals, birds, Bb. 2. 21, 29, 31.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/makindi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          makindi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>friendly intercourse;</i> í makindum ok vinskap, Eg. 41; fór þat allt í makindi ok vinskap, Ld. 192. 2. <i>rest, ease;</i> í makindum, <i>at one’s ease,</i> cp. Dan. <i>i ro og mag.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/makka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          makka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, (<strong>makk,</strong> n.), <i>to job, make and meddle,</i> akin to maka, q. v. (conversational).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/makki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          makki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m., qs. manki, [mön = <i>mane;</i> Dan.-Swed. <i>manke</i>]:—<i>the upper part of a horse’s neck,</i> freq.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/maklig-leikr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maklig-leikr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. (<strong>-leiki,</strong> a, m.), mostly in pl. <i>what serves one right,</i> Sks. 474, Fms. vii. 312, Fs. 165; at makligleik, <i>deservedly,</i> Þorst. Stang. 55, Fms. iii. 156, vi. 342.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/makliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          makliga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>fitly, properly,</i> Þorst. Síðu H. 173: <i>deservedly,</i> Ld. 148, Fms. v. 70, vi. 100, x. 325.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/makligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          makligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [Scot. <i>makly</i>], prop. <i>well ‘matched,’ meet, proper, becoming,</i> Fms. i. 3, vi. 227, vii. 285, Þorst. Síðu H. 173, Rb. 80; compar. <i>more fitting:</i>—<i>deserved,</i> Eg. 561; væri hitt makligra, at …, Fs. 57: <i>deserving,</i> of a person, with gen., makligr er Þórarinn þess frá oss, Nj. 25, Fs. 7; mikils góðs m., 35; öllum þóttu búendr makligir til skaða, Ó. H. 205; þykki mér Njáll makligr vera at ek unna honum þess, Nj. 188.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/makr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          makr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., only in compar. <i>more suitable, easier, snugger;</i> en þeir berjask er þat er makara, <i>but they fight to whom that fitted better,</i> Fms. xi. 277; hann kvað honum makara at sitja við elda, Fas. ii. 112; hann kann vel kyssa, makara væri (<i>more becoming</i>) at hann kynni jafnvel ríða með riddara vápnum, Str. 59.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/makt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          makt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [a for. word, for the genuine form is máttr, q. v.]:—<i>might, power,</i> Bs. i. 773, Clar., and in romances of a later date, freq. in mod. usage, Pass., Vídal. passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/maktar-leiki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maktar-leiki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>might,</i> H. E. i. 246.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/maktar-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          maktar-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a mighty man.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mal"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mal
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the purring of a cat,</i> Snót 132.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mal-urt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mal-urt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>wormwood,</i> Pr. 472.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mala"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mala
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pret. mól, mólu; subj. pret. mœli, Gs. 10; part. malinn; reflex. pret. mólsk, Edda 78; a defect. strong verb supplied by weak forms, thus the strong pres. indic. sing. mel scarcely occurs; in mod. usage it is weak throughout, mala, malaði, malat, although the strong pret. may still be used in writing: [Ulf. <i>malan</i> = ἀγήθειν, Luke xvii. 35, and so through other Teut. languages; cp. Lat. <i>mola, molere;</i> Gr. μύλη; derived are Icel. mylja and melja, q. v.]:—<i>to grind;</i> en sú náttúra fylgði kvernunum, at þat mólsk á kverninni er sá mælti fyrir er mól, … Fróði konungr bað þær mala gull ok frið ok sælu Fróða … þær mólu litla hríð áðr niðr sukku skipin, Edda 78, 79 (the tale of Fróði and the power-mill, cp. 221); auð mölum Fróða (dat.) mölum alsælan, Gs. 5; né mœli svá mær bergrisa … malit hefi ek fyrir mik …, mól míns föður mær rammliga, … mölum enn framar, … mólu meyjar megins kostuðu, … malit höfum, Fróði, sem munum heita, 10 sqq.; frá ek at Fróða meyjar fullgóliga mólu, Edda 81 (in a verse); hann tók klæði ambáttar ok gékk at mala, Sæm. 110; mala valbygg, Hkv. 2. 2; konungr heyrði í hús nokkut kveðandi svá fagra, at honum fannsk mikit um, hann reið til hússins ok sá inn at þar sat kona við kvern, ok kvað for- knnnar fagrt við er hón mól, Fms. vii. 233; á þeim kvörnum mólu tólf konur byggkorn ok hveiti-korn til mannfæðis, höfðu hinar konurnar þá malat sitt hveiti, Od. xx. 106; at mala þeim korn eðr baka þeim brauð, H. E. i. 503; þær er mólu ból Amlóða (q. v.), Edda 67 (in a verse): metaph., stýri mól, of a rudder in the sea, Rekst.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/malar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          malar-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
