        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., pl. mörk, [a word common to all Teut. languages; Ulf. <i>marka</i> = ὅριον; A. S. <i>mearc;</i> Engl. <i>march;</i> Germ., Swed., and Dan. <i>mark;</i> Lat. <i>margo;</i> the original sense is <i>an outline, border,</i> whence are derived mörk, <i>border-land;</i> also merki, merkja, q. v.]:—<i>a landmark;</i> mark milli Grafar ok Bakka, Dipl. ii. 2 (landa-merki); ganga yfir þat mark er náttúran hefir sett, Mar.: <i>a mark</i> for shooting, skjóta til marks, Sks. 379 (mark-bakki).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
