          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          missera-mót
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the meeting, juncture of seasons, where one begins, another ends,</i> N. G. L. i. 35.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/missera-skipti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          missera-skipti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>change of seasons, from one season to another.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/missera-tal"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          missera-tal
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>computation of the seasons, a calendar,</i> Grág. i. 2, K. Þ. K. 164, Blas. 39.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/misseri"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          misseri
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "also spelt <strong>missari,</strong> n., usually in pl.; [from a compd word, the former part of which is <i>miss,</i> denoting <i>the alternation, change of the seasons,</i> for misseri is for the year what mál is for the day; the inflexive syllable -eri is uncertain, but not from ár, see Grimm’s Gramm. ii. 471 (note): to derive this old true Teut. word from Lat. <i>semester</i> is inadmissible, for the sense of a period of six months is not the original one: A. S. <i>missare.</i>]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/misseris-vist"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          misseris-vist
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a year’s service,</i> Lv. 57.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/missi-fengr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          missi-fengr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>missing one’s aim,</i> Gísl. 71, Fms. x. 356.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/missir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          missir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = missa, <i>a loss</i>, Fms. vii. 124, Fær. 136. Am. 98, Grett. 98, freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mist"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mist
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. one of <i>the weird sisters</i> or <i>Valkyriur</i> of the heathen age, Gm., Edda (Gl.); prob. akin to the neut. mistr (q. v.), as is to be inferred from mistar-marr, <i>the mist-sea</i> = <i>the clouds, the airy region,</i> Hkv. 1. 46.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mistil-teinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mistil-teinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [O. H. G. <i>mistil;</i> Germ. <i>mistel;</i> A. S. <i>mistel</i> or <i>mislel-tâ;</i> Engl. <i>mistletoe</i>]:—<i>the mistletoe</i> or <i>mistle-twig,</i> the fatal twig by which Balder, the white sun-god, was slain, see Vsp. 36 sqq., and the legend in Edda 36, 37. After the death of Balder the Ragnarök (the last day of the heathen mythology) set in. Balder’s death was also symbolical of the victory of darkness over light, which comes every year at midwinter. The mistletoe in English households at Christmas time is, no doubt a relic of a rite lost in the remotest heathenism, for the fight of light and darkness at midwinter was a foreshadowing of the final overthrow in Ragnarök. The legend and the word are common to all Teutonic people of all ages.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mistr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mistr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [A. S. and Engl. <i>mist</i>], <i>a mist</i>, a freq. word in Icel. although not recorded in old writers; þoka (<i>fog</i>) and mistr are distinguished.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mitti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mitti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., qs. miðli, <i>the middle waist,</i> Fas. iii. 481. <strong>mittis-grannr -digr,</strong> <i>slender, stout in the waist.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mittum-stangi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mittum-stangi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a corruption from the Germ. <i>‘mit dem stange’</i> = <i>‘he with the pole,’</i> a nickname, which the Norse interpreter did not understand, and took to be a name, Þiðr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/miga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          míga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. meig, meigt, meig, mod. még, mégst, még; pl. migu; part. migit; [A. S. <i>mîgan;</i> Lat. <i>mingere</i>], Edda 58, Grág. ii. 133, Fas. iii. 99, Ls. 34, Fs. 147, Bs. i. 457.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mila"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          míla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [from Lat. <i>mille</i>], <i>a mile,</i> Rb. passim, Al. 109, but seldom. used in good old writers or in poets, for the verse Fb. i. 214 is not genuine, and the only passage from a classical Saga is Lv. 106—ok segja menn at fáar mílur gékk hann þaðan frá (paper MS., of a journey through Germany from Rome).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mimir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mímir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. name of <i>the wise giant</i> of Norse mythology, the keeper of the holy well <strong>Mímis-brunnr,</strong> m. = <i>the burn of Mimir,</i> the well of wisdom, in which Odin pawned his eye for wisdom, a myth which is explained as symbolical of the heavenly vault with its single eye, the sun, setting in the sea, Vsp. 22. Mímir also occurs in the following compds, hregg-mímir = <i>the ‘tempest-sky,’</i> and vett-mímir = <i>the top sky</i> = <i>the uppermost heaven,</i> Edda (Gl.), which are among the nine heavens, such as the ancients fancied it, which shews a connection of this name with the sky; Sökk-mímir, <i>the M. of the depth,</i> is the name of a giant (representing the sky of the Inferno?), Gm. Again, another myth says that Odin carried with him the cut off head of the giant Mímir (<strong>Míms-höfuð</strong>), which told him all hidden things, Vsp. 47, Yngl. S. ch. 7, Edda: Odin is called <strong>Míms-vinr,</strong> m. = <i>the friend of</i> Mímir, Stor. <strong>Míms-synir,</strong> m. pl. <i>the sons of</i> Mímir = <i>the winds</i> (?), Vsp.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mimungr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
