        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to murmur, maunder.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/musla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          musla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [muðr = munnr], <i>to munch.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mussa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mussa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>muza,</strong> u, f. [cp. <i>muzza,</i> Du Cange], a kind of <i>loose jacket;</i> eigi hafði hann plátu muzu né brynju, Bév., freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/mustardr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          mustarðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [from mid. Lat. <i>mustarda;</i> Fr. <i>moustarde, moutarde</i>], <i>mustard,</i> N. T.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/musteri"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          musteri
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>mustari,</strong> n., mysteri in Hom. 46, 97, [eccl. Lat. <i>monasterium;</i> A. S. <i>mynster;</i> Engl. <i>minster;</i> Germ. <i>münster</i>]:—<i>a temple,</i> freq. in old and mod. eccl. writers, as the translation of ‘templum’ in a Jewish and Christian sense, while hof is used in the heathen sense, Bs., Stj., Hom., N. T., Pass., Vídal. passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/muunn-sopi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          muunn-sopi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a ‘mouth-sip,’ draught.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/muga-menn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          múga-menn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. <i>the common people,</i> Bs. i. 732, 735, Stj. 426, 642.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/muga-vetr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          múga-vetr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>mobwinter,</i> the name of a wild winter, Fms. vii. 183.",
            }
          }
        />
