          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ná-bjargir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>‘lyke-help,’</i> see nár; in the phrase, veita e-m nábjargir, <i>to lend one ‘lyke-help,’</i> i. e. <i>to close the eyes, mouth, and nostrils of a person</i> immediately after death; hví hefir þú eigi veitt honum nábjargir er opnar eru nasirnar, <i>why hast thou not lent him the ‘lyke-help,’ for the nostrils are open?</i> Nj. 154; hann bað hvern varask at ganga framan at honum meðan honum vóru eigi nábjargir veittar, Eb. 70; hann lagði hann niðr í setið ok veitti honum þá nábjargir, Eg. 398, Bret. 32; cp. the Gr. ἰδων δε ὑ Κρίτων ξυνέλαβε το στόμα τε και τους ὀφθαλμούς (but not the nostrils as in the Northern rite), Plato’s Phaedo (sub fine); whereas with the Norsemen the closing the nostrils was indispensable, whence the phrase, lúka nösum, <i>to have the nostrils shut</i> = <i>to die,</i> see nös (nasar).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
