      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/naettr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nættr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [nott]; in compds, ein-nættr, þrí-n., <i>one, three nights old.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nodru-kyn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nöðru-kyn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a generation of vipers,</i> N. T.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nodru-aett"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nöðru-ætt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. = nöðrukyn, 625. 90.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nof"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nöf
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., pl. nafar. later nafir, [A. S. <i>nafu</i>], <i>the clasps, naves, rings</i> by which the projecting ends of beams at the corners of walls were welded together, and when they were torn or broken the wall gave way; þeir skutu öðrum endanum út í hyrninguna svá hart, at nafarnar (nafarnir Ed.) hrutu af fyrir utan, ok hlupu í sundr veggirnir, Eg. 91; þeir hlupu þá á veggina svá at af gengu nafarnar af timbr-stokkunum, Fas. ii. 43 (Hálfs S. in Bugge’s Ed., Cod. nafarnir); hann átti lokrekkju görva af timbr-stokkum ok brutu berserkirnir þegar upp svá at af gengu nafarnar fyrir útan, Eb. 41 new Ed.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nogl"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nögl
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a nail</i>; see nagl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nokkor-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nökkor
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv., qs. ne-hvar or ne-veit-hvar, <i>somewhere,</i> very freq. in old writers, <i>somewhere, anywhere;</i> to this word belong the references under nekkverr, B. IV. 3, p. 452; to which add,—hér nökkur, Fb. i. 73; nökkur lands eða lagar, Al. 107. In mod. usage this word has become obsolete and is replaced by einhvers-staðar; the explanation given under nekkverr, B. IV. 3, must be altered accordingly, and the words <i>‘somewhat, may be’</i> struck out.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nokkurr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nökkurr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>nökkvarr,</strong> <strong>nökkvat,</strong> see nekkverr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nokkverr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nökkverr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a απ. λεγ. in a dub. passage, <i>a nick</i> (= nykr?),—nökkvers nökkvi, <i>the nick’s coble</i> = <i>the stone, the rock</i> (?), lasta lauss er lifnaði á nökkvers nökkva Bragi, <i>when the guileless Bragi was left on the rock,</i> Stor. 3; cp. hann tók dvergana, ok flytr þá á sæ út, ‘ok setr þá í flæðarsker,’ Edda 48.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nokkvi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nökkvi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m.; in the phrase, þungr sem ‘nökkvi,’ or nökkva-þungr, of things like hay soaked with water or the like. This word can hardly be related to nökkvi, <i>a boat;</i> we think it is qs. n-ökkvi, cp. ökkr and ökvast, ‘þungr sem einn ökvi’ rapidly pronounced sem ‘nökvi, the <i>n</i> being taken from the preceding word, as in njóli (jóll, p. 326, col. 2).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nokkvi-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nökkvi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [A. S. <i>naca</i>; O. H. G. <i>nakko</i>; Germ. <i>nachen</i> = <i>biremis</i>]:—<i>a small boat</i> rowed with a pair of sculls, <i>a cock-boat,</i> Edda 35 (the fishing-boat of Hymir the giant), 38 (of Balder’s ship); þeir sá mann einn róa frá hafi útan á einum nökkva, … hann kastaði árunum ok hvelfði nökkvanum undir sér, Fms. i. 180, 182 (cp. the verse 181), Fas. ii. 232, 233, 236 (of the giant’s boat); stein-nökkvi, <i>a stained, painted boat</i> (?), (not <i>a stone boat</i>), 231, Bárð. 3 new Ed.; hann sá at maðr reri útan ór Kaldár-ósi á járnnókkva, Landn. 78 (of an apparition): <strong>nökkva-maðr,</strong> m. <i>a man wbo rows a</i> nökkvi, <i>a sculler,</i> Fms. ii. 180.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nokleikr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nökleikr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(<strong>-leiki</strong>), m. <i>nakedness,</i> Stj. 34, 35.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nokvidr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nökviðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., thus in old vellums, or also contr. nökðan; spelt with <i>ey</i>, neyqþan, Am. (Bugge); the true form is a single <i>k</i>, cp. mod. nakinn, not nakkinn, yet neycquiþr in Hm. 49, and necquiþ in Skv. l. c. (Bugge): contr. forms, nekðir (n., pl. m.), Eluc. 26, MS. 625. 66; nökðir, Eluc. 46; neykðra, Sks. l. c.: mod. <strong>nakinn,</strong> nakin, nakið, gen. nakins, but pl. naktir: [Ulf. <i>naqaþs</i> = γυμνός; A. S. <i>nacod;</i> Engl. <i>naked;</i> O. H. G. <i>nachat;</i> Germ. <i>nackt;</i> Dan. <i>nögen;</i> Lat. <i>nudus,</i> qs. <i>nugdus</i>]:—<i>naked;</i> lík skal eigi nökkvið niðr grafa, K. Þ. K. 24; vit nökvið hjún, Sks. 504 B; vera nökvið, Stj. 36; at þau sá sik nekvið, Eluc. 27, Maríu S. Egypt, passim; nökðra lima, Sks. 536 B; þegja (thus, as required both by sense and alliteration, not segja) skal þurs ef hann sitr nökviðr við eld, a saying, cp. ‘not to speak of a rope in a hanged man’s house,’ Ísl. ii. 317; neiss er nökviðr halr (a saying, see neiss), Hm.; hón var nökvið, Eb. 97, v. l. 2 new Ed., but nökt in the text; þeir létu þá síga nökða í vök, 623. 33; klæddir eða nökðír, Eluc. 46:—metaph. of <i>a sword,</i> nökvið sverð, <i>naked swords,</i> Skv. 3. 4; nökðan mæki, Am. 47; nökð sverð, Fms. v. 233.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/noldr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nöldr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a murmuring:</i> <strong>nöldra,</strong> að, <i>to murmur, grumble.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nollra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nöllra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, = gnöllra, Þiðr. 245.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nolta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nölta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, <i>to shiver from cold,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nop"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nöp
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [napr, nepja], <i>chilliness;</i> e-m er í nöpinni við e-n, <i>to bear malice against one, feel hurt and offended.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nordri-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nörðri
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>nörðstr,</strong> see nyrðri, nyrðstr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/norfi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nörfi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. the giant of that name, the son of Loki, Stor.; see Narfi; Nörva-sund = Njörvasund, q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nortr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nörtr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a nickname, Bs. i. 499; cp. narta.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nos"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nös
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., pl. nasar, mod. nasir; an <i>s</i> has been dropped, as may be seen from snös, berg-snös (q. v.), as also from Dan. <i>snuse</i> = <i>to smell;</i> [cp. Engl. <i>nose</i>; Germ. <i>nase</i>; Lat. <i>nasus</i> and <i>nares</i>]:—<i>the nostrils, the nose</i> as the organ of smelling, also of <i>the front of the nose;</i> nasar þessa líkams skyldu vera erchidjáknar, þeir skyldu þefja ok ilma allan sætleik, Anecd.; opnar eru nasarnar, Nj. 154; eldar brenna ór augum hans ok nösum, Edda 41; svá at blóð hrjóti ór munni eðr nösum, Grág. ii. 11; bregða e-u fyrir nasar e-m, <i>to put it before one’s nose,</i> Korm. 34; setja hnefa á nasar e-m, Ld. 36; höggit kom á nasir honum ok brotnaði nefit, Fms. iii. 186; fölr um nasar, <i>pale-nebbed</i>, Alm. 2; taka fyrir nasar e-m, Fs. 141; draga nasir at e-u, <i>to snuffle, smell at a thing,</i> Ísl. ii. 136; stinga nösum í feld, <i>to cover the face in one’s cloak,</i> Sighvat; stinga nösum niðr, <i>to bite the dust,</i> Fms. iii. 189; ef herra þinn lýkr nösum, <i>has his nostrils shut, ceases to breathe, dies,</i> Str. 27; áðr en ek lýk nösum, Þórð. 31 new Ed.; þér mun verða annat eins áðr en lýkr nösum, <i>thy nostrils will be closed before that,</i> a ditty, see the remarks to nábjargir; blóð-nasar, <i>bleeding at the nose;</i> ríða kross í nasar ok eyru ok í hjarsa, N. G. L. i. 339:—in sing. only of one of the nostrils, upp í aðra nösina; það er ekki upp í hálfa nös á ketti, <i>it will not fill the half of the nostril of a cat</i> = <i>it is nothing.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/nos-gas"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nös-gás
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. a kind of <i>goose</i>, Gsp.: mod. bles-önd = <i>anas</i>.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/notra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          nötra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, = gnötra (q. v.), Sd. 169.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/obbeldi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          obbeldi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= ofbeldi, Thom. 405.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oblata"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          obláta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>oblát,</strong> f. [Lat. word], <i>a sacramental wafer,</i> oblát, acc., 625. 192; oblátu buðkr, Vm. 6.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odd-hagr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          odd-hagr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>skilled in wood-carving,</i> Bs. i. 143, Fas. i. 292.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odd-hending"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          odd-hending
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. a metrical term, when the first rhyming syllable stands at the head of a verse; thus in <i>haf</i>-löður <i>skef</i>lir the syllable ‘haf’ is an oddhending, Edda (Ht.) 121: in mod. usage, in Ballads (Rímur), it means two rhyming syllables in the first, and one in the second line, three being an <i>odd</i> number of rhyme syllables—thus, sveipaðr m<i>undd</i> | á silki hr<i>und</i> | sat eg <i>und</i>ir kvendi is an oddhending.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odd-hendr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          odd-hendr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>written in the metre</i> oddhending, Edda 139.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odd-hvass"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          odd-hvass
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>sharp-pointed,</i> Bs. ii. 172.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odd-viti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          odd-viti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a leader, chief, who marches ahead,</i> Hkv. Hjörv. 10, Hkv. 2. 10, Ó. H. 61, 214, Niðrst. 108.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odda-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          odda-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Dan. <i>op-mand,</i> qs. <i>‘odd-mand’</i>]:—<i>the third man, who gives the casting vote, the odd man</i> (third, fifth …): as in the saying, oddamaðr er opt inn þriði, | jafntrúr skal sá beggja liði, Mkv.; hvart sem tveir megu eða fleiri göra sátt, enda verða þeir eigi ásáttir, þá er rétt at þeir taki sér oddamann, Grág. i. 485; þeir skyldi sjálfir semja sættir sínar, en Rafn vera oddamaðr, ef þá skildi á Sturl. iii. 179.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odda-tala"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          odda-tala
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>an odd number.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oddi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          oddi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a triangle, a point</i> or <i>tongue of land,</i> Landn. 294, v. l.; vaxinn með þremr oddum, Fms. x. 272.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oddr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          oddr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [A. S. <i>ord</i>; Germ. <i>ort</i> = <i>‘point’ of land, spot, place,</i> but in early Germ. = Lat. <i>cuspis;</i> Dan.-Swed. <i>od, odd</i>]:—<i>a point of a weapon</i> Am. 59, Karl. 506, K. Þ. K. 96, and in countless instances, knífs-oddr, nálar-o., als-o., spjóts-o. (but blóðrefill of a sword): the allit. phrase, oddr ok egg, Hom. 33; með oddi ok eggju, <i>with point and edge, at the sword’s point, by force,</i> Nj. 149, Grág. ii. 13; ætla ek at sækja oddi ok eggju frændleifð mína, Ó. H. 32; brjóta odd af oflæti sínu, <i>to break the point of one’s pride, to humble oneself,</i> Nj. 94: poët. <i>a point, spear,</i> fölvar oddar, Hkv. 1. 52; seðja ara oddum, 2. 7; oddar görva jarli megin, see jarl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/of"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          of
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> prep. with dat. and acc., the form varies; <strong>umb</strong> is an obsolete and rare form, hence <strong>um,</strong> sounded <strong>umm,</strong> which is far the most common form in old writers, and has altogether superseded both <strong>umb</strong> and <strong>of</strong>: [the ‘of’ answers nearest to Ulf. <i>uf;</i> O. H. G. <i>oba</i>; Germ. <i>ob</i>; Gr. ὑπό; Lat. <i>sub;</i> Sansk. <i>upa</i>.] Most of the oldest vellums, as also the poets, prefer to use ‘of,’ yet not all, for the Cod. Reg. of Sæm. Edda in nine cases out of ten writes um, so also did the Cod. Acad. primus (the Kringla) of the Hkr.; and this is important, for these two vellums are our chief sources for old poetry; on the other hand, the Cod. Reg. of the Snorra Edda prefers ‘of.’ Among other vellums the old fragment of the Orkn. S. (Arna-Magn. No. 325) mostly uses ‘of’ as of nóttina, Orkn. 110; of hans daga, 178; of Jól, 180; of daga þeirra bræðra, 182; but also ‘um’ e. g. ofan um sik, ofan um hann, id. The word will be given in full under letter U, so that a few references may suffice here:",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/of-allt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          of-allt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
