      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ofn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., spelt <strong>omn,</strong> Blas. 46; an older form <strong>ogn,</strong> Boldt 48, answering to Goth. and Swed.: [Ulf. <i>auhns</i> = κλίβανος; Engl. <i>oven</i>; Swed. <i>ugn;</i> Dan. <i>ovn, kakkel-ovn;</i> Germ. <i>ofen;</i> cp. Gr. ἴπν-ος]:—<i>an oven, furnace,</i> esp. in Norway, where there are no hot springs for bathing, Rb. 386, Ver. 29, Stj. 273, Fms. vii. 245, Bs. i. 223, Eb. 47 new Ed.; stein-ofn, <i>a furnace of bricks</i> (?), referring to the year 1316, Bs. i. 830, where the passage may refer to warming the apartments.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofn-grjot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ofn-grjót
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>oven-stones, bricks</i> (?), Fms. vii. 323, viii. 166 (referring to the latter part of the 12th century).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofn-reykr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ofn-reykr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>smoke from an oven,</i> Stj. 124.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofn-stofa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ofn-stofa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>an ‘oven-closet,’ close stove, bath-room,</i> Fms. vi. 440, where it is stated that king Olave the Quiet (1066–1093) was the first who introduced <i>ovens</i> or <i>stoves</i> (ofn-stofa) into the hall instead of the old open fires, see eldr (II); these stoves served for bathing and for heating the rooms; hann lét ok fyrst göra ofnstofur ok steingólf vetr sem sumar. The account of the death of the Berserkers in Eb. ch. 28, referring to the 10th century, may therefore be an anachronism and not an historical fact, for it is reported as extraordinary for Iceland that a bishop of Hólar (a Norseman) in the year 1316 built <i>a ‘stone-oven’</i> (<i>brick-oven</i>) in his house, Laur. S. l. c.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
