        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f., mod. <strong>orosta</strong> or <strong>orusta,</strong> with a single <i>r;</i> in rhymes <i>orr</i>ostur þ<i>orr</i>inn, Sighvat, shewing that the assimilation had even then taken place: [this word is identical with A. S. <i>eornest</i> = <i>duellum;</i> O. H. G. <i>ernust</i> = <i>pugna:</i> whence Fngl. <i>earnest.</i> Germ. <i>ernst,</i> of which orrosta is an assimilated form, qs. ornosta, see Grimm’s Dict. s. v. <i>ernst</i>]:—<i>a battle,</i> Hm., Nj. 8, Fms. v. 71, vi. 69, in countless instances, for orrosta and bardagi (q. v.) are used indiscriminately.",
            }
          }
        />
