      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óðask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, = óask, <i>to be struck with terror,</i> Bs. i. 335.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óðinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. Óðni; [A. S. <i>Wodan;</i> O. H. G. <i>Wodan,</i> in the Old High German song Phol ende Wodan vuoron zi holza; in the Norse the <i>w</i> is dropped, whence <i>Odinn</i>]:—<i>Odin, Wodan,</i> the name of the founder of the ancient Northern and Teutonic religion, who was afterwards worshipped as the supreme god, the fountain-head of wisdom, the founder of culture, writing, and poetry, the progenitor of kings, the lord of battle and victory; so that his name and that of Allföðr (<i>Allfather,</i> the father of gods and men) were blended together. For Odin as an historical person see esp. Yngl. S., the first chapters of which were originally written by Ari the historian, who himself traced his pedigree back to Odin. For the various tales of Odin as a deity see the Edda and the old poems; for the legends explaining how Odin came by his wisdom, how he was inspired, how he pawned his eye in the well of Mimir, see Vsp. 22; how he hung in the world-tree Yggdrasil, Hm. 139 sqq.; and the most popular account, how he carried away the poetical mead from the giant Suptung, etc., see Hm. 104–110. and Edda 47–49; for his travelling in disguise in search of wisdom among giants and Norns, Vþm., Gm., Vsp. For Odin’s many names and attributes see Edda (Gl.) The greatest families, the Ynglings in Sweden, Skjöldungs in Denmark, and the Háleygir in Norway, traced their pedigrees back to Odin, see the poems Ýt., Ht., Langfeðgatal. In translations from the Latin, Odin was, strangely enough, taken to represent Mercury; thus, kölluðu þeir Pál Óðin, en Barnabas Þór, <i>they called Paul Odin, but Barnabas they called Thor,</i> is an ancient rendering of Acts xiv. 12, cp. Clem., Bret., and passim. This seems to have originated with the Romans themselves; for Tacitus says, ‘deorum maxime Mercurium colunt,’ by which he can only mean Wodan; the Romans may have heard the German tales of Wodan’s wonderful travels, his many assumed names and disguises, his changes of shape, his eloquence, his magical power,—tales such as abound in the Edda,—and these might make the Romans think of the Greek legends of Hermes: accordingly, when the planetary week days were adopted from the Lat., ‘dies Mercurii’ was rendered into A. S. by <i>Wodansdäg,</i> in Engl. <i>Wednesday,</i> in Dan. <i>Onsdag,</i> in Norse <strong>Óðins-dagr,</strong> Orkn. 386, Fms. ix. 282: <strong>Óðins-nótt,</strong> f. <i>Wednesday night,</i> N. G. L. i. 17. <strong>Óðins-hani,</strong> a, m. a bird, <i>tringa hyperborea,</i> or the <i>phalaropus cinereus,</i> or the <i>red phalarope,</i> see Fjölnir viii, Faber, Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odins-liga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óðins-liga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv., Ísl. ii. 198, read ó-þínsliga, <i>unlike thee.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odlask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óðlask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to get possessed of;</i> see öðlak.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> adj., óð, ótt, [Ulf. <i>wôds</i> = δαιμονιζόμενος; A. S. <i>wod;</i> Engl. <i>wood,</i> Chaucer, Spenser; Scot. <i>wud;</i> Germ. <i>wüthend</i>]:—<i>mad, frantic;</i> nú verðr maðr svá óðr, at hann brýzt ór böndum, N. G. L. ii. 54 (band-óðr, <i>mad so as to be kept in bonds</i>); hestrinn var óðr ok kornfeitr, Fms. xi. 280; óðr maðr, <i>a madman,</i> Grág. i. 155; óðs manns víg, óðs manns verk, N. G. L. i. 64; óðr hundr, <i>a mad dog,</i> Pr. 473.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/odum"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óðum
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>rapidly;</i> jafn-óðum.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofoti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ófóti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. the name of a giant, Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofreskja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ófreskja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a monster;</i> the word is not recorded in old writers, but is freq. in mod. usage; it originally meant an apparition which can only be seen by people endued with second sight (see ófreskir); ófreskja and skrímsl are used synonymously; eg heiti ekki náðugr herra, svaraði ófreskjan, en eg heiti skrímsl, … Já, svaraði skrímslið, góðgjarn er eg, en eg er ófreskja, … Til eru margar manneskjur sem eru meiri ófreskjur en þér, Kveldv. ii. 162 sqq. in the tale of the Beauty and the Beast.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofreskr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ófreskr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., qs. of-freskr (?), a mythol. word, <i>endowed with second sight, able to see ghosts and apparitions</i> which are hidden from the common eye; þat sá ófreskir menn at landvættir allar fylgðu Hafrbirni til þings, en þeim Þorsteini ok Þórði til veiðar ok fiskjar, Landn. 271; Geirhildr hét fjölkunnig kona ok meinsöm, þat sá ófreskir menn, at …, 212; þat sá ó. maðr um kveld nær dagsetri, at björn mikill gékk …, 289; ok sá hana þeir einir er ófreskir vóru, Bs. i. 607; ok inargir sj;i þat olreskir mean, ok svá þeir er eigi vóru ófreskir, Fms. xi. 136; hann sá öngir menn í bardaga útan þeir er ófreskir vóru, Fb. i. 571 (of seeing a person invisible in a cap of darkness). The word is now obsolete in Icel., and ‘skygn’ is used instead; it remains in ófreskja, q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofrynliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ófrýnliga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>frowningly,</i> Fms. i. 70 (spelt úfrýnliga).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofrynligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ófrýnligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>frowntng-like, frowning,</i> Fær. 50, Fms. ii. 101, Boll. 358, Orkn. 440.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ofrynn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ófrýnn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., qs. of-frýnn, see frýnn:—<i>frowning,</i> Eg. 765, Ó. H. 144, 167 (spelt ofrynn).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ogn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ógn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>dread, terror;</i> ógn stendr af e-u, <i>to inspire terror;</i> svá stóð þeim af honum ógn mikil, Nj. 68; svá stóð mikil ógn af orðum konungs, Fms. xi. 246; þótti honum lítil ógn af þeim standa, i. 26; maðr kom til hans ljóss, ok af honum stóð mikil ógn, Ó. H. 107.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ogna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ógna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Ulf. <i>ôgan</i> = φοβεισθαι; cp. Icel. agi = <i>awe</i>, A. S. <i>ôga,</i> which point to an obsolete strong verb, aga, óg]:—<i>to threaten,</i> with dat.; þér hafit öðrum ógnat, Fms. ii. 266; hann fékk eigi fyrr en hann ógnaði honum til, Sd. 142; hann ógnaði þeim, Fms. x. 217.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ognan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ógnan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>awe, menace,</i> Fms. x. 274.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ognar-andi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ógnar-andi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>spirit of terror,</i> Stj. 643.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ognar-bod"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ógnar-boð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a dreadful message,</i> Fms. x. 54, Stj. 447, 649.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
