      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ogur-liga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ógur-liga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>awfully,</i> Fas. i. 383, Fb. i. 258, Fms. iii. 111, passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ogur-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ógur-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (not ógrligr), <i>awful,</i> Nj. 183, Fms. vi, 376, vii. 172, viii. 8, x. 241, 242, Ísl. ii. 447, Ó. H. 108, Hom. 13, Fbr. 57 new Ed., Sks. 159, 229, 643, Stj. 96, Bret. 96, and passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ol"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ól
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a strap;</i> var höfuðit komit á ólina, Bs. i. 314; the <i>ó,</i> which is kept throughout all the cases, is a remains of the old umlaut; for the references see ál.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/olafr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óláfr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>Olave,</i> an old and favourite pr. name; the oldest form seems to have been Áleifr, from Anleifr, as seen from rhymes, e. g. Ál<i>ei</i>fr is made to rhyme with r<i>ei</i>fum, kl<i>ei</i>f, or the like, Hallfred passim; and, on the other hand, <i>Ál</i>áfr with st<i>ál</i>a, h<i>ál</i>a, Eg. (in a verse), Fms. vi. (in a verse): then the <i>ei</i> was changed into <i>á,</i> Ál<i>áf</i>ar frið g<i>ál</i>u, Sighvat: then the initial <i>á</i> into <i>ó,</i> and Óláfr is made to rhyme with s<i>ól</i> in a poem of the end of the 11th century: lastly, the medial <i>á</i> into <i>a,</i> Ólafr. This Norse name is rendered by Anlâf in the Saxon Chron., and by Amlabh in the Irish Chroniclers; thus Righ Amlabh = <i>king Olave the White</i> in Dublin, see pref. p. iv: in local names, <strong>Ólafs-dalr, -fjörðr, -vík,</strong> Landn.: <strong>Ólafs-dælir,</strong> m. pl. <i>the men from Olave-dale,</i> Gullþ. The answering fem. pr. name is Álöf (the still older Áleif, qs. Anleif, is not recorded), mod. <strong>Ólöf,</strong> Landn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/olga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ólga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to swell;</i> ólgandi Þverá. (<i>the swoln Cross-water</i>) veltr yfir sanda, Snót 12, passim in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/olga-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ólga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [akin to válgr (?), changing <i>vá</i> into <i>ó</i>]:—<i>a swell, swelling,</i> esp. of water; sævar ólga, <i>the swell of the sea,</i> Fas. ii. 378, freq. in mod. usage; cp. also ylgja = <i>the rolling,</i> of waves. <strong>ólgu-sjór,</strong> <i>a rolling swell of sea.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/olm-leikr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ólm-leikr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>fury.</i> Post. 114.",
            }
