      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/omaga-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ómaga-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a person who has many</i> ómagar <i>to sustain,</i> Grág.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/omaga-mot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ómaga-mót
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. a law term, of the case in which a person maintains an ómagi until he becomes destitute himself, Grág. i. 289.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oman-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óman
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>ómun,</strong> f. <i>sound, voice;</i> ómon þverr, <i>the voice fails, falters,</i> Skv. 3. 68; heitir ok rödd ómun, Edda 110: <strong>ómun-lokarr,</strong> m. <i>‘sound-plane,’</i> i. e. <i>the tongue,</i> Ad. 16; see lokarr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/omi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ómi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. one of the names of Odin or Allfather, Gm., Edda: a personification of the wind as the voice of God (cp. 1 Kings xix. 12, God speaking to man through the ‘still small voice’ of the wind).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/omr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ómr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [A. S. <i>woma</i> and <i>wom</i> and <i>dæg-woma</i> = <i>aurora</i>], <i>sound, voice,</i> esp. of a tinkling sound such as a peal of bells heard afar off; klingir mér fyrir eyrum ómr, <i>a sound tinkles in my ears,</i> Bjarni; held eg sem helgan dóm, hörpunnar sætan óm, a ditty: the word is freq. in mod. usage, but is not recorded in old writers, for Edda i. 544, v. l., is from a paper MS.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/on"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ón
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> f. = ván, <i>hope</i>, Am. 67, Ls. 36, Hom. 60.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ónn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = ofn (q. v.) according to pronunciation; óns-hús, n. <i>a close stove,</i> Bs. ii. 256.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/op-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óp
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [cp. Ulf. <i>wôpjan</i> = φωνειν, βοαν; A. S. <i>wôp;</i> Engl. <i>whoop, weep</i>]:—<i>a shouting, crying:</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/op-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óp-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>weeping:</i> með ópligum tárum, <i>with weeping tears,</i> Greg. 39.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/opi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ópi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. a magical Rune character, causing hysterics, Skm.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>or,</strong> written with <i>o</i> in older vellums, or now and then even with <i>y</i>, <strong>yr</strong>; in later MSS. with <i>u</i>, <strong>ur,</strong> which in mod. Icel. is sounded long, <strong>úr.</strong> In other Teut. languages this prep. has been lost as an independent word; only the Goth. has <i>us</i> = ἐκ, ἀπό, and the O. H. G. <i>ar, ir, ur,</i> which in mid. H. G. was lost and replaced by the adverb <i>aus,</i> O. H. G. <i>uz</i>, answering to Icel. út. Engl. <i>out,</i> a word altogether different from ór, see Grimm’s Dict. s. v. er; <i>ur,</i> however, survived as a prefixed particle in a countless number of compds, in A. S. <i>â-,</i> in O. H. G. <i>ar-, ir-,</i> in mid. H. G. and Germ. <i>er-</i>; causal verbs are formed by means of this prefixed particle, e. g. Goth. <i>us-wakjan,</i> A. S. <i>â-weccan,</i> Engl. <i>to awaken,</i> O. H. G. <i>ar-wechan,</i> Germ. <i>er-wecken.</i> In the Scandin. languages, on the other hand, the independent prep. has been preserved in its fullest extent, whereas the prefixed particle is rare, mostly wiih adjectives, and is sounded and spelt <i>ör-</i>, e. g. ör-endr = <i>exanimis;</i> seldom <i>er-</i>, for erlendr (q. v.) is different; <i>ór-</i> or <i>úr-</i> seems to belong only to words of later formation, as ór-lausn, ór-skurðr, úr-kast, úr-þvætti, <i>refuse;</i> úr-hættis, <i>out of time</i> (from skera ór, kasta úr). These compds will be given under the head of ör- and úr-. The quantity of the root-vowel in the particle <i>or, ur</i> is an unsettled question; the German and Saxon forms <i>er-, ar-,</i> as also the Icel. prefixed <i>ör-</i>, seem to indicate a short, the present Icel. pronunciation <i>úr-</i> a long, vowel. The MSS. in these cases give no help; in this Dictionary it has been assumed as long (<i>ór</i>) in deference to the majority of Editions and the present Icel. spelling and pronunciation.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-daudr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-dauðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>extinct, quite dead,</i> Bs. i. 879; cp. ördauða.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-for"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-för
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>departure;</i> krefja arfs ok órfarar, N. G. L. i. 53 (Jb. 158 B).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-kosta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-kosta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = órkostr; deyja frá allri órkostu, Am. 58.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-kostr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-kostr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>means, resources;</i> hafa, eiga, órkost til e-s, Grág. i. 185, ii. 155, K. Þ. K. 90: in the mod. phrase, eiga einskis úrkosti, <i>to be destitute of means.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-lausn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-lausn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., mod. <strong>úr-lausn,</strong> [leysa ór], <i>solution of a difficulty, an expedient, help;</i> hann segir sik vera í heyþroti, ok krefr órlausna, Ísl. ii. 132; hann skal sjálfr þeirra vandræði ábyrgjask en hrepps-menn eru til engra órlausna skyldir, Grág. i. 490; vilt þú, búandi, selja oss korn? væri oss þat ó. ef vér þyrfum eigi lengra at fara, hér skalt þú fá þá órlausn, at þurfa eigi at fara lengra, Ó. H. 112: the mod. phrase, göra e-m úrlausn, <i>to let one not go empty-handed away.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>free, disengaged,</i> Nj. 76, v. l.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-nam"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-nám
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a picking out,</i> of challenging neighbours, Grág. i. 31, 51.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-rad"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-ráð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. = órræði; hvert órráð (yrráð Cd.) skulum vér nú taka, Ó. H. 88; órráð vár kvenna verða jafnan með lítilli forsjá, Ld. 42; munt þú trúa mér bezt til órráða um þitt mál, Nj. 12; liggja hér til miklu betri órráð um þetta mál, Fms. xi. 11; til atkvæðis ok órráða, 33.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-raedi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-ræði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., mod. <strong>úr-ræði,</strong> [ráða ór e-u], <i>an expedient;</i> varð þat hans ó. (vrræði Cd.) at, … sagði hann órræðit eigi gott. Fb. iii. 448. 449; þat varð ó. Özurar, at …, Dropl. 25; þótti honum þurfa nökkurra órræða í at leita, Rd. 238; hér eru skjót órræði til, Fms. ii. 7; taka gott órræði, v. 272; hvert órræði (<i>help</i>) vilt þú veita mér, Nj. 31, Glúm. 352; hann hafði mörg órræði (<i>many sources</i>) til penninga, Bárð. 173.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-skurda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-skurða
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to decide, give a legal decision.</i> Stat. 296, D. N., and in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-skurdar-bref"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-skurðar-bréf
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a writ of arbitration,</i> Pm. 43, Bs. i. (Laur. S.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-skurdar-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-skurðar-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>an umpire,</i> Ísl. ii. 233.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-skurdr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-skurðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., mod. <strong>úr-skurðr,</strong> [skera úr e-u], <i>a decision;</i> veita órskurð um e-t, Fms. i. 42, v. 333; vil ek heyra fleiri manna órskurð (<i>opinion</i>) um þetta mál, Hkr. i. 155; en er Norðmönnum þótti seinkask órskurðrinn, Fms. vi. 20; fengusk þeir órskurðir, at …, Hkr. iii. 306; ráðit hefi ek skjótan órskurð um þetta mál okkat, Lv. 53.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-slit"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-slit
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl., mod. <strong>úr-slít,</strong> [slíta úr], <i>a final decision;</i> hann veitti engi órslit. Sturl. i. 149; vóru oss engi órslit veitt, Ísl. ii. 315; ek hefi veitt eigi órslit hingat til um þat mál, Ó. H. 141; ok urðu engi ó. gör af þeim, O. H. L. 95.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-tolur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-tölur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>dissuasion;</i> hafa úrtölur um e-t.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-vinda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-vinda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., proncd. úrvinda, [the word is not recorded in old writers: the etymology may be from úr and vyndi, qs. yndi, Germ. <i>wonne,</i> = <i>out of rest, out of cheer;</i> if so, it would be an interesting instance of the retention of the <i>w</i> before <i>y</i>]:—<i>restless, distressed,</i> esp. of a person distressed from want of sleep, e. g. a child crying incessantly is said to be úrvinda; barnið er úrvinda, það er úrvinda af svefni, <i>distressed for want of sleep.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-vol"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ór-völ
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. [velja úr], <i>refuse;</i> en mér þykki þó íllt at hafa af órvöl ein, Hrafn. 5.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ora"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> að. = vára (q. v.), <i>to become spring,</i> Orkn. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ora-belgr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óra-belgr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a merry-maker:</i> in mod. usage of youths or children, þú ert mesti ó.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ora-ferd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óra-ferð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a mad undertaking,</i> Grett. 153 A.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ora-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óra-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a madman, frantic,</i> Post. 192.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ora-mal"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óra-mál
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a mad talk.</i> Post. 645. 82.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ora-vegr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óra-vegr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a way of immense length, an immense distance;</i> það er mesti óravegr, mod., perh. corrupt from afar, ofr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ora-verk"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óra-verk
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. a law term, <i>a deed done in a state of insanity,</i> Grág. ii. 64.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/orar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          órar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl., in mod. usage masc. pl. [cp. ærr = <i>insane</i>] <i>fits of madness;</i> þegar tók af honum órarnar er Davíð lék hörpuna, Stj. 467; mæla órar, <i>to talk wildly</i>, Mar. 1071; segi ek yðr satt, at hón bar eigi óra í augum, Bs. i. 204; hann varð ærr ok sagði í órunum (<i>in fits of delirium</i>) hvat þeir höfðu gört, Magn. 522; hann görði sér órar (<i>feigned insanity</i>) ok lét sem hann félli í brottfall, Landn. (Hb.) 215; af órum ok vitleysi, Stj. 467; höfuð-órar (q. v.), <i>delirium.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/orr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          órr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. an obsolete form = várr (q. v.), <i>our;</i> mara óra, Hkv. Hjörv. 5; órr alda-föðr, Vþm. 4; órum höllum, 7; óru hofi, Hým. 33; óru skipi, Hkv. Hjörv. 33; ór salkynni, Skm. 17; töður órar, Kormak; guð ór, Clem. 44; leið óra, 40; augu ór, Greg. 21; önd óra, Hom.; afrétt óra, Grág. ii. 314 A; krapta óra. Niðrst. 2; lögum órum, id.; lög ór, Íb. 17; byskopum órum, 3; órum löndum, Grág.; Drottni órum, 623. 7; úrækðir órar, Skálda 62 (Thorodd, with a nasal sound).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/orraeda-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          órræða-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>helpless.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/orraeda-leysi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          órræða-leysi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>helplessness.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/os-minni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ós-minni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the month of an</i> óss, Fb. ii. 29.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/osk"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ósk
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. dat. ósk, but ósku when it is a pr. name, [A. S. <i>wiscan;</i> Engl. <i>wish;</i> O. H. G. <i>wunsc;</i> Germ. <i>wunsch;</i> Dan. <i>önske</i>]:—<i>a wish;</i> þessi ósk veitisk þér, Fb. i. 31, passim: freq. in plur., ok er gott góðu at una er yðr gengr allt at óskum, Fas. i. 189; þú ert virðinga-maðr mikill ok gengit lengi at óskum líf þitt, Glúm. 337; ok þótti Helga þetta má hafa at óskum gengit, Dropl. 14:—óska-vel, <i>all as one wishes,</i> Fb. i. 34.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/osk-barn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ósk-barn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. = óskabarn, Al. 45, Clem. 24.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/osk-berni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ósk-berni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. = óskbarn, Stj. 103, 252.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/osk-maer"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ósk-mær
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the chosen maid,</i> the name of the Valkyriur, who were the chosen maids of Odin, Og. 18: = eskimær, Fas. i. 118.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/osk-mogr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ósk-mögr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = óskasonr, Ls. 16, Eluc. 61: <i>a beloved son,</i> Fagrsk. 123 (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oska-barn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óska-barn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a chosen, adopted child,</i> 625. 179; óskabarna andi, Rom. viii. 15; eptir óskabarna réttinum, 23; hverjum óskabarna réttr til heyrir, ix. 4.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oska-bjorn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óska-björn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Ivar Aasen <i>fiske-bjorn</i> = <i>fish-bear</i>], a kind of <i>crab,</i> Lat. <i>oniscus;</i> óska-björn is evidently a corruption from the Latin <i>oniscus,</i> which then gave rise to the legend that whosoever possessed the <i>‘oniscus’</i> might have a <i>‘wish’</i> (ósk) granted.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oska-byrr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óska-byrr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a wind to one’s mind, a fair wind to one’s heart’s content,</i> Hkv. 2. 30; the word may have a mythical bearing, as in the tale of Odd the Archer, who had but to hoist the sail to have a fair wind whithersoever he wished—a popular legend analogous to Homer’s Od. x.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oska-sonr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óska-sonr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>an adopted son,</i> Edda 13, Fas. ii. 242.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oska-steinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óska-steinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a ‘wish-stone,’</i> is the globe-formed <i>ovarium</i> of the <i>oniscus;</i> for another record see Maurer’s Volks. 182; it is also called Pétrs-vaðsteinn, q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oska-stund"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óska-stund
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the ‘wish-hour,’</i> for in the popular belief there is a point of time as short as the twinkling of an eye, recurring, some say, every day, others every week, or every year; and whatsoever one wishes at that moment comes to pass: hence the phrase, þú hefir hitt óskastundina, <i>thou hast hit on the ‘wish-hour,’</i> when a person has a piece of luck. Akin to this is the legend of three wishes granted to one by some good fairy; hence the phrase, eiga sér ósk, <i>to own a wish;</i> eina vildi eg eiga mér óskina svó góða, a ditty, Maurer’s Volksagen.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oski"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óski
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>the god Wish,</i> one of the names of the highest god, All-father (Odin), Gm., Edda 2; only the name, not the legend, of this god is left. The name reminds one of the god Eros, as described by Socrates in Plato’s Symposium.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oss-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Lat. <i>ostium</i>], <i>the mouth</i> or <i>outlet</i> of a river or lake; at ósi skal á stemma, a saying;, Edda 60; Danubius fellr með sjau ósum til sjófar, Stj. 88; þó at brjóti nýja ósa í gögnum fjöru manns, ok skal inn forni óss ráða merki sem áðr, Grág. ii. 354; hér gékk upp óss (<i>an inlet, estuary</i>) við nes þetta, ok féll sjórinn út ór ósinum, Ld. 76; vatn þat er Holtavatn heitir stemmdi upp, … grafa út ósinn, hversu torsótt mundi ósinn út at grafa, en er þeir kómu til óssins, var hann út brotinn, Bs. i. 333.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ostr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          óstr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., see hóstr; lostinn öru í óstinn, Fms. vi. 419; kom örin upp í óstinn (hóstinn, Fb. l. c.), viii. 433; hann var lostinn öru í óstinn (hóstinn v. l.) ok fékk þegar bana, ix. 311, Bs. i. 414; var hann lagðr í óstinn, Sturl. iii. 251: spelt with <i>h,</i> Bs. i. 382, Finnb. 214.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/osvift"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ósvift
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. adj., qs. of-svift; e-m verðr ósvift, <i>to be stunted;</i> þeim varð ósvift við þessa sýn. Fbr. 79; honum varð mjök ó. við óp þetta, Fb. i. 417 (vsvipt); en við þessi tiðendi varð honum svá ó., at hann mátti langa stund ekki mæla, Bs. i. 472; hinum varð svá ó. (dátt, Bs. i, l. c.) sem hann væri steini lostinn, Sturl. i. 211.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/otot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ótót
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>ó-tæti,</strong> n. <i>a wretched, bad creature;</i> ótætið þitt! <strong>ótót-ligr,</strong> adj. <i>looking wretched and rugged,</i> of sheep or beasts.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/otta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ótta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [an old Teut. word; Ulf. <i>uhtwo</i> = ἔννυχον, or <i>uhtiugs</i> = εὔκαιρος, <i>uhteigo</i> = εὐκαίρως, <i>uhteigs wisan</i> = σχολάζειν; A. S. <i>uhte;</i> Hel. <i>uhta;</i> O. H. G. <i>uohta</i>]:—<i>the last part of the night</i> just before daybreak; í nótt fyrir óttu, Fms. vi. (in a verse); en í óttu fyrir dag (<i>in the</i> ótta <i>before daybreak</i>) stóð hann upp ok klæddi sik, Edda 28; óttu ok öndverðan dag, Am. 50; í óttu, Fas. i. 148, Hkr. i. 70; þegar í óttu, iii. 417, Fms. xi. 433; hana-ótta, <i>cock-crow, gallicinium,</i> N. G. L. i. 9.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
