        >
          pax-spjald
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a peace tablet, ‘pacifcale,’</i> a tablet with a crucifix and a ‘pax vobiscum’ beneath; in the Roman Catholic times it was presented to be kissed by the worshippers (osculum pacis), see Du Cange, as also a description in H. E. i. 173, note <i>a</i>, and iv. 135, note <i>b</i>; the pacificale was either a piece of parchment or a slab, paxspjald steint, annat með bókfell, Pm. 108; it was different to altaris steinn, altaris steinar þrír, paxspjald gulllagt, ok paxblöð tvau, 112; p. með kopar, 10; p. gyllt, Vm. 83; páskaspjald ok paxspjald yfir altari, Pm. 11, D.I. passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
