        >
          pláz
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "proncd. <strong>pláss,</strong> n.; the word never occurs in good old writers, and hardly before the end of the 13th century: [Engl. <i>place;</i> Germ. <i>platz;</i> Dan. <i>plads;</i> Ital. <i>piazza;</i> all from Lat. <i>platea,</i> see Du Cange; cp. plata above]:—<i>a place, spot;</i> þat pláz eðr eng …, þat pláz sem þessi fæsti hellir var í …, kaupandi þetta sama pláz, Stj. 133; hann sá þar einn brunn í plázi nökkuru eðr eng, 171; á einn vænasta völl … á miðju placinu (sic), Bs. ii. 10; sú höll stendr á eitt fagrt pláz, 122, Karl. 545, Fms. v. 339, v. l.: freq. in mod. usage, although mostly in a limited sense, viz. of <i>a field, ground, spot,</i> but seldom in the general sense <i>‘place,’</i> as in Engl. or Germ.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
