      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/plogr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          plógr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Engl. <i>plough;</i> O. H. G. <i>pfluoc;</i> Germ. <i>pflug;</i> Dan. <i>plov</i>; Swed. <i>plog;</i> a borrowed word, for arðr (q. v.) is the genuine old Norse word; the word was also unknown to the Goth. as well as to the A. S., for Ulf. calls the plough <i>hoha</i>, and <i>sulh</i> is the A. S. term; the Engl. <i>plough</i> was borrowed later, see s. v. arðr, and Grimm’s Gramm. iii. 414]:—<i>a plough;</i> plógr first occurs in the poem Rm.—karta at görva, keyra plóg, 19; skilling silfrs af plógi hverjum, Eg. 278; bera þeir þá út plóga sína, Sks. 336; ef maðr höggr eyk fyrir plógi eðr arðri, N. G. L. ii. 115; hón setti þá fyrir plóg en plógrinn gékk svá hart ok djúpt, Edda (begin.); rekum eigi plug af akri, Orkn. (in a verse); eiga auðan plóg, <i>to have an idle plough,</i> Fms. vi. (in a verse); fjándans plógr, Gd. 33.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
