          href="/word/poki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          poki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Gael. <i>poca;</i> Du Cange <i>poucha;</i> Fr. <i>poche;</i> North. E. <i>poke;</i> as also <i>pung</i> = pungr, púss; Byzantine Gr. πουγγή, πούγγιον]:—<i>a poke, pouch, bag,</i> Fas. iii. 338; guðvefjar poki, Ld. 188, 202; in old writers of a small bag, in mod. of a big one; ullar-poki, <i>a bag of wool,</i> <strong>poka-prestr,</strong> m. <i>a bag priest, a poor illiterate priest,</i> a popular Icel. phrase, no doubt originating from the tale of the Master Thief and the Priest in the Poke, as told in the Norse Tales.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/pollr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          pollr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Gael. <i>poll;</i> Welsh <i>pwl;</i> Germ. <i>pfuhl;</i> Engl. <i>pool</i>]:—<i>a pool, pond;</i> pollrinn var svá djúpr þar er skipit flaut, Ld. 78; þeir lenda skipi sínu í poll þann, er þar gengr norðan at túni, Sturl. i. 167 C: in local names, Gislu-pollar, in Bretagne; Snóksdals-pollr, Brákar-pollr, in western Icel.; cp. <i>Liver-pool, Hartle-pool,</i> the <i>Pool</i> on the Thames.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/polotur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          polotur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl., or <strong>palata,</strong> u, f. [through Byzantine Gr., from Lat. <i>palatium</i>]:—<i>the king’s palace</i> in Constantinople; þeir ganga til konungs palatu þar er hann svaf inni, Fagrsk. 111, Fms. vi. 172. <strong>polota-svarf,</strong> n. <i>‘palace-scouring,’</i> a right belonging to the Warengs, when the Greek emperor died, of roaming through the king’s treasury for money, see Fms. vi. 171—ganga þeir um allar polotur konungs, … ok skal hverr hafa at frjálsu þat sem höndum kemr á (in fact a kind of pillage).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
