        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/rangr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rangr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "röng, rangt, adj., compar. rangari, superl. rangastr; older form vrangr, which remains in Bragi: [mod. Swed. <i>vrång;</i> Dan. <i>vrang;</i> and in southern Norway also sounded <i>vrang,</i> Ivar Aasen; as also Goth. <i>wraiqs:</i> Engl. <i>wrong.</i> The Engl. <i>wrong</i> seems to be a Dan. word, as it does not appear in the A. S., although it has the parent word <i>wringan,</i> Engl. <i>wring</i>]:—<i>awry, not straight,</i> opp. to réttr; skór er skapaðr ílla eðr skapt er rangt, Hm. 127; ofra vröngnm ægi, <i>he wuuld not paddle in the wrong water,</i> i. e. <i>pull backwards,</i> Bragi; er hann fóttreðr flein sinn rangan. Fas. ii. 122 (in a verse); fótr var rangr, <i>the foot was wrung, sprained,</i> D. N. iv. 90: as also in the compds rang-eygr, rang-hverfa (q. v.), and rang-hvolfa:—this sense, however, although common in mod. Dan. and Swed., was never used in Icel., even by the oldest writers, and the word is only used",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/rani"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rani
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a hog’s snout,</i> Fb. ii. 27; brendan rana af svíni, Fms. vi. 365 (in a verse); tún-svín þat er hringr eða knappr eða við sé í rana, Grág. ii. 232; of a snake, ein naðra gróf inn sínum rana, Fas. i. 220.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ranka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ranka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, see rakna; ranka við e-u, <i>to remember dimly.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ranka-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ranka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f, contr. for Ragneiðr, see Gramm. p. xxxiv.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/rann"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rann
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., pl. rönn, Ó. H. 23 (in a verse), Hkr. iii. 43, 74 (in a verse); gen. pl. ranna, Gm. 24: [Ulf. <i>razna</i> = οἰκία; A. S. <i>ræsn;</i> this ancient word is obsolete in prose, but remains in the Engl. law term <i>ransack,</i> prop. <i>‘house-search’</i>]:—<i>a house;</i> ossum rönnum í, Skm. 14; at háfu Heljar ranni, Vtkv. 3; rymr varð í ranni, Fas. i. 492 (in a verse); styrr varð í ranni, Hðm. 24; sköptum er rann rept, Gm. 9; í væru ranni, 13; ranna þeirra er ek rept vita, 24; í ranni Randvés, Bragi: in prose, in the saving, opt er þat í karls húsi, er ekki er í konungs ranni, Fas. iii. 155:—poët., sólar rann, éla rann, <i>the sun-hall, tempest-hall</i> = <i>the sky;</i> aldar rann, <i>man’s abode</i> = <i>the earth;</i> óðar rann, <i>the mind’s house</i> = <i>the breast;</i> Sörla rann, Reifnis rann = <i>a shield,</i> Lex. Poët.; and in compds, ský-rann, glygg-rann, há-rann, hregg-rann, þey-rann, <i>the sky-hall</i> = <i>heavenly vault;</i> hval-rann, <i>a whale’s home</i> = <i>the sea;</i> fjör-rann, <i>life’s house</i> = <i>the breast;</i> dverg-rann, <i>a dwarf’s house</i> = <i>the rocks;</i> leg-rann, <i>the bed’s room</i> = <i>the house;</i> mjoð-rann, <i>mead’s hall</i> = <i>a drinking-hall;</i> auð-rann, <i>a treasury;</i> böl-rann, <i>bale’s abode</i> = <i>death,</i> etc., Lex. Poët. The word is still used by Icel. poets, but is masc. <strong>rannr,</strong> though it is still neut. in poems of the 16th century, heilagt rann, … rannið friða, Bs. ii. 309 (a poem of 1540); it is freq. even in mod. hymns, í heimsins rann, Hallgr.; sælu-ranns, Pass. 25. 10.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/rann-sak"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rann-sak
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a ransacking,</i> N.G.L i. 83, 255; slíkt ransak sem þeim hæfir framast at prófa, Gþl. 33; sem hefir bréf konungs várs fyrir sér til lanðs vistar eða rannsaks, 139",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/rann-saka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rann-saka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Swed. <i>ransaka;</i> Dan. <i>ransage;</i> Engl. <i>ransack;</i> a word which must be of Dan. origin, for it does not occur in A. S.; moreover, the A. S. form of the first part of the compd is <i>ræsn,</i> and the assimilation of <i>zn</i> or <i>sn</i> into <i>nn</i> is peculiar to the Scandin. language]:—<i>to ransack,</i> prop. <i>to ‘search a house;’</i> ef hann vill fleiri bólstaði r. en einn, þeir lagsmenn skolu ganga at garði þar er þeir vilja r., Grág. ii. 193; ef þeir bera f. la inn á hendr mönnmn er r. skolu, 195, Stj. 181, Rd. 285; Birkibeinar höfðu eigi rannsakat bæinn, Fms. viii. 191; en þá er allar vánir vóru rannsakaðar fannsk sveinninn eigi. v. 216; hann rannsakaði með sundi djúpit, x. 370; ok var rannsakat liðit (<i>mustered</i>) ok hafði hann eigi meirr en tvau hundruð, ix. 367; síðan rannsakaði hann rúmit er hón hafði hvílt í, Eg. 566; skulu vér rannsaka alla eyna, Eg. 218; r. Guðs boðorð, 677. 6; r ritningar, Al. 6.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/rann-sakan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rann-sakan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>ransacking,</i> Stj. 181, Ld. 44—<i>a searching, enquiry.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/rann-sokn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rann-sókn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f, as a law term, <i>ransacking a house</i> for stolen things or the like, for a description of which see N. G. L. i. 83, 84, 255, in Grág. ii. 188–195 called <strong>rannsókna-þáttr,</strong> as also Rd. ch. 2, 18, Njarð. 376: metaph. <i>a search, enquiry,</i> passim in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
