      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/raudi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rauði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>red iron-ore, haematite,</i> from which the Norse settlers wrought iron (whence <strong>rauða-blástr,</strong> m. = <i>the forging of haematite</i>); hann bjó í Dalsminni (in western Icel.), hann blés fyrstr manna rauða á Íslandi. ok var hann af því kallaðr Rauða-Björn, Landn. (Melab.) 71; Skallagrímr var járnsmiðr mikill ok hafði rauða-blástr mikinn á vetrinn, Eg. 141, cp. the description in Sks. 162, 163; for remains of furnaces found in Icel. see Eggert Itin. ch. 575. 719, 720: for the phrase rauða undr, <i>the red wonder</i> Sks. l. c.:—<i>ore</i>, hann (Saturnus) fann ok rauða þann í jörðu er hann blés gull af, Edda (pref.) 148.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/raudka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rauðka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a red mare,</i> (mod.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/raudr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rauðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., rauð, rautt, compar. rauðari, rauðastr, [common to all Teut. languages, although it appears not in Ulf. himself, but in the Skeirings]:—<i>red;</i> rautt klæði, Nj. 35; rauðr hestr, Fs. 67: rautt skegg, Fb. iii. 246; blátt eða rautt, Grág. ii. 13; rauðr sem blóð, Ísl. ii. 220; rautt gull, Þiðr. 187; rautt berg, <i>a red quarry,</i> Bs. i. 830:—phrases, rautt brennr fyrir, <i>‘red burns afar,’</i> i. e. <i>there is some hope yet;</i> taldi enn nokkut rautt mundu fyrir brenna, Fms. viii. 34, Fs. 68; snýta rauðu, <i>to spout blood,</i> Fb. i. 412, Karl. 149; falda rauðu, <i>to wear a red hood, to die a bloody death,</i> Landn. (in a verse):—neut., et rauða, <i>the yolk of an egg,</i> Pr. 472:—metaph. <i>bloody. fierce, arch,</i> rauðr víkingr = rauða-víkingr, Fms. xi. 121; see rauðahaf, rauðarán, rauðkinni:—various shades of red, fagr-r. <i>fair-red,</i> Vsp.: dreyr-r., <i>crimson;</i> dumb-r., <i>chestnut-red:</i> dökk-r., <i>dark-red;</i> mó-r., <i>coffee-coloured.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/raudum-skjaldi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rauðum-skjaldi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
