          reðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. [Dan. <i>ræder;</i> cp. also hreðjar], <i>the genitals,</i> esp. of a beast, <i>phallus;</i> flennt reðr, Fb. ii. 335 (in a verse), iii. 427 (in a verse); hest-reðr, Fms. vi. 194 (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ref-gardr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ref-garðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a fox-yard</i> or <i>pit for shooting foxes,</i> Gþl. 457.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ref-hvorf"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ref-hvörf
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. a kind of <i>equivocation</i> which consisted in pairing off words of opposite bearing, as ‘hot, cold,’ ‘water, fire,’ Edda (Ht.) 17–23.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ref-keila"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ref-keila
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a she-fox, vixen,</i> Háv. 55, Fas. ii. 413.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ref-ormr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ref-ormr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., medic. <i>the ringworm,</i> Fms. vi. 438 (Fagrsk. 142), Fél. x. 28. <strong>reforma-sótt,</strong> f. id., Hkr. iii. 178.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refdi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [cp. Gr. ράβδος], a kind of <i>rod, staff, cudgel;</i> þeir sá mann, hann hafði r. í hendi, Fær. 220, 221; þat var búningr hans hvers-dagliga, at hann hafði kyrtil svartan ok refði í hendi. Boll. 358; hann hafði r. um öxl, Fms. vii. 19; konungr hafði í hendi r. gullbúit, … konungr hóf upp refðit ok slé með Þór, svá at hann hraut af stallanum ok brotnadi, i. 44; r. silfrbúit ok gyllt, vii. 194; hann hafði öxi í hendi, ok lýstr til Þorsteins, kom öxar-skaptið í herða-toppinn, en refðis-munnrinn …, Sturl. i. 152; hann sló með einn r. á brún honum svá at hón sprakk í sundr, Karl. 61; konungr sló hann með gullbúnu refði í höfuðit, Fms. iii. 196.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refhvarfa-brodir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refhvarfa-bróðir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a kind of <i>spurious</i> refhvörf, viz. when the opposed words stand separated in the verse-line, Ht. 23.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refhvarfa-hattr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refhvarfa-háttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a metre</i> or <i>stanza in</i> refhvörf.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refil-stigar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refil-stígar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. an obscure word, <i>a serpent-path</i> (?), <i>a hidden, mysterious path;</i> hann nefndisk Gangleri ok kominn af refilstigum, Edda 2; hann hvarf refilstíga (acc.), <i>he disappeared by a mysterious way,</i> Fb. i. (in a verse), cp. Prov. xxx. 19.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refill"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refill
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. refli, pl. reflar, <i>tapestry, hangings</i> round the walls of ancient halls; refil sextögan at lengd, Gísl. 21; ok skyldu tjalda húsin … vel kæmi oss nú reflarnir þeir hinir góðu, 27; hann fal sik á bak reflunum, MS. 4. 41; Þyri lét taka ofan allan hallar-búning, en síðan lét hón tjalda í staðinn blám reflum, þar til er altjölduð var höllin, Fms. xi. 17; refla sæmiliga, Bs. i. 877. The churches in the Roman Catholic times were hung with such tapestry; reflar um kirkju, reflar um alla kirkju are standing phrases in the má’dagar; kirkja á refil er tekr um fram-kirkju alla, Vm. 46; fornan refil um kór, 21; refill fjórar álnir ok tuttugu ok er á Karlamagnús Saga (of hangings with embroidery from the Life of Charlemagne), Jm. 32; reflar um alla kirkju ok engi tjöld undir, Pm. 16; fornir reflar vándir, fimm reflar góðir, Dipl. iii. 4; refil-stubbr, <i>a fragment of a</i> refil, Vm. 157. In poetry <i>a lady</i> is called refla grund, brú, brík, Lex. Poët.: <i>the shield</i> is refill Óðins, Edda ii. 428: of <i>sails</i>, Fas. iii. 204 (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refjottr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refjóttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>tricky, knavish,</i> esp. of a bad payer.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refjur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refjur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>cheats, tricks,</i> Grett. 75; munu þeir göra yðr íllar refjur, Fms. viii. 371, v. l. <strong>refju-samr,</strong> adj. = refjóttr, Glúm. 364.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [the word is obsolete in Icel., and only found here and there in old writers, esp. in the old Norse law: but the Swed. has a word <i>räfsa</i> of exactly the same sense, and as <i>s</i> and <i>l</i> are often hardly distinguishable in vellums, it is not impossible that refsa, and not refla, is the true form]:—<i>to make enquiry, scrutinise;</i> en er þeir kómu í hús hans, þá var at reflat í hljóði hverr þar myndi vera Guðs vinr, Pr. 443; eða missker hann krossa, eða reflar hann eigi, þá gjaldi …, N. G. L. i. 137; ef þingboð ferr eða hvatki boð, þá skal þingmaðr refla á fyrsta þingi ok hafa sótt fyrir þriðja þing, 138; þá sé nemdr váttr við, ok þess í millum sé reflat, at engi finnisk meinbugir á, ii. 368.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/reflan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          reflan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. (<strong>refsan</strong>?), [Swed. <i>räfst</i>], <i>an enquiry;</i> stemna honum þing til reflanar, N. G. L. ii 373, (undan færslu, v. l.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., pl. refar, mod. refir, [Dan. <i>ræv;</i> the root word may be Lat. <i>repere, serpere,</i> Gr. ἔρπειν]:—<i>a fox,</i> Þorst. Siðu H. 180, Stj. 412, 413, Grág. ii. 122: mostly in sayings, þar sá refr rakka, en rakki hafði ekki, Sturl. iii. 116, Þjal. Jóns. 41; sem kona hræðir barn sitt, þegi þú, barn, segir hón, ek læt refinn at þér ef þú þegir ekki, Hom. 144; slægr sem refr, Bs. i. 750, Fb. ii. 330; þú ert mestr í máli sem refarnir í hölunum, Háv. 41; putt, putt, skömm hunda, skitu refar í brunn karls, Fms. vii. 21; hafa skal ráð þó ór refs belg komi, Gullþ. 28: metaph. <i>a tricky person, sly fox,</i> hann er mesti refr, bragða-refr; þeir skyldi ekki láta þann gamla refinn sleppa, Safn i. 74; er Sigvaldi átti, refr, <i>S. that fox,</i> Fms. xi. 106.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, pret. refsti, Ól. 5; part. refst, Karl. 293; but refsat, Fms. viii. 240: [Dan. <i>rævse</i>]:—<i>to punish,</i> with dat. of the person; refsa e-m, vii. 218, viii. 240, Karl. 319: with acc. of the thing, refsa níðings-verk Fms. xi. 241, Sks. 83; r. rán ok stuldi, Ól. 5; r. e-m rangindi sín, Fb. i. 363.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. = refsing, Fb. ii. 316, (rare, see refsing.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsi-thing"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsi-þing
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [early Swed. <i>räfsinga-thing,</i> Schlyter]:—a kind of <i>public meeting</i> or <i>high court</i> in old Sweden; stefna refsiþing, Ó. H. 88 (in Sweden).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsing"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsing
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>punishment,</i> N. G. L. ii. 60, Eg. 89, Nj. 134, Sturl. iii. 261, Stj. 533, Str. 24, Fms. xi. 242, Ó. H. 60; lét hann líka refsing hafa ríkan ok úríkan, 190.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsinga-samr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsinga-samr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a severe punisher,</i> Fms. vii. 102, viii. 299, Ó. H. 190, Stj. 552.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsingar-domr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsingar-dómr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a sentence of punishment,</i> Sks. 676.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsingar-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsingar-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>unpunished,</i> Sks. 591, Eg. 423, ÓH. 53, 60.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsingar-leysi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsingar-leysi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>impunity,</i> Stj. 513.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsingar-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsingar-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a punisber,</i> Anecd. 90, Sks. 666.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsingar-sverd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsingar-sverð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>-vöndr,</strong> m. <i>a sword, wand of punishment,</i> Sks. 695, 785, Stj. 651.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsingar-verdr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsingar-verðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>deserving punishment,</i> Gþl. 531.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refsingar-thing"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refsingar-þing
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n = refsiþing, Fb. ii. 172.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/refst"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          refst
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. = refsing, Fr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/regg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          regg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., poët. a kind of <i>ship,</i> Edda (Gl.) <strong>Regg-búss,</strong> m. a Wendish pr. name, Fms. vi.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/regi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          regi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [ragr], <i>cowardice,</i> Krók. 48 C. <strong>regi-maðr,</strong> m. <i>a coward,</i> Karl. 80, 398, 503.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/regi-legr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          regi-legr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>obscene;</i> regilig kvæði, <i>amorous songs.</i> Bs. i. 237.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/regin"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          regin
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl., only in nom. and acc., for ragna, rögnum are formed from rögn (q. v.), analogously to magn and megin; [Ulf. <i>ragin</i> = γνώμη, δόγμα, and <i>raginon</i> = ἡγεμονεύειν, <i>ragineis</i> = σύμβουλος, βουλευτής; Hel. <i>reginu-gescapu</i> = <i>mighty weird</i>]:—<i>the gods</i> as the makers and rulers of the universe, the word being peculiar to the ancient poems; regin heita goð heiðin, bönd ok rögn, Edda ii. 430: freq. in the Vsp., þá gengu r. öll á rökstóla, ginnheilög goð, 6, 9, 27, 29; nýt regin, Vþm. 25; fróð regin, 26; vís regin, 39; fjöld ek fór fjöld ek reynda regin, 44, 46, 48, 50, 54; blíð regin, Gm. 6, 37, 41, Ls, 32; holl regin, 4; þá er regin deyja, Vþm. 47; urðu heldr hamljó: regin, Haustl. 10; ráð öll ok regin, Hkm. 18; Hrímfaxi heitir er hverja dregr nótt of nýt regin, Vþm. 13, 14:—regin is a pantheistic word, including <i>the world,</i> in such phrases as, unz rjúfask regin, 40; þá er rjúfask regin, 52, Gm. 4, Ls. 41; þá er í ráði at regn (i. e. regin, acc.) um þrjóti, <i>then is the end of the world nigh,</i> Hdl. 41; cp. ragna rök, <i>the world-doom,</i> answering to Saxon <i>muspilli;</i> as also ragna-rökr, for the explanation of which word see rök and rökr: ginn-regin, q. v.; upp-reginn, <i>the heavenly powers,</i> Haustl.; þrym-regin, q. v.; ragna sjöt, <i>the seat of the gods</i> = <i>the heavens,</i> Vsp. 33: in prose only in the phrase, enda mælir rán ok regin (acc.) við oss á sogurt ofan, <i>he speaks to us</i> rán <i>and</i> regin, i. e. <i>he scolds and curses,</i> Ölk. 36; hann var Baldr með Ásum, er öll regin grétu, Fas. i. 473, in a paraphrase from a lost poem.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/regla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          regla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [Lat.], <i>a rule</i>, Sks. 641, Mar.; Eddu regla, Lil. 97, Gd. 2, and mod. passim: <i>a convent, convent life,</i> Sks. 694, Fms. viii. 245, 276, Ó. H. 195, Bs. passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/reglu-bok"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          reglu-bók
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a book of rules,</i> Vm. 66.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/reglu-brodir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          reglu-bróðir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., <strong>-systir,</strong> f. = <i>frater, soror regularis,</i> Dipl, i. 11, Bs. i. 840, H. E. i. 508.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/reglu-hald"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          reglu-hald
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>-líf, -lifnaðr,</strong> m. <i>convent-life, discipline,</i> Bs. i. 96, K. Á. 105, Fms. v. 37, Laur. S.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/reglu-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          reglu-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (<strong>-liga,</strong> adv.), <i>according to rule,</i> H. E. i. 492: <i>belonging to convent life, regularis,</i> Mar.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/reglu-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          reglu-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
