          className="link"
          href="/word/rigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          rígr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. the name of the hero of the poem <strong>Rígs-þula,</strong> in the Edd. erroneously called <strong>Rígs-mál,</strong> Edda ii. 496, a poem which traces the origin of royalty to king Ríg as the ancestor of all kings. This myth belonged to Heimdal, Vsp. 1; it is very likely that the Ríg of the poem is an invented name, a poetical disguise, borrowed from the Gaelic word <i>Righ,</i> which means <i>a king;</i> <strong>Rígs-þula</strong> would therefore literally mean Konungs-þula = <i>the King’s Lay.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
