      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seida"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seiða
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, [answering to síða, q. v.], <i>to enchant by a spell;</i> seiða seið, <i>to work a spell.</i> Gísl. 31; Gunnhildr lét þat seiða, at Egill skyldi aldri ró bíða. Eg. 403: s. til e-s, seiddi hón til þess í hallæri, at hvert sund var fullt af síld, Landn. 147; hann hefir látið s. til, at honum skal ekki vápn at bana verða nema hann, Nj. 44.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seidr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seiðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Norse <i>sei</i>], <i>the gadus virens,</i> a kind of <i>fish,</i> L., Edda (Gl.), Lex. Poët.; hence the mod. <strong>seiði,</strong> <i>a fry</i>; vara-seiði, <i>the fry</i> or <i>young of fish.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seidr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seiðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. seiðar, dat. seiði; the fem. seið sina (sinn), Fms. ii. 136, and seiðit, Fas. iii. 319, are false forms:—<i>a spell, charm, enchantment, incantation,</i> which in the heathen times was solemnly performed at night; the wizards or witches were seated with certain solemn rites on a scaffold (seiðhjallr), from which they chanted their spells and songs; the ‘seidr’ was performed either to work any kind of good or evil to another person, or to be a kind of <i>oracle</i> or <i>fortune-telling,</i> to foreshow future events, such as the life and fate of those present, the weather, or the like; of the evil kind is the charm in Gísl. l. c., Ld. 152; fá at seið, Hkr. i. 21; Ingjaldr ok völvan ætluðu til seiðar mikils um nóttina, Fas. ii. 507; Freyja kenndi fyrst með Ásum seið, 8; fremja seið, Þorf. Karl. 376; efla seið, Eg. 403, Fas. ii. 72; magna seið, Gísl. 116; konungr bað hann hætta seiði, Fms. i. 10: hón bað fá sér konur er kunnu fræði þat sem til seiðsins þarf, Þorf. Karl. 378; var þangat at heyra íll læti er þeir frömdu seiðinn (seiðit Ed. wrongly), Fas. iii. 319: seiðis-hús, <i>the house where the spell was worked.</i> Fas. iii. 166, v. l.; in Yngl. S. ch. 7 the charm of ‘seidr’ is attributed to Odin; Óðinn kunni þá íþrótt, er mestr máttr fylgdi, ok framði sjálfr, er seiðr heitir, en af því mátti hann vita örlög manna ok úorðna hluti, svá ok at göra mönnum bana eðr úhamingju eða vanheilindi, svá ok at taka frá mönnum vit eðr afl ok gefa öðrum, en þessi fjölkyngi, er framið er, fylgir svá mikil ergi, at eigi þótti karlmönnum skammlaust við at fara, ok var gyðjunum kennd sú íþrótt, Yngl. S. ch. 7; as to the rites and ceremonies of the ‘seidr’ see esp. the interesting account in Þorf. Karl. S. ch. 3, compared with that in Vd. ch. 10 and Örvar Odds S. ch. 2 and 3; even the old poem Völuspá is framed as a song delivered by a prophetess working a spell. The witch scene in Macbeth is an echo of the ancient ‘seidr’ as it survived in tradition in Shakespeare’s time, though the devilry and the cauldron are later additions.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seidsla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seiðsla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = seiðr, Fas. iii. 319.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seigildi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seigildi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a tough substance, a knot.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seigja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seigja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>toughness.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seigla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seigla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>toughness, difficulty.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seigr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [Dan. <i>seig</i>], <i>tough;</i> seigu leiri, Sks. 416; seigr í sinum, Flóv. 27, Karl. 475; seig bönd, Hom. 124.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seil"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seil
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [a Goth. form <i>sail</i> is assumed from <i>sailjan</i> = χαλαν, Mark ii. 4; A. S. <i>sæl;</i> Germ. <i>seil</i>]:—<i>a string, line,</i> esp. in Icel. used of a line on which fishermen string their catch of fish and trail them behind the boat; the word is rare in old writers, koma á seil e-m, <i>to be carried along by one,</i> Þd. 9; rás seil, Merl. 2. 12; seil grundar, <i>‘earth-thong,’ a snake,</i> Lex. Poët.; seilar sól, <i>a shield;</i> þrym-seil, id.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seila"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seila
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a hollow,</i> Björn: a local name.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seilask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seilask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, dep. <i>to stretch out one’s hands</i> as high or as far as one can reach; þótti mér svá löng höndin á mér, atek þóttumk s. upp á bjargit, Þorst. Síðu H. 178; Þórr seildisk svá langt upp sem hann mátti lengst, Edda 33; hann bað Þorfinn þá s. í móti djáknanum, Orkn. 112; Kormakr seildisk til ok hjó, Korm. 142, Ísl. ii. 269; s. til sverðsins, Fms. viii. 332.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seiling"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seiling
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a stretching up the hands;</i> in Icel. <i>the height</i> of a person stretching his hand up is called seiling, það er seiling mín, or það er seilingar-hæð, það er seiling upp undir loptið, and the like.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seimr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seimr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [síma], <i>a wire</i> or <i>string;</i> draga seiminn, <i>to drawl out one’s words,</i> i. e. <i>talk with a canting voice.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a delay;</i> nú var eigi sein á (seinat?) konungi til mótsins, <i>the king did not wait for him,</i> Fms. vi. 239: the saying, ein stund verðr opt at seinum, <i>one hour may make it too late,</i> Harms. 41; aldri læt ek at munni sein, Mkv. 24; frið-sein, <i>lack of peace, disturbance,</i> Þd. 9.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-buinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-búinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>‘late-boun,’ slow in getting ready,</i> Fms. ix, 304.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-fyrndr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-fyrndr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>long-lived, lasting,</i> Edda (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-faerr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-færr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>slow,</i> Grett. 90 A, Fms. xi. 434; brú var á, ok var seinfært yfir, <i>it took a long time to pass,</i> Sturl. iii. 24.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-gorr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-görr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>‘slow-made,’ slow-growing;</i> hann var s. maðr í uppvexti, Sturl. iii, 122; opp. to bráðgörr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-heppiligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-heppiligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>slow, dull-looking,</i> Fms. vi. 204.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-latr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-látr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>slow, dull of motion,</i> Bs. i. 795; opp. to bráð-látr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-liga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-liga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>slowly;</i> taka s. undir e-t, or taka e-u s., <i>indifferently,</i> Nj. 217, Fms. i. 74.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>slow, dull;</i> Oddr var eldsætr ok s., Landn. 235; s. í viðbragði, Grett. 90; Sighvatr þótti heldr s. fyrst í æskunni, Fb. iii. 243; hann beiddi hann liðveizlu, Hálfdán var hinn seinligasti, <i>H. was slow, unwilling,</i> Sturl. iii. 16.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-laeti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-læti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>slowness, dulness, sluggishness.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-maeltr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-mæltr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>slow-speaking.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-taladr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-talaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>slow-spoken,</i> Stj. 260.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sein-threyttr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sein-þreyttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>long-suffering,</i> Nj. 90, Fms. vi. 371; s. til reiði.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seina"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seina
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Ulf. <i>sainjan</i> = βραδύνειν; Germ. <i>sehnen,</i> but only in a metaph. sense]:—<i>to delay, slacken;</i> skynda skal hverr sem einn at snúask til Guðs meðan hann má, at eigi seini hann, <i>lest he be too late,</i> Hom. 13: seina e-u, <i>to delay;</i> verðr mein ef því seinum, Leiðarv. 39: s. at hróðri, <i>to lag with his verses,</i> Orkn. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seinka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seinka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to delay, slacken,</i> Ísl. ii. 217: with acc., s. gönguna, Rb. 106; s. e-t mál, <i>to put a case off,</i> Fms. i. 74: with dat., and so in mod. usage, seinka e-u, Ísl. ii. 217, Gísl. 121.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seinkan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seinkan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a hindrance, delay,</i> Eg. 546, Bs. i. 482.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., compar. seinni, superl. seinst, seinstr, mod. seinastr, and so in Fb. i. 74, Orkn. 402; in mod. usage compar. seinni, but superl. seinastr; [A. S. <i>sæne;</i> mid. H. G. <i>seine;</i> Swed. <i>sen;</i> Dan. <i>seen</i>; Lat. <i>segnis</i>]:—<i>slow, slack,</i> opp. to fljótr; seinn á fæti, Fms. vii. 169; hann er seinn, Rb. 358; ertú seinn mjök á slíkum sögum, Fs. 69: gramm., samstöfur seinar eðr skjótar, Edda 123, passim in old and mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/seizla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          seizla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "qs. seiðsla = seiðr, Fas. iii. 319.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., see sekt. <strong>sekð-fé,</strong> n. = sektarfé, Nj. 110.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekd-audigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekð-auðigr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>‘guilt-rich,’ wicked,</i> Landn. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekdar-domr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekðar-dómr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a conviction, sentence of outlawry,</i> opp. to sættardómr, Grág. i. 487.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekdar-fe"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekðar-fé
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the property of an outlaw,</i> which was confiscated, one half to the community (fjórðungs-menn), the other half to the prosecutor, Nj. 110, Grág. i. 120, Sturl. i. 34, Njarð. 382, Eb. 36, 110 new Ed.; af hans s. urðu almenningar, Landn. 121: <i>a price put on the head of the culprit,</i> Grett.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekdar-gord"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekðar-görð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a sentence of</i> sekt, Grág. i. 487.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekdar-handsal"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekðar-handsal
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a ‘hansel’</i> or <i>first trial of</i> sekt, Grág. i. 118, 488.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekdar-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekðar-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>free, not convicted;</i> eigi ann ek þess Þóri at fara sektalausum (<i>unconvicted</i>) af þessum fundi, Lv. 45; sektalaust, <i>with impunity,</i> N. G. L. i. 349, K. Á. 176, Jb. 22 B, Sks. 602 B, Gþl. 23.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð or t, also spelt sekkja, <i>to fine, sentence to a fine.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, <i>to pack up;</i> sekka vöru, Nj. 259: mod. <strong>sekkja,</strong> in the phrase, sekkja skapi sínu, <i>to shut up</i> (i. e. <i>suppress</i>) <i>one’s indignation.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. sekkjar, Stj. 214; pl. sekkar; but mod. sekkir, also Stj. 214, Nj. 134, l. 2 from bottom: [a word common to all Indo-Germanic languages]:—<i>a sack, bag;</i> s. er ílát, Skálda 168; þeir höfðu með sér sekka, Blas. 45; but acc. sekki, Stj. 217; í sekkunum, 215; sekkjar munnr, 214; þeir báru milli sín sekk, Ó. H. 135; sekkr manns heitir byrðr þær er einn fetill er í, N. G. L. i. 349.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj.; in this word in old vellums a <i>j</i> appears after the <i>k</i> and before a vowel, whence also came the old change of the root vowel; thus, sekjan, sekjum, sekjar; in later vellums this <i>j</i> is dropped, sekan, sekum, etc.: [from sök]:—prop. <i>sentenced,</i> to pay in money or person: esp. of a fine, <i>mulcted,</i> verðr hann sekr um þat þremr, sex mörkum, Grág. i. 37, 296, 363, 375; þá eru þeir sekir fimtán mörkum, N. G. L. i. 21, 359 (else the Grág. has útlagr, q. v.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/sekt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sekt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f.; in the Grág., esp. Kb., the older form <strong>sekð</strong> or sekþ prevails; in Kb. ch. 60, sekt occurs nine times, sekð or sekþ seventeen times:—<i>a penalty, fine, mulct;</i> varðar búanda þat þriggja marka sekt, Grág. i. 158; ef maðr handsalar manni ákveðna sekt sína, 119.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
