              "__html": "a, m. <i>a vain boaster,</i> Karl. 284; hence are prob. corrupted the mod. gort and gortari, q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skat-vida"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skat-viða
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>large spars of wood;</i> en sperrur eða skatviðu yfir þann veg at færa fyrir-bjóðum vér, D. N. i. 595.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skat-yrnir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skat-yrnir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the ‘top-sky,’ ether</i> (see skati), Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skata"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skata
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a skate</i> (the fish), Edda (Gl.), passim in mod. usage; þegir barnið meðan það étr skötu-fótinn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skati"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skati
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m., pl. skatnar, poët.; [cp. Swed. <i>skata</i> = <i>the top of a tree, a spar,</i> and skat-vegr or skötu-vegr, skat-viða]:—<i>a towering, lordly man,</i> but only used in poetry, Edda (Gl.); skapleik skata, Höfuðl.; skati enn ungi, Hdl. 9; skatna margra, 21; er at skamt milli skata húsa, a saying, <i>great men are not found at every door,</i> Ad. 21; enginn veifiskati, <i>no open-handed men,</i> Ölk. 34; gull-skati, Edda (in a verse); þjóðskati, <i>a great, lordly man,</i> Höfuðl.: plur. <i>men</i>, skatna vinr, <i>the friend of men,</i> Yngl. S. (in a verse); skatna dróttinn, Skv. 1. 5; skatna mengi, Akv. 31, Skv. 3. 54; as a nickname, Fms. xi. 351.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skatt-bondi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skatt-bóndi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a franklin who has to pay</i> skattr, Bs. i. 834.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skatt-fe"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skatt-fé
