        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f.(?), <i>a plug;</i> en í blegðunum ætla ek vera skaup, Krók. 56 C.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skaup-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skaup
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>mockery, ridicule;</i> skaupi gnegr, Ad. 2; þat varð hlaup at skaupi, Kormak; hafa at skaupi, <i>to mock, scoff at,</i> Clem. 43, Fms. iv. 259; hann görir af mikit skaup, Sks. 247; skaup ok skemmt, Fms. ii. 142; skaup eðr atyrði, Fs. 72; hafa í skaupi ok hlátri, Bs. i. 812; draga þeir glott at ok mikit skaup, 647; verða at skömm ok at skaupi, Stj. 569: mod. skop.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skaut"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skaut
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Ulf. <i>skauts</i> = κράσπεδον, Matth. ix. 20, Mark vi. 56, Luke viii. 44; A. S. <i>sceât;</i> Engl. <i>sheet;</i> O. H. G. <i>skoza;</i> Germ. <i>schoss;</i> Dan. <i>sköd</i>]:—<i>the sheet,</i> i. e. <i>the corner</i> of a square cloth or other object; hann sá niðr síga dúk mikinn af himni með fjórum skautum, 656 C. 8 (Acts xi. 5); hann var borinn í fjórum skautum til búðar, Glúm. 395, Fbr. 95 new Ed.; var hann fluttr heim í fjórum skautum, Vígl. 24; feldr fimm álna í skaut, <i>a cloak of five ells square,</i> Korm. 86: of the heaven, þeir görðu þar af himinn ok settu hann yfir jörðina með fjórum skautum, <i>with four ‘sheets,’</i> i. e. <i>corners</i> (east, west, north, south), Edda; whence himin-skaut, <i>the airts, four quarters of the heavens;</i> or heims-skaut, <i>the poles,</i> norðr-skaut or norðr-heims-skaut, <i>the north pole;</i> jarðar-skaut, <i>the earth’s corner, outskirt of the earth,</i> Edda (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skaut-bjorn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skaut-björn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>skaut-hreinn,</strong> m. <i>the ‘tack-bear,’ a ship,</i> Edda.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
