          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skauta-sigling
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>square rigging,</i> in western Icel.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skauti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skauti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a kercbief</i> used as a purse by knitting all four corners together so as to make a bag (see knýti-skauti), Háv. 43, Bs. i. 337, 340.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ska"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ská
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. [cp. Dan. <i>skraa;</i> Germ. <i>schräge</i>], <i>askew, askance;</i> and á ská, <i>id</i>.; hence <strong>ská-hallr,</strong> adj. <i>sloping.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>askew,</i> Lat. <i>obliquus;</i> á skáðum veg til suðrs, Sks. 50 new Ed., for 427; see skjáðr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skai"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skái
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>relief,</i> of pain; ok þótti henni nekkverr skái verða á hverju dægri á sínum mætti, Bs. i. 352; varð engi skái á hans meini, 336; var fyrst með ská (= skáa acc.), <i>it was at first with some relief,</i> Þiðr. 248; cp. skána, skárri.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skak-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skák
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [of Persian origin], <i>chess,</i> Vm. 177; tefla skák, Gsp.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skak-bord"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skák-borð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a chess-board.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skak-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skák-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a chess-man,</i> Skíða R. 164: <i>a chess-player.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skaka-3"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to check.</i> Fms. iv. 366, v. l. (skekði, Ó. H. l. c.), freq. in mod. usage:—the metaph. phrase, skáka í því skjóli, <i>to check one in that shelter,</i> i. e. <i>to take advantage of (unduly).</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skal"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skál
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., pl. skálir and skálar, Vkv. 24, 35 (Bugge), and so in mod. usage; [Germ. <i>schale;</i> Dan.-Swed. <i>skål</i>]:—<i>a bowl;</i> skál fulla vatns, Stj. 392; skál full mjaðar, Fms. vi. 52; þær skálir er Þórr var vanr at drekka, Edda 57.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skal-hus"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skál-hús
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. = skáli, 655 xxx. 9.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skala-glam"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skála-glam
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a nickname, see Jómsv. S. ch. 42; whence <strong>Skál-eyjar,</strong> Landn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skala-mark"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skála-mark
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>-merki,</strong> n. <i>the sign Libra,</i> Rb.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skala-pund"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skála-pund
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a weight,</i> Dan. <i>skaal-pund,</i> Rétt.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skala-veginn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skála-veginn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>weighed in scales,</i> D. N.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., pl. skáld; the word is in poetry rhymed as skald (with a short vowel), sk<i>al</i>d and k<i>al</i>da, <i>al</i>dri and sk<i>al</i>di, Kormak, and so on; but the plural is always spelt skáld, not sköld; the mod. Dan. <i>skjald</i> is borrowed from the Icel.: [the etymology and origin of this word is contested; Prof. Bergmann, in Message de Skirnir, Strasburg, 1871, p. 54, derives it from the Slavonic <i>skladi</i> = <i>composition, skladacz</i> = <i>compositeur;</i> but the earliest usages point to a Teutonic and a different root. In the ancient law skáldskapr meant <i>a libel in verse,</i> and was synonymous with flimt, danz, níð, q. v.; the compds skáld-fífl, leir-skáld (q. v.) also point to the bad sense as the original one, which is still noticeable in popular Icel. usages and phrases such as skálda (the verb), skáldi, skældinn (<i>libellous</i>), see also skáldmær below. On the other hand, skálda, Germ. <i>schalte,</i> means <i>a pole</i> (sec skálda, skáld-stöng below); libels and imprecations were in the ancient heathen age scratched on poles, see the remarks s. v. níð, níðstöng. The word is therefore, we believe, to be traced back to the old libel-pole, ‘scald-pole;’ if so, Engl. <i>scold</i> = <i>to abuse,</i> Germ. <i>schelten,</i> may be kindred words; the old Lat. phrase (of Mart. Capella) <i>barbara fraxineis sculpatur runa tabellis</i> may even refer to this scratching of imprecations on pieces of wood.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-eik"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-eik
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [Germ. <i>schalt-eiche</i>], <i>the holm-oak, ilex,</i> Þd. (the MS. has skal-eik).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-fe"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-fé
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a ‘skald-fee’ reward for a poem,</i> Ad.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-fifl"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-fífl
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a poetaster</i> (perh. originally <i>a libeller</i>), Edda 49.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-kona"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-kona
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a ‘skald-quean,’ a poetess,</i> a nickname of a woman, for which the reason given is this; hann átti Þórhildi skáldkonu, ‘hón var orðgífr mikit ok fór með flimtan,’ <i>she was a ‘word-witch,’ and made libels,</i> Nj. 49.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (<strong>-liga,</strong> adv.), <i>poetical,</i> Fms. ii. 50.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a poet;</i> skáldmenn miklir, Ísl. ii. 191.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-maer"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-mær
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>a ‘skald-maid,’ poetess,</i> a nickname of the poetess Jórunn, Fms. i. 13; the name of her poem Sendi-bít looks as if it had been of a ‘biting’ libellous kind.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-pipa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-pípa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a ‘skald-pipe,’ a flute</i> (?), Clar. 135.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-skapr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-skapr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>‘scaldship,’ poetry:</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skald-stong"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáld-stöng
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a ‘libel-pole,’ a pole with imprecations</i> or <i>charms scratched on it;</i> ef maðr reisir stöng ok kallar s., þá hefir hann fyrir-gört hverjum penningi fjár síns, N. G. L. i. 430.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> u, f. [O. H. G. <i>scalta</i>; mid. H. G. <i>schalte</i>], <i>a pole</i> or <i>staff,</i> whence <i>a flute, pipe;</i> skálda með tönn, <i>a flute made of walrus tusk,</i> D. N. iv. 359.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalda-gemlur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálda-gemlur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl., see Ísl. Þjóðs. ii. 557.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalda-spillir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálda-spillir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>‘skald-spoiler,’</i> the nickname of the poet Eyvind; the name was, we believe, a bye-word, <i>a ‘poetaster,’ ‘plagiarist;’</i> we believe that this nickname was given to this poet because two of his chief poems were modelled after other works of contemporary poets, the Háleygja-tal after the Ynglinga-tal, and the Hákonar-mál after the Eiríks-mál; (as to the latter poem this is even expressly stated in Fagrsk. 22); the word would thus be the same as íll-skælda, a word applied to a poet for having borrowed the refrain of his poem, Fms. iii. 65.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalda-tal"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálda-tal
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a List of Poets,</i> a short treatise affixed to. the Cod. Ups. of the Edda and the Cod. Acad. primus of the Heimskringla.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skaldi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáldi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a poetaster,</i> a nickname given in Icel. to vagrant, extemporising verse-makers; thus in this century Páll skáldi (a vagrant priest and verse-maker); and in the 16th century Bjarni skáldi; the word is never applied to really good poets.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalgi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálgi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a fish</i> of the carp kind (?), Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skali"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [cp. Scot. <i>shieling;</i> Ivar Aasen <i>skaale</i> = <i>shieling</i>]:—prop. <i>a hut, shed,</i> put up for temporary use; this is the earliest Norse sense, and it is still so used in Norway; þar sér enn skála-tópt þeirra ok svá hrófit, Landn. 30; skála vist at Rauðabjörgum, of a fisherman’s hut, Vm. 147; skála búi, <i>a hut dweller</i> = <i>a robber,</i> Fs.; hence, leik-skálar, <i>play-shielings,</i> put up when people assembled for sports; gufu-skálar, <i>‘steam-shieling’</i> a local name, of bathing-sheds (?), Landn.; fiski-skálar, <i>fishing shielings;</i> it also remains in local names as <strong>Skála-holt. II.</strong> <i>a hall</i> (höll is only used of the king’s hall), see Orkn. ch. 18, 70, 115, Gísl. 29, Dropl. 18, 28, Fms. i. 288–292, Korm. 58, Bs. i. 41, Fbr. ch. 13 new Ed, Nj. ch. 78, Gunnl. S. ch. 11; in Landn. 1. ch. 2, 2. ch. 13, the skáli is a detached building; drykkju-s., <i>a drinking hall;</i> svefn-s., <i>a sleeping hall.</i> In Grág. i. 459 distinction is made between eldhús and skáli; in the Sturl. skáli is distinguished from stofa; and it seems that the men were seated in the former, the women in the latter. At still later times, and so at present, the skáli is an apartment near the entrance, a kind of for-skáli, q. v.; til þess er sér mann ór skála-dyrum ór fjöru í Nesdal, Vm. 87.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalk-heidr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálk-heiðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>mockery</i>, Stj. 63, 122, 127, 241, 263.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Ulf. <i>skalks</i> = δουλος, <i>skalkinon</i> = δουλεύειν, <i>skalkinassus</i> = δουλεία; A. S. <i>scealc;</i> Germ. <i>schalk</i>; the word remains in <i>siniscalc, seneschal; mariscalc, mar-shall</i> = <i>a horse-groom</i>]:—prop. <i>a ‘slave,’ ‘servant;’</i> skálka þeirra er skjöld bera, Fas. i. (in a verse); but that sense is else lost.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalm"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálm
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a short sword,</i> Hom. 14, Gkv. 2. 19, Fas. ii. 229, Ld. 214, Hkr. iii. 150, Fb. i. 259, ii. 138, Fas. i. 56 sqq., Fms. vi. 402, Grett. 140, Band, (in a verse); ryð-skálm.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalm-old"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálm-öld
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the ‘sword-age,’</i> Vsp. 46; at margir góðir menn mundu verða drepnir í s. þeirri, Clem. 28.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalma"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to stride with long paces,</i> Hallfred (Fs. 106, where reflex.): freq. in mod. usage, hann gékk burt og skálmaði stórum, Od. xi. 539.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalp"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálp
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., qs. skvalp, mod. skolp, prop. <i>scullery-water, wash.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalp-grani"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálp-grani
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Dan. <i>grön-skolding</i>], <i>a greenhorn,</i> Fms. ii. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalp-haena"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálp-hæna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. the name of a bird (?), <i>a hen; the scaup-duck, anas marila,</i> see Bewick.; a nickname, Landn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skalpr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skálpr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a leather sheath;</i> varð laust sverðit, Sigurðr héit um skálpinn, Sturl. iii. 163; þeir átu skálpana af sverðum sínum, Fms. viii. 436; drag sverðit ór skálpinum, Karl. 72; skálp-hús, in a pun, Krók.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skán
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a thin membrane, film;</i> hann laust hann með líkþrá, svá at ein skán var alt af hvirfli ofan ok niðr á tær, Hom. (St.); myki-skán, <i>a cake of cow-dung,</i> Þorf. Karl. 430.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skana"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skána
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [skái], <i>to get better,</i> of illness and the weather; mér er farið að skána, and veðrið er farið að skána.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skani"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skáni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>Skáney,</strong> f.; the gen. Skáneyjar occurs as early as in a poet of the 10th century, the syllable <i>-ey</i> answering to the Latinised <i>-avia</i>:—<i>Scania,</i> a local name, <i>the Scandia</i> or <i>Scandinavia</i> of Pliny and succeeding geographers, mod. Dan. <i>Skaane;</i> from the Saga time downwards the name of a county formerly belonging to Denmark, but since 1658 to Sweden; it is said to mean <i>border-land,</i> and may be akin to skán. Skáni forms the southernmost point of the great northern peninsula, and was accordingly the first district in the peninsula known to the Romans, whence in Latin writers it became the general name for the whole of the north; but not so in Icel. vernacular writers, who use it only in its proper sense of the county Skáni, Fms., Fb. passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skanungar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skánungar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. <i>the men</i> of Skáni, Fms.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skapr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skápr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a case</i> or <i>drawer with shelves;</i> klæða s., <i>a clothes-drawer;</i> boka-s., <i>a book-case;</i> matar-s., <i>a pantry.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skar-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skár
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [ská, skátt; cp. Ulf. <i>us-skaws,</i> 1 Thess. v. 8, and <i>us-skawjan</i> = ἀνανήφειν; whence A. S. <i>sceawjan;</i> Germ. <i>schauen</i>]:—<i>open;</i> only used in the compds opin-skár, <i>made public;</i> her-skár, <i>open to inroads,</i> of a country, see herr (p. 259).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skari-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skári
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> or <strong>skárri,</strong> a compar., superl. skástr, with no corresponding positive, [skái]:—<i>better, best;</i> þat mun þér ráð skást, <i>it will be most advisable for thee,</i> Fas. i. 421.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ske-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ske-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "see skímaðr, Fb. i. 448 (see skí).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skedja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeðja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. skeðr; pret. skaddi; the subj. skeddi does not occur; part. skaddr, skatt; [see skaða]:—<i>to scathe, hurt,</i> with acc.; skeðja líkami þeirra, H. E. ii. 68; ok vilda ek aldri skeðja, Fas. i. 209; ef maðr skeðr þar jörð, Grág. ii. 229; s. þá jörðu, 216; eigi á þá jörðu at s. (<i>to violate</i>) til þess at grafa lík, K. Þ. K. 22; þær þora ekki mýss skeðja, Pr. 474.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skefill"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skefill
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [skafa], <i>a scratcher;</i> eyrna-skefill, <i>an ear-picker.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skefjar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skefjar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>a sheath</i> (?); only used in the phrase, hafa sig í skefjum, <i>to restrain oneself.</i> <strong>skefju-maðr,</strong> m. <i>a wary person, one who restrains himself,</i> Grett. (Ub.) 95.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skefjur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skefjur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>scrapes, rough handling;</i> (ungar) svá, styrknaðir at þeir megi skefjur þola, Post. 636.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skefla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skefla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, [skafl], <i>to be drifted together, massed,</i> of snow; það skeflir yfir það, <i>it was covered with snow:</i> of the waves, haflauðr (acc.) skeflir, Edda (Ht.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Engl. <i>shaggy</i> is akin, but in the sense of <i>the beard</i> the word is peculiar to the Scandin. languages, which use barð (q. v.) in a different sense; Dan. <i>skæg;</i> Swed. <i>skägg</i>]:—<i>a beard,</i> prop. originally = <i>shagginess,</i> Þkv. 1, Rm. 15; honum óx eigi skegg, Nj. 30, Fms. ii. 59; stutt skegg ok snöggvan kaup, … jaðar-skegg, Sks. 288; kanpa ok skegg, K. Þ. K.; hón sér undir skegg Hagbarði, Korm. 12: phrases, Úlfarr vatt við skegginu, Eb. 164; skríða undir skegg e-m, <i>to hide behind another’s beard,</i> Fs. 31; konu skegg, <i>a woman’s beard,</i> Germ. <i>Kaisers-bart,</i> cp. Edda 19; höggva skeggi niðr, <i>to bite the dust,</i> Fms. xi. (in a verse); meðan upp heldr skeggi, <i>as long as we can stand upright,</i> Orkn. (in a verse); höggvask til skeggjum, <i>to put beards together,</i> Grett. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-barn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-barn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a ‘beard-bairn,’ bearded baby,</i> a name given to a man by a giant, Fas. ii. 517.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-broddr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-broddr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>bristles of the beard;</i> þeyta skeggbroddana, Fb. i. 296 (the skeggröddina and skeggraustina, Fms. i. 303, is prob. only a false reading for skeggbroddana).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-brusi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-brúsi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>an earthen jug.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-hvitr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-hvítr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>white-bearded,</i> Karl. 416.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-karl"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-karl
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = skeggbrúsi; skyldir erum við skeggkarl tveir, Hallgr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>beardless,</i> Nj. 52, Landn. 283.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-madr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-maðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a bearded man,</i> Fas. i. 150.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-sidr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-síðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>long-bearded,</i> Þiðr. 18.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-stadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-staðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., mod.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-staedi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-stæði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the bearded part of the face,</i> Fb. i. 530, Fas. ii. 256.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegg-ox"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegg-öx
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. = skeggja or barða, Sks. 388, Eg. 189.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeggi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeggi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m., pl. skeggjar, in the compds, eyjar-skeggjar, <i>‘island-shaggies,’</i> i. e. <i>islanders,</i> freq. in the Sagas, prob. originally a sort of soubriquet, owing to the notion that islanders were more rough and wild in their habits than other men; the word is particularly used of the Faroe islanders, Fær., Ó. H.: cp. Götu-skeggjar, the name of a family from Gata in Faroe; Mostrar-skeggr, the nickname of Thorolf of Moster, an island in Norway, Eb., Landn.; cp. hraun-skeggi, <i>the man of the wilderness,</i> Fs.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeggja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeggja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. a kind of <i>halberd,</i> also called barða (q. v.), Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeggjadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeggjaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>bearded,</i> Greg. 74, Fb. i. 134; ú-skeggjaðr, <i>beardless,</i> Sighvat.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skegglingr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skegglingr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a kind of <i>bird</i>, Engl. <i>shag</i> or <i>green cormorant</i> (?), Edda (Gl.); mod. <strong>skeggla.</strong>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeid"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeið
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> f., pl. skeiðr, Fb. i. 532. l. 1, ii. 42. l. 4, Fms. iv. 135, vi. 78, x. 54 (in a verse); the form skeiðar (see Lex. Poët.) seems to be erroneous: [akin to skíð and skeið, n.]:—a kind of <i>swift-sailing ship of war</i> of the class langskip, but distinguished from dreki, freq. in the Sagas; Erlingr átti skeið mikla, hón var tvau rúm ok þrjátigi, Fms. iii. 41, Ó. H. passim, cp. Fms. i. 46, vi. 308; tuttugu langskip, tvær skeiðr ok tvá knörru, v. 169, cp. snekkja.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeid-brimir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeið-brímir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. the name of a mythical steed, Edda.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeid-gata"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeið-gata
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a broad causeway</i> (to ride on), Ísl. ii. 339.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeid-hestr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeið-hestr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a race-horse,</i> also of a horse that ambles (skeið II).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeid-kollr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeið-kollr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a nickname, Sturl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeid-reitt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeið-reitt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. part. <i>a broad way for riding;</i> þá var allt s., Sturl. iii. 23.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeida"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeiða
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [skeiðir], <i>to sheath</i> a sword, knife, Fas. i. 460.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeidir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeiðir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. [Engl. <i>sheath;</i> Dan. <i>skæde;</i> Germ. <i>scheide</i>]:—<i>a sheath;</i> ná knífi ór skeiðum, Bs. i. 385; taka kníf ór skeiðum, 229, Háv. 49 new Ed.; mér sýnisk sem réttindin skríði nú í skeiðir, Róm. 116.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeif-hoggr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeif-höggr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>cutting askew, using a hammer</i> or <i>axe awkwardly.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeif-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeif-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>askew, awry, wrong,</i> D. N. iii. 153: <strong>skeif-liga,</strong> adv., Karl. 478.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeifa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeifa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [skeifr], <i>a horse-shoe,</i> Þiðr. 105; hálf-s., <i>a broken horse-shoe;</i> skafla-s., <i>a sharp-shoe:</i> metaph., það er skeifu-mynd á e-u, <i>it is in the shape of a s., it is crooked, askew, goes wrong,</i> Sturl. ii. 93 (in a verse); mod., það er skeifu-lag á því: as a nickname, Sturl. ii. 120: skeifa is rare in old writers, but is the common word in mod. Icel. use; the ancients said skór, <i>a shoe.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeifr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeifr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [Engl. <i>skew;</i> Germ. <i>schief;</i> Dan. <i>skjæv</i>]:—<i>askew, oblique;</i> ör Jonate fló aldri vint né skeift, Stj. 495; koma skeift við, <i>to go crookedly,</i> Bret. 174: of the feet, skeifum fæti, Fms. vi. (in a verse); inn-skeifr = Lat. <i>varus;</i> út-s. = Lat. <i>valgus:</i> skeifr, a nickname, Orkn.; Fjöru-skeifr, a nickname, Fms.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeika"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeika
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [Dan. <i>skeje;</i> Swed. <i>skeka</i>], <i>to go askew, swerve, deviate;</i> hann stýrði svá at landi at aldri skeikaði, Bs. i. 326; þar skeikaði mjök stjórnin, 726: the phrase, láta skeika at sköpuðu (see skapa), Fms. ii. 112, Eg. 90, Ó. H. 146, Gg. 4: with prep., skeika af, <i>to swerve from;</i> af trúnni svá aldri skeiki, a hymn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeina"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeina
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> u, f. <i>a scratch, slight wound;</i> kalla ek þetta skeinu en ekki sár, Nj. 205, Háv. 50, Fms. ix. 497, Róm. 239; var skeinan saman hlaupin, Grett. 152.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeina-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeina
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, [provinc. Swed. <i>skeina</i> = <i>to cut with a scythe</i>], <i>to scratch, wound slightly;</i> hefir þú skeint þik? Ó. H. 72; ef maðr höggr til manns ok skeinir klæði hans, N. G. L. i. 164; nú hyggr hann at, hvar hann væri skeindr, Rd. 240.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeini"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeini
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [skæni, skán], <i>folium tergendi.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/skeini-samt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          skeini-samt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. adj.: verðr honum þá skeinisamt, <i>he was then much exposed to being wounded,</i> Eb. 190; varð þeim þat s., 214.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
