        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/smeittr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          smeittr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. [for. word, qs. smelt, q. v.], <i>enamelled;</i> s. söðull, Ld. 274; s. hjálmr, skjöldr, bitull, El., Flóv., Karl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/smekkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          smekkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [see smakka; from Germ. <i>ge-smack;</i> Dan. <i>smag</i>]:—<i>taste;</i> a mod. word, as also deriv. <strong>smekk-laus,</strong> <i>tasteless;</i> <strong>smekk-ligr,</strong> <i>tasteful</i>:—the ancients seem to have had no exact word for Lat. <i>gustus,</i> for even bragð (IV) is not found in old writers; the Germ. has <i>kosten,</i> which answers to Lat. <i>gustare,</i> but the Norse kosta (q. v.) is never used in that sense.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/smella"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          smella
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, a causal to the preceding, <i>to make to crack,</i> with dat.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/smella-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          smella
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "smell, pret. small, defect.; [Swed. <i>smälla;</i> Ivar Aasen <i>smella;</i> Dan. <i>smælde</i>]:—<i>to smack, crack,</i> as a whip; the word is freq. in mod. usage, but not found in old writers.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/smellr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
