        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Ulf. <i>stiurs;</i> A. S. <i>steôr, stirc;</i> Engl. <i>steer</i>; North. E. and Scot. <i>stirk;</i> Germ. <i>stier</i>]:—<i>a steer, stirk, young bull,</i> an obsolete word, which seems to occur in Edda i. 460 (in a verse), unless the true reading be stjórnviðjar, q. v. The word may be preserved in such local names as <strong>Stjóra-dalr,</strong> and prob. in the dimin. Sturla, q. v. (qs. stjuri-la).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/stjup"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          stjúp-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "in later, esp. Norse, MSS. the form is deteriorated into <strong>stýp-,</strong> N. G. L. i. 170; thence into <strong>stýf-,</strong> 392; and, lastly, the <i>f</i> is changed into <i>g</i> or <i>k,</i> <strong>stjúg-,</strong> 405, <strong>stjúk-,</strong> D. N.: [A. S. <i>steôp-;</i> Engl. <i>step-;</i> Germ. <i>stief-;</i> Dan. <i>stiv-;</i> Swed. <i>styf-:</i> the mod. Dan. <i>sted-</i> is a corruption of quite modern date; the original sense of stjúp (= <i>bereft, orphan</i>) is preserved in the A. S. verb <i>steôpan.</i>]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
