          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [Ulf. <i>swêrs</i> = ἔντιμος; A. S. <i>swær;</i> Scot. <i>sweir</i> (= <i>heavy</i>); Germ. <i>schwer</i>]:—<i>heavy, grave;</i> sváran súsbreka, Skm. 29; síns ins svára sefa, <i>for her strong affection,</i> Hm. 106; svárra sára, Gh. 11; svárt ok dátt, Skv. 3. 26; at svárra fari (compar.), Kormak: sváran, as adv. <i>sorely,</i> sló sváran sínar hendr (thus to be emended, svárar Cod.), <i>she wrung her hands so sore,</i> Skv. 3. 25, 29. The word is poët. and obsolete, and not used in prose, either ancient or modern; the mod. Dan. <i>swær</i> is borrowed from the Germ.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/svas-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          svás-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>lovely, delightful;</i> af hans nafni er þat svásligt kallat er blítt er, Edda 13.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
