          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sælingr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a wealthy man</i> (cp. Gr. ὄλβιος), Edda (Gl.), Eb. (in a verse); sælingr, opp. to úgöfgir menn, Hom. (St.): a nickname, Landn.; whence <strong>Sælings-dalr,</strong> a local name.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/saell"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sæll
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [sæl, sælt], compar. sælli, sælstr (mod. sælli, but sælastr); [A. S. <i>sæl;</i> Old Engl. <i>seely;</i> Engl. <i>silly;</i> Germ. <i>selig;</i> Dan. <i>sæl, salig;</i> cp. the double use of Gr. εὐήθης; Engl. <i>simple</i>]:—<i>blest, happy;</i> hann þóttisk sæll ef þeir skyldi dæma mál hans, Ölk. 35; þrællinn mælti, at hann þættisk sæll ef Otkell ætti hann, Nj. 73; hann görði hana svá sæla sem þá at hón væri sælust, Sd. 187 (paper MS.); eru þeir því sælli, sem …, Gþl. 173.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/saelund"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sælund
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "better <strong>Selund</strong> (q. v.), rhymed S<i>il</i>unz k<i>il</i>ir, Ó. H. (in a verse), f.; the gender varies between fem. and neut., gen. Selundar, Hkr. i. 132; but Selundz, Fms. i. 27, l. c.; Selund, Skáney, Gautland, x. 381; heima á Selund, ríkit á Selund, 366; af Selundi, 371:—the old name of <i>Zealand</i>; þar setti Gefjun landit ok gaf nafn ok kallaði Selund, Edda 1, Fms., Fas., Lex. Poët.; svals Silunz, Ó. H. (in a verse of A. D. 1027): dat. Selundi, Fms. i. 115, but Selund, v. l.; af Selundi, x. 371. The word is said to be derived not from Sæ-lund (i. e. <i>Sea-grove</i>), but from the root <i>sal-,</i> the <i>und</i> being inflexive, cp. ‘Insula Oceani,’ Tacit. Germ. ch. 40, which is not improbably a kind of translation of Selund, cp. Prof. Munch’s remarks on this name.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/saem-leitr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sæm-leitr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>fine to look at;</i> s. sólar-geisli, Gh. 15.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/saema"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          sæma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(i. e. <strong>sœma</strong>), d, [sama, sóma], <i>to honour;</i> ef hann vildi sæma (<i>endow, grant</i>) hann í nökkuru léni, Fms. vi. 52; þeirra sætta er vér sém vel sæmdir af í alla staði, Nj. 176; rituðu þá sér hverir þat sem eigi vildu sæma né játa, Bs. i. 718.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
