            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjald-toturr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjald-töturr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>worn hangings,</i> Pm. 36.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjald-vidir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjald-viðir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. <i>the wooden frame of a tent,</i> K. Þ. K. 90, Stj. 321.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjalda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjalda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to pitch a tent,</i> Fms. vi. 181, v. 286, Hkr. iii. 286: on ships, þat var annarr siðr þeirra at tjalda aldri á skipum, Fas. ii. 37; þeir lögðu skip sitt til hafnar, en er þeir höfðu tjaldat ok um búizk, Eg. 37; þeir sá þar fyrir bænum fljóta langskip tjaldat, 88, Hkr. ii. 43; er þeir höfðu tjaldat ok fest skip sitt, Fms. vii. 314; þeir höfðu tjaldat yfir skipi sínu, Eg. 121: vagn tjaldaðan, <i>a tilted</i> or <i>covered wagon,</i> Hkr. i. 70; tjalda klæðum of kistu, Bs. i. In places of annual popular meetings such as the Icel. Alþing, each priest or man of mark had his own búð, viz. four roofless walls, which remained open; and when parliament met, he threw a tent over his booth as a roof, dressing it out as a room with hangings and benches; this was called ‘tjalda búð,’ see Grág. i. 186, and Nj. passim, Ó. H. ch. 133 (for the Faroe), and Mr. Dasent’s Burnt Njal.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjalda-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjalda-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. id., Hkr. i. 108.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjalda-slitr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjalda-slitr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>worn hangings,</i> Dipl. v. 18, Pm. 23, 27.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjaldan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjaldan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the pitching a tent,</i> N. G. L. ii. 256.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjaldari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjaldari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [tjaldr; O. H. G. <i>zeltari</i> and <i>zeltian</i>], <i>a racer, race-horse,</i> Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjaldr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjaldr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a bird, <i>an oyster-catcher</i> or <i>sea-pie, hæmatopus ostralegus</i> L., Edda (Gl.), and mod. usage, (Dan. <i>tjald</i>); so called prob. from its long legs, like tent-spars.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjalds-nagli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjalds-nagli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a tent-peg,</i> Fas. ii. 262: also of <i>the pegs to which hangings are fastened,</i> Sturl. iii. 146.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjalds-rum"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjalds-rúm
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a lodging in a tent,</i> Grág. ii. 55.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjalds-tronur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjalds-trönur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>a platform on which to pitch a tent,</i> Sturl. i. 147.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjara"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjara
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [A. S. <i>tearo;</i> Engl. <i>tar;</i> Dan. <i>tjere</i>], <i>tar,</i> Grág. ii. 404, Gþl. 43, Sks. 425, Fas. i. 18; bera tjöru í höfuð sér, Nj. 181, Fms. i. 127; svart sem t., <i>black as tar,</i> Band. 15; tjöru-pinnr, <i>a tar-pin,</i> Sturl. iii. 189; tjöru-skinn, <i>a tarred skin,</i> a nickname, Sturl. i. 112, 155 (a kind of <i>waxen cloth</i>?); tjöru-spann, N. G. L. i. 198; tjöru-tjörn, <i>the tar-tarn</i> = Lat. <i>lacus asphalti,</i> Stj. 73; tjöru-tunna, <i>a tar-barrel,</i> Vm. 62: the law phrase, torfs maðr ok tjöru, a sort of running the gauntlet, cp. the Engl. ‘tarring and feathering,’ NG.L. i. 253, 334 (§ 168). <strong>tjöru-virki,</strong> n. <i>tar-works, where tar is made;</i> sætr, smiðju, tjöru-virki, veiðibúðir eða andvirki, N. G. L. ii. 145.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjarga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjarga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to tar:</i> in part. <strong>tjargaðr,</strong> <i>tarred,</i> Rekst. 4.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjasna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjasna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [akin to Engl. <i>tassel</i>?], an old obscure word; <i>the pegs</i> by which lists for battle were marked off were called ‘tjösnur,’ for the description see Korm. 86.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjá
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "qs. téa; the pres. varies between several forms, tér, tjár, tjáir; pret. tjáði; imperat. té; part. téðr (analogous to sjá); tjá is a contracted form from an older <strong>tega,</strong> which only remains in the pres. reflex. tegaz, tegumk, in four instances, (see B. III): [Ulf. <i>teihan</i> = ἐπαγγέλλειν; Hel. <i>tihan;</i> O. H. G. <i>zihan;</i> Germ. <i>zeigen</i> or <i>zeihen;</i> cp. Engl. <i>teach</i>; A. S. <i>tæcan;</i> Lat. <i>dicere, in-dicare;</i> Gr. δεικνύναι; cognate or derivative is Goth. <i>taiknjan</i> = δεικνύναι, whence tákn, teikn, Engl. <i>token</i>, and so on.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjalgr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjálgr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [A. S. <i>telgor</i> = <i>a branch, bough;</i> Gr. δολιχός; Let. <i>dilgas</i>]:—<i>a prong, fork</i> (?), an obsolete word, which occurs only twice, viz. handar-tjálgr, <i>‘hand-prongs’</i> i. e. <i>the arms</i> or <i>the fingers</i> (?), Sighvat; uxu tjálgur, langir leggir ok ljótt höfuð, Fas. iii. 18 (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjogu"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjogu
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "prop. an acc. from tjogr, = togr, tigr; [Swed. <i>tiogo</i>; Dan. <i>tyve;</i> Early Dan. <i>tjuge;</i> Norwegian <i>kjogo</i>]:—<i>twenty,</i> Sighvat, Ó. H. 233 (in a verse); else not used in Icel. except in the compd tut-tugu; but in full use in Swed. as well as in Dan.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjossi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjossi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a he-goat</i> (?), Merl. 2. 75.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjodr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjóðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Engl. <i>tether;</i> Ivar Aasen <i>tjor</i>], <i>a tether,</i> N. G. L. i. 390; hestr í tjóðri, 46, passim. <strong>tjóðr-hestr, -kýr,</strong> <i>a tethered horse</i> or <i>cow,</i> Gþl. 388.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjodra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjóðra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to tether,</i> Vm. 14, D. N. v. 518, passim in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjon"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjón
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., the gender varies:",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjuga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjúga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [Dan. <i>hö-tyv;</i> Swed. <i>tjuga;</i> from the obsolete verb tjúga]:—<i>a pitch-fork,</i> prop. <i>a ‘drawer;’</i> hey-tjúga, <i>a hay-fork;</i> rann verkþræll á árbakkann, ok skaut hey-tjúgu í lið þeirra, Hkr. i. 25: a nickname, Sturl. ii. 160. <strong>tjúgu-skegg,</strong> n. <i>fork-beard,</i> a nickname of the famous Danish king Swein, the conqueror of England, Fms. This word is quite obsolete in Icel., but in full use in Swed. and Dan.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjuga-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjúga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "taug, tugu, toginn; an ancient obsolete verb; [Ulf. <i>tiúhan,</i> = ἄγειν. όδηγειν; O. H. G. <i>ziuhan;</i> Germ. <i>ziehen;</i> cp. Lat. <i>ducere</i>—is in the Icel. and Norse only preserved in the part. toginn]:—<i>to draw;</i> enn togni hjörr, <i>a drawn sword,</i> Merl. 2. 66; með sverð um togin, Hkm. 9; tognum sverðum (Germ. <i>ge-zogenes schwert</i>), Darr.; toginn skjómi, Vellekla; cp. the derivatives toga, teygja, as also in tjúga.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjugari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjúgari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m., prop. <i>a pitch-fork;</i> hence poët. tungls tjúgari, <i>the pitch-forker of the moon,</i> who forks the moon out of heaven, Vsp.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjustr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjústr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [Dan. <i>tyst</i>], Fms. ix. 510, v. l.; see tvistr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjorgadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjörgaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>tarred,</i> Fms. i. 128.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjorn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjörn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [North. E. and Scot. <i>tarn</i>], gen. tjarnar, pl. tjarnir, <i>a tarn, small lake;</i> tjörn ein, Fær. 46, Rb. 352, Stj. 75, 268; þeir leika knatt-leika á tjörn þeirri er Sef-tjörn heitir (viz. on the ice), Gísl. 26 (cp. leikpallr íss á vötnum varð | í vetrinn þannig hjuggu skarð, Bb.), cp. Vígl. S. ch. 13 new Ed., very freq.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjorugr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjörugr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>tarred;</i> tjörgum árum, Hornklofi, (but in mod. usage uncontr. throughout.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjorvi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjörvi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. a pr. name, prop. <i>a charmer, wizard</i> (?), akin, by way of metathesis, to Tyrfingr, q. v.; as also taufr; the later and common form is <strong>Torfi,</strong> Landn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjosnu-blot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjösnu-blót
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. a kind of <i>sacrifice</i> or <i>rite</i> to be performed at a wager of battle; með þeim formála sem síðan er eptir hafðr í blóti því er kallat er tjösnu-blót, Korm. l. c.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tjosull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tjösull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [cp. A. S. <i>tæsel;</i> Engl. <i>teasle; Lzt. dipsacus fullonum;</i> perh. from the herb being used for charms]:—<i>a magical character,</i> Skm. 29; cp. Swed. <i>tjusa, fortjusa,</i> = <i>to charm, spell-bind.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/todda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          todda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. a nickname, Dropl. 9.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/toddi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          toddi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [an almost obsolete word in Icel., but preserved in Engl. <i>tod</i>, a weight of wool = 28 lbs.; <i>a tod</i> is also = <i>a bushel;</i> in Jamieson <i>toddie</i> is a bit of cake; Germ. <i>zotte</i> answers in form to the Norse <i>toddi</i>]:—<i>a tod</i> of wool; toddu gefn, <i>the fairy of the tod,</i> i. e. <i>a woman,</i> Bjarn. (in a verse): <i>a bit</i>, in vinjar-toddi, q. v.; þá eru tveir um toddann, <i>than two go on each piece,</i> cp. Maurer’s Volks. 306; hón gaf aldregi minna enn stóra todda þá hón skyldi fátækum gefa, Dropl. (viz. the large apocryphal Saga).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tog"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tog
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a ‘tow,’ rope, line;</i> flota ok tog í bæði lönd, Gþl. 410; hafi sá varp er fyrr renndi togum sínum, of an angler’s line, 426; akkeri með digru togi, Gsp.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tog-drapa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          tog-drápa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a</i> drápa <i>composed in a special metre,</i> called toglag, for specimen see Edda (Ht. 68–70), and the fragments in Ó. H.; togdrápu-háttr, -lag, <i>the metre of a</i> togdrápa, Edda (Ht.), 137, 138.",
