          className="link"
          href="/word/tyna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          týna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, [tjón; Scot. <i>to tyne</i>], <i>to lose;</i> þeir týndu hestunum, Nj. 21; þeir týndu þar öxi sinni, Landn. 312; týna honum. Fms. vi. 121; týna lífi sínu, Str. 86; t. þeim þremr hlutum, er …, Fms. x. 338; þér skolut öngu fyrir týna nema lífinu, Nj. 7; with acc. a Latinism, Mar.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tyni-samligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          týni-samligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>destructive,</i> Anecd. 34.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tyning"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          týning
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>destruction,</i> Art.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tyr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          týr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. Týs, acc. dat. Tý; the form tívar, see tívi, may even be regarded as an irreg. plur. to tý-r; cp. <i>Twisco,</i> qs. <i>Tivisco,</i> in Tacit. Germ.; [for the identity of this word with Sansk. <i>dyaus, dîvas</i> = <i>heaven,</i> Gr. Ζεύς, Διός, Lat. <i>divus,</i> O. H. G. <i>Ziw,</i> see Max Müller’s Lectures on Science of Language, 2nd Series, p. 425]:—prop. the generic name of <i>the highest divinity,</i> which remains in compds, as Farma-týr, hanga-týr: as also in <strong>Týs-áttungr,</strong> <i>the offspring of gods</i> (Gr. διο-γενής), Ýt.: <strong>tý-framr,</strong> adj., Haustl. 1: <strong>tý-hraustr,</strong> <i>valiant as a god:</i> <strong>tý-spakr,</strong> <i>godly-wise,</i> Edda 16.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tyr-eygdr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          týr-eygðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>with peering eyes.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tyra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          týra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> ð, <i>to flame faintly;</i> cp. tóra.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tyta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
