      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/una"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          una
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. uni; pret. unði, later undi; subj. ynði; imperat. uni, Glúm. 354, Fas. i. 146, Eb. l. c.; part. unat: [a Goth. <i>wunan</i> is assumed from the participle <i>unwunands</i> = ἀδημονων, Phil. ii. 26; the word prop. means <i>to dwell, abide;</i> A. S. <i>wunian;</i> Old Engl. <i>to wone;</i> Germ. <i>wohnen</i>]:—<i>to abide, dwell;</i> börn áttu þau bjoggu ok unðu, <i>dwelt and abode,</i> Rm.; fiskr unir í flóði, <i>the fish lives in water.</i> Gm.; hér munda ek eðli una, Fsm.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/unad-samligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          unað-samligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>delightful,</i> Greg. 30, Eluc. 45, Sturl. i. 206 C, Fas. iii. 87, Mar.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/unad-samr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          unað-samr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>delightful;</i> auðræði ok unaðsamar vistir, <i>a happy home,</i> Bs. i. 146 (better unaðs vistir, see the foot-note).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/unad-semd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          unað-semd
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(<strong>-semi,</strong> 655 xxvi. 1), f. <i>a charm, delight;</i> blómgaða með allri u., Fms. i. 137; eilíf u., Th. 6, Stj. 15; unaðsemdar vist = unaðs vist, Mar. (655 xxxii. 1).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/unadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          unaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. and <strong>unað,</strong> n.; eilíft unað, Hom. (St.); æzta unað, Sól. 71; lítið unað, Skv. 1. 46: rarer <strong>unaðr,</strong> m., Eluc. 49, and so in mod. usage, although unan (q. v.) is more freq.: [A. S. <i>wyn;</i> Germ. <i>wonne;</i> Dan. <i>ynde</i>]:—<i>delight, happiness;</i> friðar fagnaðar, ok unaðs, 623. 22; öllum þykkir unat í, á at heyra, Fb. i. 348; unaðr es, Eluc. 49; eilífs unaðar, 625. 188; með unaði ok inndæli, 168; slikt er æzta unað, Sól.; í Paradísar unað, Hom. (St.); unaðs-bót, skömm unaðs-bót, <i>a short delight,</i> Fms. xi. 329; unaðs hilmr, <i>a sweet smell,</i> Eluc. 54; unaðs-sýn, <i>a happy sight,</i> 53; unaðs-vist, <i>a happy home,</i> Bs. i. 146; cp. ynði.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/unan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          unan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>unun,</strong> f. <i>a charm, delight</i> (Germ. <i>wonne</i>), freq.; this is the current mod. form. <strong>ununar-samr,</strong> adj. <i>delightful,</i> Fas. iii. 644.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/und"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          und
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> f. [Goth. <i>wunds</i> = <i>wounded</i> and <i>wundufni</i> = μάστιξ; A. S. <i>wund;</i> Engl. <i>wound;</i> O. H. G. <i>wunta;</i> Germ. <i>wunde</i>]:—<i>a wound;</i> undir svella, Skv. 3. 68; undir dreyrgar, 32; blóð hljóp ór undinni. Eg. 216, Sæm. 179; taka vápnit ór undinni, Gísl. 22; hann beit yðr stóra und, Fas. ii. 378; tók at láta í undum þeim er vóru fyrir brjóstinu, Róm. 232; hol-und, merg-und. This word is little used in prose, having been superseded by the word sár, <i>a sore</i>: in poët. circumlocutions, <strong>unda-log, und-bál, und-leygr,</strong> <i>wound-fire,</i> i. e. <i>weapons;</i> <strong>und-bára, -gjálfr, -lögr,</strong> <i>a wound-wave,</i> i. e. <i>blood;</i> <strong>und-reyr, -fleinn, -linnr,</strong> = <i>a wound-reed, wound-snake, a sword;</i> <strong>und-gagl,</strong> <i>a carrion bird,</i> Lex. Poët. <strong>unda-fífill,</strong> m., botan. <i>hawkweed, hieracium.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/und-genginn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          und-genginn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>wound-printed,</i> Nj. (in a verse), an epithet of wounds, as sword-prints.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/und-varp"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          und-varp
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "see unnvarp.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/undadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          undaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>wounded;</i> geiri undaðr, Hm. 139; vápn-u., hjör-u., <i>sword-wounded,</i> Skv. 3. 46, Hkr. i. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/undan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          undan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "prep. with dat. and adv. <i>from under, from underneath;</i> hann kastaði í pallinn undan sér hásætinu, <i>he threw the cushion away from the seat he sat on,</i> Nj. 175; hjó undan honum fótinn, <i>cut his foot from under him, cut his leg off,</i> 9; madr kippti fótum undan honum, svá at hann féll, Fms. ii. 149; hann hafði rétt fingrinn út undan húðinni, Nj. 208; berjask undan skildi eða buklara, Sks. 374 B; hann spratt upp undan borðinu, <i>he sprang up from the table,</i> Nj. 152; spratt upp u. garðinum, <i>up from under the fence,</i> where he had been hidden, 170; róa fram undan eyjunni, Fms. ii. 305; sjá þeir renna skip undan eyjum fram, x. 205; halda skipum undan landi, <i>to keep with his ship from under the land, stand off land,</i> i. 225; gaf byr undan landi, Ísl. ii. 243; þá er hann var þrévetr, gékk hann eigi u. konum, Eb. 320; hestisk Þórólfr á hann en graðungrinn gékk eigi u. at heldr, 324 (of a vicious bull).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/undan-bod"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
