              "__html": "f. = yrþjóð = verþjóð, Ad.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [the origin of this word is uncertain; the <i>ð</i> is radical, for were it inflexive, an ‘umlaut’ would have taken place in the vowel (it would then be yrð, not urð), see Gramm. xxxii, col. 2, l. 10 sqq.]:—<i>a heap of stones,</i> on the sea-beach, or from an earth-slip; sævar-urð, <i>piles of broken stones on the sea-shore,</i> Orkn. 114; at veiða otr er lá í urðinni undir höfðanum … þeir segja at hann væri þar á urðinni, 276; grjót ok urðir, Edda 5; urð sú lá í dalnum er Sefsurð heitir, ok er þar hvárki fært mönnum né hrossum … urðar-brot, <i>breaking through an</i> urð, Ó. H. 186; fætr Loka taka niðr grjótið, urðir ok viðu, Edda 45; látum liggja Ljotúlf goða, í urð ok í urð, Sd. (in a verse); draga urð at e-m, <i>to pile stones on,</i> Fms. vii. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urd-haeingr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urð-hæingr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>urð-þvengr,</strong> m. <i>the fish, the thong of the</i> urð, i. e. <i>a snake,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urdar-brunnr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urðar-brunnr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the Weird’s spring,</i> the holy well where the Norns reside, Vsp., Edda; there is a curious passage in an Icel. Christian poem written shortly after the introduction of the new Faith, where Christ is represented as sitting at the well of Urðr in the south, id. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urdar-far"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
