          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., qs. vurðr; gen. urðar; acc. dat. would be urði, but does not occur unless it be Vsp. 20, where urð must stand either for urði, dropping the vowel, for the next word begins with <i>h;</i> or it is nom. = urðr, according to the A. S. and general rule (cp. Rm. 36), that verbs signifying to call, name, are followed by a nom.: plur. urðir: [A. S. <i>wyrd;</i> Engl. <i>weird;</i> Hel. <i>wurth</i>]:—<i>a weird, fate;</i> the word is obsolete in prose; en sjá urðr sjallgætust (-gætastr, Cod. wrongly) með Svíum þótti, <i>that weird, extraordinary accident,</i> viz. that he slew himself, Ýt.; gengu þess á milli grimmar urðir, <i>‘grim weirds.’ a cruel fate prevented it,</i> Skv. 3. 5; urðr öðlinga þú hefir æ verit, <i>the evil Norn, evil angel of kings,</i> Gkv. 1. 23.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> u, f. [provinc. Norse <i>urve</i>], <i>a strap, rope’s end;</i> ef urgur eru í fjósum, Jb. 320; þegar drengrinn vildi festa á sig mannbroddana, sagði hann, ‘nú er týnd urgan mín,’ … eg spurði hann hvort þessar ólar bæði útan og innan fótar héti urgur, hann kvað já við því, Pál Vidalín in Skýr. 591.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urgur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urgur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f, pl. [urigr = <i>peevish</i>], <i>peevishness, ill temper;</i> það eru urgur í honum, <i>to be in bad mood.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. [is a mod. participle (16th century, see urningr below) formed from yrja, urði, urinn, = erja, arði, arinn, cp. erja β; it can therefore have no bearing on the false reading, Gsp., Fas. i. 475]:—<i>rubbed, scratched;</i> jörðin er öll upp urin, <i>the crop bitten close off,</i> as if shaven.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. a nickname, Fms. x. 120.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/url"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          url
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Ital. <i>orlo;</i> Fr. <i>ourlet;</i> mod. Lat. <i>orlum</i>], a kind of <i>hat</i> or <i>hood,</i> Ó. H. 30, a απ. λεγ.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urmull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urmull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "see örmöl.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urningr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urningr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [yrja = erja], <i>a rubbing;</i> af ari eðr urningi, Skýr. 590 (Björn á Skarðsá).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to snarl,</i> of a dog.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a herb;</i> see jurt.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urt-hvalr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urt-hvalr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a kind of <i>whale,</i> whence <strong>Urthvala-fjörðr,</strong> a local name, Eb. 8 new Ed.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          urta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a female seal with litter,</i> Skáld H. 6. 5, and in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/usli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          usli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [A. S. <i>ysla</i> or <i>ysela</i> = <i>fire, embers;</i> a compd form is auvisli (q. v.) qs. af-usli (?); cp. Lat. <i>urere</i>]:—<i>a conflagration,</i> esp. in the allit. eldr ok usli, Fms. i. 201, viii. 341: <i>a field of burning embers,</i> xi. 35: the sense <i>damages</i> (see auvisli) is prob. secondary. <strong>usla-gjald</strong> or <strong>usla-bót,</strong> n. <i>compensation for</i> u., N. G. L. i. 246, Gþl. 387; see auvisli.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/uxi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          uxi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m., older form <strong>oxi;</strong> in plur. yxn, öxn (cp. the A. S. <i>oxa,</i> pl. <i>oxan;</i> Engl. <i>ox, oxen</i>); also spelt eyxn, exn, eoxn; the masc. forms ‘yxn’ and ‘yxninir’ being formed like menn, menninir from mann-r; uxar is rare and later; thus fjórir öxn, Edda i. 30, v. l. 7; öxnernir, id., v. l. 12, Cod. U; fjóra öxn, id.; but öxninn (for oxninnir), Cod. Reg. l. c.; tvá gamla arðr-yxn, Stj. 446; vexnum, Fms. x. 404; tveir yxn, Bret. 22; feita eyxn, Sks. 697 B; tvá yxn, þrjá yxn, Eg. 181, 733; marga yxn, 181; korn ok yxn, N. G. L. i. 75; yxninir, Fms. vi. 69; yxnennir, xi. 7; yxnina, Bret. 26; eyxn þrír hvítir, Fms. xi. 6; eyxn marga. Eg. 733; öxn mínir, Greg. 44; eoxkn (sic) fyrir arðri, MS. 1812. 65; öxnunum, Bret. 26; yxn þeir er Þórólfr var ekinn á … tvá sterka yxn, … vóru þá þrotnir yxninir ok teknir aðrir …, þá ærðusk yxninir ok urðu þegar lausir, Eb. 6l, 62 new Ed.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/u"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ú-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>ó-</strong> is the negative prefix before nouns, adjectives, and adverbs (Engl. and Germ. <i>un-</i>), for the spelling of which see p. 469, col. 2. The use of this particle is almost unlimited; it may e. g. be prefixed to almost every past part., in frequent instances answering to Engl. <i>‘not;’</i> ókominn, <i>not come;</i> ófarinn, <i>not gone;</i> úgefinn, <i>not given;</i> or to the part. act. as gerundive, það er óhafandi, <i>unfit for use;</i> ógöranda, <i>not feasible;</i> ódrekkandi, <i>undrinkable;</i> óetandi, <i>uneatable;</i> úsigrandi, óvinnandi, <i>invincible;</i> ótakandi, <i>impregnable.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/u-kvaedi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ú-kvæði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. (p. 662, col. 2), = Lat. <i>ne-fas;</i> eru þat ókvæði að hugsa, að …, Vídal. i. 320.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/u-magi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ú-magi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [mega], <i>a helpless one, who cannot maintain himself,</i> a law term, relating to the duty of maintenance; it included children, aged people, men disabled by sickness, paupers, etc.; maðr hverr til þess hann er fimtán vetra, þá er hann ómagi, N. G. L. i. 168; sinn ómaga á hverr fram at færa, Grág. i. 232; óðr maðr er ú. arfa síns, Js. 26; ef þræll verðr ú. af bardögum, Grág. ii. 155: the saying, úmæt eru ómaga orð. Gísl. 5; sveitar-ómagi, <i>a pauper, a charity-boy</i> or <i>girl;</i> úmaga aldr, meðan (the children) þau eru á ómaga aldri, Grág. i. 240; vera af ómaga aldri, <i>to be grown up,</i> Dipl. v. 3; ómaga bálkr, a section in the law, Grág. i. 230 sqq.; ómaga eyrir, <i>the money of a minor,</i> 176; ómaga bú, ómaga lýsing, Grág. (Kb.); ómaga skipti, ómaga sök, Grág. i. 264; ómaga tíund, K. Þ. K. 156; ómaga verk, Jb. 255; ómaga vist, Dipl. v. 5.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/u-megd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ú-megð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the state of being</i> úmagi, but also as collect. term = úmagi, of the people themselves; börn í úmegð, Js. 60; meðan erfingjar vóru í ú., <i>whilst the heirs were in infancy,</i> Fs. 65; enda sé dóttir þeirra í ú., Grág. i. 172; þóttisk hón svá helzt mega forðask ú. sína, Rb. 237; fyrir ómegðar sakir, K. Þ. K. 116; eitt haust er fundr fjölmennr at Skörðum, at tala um hreppa-skil ok ómegðir manna, Lv. 17; þeir skiptu ok ómegð, þat vóru börn tvau, Gísl. 17; hann lét eptir ú. aðra, Fs. 140; ok þat var þá siðvandi nökkurr er land var allt alheiðit, at þeir menn er félitlir vóru en stóð ú. mjök til handa létu út bera börn sín, ok þótti þó ílla gört ávallt, Ísl. ii. 198; ómegðar-bú, K. Þ. K. 90; ómegðar-maðr = ómagamaðr, Eb. 164.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/u-skap"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ú-skap
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>‘unshape,’ shapelessness, deformity;</i> með úskapi, þér hafit málit meirr til búit með úskapi enn eigi sé spjöllin á, Glúm. 347: <i>spleen, madness,</i> æði ok úskap, Hom. 113; hugr heitir úskap, Edda 110. <strong>úskaps-maðr,</strong> m. <i>an ill-disposed person,</i> Sturl. ii. 149.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/u-svifinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ú-svifinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>coarse, impudent</i> (prop. <i>‘unclean?’</i>), Fb. i. 216: <strong>ú-svífni,</strong> f. <i>impudence.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/u-svifr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ú-svifr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(not úsvífr), adj. (the <i>r</i> is radical); [the latter part, which only exists in this and the following compds, answers to A. S. <i>syfer,</i> O. H. G. <i>subar,</i> Germ. <i>sauber,</i> Engl. <i>sober,</i> Lat. <i>sobrius,</i> meaning <i>clean;</i> úsvifr = A. S. <i>unsyfre</i>]:—prop. <i>unsober, unclean,</i> but only used in a metaphorical sense.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/u-svifrandi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ú-svifrandi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>polluting,</i> a απ. λεγ. in Haustl. as an epithet of the giant Thiazzi in an eagle’s shape; ú. Ása, <i>the defiler of the gods</i> (?).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/u-vaegr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ú-vægr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., qs. of-ægr, <i>furious;</i> þeir hlaupa í mót honum úvægir ok berjask, Ísl. ii. (Heiðarv. S.) 367.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ua"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. úir, pret. úði, <i>to swarm;</i> hvert vatn úði af fiskum, Eg. 134 (Cod. Wolph.): in mod. usage, úði, það úir og grúir.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ud"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., qs. hugð, contracted [A. S. <i>hyde</i>], <i>the mind,</i> but only existing in compds, harð-úð, íll-úð, létt-úð, úlf-úð, var-úð, etc., qs. harð-hugð, etc.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/udi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [a corruption for úr, q. v., changing <i>r</i> into <i>ð,</i> as in fre<i>ð</i>inn from fre<i>r</i>inn], <i>a drizzling rain,</i> freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/udigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úðigr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>minded;</i> harð-úðigr, létt-úðigr, íll-úðigr, etc.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ufat"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úfat
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. part. <i>roughened, edged;</i> only in the phrase, það er svó úfað, eg veit hvernig það er úfað, <i>I know all its rough edges, all its difficulties,</i> of matters troublesome or of fishing in troubled waters.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ufr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úfr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> adj. <i>ruffled, rough;</i> svá úfr ok þrjótr, at allir þurfi til at ganga, N. G. L. i. 335; úvar ‘ro dísir, <i>the fairies are wrath,</i> Gm. 53.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ufr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úfr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a roughness, rough edge,</i> e. g. on a board being shaped by an adze, also of <i>ruffled hair,</i> as when stroked backwards; hann sá járnloku eina, þar hafði komit högg í mikit ok reis á röndinni úfr hvass, Fas. iii. 380.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ula"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to howl</i> (?), a doubtful απ. λεγ.; ef maðr skerr hár af höfði manns eða úlar (<i>whistles</i>?) honum nökkut til háðungar, Grett. ii. 131 A; see ýla.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulbud"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlbúð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., see úlfúð.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/uldinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úldinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>decomposed, putrid.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/uldna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úldna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [<i>ulna,</i> Ivar Aasen], <i>to rot</i>; rotna ok úldna, Stj. 268–273, passim in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-gardr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-garðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a wolf-pit,</i> Gþl. 457, v. l.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-gi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-gi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= úlf-gi; úlfr (q. v.), with a neg. suffix, Ls. 39.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-grar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-grár
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>wolf-grey,</i> Fær. 48; úlfgrátt hár, Eg. 305, cp. Ad. 7.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-hamr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-hamr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a wolf’s skin,</i> referring to the superstition of men turning into a wolf’s shape, Fas. i. 130; cp. hamr: also a nickname, Hervar. S.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-hanzki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-hanzki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a glove of wolf-skin,</i> used by a sorceress, Fas. i. 50.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-hedinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-héðinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a wolf’s skin:</i> a pr. name, Úlf-héðinn, Landn.: also as an appellative of berserkers wearing wolf-skins, Hornklofi,—at ‘berserkja’ reiðu vil ek spyrja …?—answer, ‘úlfhéðnar’ heita, cp. þeir berserkir er úlfhéðnar vóru kallaðir, Fs. 17.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-hugadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-hugaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>‘wolf-mooded,’ fiery,</i> Skv. 2. 11.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-hugr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-hugr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a wolf’s mind,</i> = úlfúð; ú. sá er þér þótti dyrit hafa á okkr, Fas. ii. 172.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-hvelpr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-hvelpr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a wolf’s cub,</i> Fas. i. 181.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-idi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-íði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a wolf’s lair</i> (cp. bjarnar-híði), Hkv. 1. 16.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-lidr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-liðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the wolf’s joint,</i> i. e. <i>the wrist,</i> see the story of Ty and the Wolf Fenrir, Edda 20,—‘then bit he (the wolf) the hand off, whence it is now called wolf’s joint (the wrist):’ the word is often spelt as above, e. g. Gullþ. 59, Fms. i. 166, Nj. 84, 262 (Cod. 468 in both instances gives ‘aulflið’). This etymology, although old, is quite erroneous, for the word is derived from oln- or öln-, see alin (p. 13, col. 2); the true form being öln-liðr, q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulf-vidr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlf-viðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Norse <i>ulv-ved</i>], <i>privet,</i> Lat. <i>viburnum,</i> Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulfaldi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlfaldi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Ulf. <i>ulbandus</i> = κάμηλος; A. S. <i>olfend;</i> Hel. <i>olvunt;</i> O. H. G. <i>olpente;</i> from the Gr. ἐλεφάς, -άντος, although in an altered sense]:—<i>a camel,</i> Stj., Greg. passim; the word occurs as the nickname of a man early in the 11th century, Fms. vi. (Brynjólfr úlfaldi); it is still in full use in Icel., hægra er úlfaldanum at ganga í gegnum nálar-augað enn ríkum manni at komast í Guðs ríki, Luke xviii. 25; hann tók tíu úlfalda … af síns herra úlföldum … hún segir drekk þá, eg vil og gefa þínum úlföldum að drekka, Gen. xxiv. The word ‘camel’ has never been adopted in the Icel.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulfr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlfr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., úlf-gi, Ls. 39; [Ulf. <i>wulfs;</i> A. S. and Hel. <i>wulf;</i> Engl.-Germ. <i>wolf;</i> North. E. <i>Ulf-,</i> in pr. names, <i>Ulpha, Ulverston;</i> Dan.-Swed. <i>ulv;</i> cp. Lat. <i>lupus</i> and <i>vulpes;</i> Gr. λύκος]:—<i>a wolf,</i> Grág. ii. 122; lýsa þar vígi, … kallask hvárki úlfr né björn nema svá heiti hann, N. G. L. i. 6l; úlfa þytr mér þótti íllr vera hjá söngvi svana, Edda (in a verse); úlfa hús, <i>wolf-pits,</i> Gþl. 457: freq. in poets, where ‘to feed the wolf,’ ‘cheer the wolf’ are standing phrases, see Lex. Poët.: a warrior is hence called úlf-brynnandi, -gæðandi, -grennir, -nestir, -seðjandi, -teitir, i. e. <i>the refresher, cheerer, … gladdener of the wolf;</i> úlf-vín, <i>wolf’s wine,</i> i. e. <i>blood,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulfud"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlfúð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., in Icel. now sounded <strong>úlbúð,</strong> and so spelt, Stj., Sturl., Eg. l. c., <i>‘wolf’s mood,’ savageness;</i> enn er Halli fann þat sló hann á sik úlfúð ok íllsku, Eb. 114; hann er fullr upp úlfúðar (úlbúðar, v. l.), Eg. 114; tóku menn þegar at reisa úlfúð í móti, Fms. v. 102; sakir þeirrar úlbúðar er faðir hans hafði á Davíð, Stj. 473; þó var úlbúð ærin í ambhöfða brjósti, Sturl. i. 35 (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ulpa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úlpa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f., see ólpa.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> n. [cp. Swed. <i>ur-væta, ur-väder</i>], <i>a drizzling rain;</i> úr eða dögg, Stj. 531; úri þafðr, of the sea-serpent, Bragi; var þoka yfir héraðinu, vindr af hafi ok úr við (úr-viðri?), Ísl. ii. 308; er þá létt af allri sunnanþokunni ok úrinu, Hrafn. 8; þá héldi yfir þannig úr þat er af stóð eitrinu, Edda i. 42 (Cod. Worm.; oc þat = or þat = úr þat, Ub. l. c.): a remnant is in the mod. phrase, það er ‘úr’ honum, <i>it rains;</i> cp. also úr-koma and úði.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ur-drifinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úr-drifinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>foam-besprent,</i> of a ship, Edda (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ur-felli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úr-felli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. = úrkoma.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ur-illr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úr-íllr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [úrigr and íllr], <i>fretful,</i> esp. from want of sleep; hann er ú. af svefni.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ur-koma"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úr-koma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>rain</i>, freq. in mod. popular usage, esp. of a mild rain.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ur-svalr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úr-svalr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>wet-cold,</i> Hkv. 2. 42; úrsvalar unnir, 2. 11; úrsvöl Gýmis völva, Edda (in a verse); úrsvölum munni, Grett. (in a verse), of the eddying stream.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ur-van"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úr-ván
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. a poët. name of <i>the clouds,</i> Alm.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ur-vaeta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úr-væta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = úrkoma, Fb. ii. 222.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ur-thveginn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úr-þveginn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>wave-washed,</i> Hallfred.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urig-hlyra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úrig-hlýra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>wet-cheeked, weeping,</i> Gh. 5.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urig-toppi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úrig-toppi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>dewy-mane,</i> poët. epithet of a horse, Nj. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úrigr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [úr], <i>wet</i>; úrgan stafn, Hkv. Hjörv. 15; úrgu barði, Orkn. (in a verse); úrga strönd, Fms. xi. 307 (in a verse); úrgar brautir (cp. Homer’s ὑγρα κέλευθα), Rm. 36; úrig fjöll, Skm. 10, Hðm. 11; úrgum hjörvi, Ad. 4.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/urr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          úrr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. úrar, [Germ. <i>ur-ochs;</i> Lat. <i>urus</i>], <i>the urus</i> or <i>ur-ox;</i> úrar-horn, <i>an ur-ox horn,</i> Fas. iii. 616: as a nickname, Ó. H.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv., compar. <strong>útarr,</strong> superl. <strong>útarst,</strong> and later form <strong>yzt;</strong> [Ulf. and A. S. <i>ût</i>; Engl. <i>out</i>; Scot. <i>b-ut;</i> O. H. G. <i>ûz;</i> Germ. <i>aus,</i> qs. <i>auz;</i> Dan. <i>ud</i>]:—<i>out, towards the outer side</i> (of a door, outskirt, circumference), opp. to inn, q. v.; út eptir ánni, Eg. 81; út ok inn með hverjum firði, 48; út með sjó, 746; út eptir firði, 87; inn til Leirulækjar, ok út til Straumfjarðar, 140; út eða inn, Nj. 104; kalla mann út, <i>out of doors,</i> 17; sjá út, <i>to look out,</i> Ld. 148; út þær dyrr, Sturl. i. 178; út ór, <i>out of, out from,</i> Nj. 182; út munninn, <i>out of the mouth,</i> Fms. vi. 351; snúa út, <i>to turn out,</i> Mar.; út þar, <i>out there,</i> Eg. 394; þangat út, <i>out there</i>, Fms. x. 400; stíga á skip út, Ld. 158; bera fé á út, <i>on board</i>, Eg. 98; garðr var í túninu meirr út (<i>farther out</i>) á völlinn, Háv. 53: of time, út Jól, <i>‘Yule out,’ all through Yule,</i> Pm. 104; vetrinn út, sumarit út, <i>throughout the winter, summer;</i> láta út, <i>to stand out to sea,</i> Band. 39.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-altari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-altari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>the low altar,</i> Vm. 58, Dipl. v. 18.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-arfi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-arfi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>an ‘out-heir,’ distant heir,</i> not in the direct line, K. Á. 54, Gþl. 226.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-armr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-armr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the outer branch,</i> Rb. 440.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-asa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-ása
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to tack out,</i> as a naut. term: hence metaph., útása sig, <i>to make one’s preparations.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-beit"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-beit
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>an ‘out-bait,’ grazing,</i> opp. to stall-feeding; góð ú., Eg. 710; ek þarf bæði hey ok ú., Fms. vi. 103.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-beizla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-beizla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>sequestration, execution,</i> for fines; sækja e-n út með útbeizlu, N. G. L. i. 249.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-bita"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-bita
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að; ú. augunum, <i>to turn the eyes in the head,</i> so that the white alone is seen, Fb. i. 566.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-bod"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-boð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., mostly in pl. <i>‘out-biddings,’ a calling out, levy, conscription,</i> of ships and men, Sks. 27; hafa leigu-laust ok útboða., <i>free from levy,</i> Gþl. 432; synja honum leiðangrs né útboða, 76; hann var opt á sumrum í hernaði ok hafði útboð mikil í landi, … þat var eitt var at jarl hafði útboð mikit sem hann var vanr, Orkn. 40; í því biskups-ríki eru ellifu tigir skipa konungi til útboðs, Fms. xi. 229; ek vil at þú farir sendiferð mína norðr á Hálogaland ok hafir þar útboð, bjóðir út almenning at liði ok at skipum, … þá átti hann þing en sendi menn sína frá sér at krefja útboðsins, Ó. H. 147; útboða-bréf, <i>a writ of conscription,</i> Fms. ix. 297, x. 64; útboða framlag, Sks. 27 B.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-bordi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-borði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>the outboard, seaward side;</i> in the phrase, á útborða, Eg. 74, 195, 354, Fms. viii. 138, 417, v. l.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-borg"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-borg
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>an ‘out-borough,’ outworks,</i> Fms. ix. 41, x. 153, v. l.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-brjotr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-brjótr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>an outburst,</i> Thom.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-brot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-brot
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>an eruption.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-brotning"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          út-brotning
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>an outbreak,</i> Greg. 22.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ut-burdr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
