          valda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. veld, pl. völdum, valdit, valda: pret. olli, ollir, olli; <i>olli</i> ofrausn <i>stillis,</i> in a verse of A. D. 1066, as also by Ari, Íb. 7: in alliteration as a vowel, <i>e</i>inn þú því <i>o</i>llir, <i>e</i>kki …, Am. 80; a pret. voldi or oldi also occurs, for references see B: subj. ylli, also voldi, vildi, see B; imperat. vald: with neg. suff. vald-at-tu, <i>cause thou not,</i> Gísl. (in a verse); veldr-at, Nj. 61: part. valdit: a mod. verb has been formed from the pret. olli,—olla, olli, ollat, olla being used of <i>to cause,</i> valda <i>to be able</i>: [Ulf. <i>waldan, ga-waldan</i> = <i>to rule;</i> A. S. <i>wealdan;</i> Engl. <i>wield;</i> O. H. G. <i>waltan;</i> Germ. <i>walten;</i> Dan. <i>vold</i>; cp. Lat. <i>valere</i>.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
