        >
          véorr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>véoðr,</strong> contr. <strong>veiðr</strong> (Haustl.), only used as a name of Thor, Hým., Vsp., Edda (Gl.), meaning either <i>the holy, a priest</i> (= Goth. <i>weiha</i>), or from vé, n., referring to Thor ‘as the defender of hearth and home’.",
            }
          }
        />
