              "__html": "n. pl. <i>‘war-tears,’</i> i. e. <i>blood;</i> fella vígtár, <i>to shed war-tears, to bleed,</i> Sighvat.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-teitr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-teitr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. = vígglaðr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-tonn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-tönn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a war-tooth, tusk,</i> Vígl. 20, Fas. i. 214, iii. 231: <i>an eye-tooth,</i> N. G. L. i. 171.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-vel"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-vél
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a war-trick, ruse, engine of war,</i> Fms. i. 103; vápnum ok vígvélum, vi. 69, vii. 93; heiðingjar höfðu vagna járnvarða ok margháttaðar aðrar vígvélar, vi. 145; vinna borg með vígvélum, Stj. 512 (vígvælar).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-vollr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-völlr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a battle-field,</i> Bret. 54, Eg. 491, Nj. 212, Ld. 224, Hkr. i. 159, Fms. xi. 372.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-volr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-völr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a ‘war-stick,’ weapon,</i> a collective term; með öxar-hamri, eða hvárngi vígvöl er maðr hefir, Grág. ii. 14, Pr. 415, Fms. viii. 249.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-theyr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-þeyr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a ‘war-breeze,’</i> i. e. <i>battle.</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-throt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-þrot
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>‘war-abatement’ end of the battle,</i> Vþm.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-thryma"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-þryma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a ‘war-storm,’</i> i. e. <i>battle,</i> Hkv. 1. 6.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-aesa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-æsa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, (vígáss), to furnish with vígáss.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vig-orr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víg-örr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>eager for war,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vigi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vígi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a vantage-ground, stronghold;</i> þar var svá mikill vígis-munr, at ekki …, Fms. viii. 427; var hamarrinn víðr ofan ok vígi gott, ii. 93, Eb. 188, 238, Fs. 90; öruggt vígi, Gullþ. 52 (Ed.); þar er vígi nakkvat, Nj. 95; renna til vígis í Almanna-gjá, 228: metaph., engi vörn eðr vígi, Sks. 131.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vigi-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vígi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a fighter,</i> only used as the name of <i>a hound,</i> e. g. Vígi, the dog of king Olave Tryggvason, Fms. i-iii; and so in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/viging"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víging
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a consecration,</i> N. G. L. i. 345, 352.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vigja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vígja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, [Ulf. <i>weihan, ga-weihan,</i> = ἁγιάζειν; Germ. <i>weihen;</i> Dan. <i>vie;</i> Swed. <i>viga;</i> cp. Ulf. <i>weiha</i> = ἱερεύς, <i>weihiþa</i> = <i>holiness, weis</i> = ἄγιος; the adjective has been displaced by heilagr, q. v.; the vé (q. v.) is a different word]:—<i>to consecrate;</i> in heathen sense, with the hammer of Thor, vígit okkr saman Várar-hendi, Þkv. 30; tók upp hamarinn Mjölni ok brá upp ok vígði hafr-stökurnar, Edda 28; konungr vígði þá (the dwarfs) útan steins með mála-saxi, Fas. i. 514, ii. 327, 338.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vigolfs-stadir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vígólfs-staðir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a local name in western Iceland.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vigr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vígr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>in fighting state, serviceable;</i> allir vígir karlar, Fms. i. 209: <i>skilled in arms,</i> vígr vel, Nj. 2; vígr manna bezt, Fms. ii. 20, Eb. 32.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vigsla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vígsla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a consecration, ordination;</i> messu-djákn at vígslu, Nj. 272; kom erkibiskup heim frá vígslu, Fms. ix. 423; taka vígslu af biskupi, Bs. i, Grág. passim; kirkju-vígsla, <i>consecration of a church;</i> biskups-vígsla, prests-vígsla, <i>ordination of a bishop, priest;</i> hjóna-vígsla, <i>a wedding;</i> konungs-vígsla, <i>a coronation;</i> vatns-vígsla, Bs., passim: vígslu-dagr, <i>the day of consecration;</i> vígslu-faðir, <i>an ordaining father</i> (of a bishop), cp. ‘god-father,’ Bs.; vígslu-görð, <i>a performance of ordination.</i> Fms. x. 11; vígslu-maðr, <i>a man in holy orders,</i> viii. 269; vígslu-gjöf, id., Ann. 1356; leggja vígslu-hendr yfir e-n, <i>to lay hands on,</i> of a bishop, Bs. i. 850; vígslu-hrútr, <i>the sacrificial ram,</i> Stj.; vígslu-eiðr, <i>the coronation-oath,</i> Fms. viii. 155; vígslu-gull, <i>a coronation-ring,</i> x. 15; vígslu-kaup, <i>a consecration-fee,</i> K. Á. 76; vígslu-klæði, -skrúð, <i>the coronation-robes,</i> Fms. x. 16, viii. 193; vígslu-sverð, <i>a coronation-sword,</i> x. 15, 109; vígslu-taka, <i>a receiving consecration,</i> H. E. i. 255; vígslu-pallr, <i>a degree of ordination,</i> H. E., K. Á.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vik-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vík
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. víkr, pl. víkr, [from víkja; Dan. <i>vig</i>], prop. <i>a small creek, inlet, bay;</i> vík gékk upp fyrir austan nesit en upp at víkinni stóð borg mikil, Eg. 161; þeir námu víkr þær er við þá eru kenndar, Landn. 236; í vík eina … hjá vík þeirri, 57; sá ek at í hverja vík vóru rekin brot af þessu tré, Fms. vii. 163; víkr ok fjörðu, Fbr. 14 new Ed.; tveim megin víkriunar, Fs. 143; margar víkr, 146; róa vik á e-n, <i>to row one round, get the better of another;</i> þætti mér mikit vaxa mín virðing, eðr þess höfðingja er á Hrafnkel gæti nökkura vík róit, Hrafn. 16 (metaph. from pulling in a race), Þjal. 48.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vik-daelskr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vík-dælskr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>from the county W.,</i> Fms. vii.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vik-marr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vík-marr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. the bay at Bergen. Fms. vii.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vik-skart"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vík-skart
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= víkskorit, <i>indented with bays,</i> Post. (Unger) 234.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vik-verjar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vík-verjar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. <i>the men from the county Wik</i> in Norway, Fms. passim; Víkverja biskup, -konungr, etc., Landn. 313, Ann. 1209: <strong>Vík-verskr,</strong> adj., Fær. 34, Nj. 40, Eg. 72.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/viking"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víking
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a freebooting voyage, piracy;</i> see víkingr. In heathen days it was usual for young men of distinction, before settling down, to make a warlike expedition to foreign parts, this voyage was called ‘víking,’ and was part of a man’s education like the grand tour in modern times; hence the saying in the old Saga,—‘when I was young and on my voyage (víking), but now I am old and decrepit;’ so a son begs his father to give him a ‘langskip,’ that he may set out on a ‘víking,’ cp. the scene of the young Egil and his mother Bera, and the reference Fms. i. 69; see B. The custom was common among Teutonic tribes, and is mentioned by Caesar B.G. vi. ch. 23 (latrocinia nullam habent infamiam, quae extra fines cujusque civitatis fiunt, sqq.), only there it is a foray on land; (cp. the mod. <i>American filibustering.</i>)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vikingligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víkingligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>like a viking, martial,</i> Ld. 276.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vikingr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víkingr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a freebooter, rover, pirate,</i> but in the Icel. Sagas used specially of the bands of Scandinavian warriors, who during the 9th and 10th centuries harried the British Isles and Normandy: the word is peculiarly Norse, for although it occurs in A. S. in the poem Byrnoth (six or seven times), it is there evidently to be regarded as a Norse word; and prob. so too in the poem ‘Exodus,’ in the words <i>rondas bærun sæwicingas, over saltne mere;</i> lastly, in ‘Widsith,’ as the name of a people, and <i>Liðvicingas</i> (= Liðungar? q. v.) The word ‘víkingr’ is thought to be derived from vík (<i>a bay</i>), from their haunting the bays, creeks, and fjords;—or it means ‘the men from the fjords,’ the coincidence that the old Irish called the Norsemen <i>‘Lochlannoch.’</i> and Norway <i>‘Lochlan,’</i> is curious.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vikingskapr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víkingskapr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>piracy,</i> Fms. i. 98, Fs. 13.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vikja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víkja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "older <strong>vikva,</strong> MS. 325. 76; the spelling with <i>y</i> is curious; pres. vykr, Hom. (a very old vellum); pret. veyk, Ó. H. 174. l. 9, Mork. 171. l. 34; <strong>ykva,</strong> q. v., also occurs (<i>vi</i> = <i>y</i>); pres. vík; pret. veik, veikt, veik, pl. viku; subj. víki; imperat. vík (víktu); part. vikinn; a pret. vék (like sté, hné, from stíga, hníga) has prevailed in mod. usage (v<i>ék</i>, l<i>ék</i>, Úlf. 3. 34), but is hardly found in old writers: [Dan. <i>vige;</i> Swed. <i>vika</i>.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vikjanligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víkjanligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>movable.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vikr-barmr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víkr-barmr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a little bay;</i> kómu í einn víkrbarm, Krók. 460.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vikr-hvarf"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víkr-hvarf
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a creek,</i> Grett. 128 new Ed.; spelt víkhvarf, Fms. vii. 260.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vil-3"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víl
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [A. S. <i>wîl-</i> in <i>wîl-bec;</i> cp. Lat. <i>vīis</i>], <i>misery, wretchedness;</i> erfiði ok víl, Skálda; við víl ok erfiði, Hbl. 58; lifa við víl ok erfiði, Blanda; víls ok vesaldar, Fms. iii. 95; þá er móðr er at morni komr, allt er víl sem var, Hm. 23; hafa víl at vinna, <i>to have hard work to win</i>, Kormak (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vil-mogr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víl-mögr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., pl. vílmegir, <i>a son of toil, bondsman,</i> Hm. 135, Skm. 35, Bm. 1 (Ó. H. 208), Edda (Gl.), but obsolete in prose.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vil-sidr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víl-siðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = vílstigr; hungr ok þorsti, válað ok vílsiðr, Hom. (St.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vil-sinni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víl-sinni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a ‘walk of misery,’ distress;</i> v. ok nauð, Barl. 60; vás ok vílsinni, 63; vílsinni ok erfiði, 132; í vílsinni við sjálfan sik, <i>in self-inflicted misery,</i> Þiðr. 176; vinna vílsinn, <i>to toil,</i> Gísl. (in a verse); vílsinnis spá, <i>a dismal prophecy,</i> Gkv. 2. 3.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vil-sinnr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víl-sinnr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a companion in distress;</i> v. völu, Edda (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vil-stigr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víl-stigr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a path of misery;</i> margan vílstíg varð hann at ganga, Fms. viii. 48; sá var mér vílstigr of vitaðr, Hm. 99.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vila"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, (qs. vífla?), <i>to hesitate, waver;</i> víla e-ð fyrir sér.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vim-laukr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vím-laukr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a kind of <i>narcotic leek,</i> Fas. i. 229.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vima"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          víma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [cp. vim], <i>giddiness, hesitation,</i> (in Sturl. ii. 54 for vímur read vámur); öl-vima, <i>giddiness from drink,</i> Fél. x.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/vin-3"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          vín
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [this word, though foreign, is common to all Teut. languages, and is one of the few words which at a very early date was borrowed from the Lat.; it is found in the oldest poems, and appears there as a naturalised word; Ulf. has <i>wein</i> = οινος; A. S. and O. H. G. <i>wîn;</i> Germ. <i>wein</i>; Engl. <i>wine;</i> Dan. <i>vin</i>]:—<i>wine</i>; at víni, Hðm. 21, Gísl. (in a verse); en við vín eitt vápn-göfigr, Óðinn æ lifir, Gm. 19; vín var í könnu, Rm. 29. Wine was in early times imported into Scandinavia from England; þeir kómu af Englandi með mikilli gæzku víns ok hunangs ok hveitis, Bs. i. 433, (in the Profectio ad Terram Sanctam, 146, for <i>vim</i> mellis, tritici, bonarumque vestium, read <i>vini,</i> mellis, etc.); or it was brought through Holstein from Germany, as in Fms. i. 111; Þýðerskir menn ætla héðan at flytja smjör ok skreið, en hér kemr í staðinn vín, in the speech of Sverrir, Fms. viii. 251; the story of Tyrkir the Southerner (German), Fb. i. 540, is curious:—for wine made of berries (berja-vín), see Páls S. ch. 9, and Ann. 1203: cp. the saying, vín skal til vinar drekka, Sturl. iii. 305; eitt silfr-ker fullt af víni, id.: allit., vín ok virtr, Sdm.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
