          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þarfindi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>things needful, useful things,</i> H. E. ii. 72, Bs. i. 694; hve mörg þ. þeir mætti hafa af Noregi, Fms. vii. 101; honum til þarfinda, <i>for his use,</i> Finnb. 290; með öllum búnaði ok þarfindum, Stj. 574; ef lands-dróttinn leyfir manni nokkur þ. at vinna í mörku sinni, N. G. L. i. 244. <strong>þarfinda-hús,</strong> n. <i>a hospital,</i> D. N. iii. 78: <i>a necessary</i>, D. N.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tharfna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þarfna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>þarfnan,</strong> see þarna, þarnan.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tharfnadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þarfnaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a need, want,</i> H. E. i. 562 (note); older form <strong>þörfnuðr.</strong>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tharfr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þarfr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., fem. þörf, neut. þarft, sounded þart (for it rhymes with <i>mart</i>); [see þurfa]:—<i>useful;</i> mæli þarft eða þegi, Hm. 19: vinna þat er þarft er, Grett. 94; þafr maðr, 92 A; hann var þeim þarfr í öllu því er hann mátti, Finnb. 216; er hann mér þó ekki þarfr, <i>he brings no good to me,</i> Fs. 134; ú-þarfr, <i>useless, mischievous;</i> all-þarfr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [Dan. <i>tarre;</i> Shetl. <i>tarri</i>- in <i>tarricrook,</i> a fork to gather sea-weed with]:—<i>sea-weed,</i> Lat. <i>alga;</i> þari and þang are almost synonymous; hann grefsk milli tveggja steina, ok berr á sik ofan þarann, Fbr. 103 new Ed., Grág. ii. 358; land eigandi á þara allan, 359; beltis-þari = <i>fucus saccharius;</i> Skíði datt er skyldi hann skjótt á þaranum ganga, Skíða R.; brenna þara, Frissb. 255.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tharmr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þarmr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [A. S. <i>þearmas;</i> provinc. Engl. (Lincolnshire) <i>tharm;</i> Germ. <i>darm;</i> Dan.-Swed. <i>tarm</i>]:—<i>the guts;</i> legg við enda þarms, Pr. 472; enda-þarmr, <i>the end-gut, colon,</i> 473; ok rakti ór honum þarmana, Nj. 275, Fb. i. 530; þá tóku Æsir þarma hans ok bundu Loka með, Edda i. 184; smá-þarmar (q. v.), passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tharna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þarna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. = þar with suffixed -na (q. v.), <i>there;</i> menn fara þarna, kvað hann, <i>men go there, quoth he,</i> Ísl. ii. 356; this form is very freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tharnan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þarnan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. (qs. <strong>þarfnan</strong>), <i>a want, need;</i> af þarnan þeirrar tillögu, N. G. L. ii. 62.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tharnask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þarnask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, (qs. <strong>þarfnask</strong>), <i>to want, lack, be without;</i> svá at vit þarnimk eigi alla góða hluti, Fms. i. 263; þeir er þarnask sína jartein, Skálda 168; þarnask þess sem hann beiðisk, <i>not to get it,</i> K. Á. 230; en þau þarnast hitt er þarf, Fb. ii. 13; nú léði Guð honum ljóss þess er hann hafði lengi þarnast, Hom, 111.; sem hann þarnask ok hans heimamenn, K. Á. 78; alla bús-búhluti þá er þat bú má eigi þarnask, Grág. ii. 42; nær hann má í frelsi bera hött eða kveif, eða nær hann skal þarnask, <i>when he shall wear it and when he shall want it,</i> Sks. 434 B: impers., tjaldstað ok hrossa-beit sem þeim þarnast, Pm. 38.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thars"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þars
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= þar es; see er, p. 131, col. 2, to which add, þars ek em nú til kominn, Fms. xi. 65; þars hann hafði beran skallann fyrir, 132; þars ek em þræll þinn, Hom. (St.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thas-ramr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þas-ramr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. a nickname, Fms. ix. 54.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/that"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þat
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or mod. <strong>það,</strong> neut. of a demonstr. pron.; the nom. sing. is of a different root, sá, sú (p. 516); the other cases are,—gen. þess, þeirar, þess; dat. þeim, þeiri, því and þí; acc. þann, þá, þat: plur. þeir, þær, þau; gen. þeirra; dat. þeim; acc. þá, þær, þau (mod. þaug): the mod. forms have <i>rr</i> in þeirrar, þeirri, þeirra; but for the olden time they are less correct, as may be seen from rhymes: [Goth. <i>þata;</i> Engl. <i>that</i>; Germ. <i>dass</i>, i. e. <i>daz</i>; Dan. <i>det</i>.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/that-ki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þat-ki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<i>‘that not’, not even that!</i> þatki þú hafir brækr þínar! Hbl.; þatki ek fá, mála minn falslausan! Mork. 83; at þatki sé, 677. 4; see -gi, p. 199, col. 2.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/that-na"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þat-na
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<i>that there,</i> see -na; postulinn segir, ‘er þatna,’ <i>is that there? is it?</i> 623. 19.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thatta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þattá
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= þat þá, <i>that then!</i> hvattá? segir jarl,—þattá! segir Ögmundr, at …, Fms. xi. 118.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thatz"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þatz
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= þat es, <i>that which,</i> see er, p. 131, col. 2; allt þatz hann görir, 677. 6; þatz maðrinn af lifir, 3.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thatztu"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þatztu
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= þat-es-þú, <i>‘that which thou,’ what thou,</i> Am. 83.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thauf"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þauf
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [akin to þóf, þæfa]: <strong>þaufast,</strong> að, dep. <i>to grope</i> or <i>fumble.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thaular"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þaular
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. [the etymology and exact sense of this word is not certain, perh. akin to þylja, referring to a lost strong pret. þaul, þulu]:—<i>a long-winded and complex thing;</i> it is, however, only used in metaph. phrases; svá lízk mér sem mínir menn muni hafa mælt sik í þaular um þetta mál meirr enn þú, <i>would have talked themselves into troubles,</i> Fb. i. 348; rekum af oss tjöldin, róum út ór þessum þaular-vági, reisum viðu ok siglum norðr undan, <i>let us row out of this winding creek, hoist sail and stand out northwards!</i> Fms. viii. 130: the mod. phrase, læra, lesa í þaula = læra í belg, <i>to learn, read by rote;</i> as also, <strong>þaul-lesinn,</strong> adj.; hann er þaullesinn, <i>one who has read a thing through and through, got through a weary task:</i> <strong>þaul-reið,</strong> f. <i>a riding steadily on like a log, plodding wearily on:</i> <strong>þaul-sætinn,</strong> adj. <i>sitting log-like without stirring.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thausn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þausn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [cp. þysja, þeysa, þyss], <i>a bustle, wild fray, mélée;</i> margar þausnir ok þrætur, Róm. 290; nær var ek þausnum þeira, <i>I was present at their fray,</i> Sighvat; var nú eigi þausna-laust, <i>there was no little bustle,</i> Fas. iii. 229; þat má kalla þausnar-vers, þrjátigi at honum ganga, <i>that may be called a hurly-burly song,</i> Skiða R.: in mod. usage the word remains in <strong>þjösnast,</strong> að, <i>to chafe, rage, rave wildly;</i> and <strong>þjösna-legr,</strong> adj. <i>coarse, raving:</i> <strong>þjösna-skapr,</strong> m. <i>coarseness, ravings.</i> From this same root, we believe, comes the mod. Norse <i>‘tausa,’</i> Dan. <i>tös,</i> = <i>a romping girl,</i> (from <strong>þausa,</strong> u, f.?)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thausna-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þausna-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>without tumult, quiet.</i> Fas. iii. 229.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thausnast"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þausnast
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, or <strong>þjösnast,</strong> <i>to rush on heedlessly.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thausnir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þausnir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a romping fellow,</i> a nickname, Ann. 1166.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tha"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þá
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. [from the verb þeyja; Engl. <i>thaw</i>; Germ. <i>thau,</i> in <i>thou-wind;</i> Dan. <i>tö</i>]:—<i>a thaw,</i> esp. in the sense of <i>thawed ground;</i> þat er einn eykr má draga á þá á sléttum velli, Grág. ii. 362; þeir rekja spor sem hundar bæði á þá. ok á hjarni, Hkr. i. 111.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tha-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þá
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. [Goth. <i>þan</i> and <i>þanuh;</i> A. S. <i>þon, þanne;</i> Engl. <i>then;</i> Germ. <i>dann</i> and <i>denn;</i> Dan. <i>da</i>; from the Germ. <i>dan</i> is formed the mod. Dan. <i>so-dan, lige-dan,</i>—Germ. <i>so-dann, als-dann;</i> and hence again the mod. Dan. verb <i>danne</i> = <i>to form,</i> see Grimm’s Dict. ii. 740]:—<i>then, at that time;</i> var hón þá fjórtán vetra gömul, Nj. 50: þá sá ek, <i>then I saw,</i> Sks. 1; þá sæmi, 11.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tha-fjall"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þá-fjall
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a ‘thawed fell,’ wet and slippery hill;</i> henda hrein í þáfjalli, Hm.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tha-gi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þá-gi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<i>not then,</i> Sighvat.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tha-leidis"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þá-leiðis
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>this way, thus,</i> Stj. 1, 67.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tha-mikill"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þá-mikill
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>much thawed</i> (?); or does þá mikla stand for ‘mikla þá’ (see þat A. IV), Gísl. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tha-na"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þá-na
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "interj. <i>then! yes, then!</i> er ek get þána, <i>then I guess!</i> Hbl. 58; þána is hardly a verb, although Egilsson (Lex. Poët.) explains it = þeyju = <i>I think it will thaw.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thaga-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þága
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [þiggja], <i>a quittance, receipt;</i> hvárki með gjöfum né þargum (sic), Anecd. 72 new Ed.: freq. in mod. usage, mín er þága, <i>it is in my interest;</i> or göra e-t í þágu e-s; þú skalt ekki göra það í mína þágu, <i>thou shalt not do it for my sake</i>.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tham"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þám
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [akin to þá, f.?], <i>a thickness, mugginess,</i> Björn: þámaðr, part. <i>misty;</i> þámað lopt, <i>a misty sky</i>: and þáma, að; það þámar af.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thattr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þáttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. þáttar, dat. þætti, pl. þættir, þátta, acc. þáttu, mod. þætti; [Germ. <i>docht;</i> Dan. <i>tot</i>; cp. Lat. <i>texo, textum</i>]:—<i>a single strand of a rope;</i> ok skar í sundr átta þáttuna í festinni, Bs. i. 599, ii. 111; sneru þær af afli örlög-þáttu, Hkv. 1. 3; öfundar-þáttr, Fms. xi. 442.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thef-godr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þef-góðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>sweet-smelling,</i> Grett. 96.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thef-illr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þef-íllr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>ill-smelling.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thef-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þef-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>smell-less, without scent, vapid.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thefa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þefa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to smell, sniff;</i> þefaði sem hann rekti spor sem hundar, Fær. 170; matr svá lítill at hón þefaði af, Bárð. 175: part., ílla þefaðr, <i>ill-smelling, foul,</i> Fms. x. 208; vel þefaðr, Pr. 473.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thefan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þefan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a smelling,</i> Stj. 93.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thefja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þefja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> pret. þafði, = þæfa, remains in the part. þafðr:—<i>to stir, thicken;</i> hann hafði þá eigi þafðan sinn graut, <i>he had not cooked his porridge thick;,</i> Eb. 70 new Ed,; úri þafðr, <i>‘wave-beaten,’</i> of the sea-serpent, Bragi.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thefjan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þefjan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "in ú-þefjan (q. v.), <i>a stench.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thefka"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þefka
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to smell,</i> = þefja; nasar þefka daun, Anecd. 8.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thefr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þefr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a smell;</i> ok kenna þó eigi þef af reykinum, Barl. 49; íllr þefr, Bárð. 38 new Ed.; ú-þefr, q. v.; hefir þat þef mest í munninum, Stj, 293, and passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv., prop. a gen. of an obsolete noun; [Ulf. <i>þeihs</i> = χρόνος and καιρός]:—<i>at once, forthwith;</i> Höskuldr kallar á hana, farðú hingað til mín, segir hann. Hón gékk þegar til hans, Nj. 2; þegar á morgun, <i>to-morrow presently,</i> Ísl. ii. 147; hann var þá skírðr þegar, 645. 86; þá var hann þegar hvar fjarri …, hann sofnaði þegar, Fms. iv. 337; Þórólfr bar merkit þegar eptir honum, <i>following immediately after him,</i> i. e. <i>next after him,</i> Eg. 297; þegar frá öxlum ofan, Sks. 167, passim: the phrase, þegar-leið-sem, <i>straightway, forthwith,</i> Fms. x. 386, Stj. 94, 101, 267, Barl. 157; see leið.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegars"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegars
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= þegar es, <i>as soon as,</i> Grág. i. 97, Am. 30.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [þiggja], <i>a receiver, keeper;</i> in arf-þegi, far-þ., heið-þ., heim-þ., qq. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. þegi; pret. þagði; subj. þegði; imperat. þegi, þegiðu; with neg. suff. þegj-attu, Vtkv.; part. þagat(þagt, Anecd. 10, Sks. 562 B); [Ulf. <i>þahan</i> = σιωπαν, σιγαν; Hel. <i>þagjan;</i> O. H. G. <i>dagen;</i> Dan. <i>tie</i>; Swed. <i>tiga;</i> Lat. <i>tăceo</i>; cp. also þagga and þagna]:—<i>to be silent;</i> Rútr þagði við, Nj. 2; þegi, <i>be silent</i>! Art. 22; þegi skjótt (imperat.), Ld. 220; sitja þegjandi, Fms. vii. 160; sá er æva þegir, <i>whoever keeps silence,</i> Hm.; mæli þarft eðr þegi (subj.) … þá hefir hann betr ef hann þegir, … fátt gat ek þegjandi þar, id., and passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegjandi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegjandi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>the silent</i>, a nickname, Landn. (Orkn.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [A. S. <i>þegn</i>; Engl. <i>thegn, thane;</i> O. H. G. <i>degan;</i> Hel. <i>þegan;</i> whence Germ. <i>unter-than,</i> Dan. <i>under-dan</i> (?); Gr. τέκνον; the root word remains in Germ. <i>ge-deiben,</i> answering to Gr. τεκειν; Germ. <i>degen</i> (<i>a sword</i>) is quite a different word, being a Romance word, qs. <i>deger,</i> akin to <i>dagger,</i> see Grimm’s Dict. ii. 895, 896]:—<i>a thane, franklin, freeman, man;</i> sá þegn er þenna gyrðil á, Post. 298; þegn kvaddi þegn, Fms. vii. (in a verse); gamall þegn, Stor. 9; ungr þegn, Hm. 159; ef mik særir þegn, 152; þegns dóttir, <i>a man’s daughter,</i> Ó. H. (in a verse); Mörðr kvaddi oss kviðar þegna níu, <i>us nine franklins, nine neighbours,</i> Nj. 238; ek nefni þegn í fimmtardóm, Grág. i. 73; hann lézk eigi vita hverr þegn hann væri, <i>he said he knew not what person he was,</i> Fs. 100: (lítið er mér um þat, veit ek eigi hverr þegn þú ert, Fms. ii. 81); hvat þegna er sjá enn orðfæri maðr? Post. (Unger) 221; prúðr þegn, <i>a brave yeoman,</i> Eb. (in a verse); öndverðr þegn, <i>a brave thane, a brave man,</i> Rafn 193; vígligr þegn, Am. 51; þegiðu Þórir, þegn ertú úgegn, Fms. vi. (in a verse): allit., þegn ok þræll, <i>thane and thrall,</i> i. e. <i>freeman and bondman,</i> i. e. <i>all men,</i> Hkr. i. 270, N. G. L. i. 45, ii. 35; bú-þegn, <i>a franklin;</i> far-þegn, <i>a traveller;</i> ek ok mínir þegnar, <i>I and my men,</i> Fms. v. 138; Búa þegnar, x. 258; þegns hugr, þegns verk, = drengs hugr, drengs verk, Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegn-gildi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegn-gildi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the weregild for a</i> þegn (II), Fms. iv. 313, v. 74, x. 112, Gþl. 21, 130, N. G. L. i. 121, 384, Sks. 253.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegn-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegn-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (<strong>-liga,</strong> adv.), = Germ. <i>under-thanig,</i> (mod.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegn-skapr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegn-skapr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>an honour,</i> = Germ. <i>ehre</i>, as a law phrase; in the law phrase, leggja e-t undir þ. sinn, <i>to swear upon one’s honour,</i> Grág. i. 29, Nj. 150; þegnskapar lagning, and þegnskapar-lagningar-eiðr, <i>an oath upon one’s honour,</i> Grág. i. 30, 321.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegn-skylda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegn-skylda
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>the duty of a thane towards his liege-lord, allegiance;</i> hollosta, þ., ok hlýðni við konung, Gþl. 67; alla þá er í hans þegn-skyldu eru, 62; játa e-m þegnskyldu, Fms. ix. 257; leggja krafir eða þegnskyldur (<i>duties</i>) á e-n, H. E. i. 465.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thegna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þegna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to serve as a</i> þegn (II); ok þegnuðu honum, Stj. 568, v. l.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/theima"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þeima
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "dat., sing. and plur. <i>to this, to them</i>, see þessi; á þeima hlut, Fms. vii. 102; á þeima bæ, ÓH. 106, Fms. viii. 210; með þeima atburð, 233; í þeima flokki, 325; með þeima eiðstaf, Gþl. 14; með þeima hætti, Fms. v. 336, x. 183, 402: plur., á þeima mánuðum, viii. 173; á þeima átta vetrum, 219; gangvegum þeima, Kormak; þeim mönnum, Sks. 60 new Ed.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/theims"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þeims
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= þeim es, Hm. 3, Fms. i. 100 (in a verse), vi. 38.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/their"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þeir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "þær, þau. This is the plur. of the personal pron., answering to sing. hann, hón, þat; gen. þeira and mod. þeirra; dat. þeim; acc. þá, þær, þau; in mod. speech þau is sounded þaug, which form occurs as early as Run. Gramm. of 1651, and often rhymes in mod. poets with words ending in <i>g</i>, e. g. <i>flaug, þaug,</i> Bb. 2. 17: [the A. S. uses the forms <i>hi</i>, <i>hira, him, hi</i>, and so in early South. E., whereas the North. E. has <i>thay</i>, <i>thair, thaim;</i> South. E. and Chaucer <i>hii, here, hem</i>, Morris’ Specimens, p. xv; Dan. <i>de, deres,</i> early Dan. <i>deræ</i>, dat. <i>dem</i>.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/theirs"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þeirs
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= þeir es, Hm. 165 (heilir þeirs hlýddu), Þd.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/theist"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þeist
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>þeisti,</strong> a, m. a bird, <i>uria grylle</i> or <i>colymbus grylle</i> L., <i>the sea-pigeon,</i> Edda (Gl.): mod. teisti-kofa, or also <strong>þeista,</strong> u, f., Fél. i. 19; mod. Norse <i>teiste</i>, Edda (Gl.), passim in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a thatch, roof,</i> Nj. 115, Fms. vi. 153, Stj. 60, Sks. 138 new Ed.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekja-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. þek; pret. þakði and þakti; subj. þekði; part. þakiðr, þaktr, þakinn: [A. S. <i>þeccan;</i> Engl. <i>theck</i> and <i>thatch;</i> Scot. <i>thack</i>; Germ. <i>decken, dach;</i> O. H. G. <i>dechan;</i> Dan. <i>tække</i>]:—<i>to thatch;</i> skjöldum er salr þakiðr, Gm. 9; þar er þakiðr kryplingr, Fms. v. 160; þekja sundit með skipum, Nj. 273; gulli þakðan sal, Vsp. 63; hann reið a brúna, hón er þökt lýsi-gulli, Edda 38; allt annat, þá er ísum þakt, Sks. 43 new Ed.; þakt reyr eðr hálmi, Fms. vi. 153; þakit gull-spöngum, Ver. 27.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekjull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekjull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a kind of <i>thatched shed,</i> D. N. i. 477, 502.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekki-liga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekki-liga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>with grace;</i> veita þ., Bs.; þiggja þ. þær fórnir, 655 xxiii. 1.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekki-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekki-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [Dan. <i>tækkelig</i>], <i>handsome, lovely, pleasant</i> (Germ. <i>anmuthig</i>), Haustl.; þýðr ok þ., Bs. i. 76; göfugligr maðr ok þ. ok þó ógurligr, Ó. H. 23; manns-höfuð bjart ok þekkiligt, Fms. i. 228; með þekkiligu yfirbragði, x. 232; var líkit bjart ok þekkiligt, xi. 281; eigi þ., <i>ill-favoured,</i> vi. 143; ú-þekkiligr, <i>id</i>.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekking"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekking
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>knowledge.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekkinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekkinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. = þekkiligr, rendering of Lat. <i>‘delectabilis,’</i> 655 xxvii. 11.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekkja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekkja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "ð, and later t; an older pret. þátti answers to Goth. <i>þagkjan, þahta,</i> and occurs in old poems in four instances, which see below: [Goth. <i>þagkjan</i> = λογίζεσθαι; A. S. <i>þencan, þôhte;</i> Engl. <i>think,</i> pret. <i>thought;</i> Hel. <i>þenkjan,</i> pret. <i>þahta;</i> O. H. G. <i>dankjan;</i> Germ. <i>denken,</i> pret. <i>dachte;</i> whence mod. Dan. <i>tænke;</i> Swed. <i>tänka;</i> whence mod. Icel. þenkja. In the old Norse the sense of ‘to think’ is still undeveloped, and only appears in the borrowed mod. form þenkja; cp. þykkja.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>agreeable, pleasant, liked;</i> þýðr ok þekkr við sína menn, Fms. x. 420.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekt"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a liking;</i> engi þekt mun mér á þeim vera, Fs. 88; ok bauð þeim mikla þekt (<i>a pleasant sensation</i>) er þeir sá líkit, Bs. i. 208; óþekt, <i>a dislike, nuisance:</i> also <i>the being refractory.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thekta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þekta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "t, [from þekkja], <i>to know,</i> with the notion <i>to reprove, chide,</i> cp. kenna A. II. 2; nema Þráinn hann þekti menn af orðum þessum, Nj. 141 (þekði, v. l.); þat fær engi gört, at þekta þik af því sem þú tekr upp, … en nú til þess at þú þagnir, Bs. i. 567: in a good sense, <i>to know;</i> sá er hann heyrir fá orð varranna þektir (þekkir, v. l.) hann mörg orð hugrenningarinnar, Sks. 120 new Ed.; þá má hann vel þekta alla vegu, 121.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thel"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þel
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [cp. A. S. and Engl. <i>felt</i>; Germ. <i>filz;</i> Lat. <i>pilus,</i> Gr. πιλος, <i>þ</i> = <i>f,</i> cp. Gr. θήρ = φήρ, Lat. <i>ferus</i>]:—<i>the nap on woollen stuffs;</i> þel er á hnefa bundini eða hlutr feldar, Skálda (Thorodd): in mod. usage þel is <i>the soft fine wool,</i> as opp. to the tog or kemp, on Icel. mountain sheep; úr þeli þráð að spinna, a ditty.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thel-hogg"
