              "__html": "adj. <i>enduring, persevering.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thol-gaedi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þol-gæði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>patience.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thol-lauss"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þol-lauss
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>impatient, having no endurance.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thol-leysi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þol-leysi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>lack of endurance, unsteadiness,</i> Grett. 118.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thol-raun"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þol-raun
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a trial,</i> Bs. i. 45.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thola"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þola
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. þoli, pret. þolði, subj. þylði (þølði); part. þolt, later form þolat; [Goth. <i>þulan</i> = ἀνέχεσθαι, στέγειν; A. S. <i>þoljan;</i> Old Engl. and Scot. <i>thole</i>.; O. H. G. <i>doljan, dolon;</i> Dan. <i>taale;</i> Germ. <i>dulden;</i> Lat. <i>tulisse, tol-erare;</i> Gr. τλα- in τληναι, etc.]:—<i>to bear, endure, suffer;</i> reyna hvert hann þyldi járn eðr eigi, <i>whether he could bear it or not,</i> Fms. vii. 250; hvárt Þrændir þyldi atgörða-laust, ef …, vi. 38; ok þoli skor, Grág. ii. 188; at þau (the ships) þeyldi (i.e þøldi) mannfarminn, Fms. viii. 380, v. l.; mannraunir er hann hafði þolat, vi. 19; hversu þoldi Skarphéðinn í brennunni … vel fyrst en þó lauk svá at hann grét, Nj. 270; ef slíkt þolist, Ísl. ii. 406; eigi er þat þolanda (gerund.), <i>it is intolerable,</i> K. Á. 36; spyrr hversu lengi hann hafði þat áfelli þolt, Fms. x. 226; lengi höfu vér þolt þeirra ofsa, 237; þau hafa mart högg þolt í dag, 360; hversu hart þeir hafa þolat, Fas. i. 339.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tholandi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þolandi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "part. <i>a sufferer,</i> Skálda (= accusative).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tholanligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þolanligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (<strong>-liga,</strong> adv.), <i>tolerable,</i> H. E. i. 457; eigi rétt eðr þolanligt, <i>to be tolerated,</i> Bs. i. 281.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tholin-modliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þolin-móðliga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>patiently,</i> Fms. ix. 278, Rb. 382, MS. 623. 54, passim in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tholin-modr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þolin-móðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [Dan. <i>taalmodig</i>], <i>‘thole-moody,’ patient, enduring,</i> Stj. 158, Fb. ii. 261, Greg. 20, passim esp. in eccl. writers, N. T., Vídal.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tholin-maedi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þolin-mæði
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>patience, long-suffering,</i> Ld. 256, Fms. x. 217, Sks. 12, Mar. passim, N. T., Pass., Vídal.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/tholinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þolinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>one who holds out longest, lasting, durable;</i> skjöldr þjokkr ok þolinn, Karl. 97: <i>enduring,</i> þrekinn ok þolinn við vás ok erviði, Róm. 330, Fms. ii. 69: of one who never gets exhausted, never loses his breath, of a runner, horse, or the like, minn hestr er þolnari en þinn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thollr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þollr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Ivar Aasen <i>toll</i>; cp. þöll, þella], <i>a fir-tree,</i> esp. <i>a young fir,</i> see Ivar Aasen, Edda (Gl.); but in poets of <i>trees</i> in general; er und þolli stendr, Vsp. (of an ash); ask-þollr, <i>an ash-tree,</i> Lex. Poët.; álm-þollr, <i>an elm-tree,</i> id.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thopta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þopta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "see þópta.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thora"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þora
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. þori, pret. þorði; subj. þyrði, older þørði; part. þorat (þort?): with neg. and personal suff., þoriga ek, <i>I dare not</i>, Vkv.; [cp. Engl. <i>dare</i>; the Dan. <i>lurde,</i> = <i>to dare,</i> is formed from the pret.]:—<i>to dare, have the courage to do a thing;</i> with infin., þoriga ek at segja nema þér einum, Vkv.; þora mun ek þann arm verja, Ó. H. (in a verse); þorði hann ekki at synja þeim gistingar, Fbr. 19; get ek at hann hafi ekki þorat at koma á minn fund, 33;, en skal þessi enn gamli þora at sjá í mót vápnum, Ld. 280; ek þorða at leggja mik í hættu, Fs. 4; hann þorir at berjask, Gullþ. 50; þora man ek at heimta fé þetta, Nj. 31; var engi svá grimmr at þyrði á hann at ráða, Fms. ii. 174; þar hafði engi maðr þorat at nema fyrir landvættum, síðan Hjörleifr var drepinn, Landn. 272: leaving out the infin., ef þeir fá þann kvið at þeir mætti eigi ganga enda þörði þeir eigi, Grág. ii. 158.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thoran"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þoran
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>daring, courage,</i> Bs. i. 42, Al. 15; þoranar-raun, Ld. 92: neut., svá mikit þoran, Mar. 491.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thori"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þori
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. so the vellums with a single <i>r;</i> the mod. form is <strong>þorri,</strong> but less correct, for the word is akin to þyrja, q. v.:—<i>the greater part, main part,</i> of a crowd, multitude, assembly, or the like; allan þora. (thus the vellum) landsins, <i>the main part of the land,</i> Fms. vii. 177; allr þori liðsins, Trist.; var þat mestr þori múgsins, viii. 411 (þori, Fb. ii. 687, l. c.); mestr þori var á land rekinn fjárins, Finnb. 244; en mikill þori var þat er þær sögðu eins báðar, Landn., Hb. 320; lætr hann brott flytja mestan þora fjárins, Al. 28; mestr þori manna, Barl. 26, N. G. L. ii. 418; hann má oss þjóna at miklum þora. <i>for a great deal,</i> Norske Saml.; and so freq. in mod. usage, það er mestr þorri búinn, <i>the most part ready, all but ready.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [Ulf. <i>þaurnus</i> = ἄκανθα; A. S. <i>þorn;</i> Engl. <i>thorn;</i> O. H. G. and Germ. <i>dorn;</i> Dan. <i>torn</i>]:—<i>a thorn;</i> þorna ok þistla, Eluc. 45; með þornum, Greg. 31; þorn ok klungr, Stj. 38, 47, passim; hag-þorn, cp. þyrnir.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorn-gord"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorn-görð
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. = þornkrúna, Symb. 22, Hom. (St.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorn-kruna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorn-krúna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a crown of thorns,</i> Ann. 1274.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to become dry,</i> Glúm. 364, Eb. 260, Bs. i. 339, Ísl. ii. 131, 364, Greg. 58, Al. 95, Sks. 28, Barl. 78, Stj. 589.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorp"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorp
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [Ulf. <i>þaurp</i> = ἀγρός, once in Nehem. v. 16; A. S. and Hel. <i>þorp</i>; Old Engl. <i>thorp;</i> O. H. G. and Germ. <i>dorf;</i> Lat. <i>turba</i> is taken to be the same word: this word, we think, was originally applied to <i>the cottages of the poorer peasantry crowded together in a hamlet,</i> instead of each house standing in its own enclosure, like the ‘tún’ or ‘bær’ or ‘garðr’ of the ‘búandi,’ hence þorpari = <i>a churl</i> (see below); the etymological sense being <i>a crowd, throng,</i> as seen in þyrpast, þyrping (qq. v.), as also in Lat. <i>turba</i>]:",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorp-karl"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorp-karl
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. = þorpari, <i>a churl,</i> Fms. x. 372, Þiðr. 231. <strong>þorpkarl-ligr,</strong> adj. <i>churlish,</i> Hkr. iii. 129.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorpara-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorpara-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (<strong>-liga,</strong> adv.), <i>boorish, clownish</i>, Hkr. iii. 129, Al. 119.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorpara-skapr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorpara-skapr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>clownishness,</i> Sks. 276: mod. <i>villainy.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorpari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorpari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a cottier, peasant, boor, churl, clown,</i> of the lower peasantry; búandkarl eða þ., Fms. ii. 48; þorparar ok verkmenn, opp. to ríkir búendr, Ó. H. 212; þorpari (opp. to hæverskr maðr), Sks. 276, 317; ‘colonus’ and ‘miles gregarius’ are rendered by þ., Róm. 132, 152; þorpara sonr, þorpara sveinn. a term of contempt, Fms. viii. 221, Fas. i. 150.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorra-blot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorra-blót
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>the great sacrifice when Thorri begins</i> (in heathen times), Fas. i. 17.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorra-kyrrur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorra-kyrrur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>calm, frosty weather,</i> said to prevail in this month.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorra-manudr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorra-mánuðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the month Thorri,</i> Fb. i. 22, Rb. 516.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorra-thraell"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorra-þræll
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the thrall of Th.,</i> i. e. the last day of Thorri, see Almanack, 1873, Feb. 22.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorri"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorri
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. [perh. from þverra þorrinn = the month of the waning or ‘ebbing’ winter]:—the name of <i>the fourth winter month,</i> the first after mid-winter; of thirty days, beginning on a Friday and ending on a Saturday inclusively; in the old calendar Þorri is entered as beginning between the 9th and 16th of Jan., and the next month, Góe (q. v.), between the 8th and 15th of Feb., see H. E. i. 595; but in the new style, in Icel. Almanack, the first day of Thorri, 1873, is Friday, Jan. 24, and the last, Saturday, Feb. 22; mið-þorri, <i>the middle of the month Th.,</i> Edda 103, Grág. ii. 306, Rb. 46, Landn. 324: the name of this month is still the common term in Icel., the names of Jan. and Feb. being almost unknown in Icelandic country life; Þorra-dægrin þykja löng | þegar hann blæs á norðan, a ditty, see Gói. For the mythical origin of this month, see Orkn. (begin.) and Fb. i. 21, 22.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thorskr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þorskr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., proncd. <strong>þoskr,</strong> and spelt so, Edda ii. 623; [Dan. <i>torsk</i>]:—<i>a codfish,</i> Edda (Gl.), Grág. ii. 359; passim in old and mod. usage, þorsk-höfuð, þorsk-lifr, þorsk-lýsi, <i>a cod’s head, liver, oil:</i> <strong>þorska-bítr,</strong> m. nickname of a great fisher, Eb.: <strong>Þorska-fjörðr,</strong> m. a local name in western Icel., Landn.: <strong>Þorskfirðingar,</strong> m. pl. <i>the men from Th.:</i> <strong>Þorskfirðinga-saga,</strong> u, f., Landn., see Index.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
