              "__html": "= þröngving, q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throngja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröngja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "see þröngva.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throngr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröngr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "þröng, þröngt, adj., often spelt <strong>þraungr,</strong> or even þrængr, þreyng-; the <i>v</i> appears before a vowel; compar. þröngvari, superl. þröngvastr, or contracted þröngri, þröngstr, þreyngstr; [North. E. <i>thrang;</i> Dan. <i>trang;</i> cp. A. S. <i>þrang;</i> Engl. <i>throng,</i> only as subst.]:—<i>narrow, close, tight;</i> skyrtu þröngva, Rm.; vefjar upplutr þröngr, <i>tight,</i> Ld. 244; þar sem vóru þröngastir vegir, Fms. ix. 366; skógrinn var mikill ok þröngr, Nj. 130, Fms. i. 111; þar sem helzt vóru kleifar ok skógar þröngvastir, ix. 359; íkorninn fór jafnan þar sem þröngstr (þreyngstr, Hkr. l. c.) var skógrinn, Ó. H. 85; í þröngva dal þeim, <i>in that narrow dale,</i> Al. 26; geilar þreyngar at ríða at bænum, Orkn. 450; sú á heitir nú Þjórsá, féll þá miklu þraungra ok var djápari en nú, Eg. 99; þröngt varðhald, <i>a close watch,</i> Eluc. 60; settr í hit þröngasta klaustr, H. E. i. 487; þröngvar nauðsynjur, Sks. 321; var honum svá þröngt (<i>his enemies were so close on him</i>) at hann hleypti inn í kirkju, Fms. ix. 485.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throngsl"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröngsl
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl., mod. <strong>þrengsli;</strong> [Germ. <i>drangsal;</i> Dan. <i>trængsel;</i> cp. Ulf. <i>þreihsl</i> = στενοχωρία, and <i>þraihns</i> = <i>a heap</i>]:—<i>narrows, straits;</i> í þrengslum, fjalla-þrengsli.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throngsla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröngsla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. = þröngsl, Stj. 495.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throngva"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröngva
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>þryngva,</strong> <strong>þreyngva;</strong> the later and mod. form is <strong>þrengja.</strong> In old poets this verb is strong, pret. þröng, þrungu, þrungit; thus pres. þröngr or þryngr, Ó. H. 107 (in a verse); pret. þröng, þrungu, Edda (in a verse), Fms. ix. (in a verse); subj. þryngvi, Orkn. (in a verse), Edda (in a verse); part. þrunginn, Hm., Skm. 31, Rm. 4, Skv. 34; in prose the participle þrunginn remains only as adjective, else the verb is now weak throughout, þröngva, ð: [Engl. <i>throng;</i> Germ. <i>drängen;</i> Dan. <i>trænge;</i> cp. Ulf, <i>þreihan</i> = θλίβειν, στενοχωρειν.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throngvan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröngvan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a constraint;</i> án allri þ., Grett. 162 A.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throngvi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröngvi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. = þröng, hósta ok þrönga, Hkr. i. 260.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throngving"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröngving
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. (<strong>þrönging,</strong> Magn. 478, H. E. i. 408), mod. <strong>þreynging,</strong> Fms. v. 307: <strong>þrenging,</strong> Bs. i. (Laur.):—<i>straits,</i> and metaph. <i>distress</i>, also <i>oppression, compulsion,</i> þröngving ok mæðu, Fms. v. 309.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throngvir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröngvir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a presser,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throsk"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þrösk
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [þreskja], <i>a noise, beating,</i> as if from threshing, Fas. i. 66.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throskuldr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröskuldr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., see þreskjöldr, <i>a threshold.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/throstr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þröstr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., þrastar, þresti, plur. þrestir, þröstu; [A. S. and Engl. <i>thrush, throstle;</i> Dan. <i>trost;</i> Germ. <i>drossel;</i> Lat. <i>turdus</i>]:—<i>a thrush</i> (the bird), Edda (Gl.): skógar-þröstr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thudr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þuðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., see þunnr, <i>thin.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thukla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þukla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [cp. þjökka; the -<i>la</i> may be an inflex. dimin.]:—<i>to grope for, feel, touch,</i> like a blind man; hann fór höndum um kverkr sveininum ok þuklaði sullinum (of a king’s touch), Ó. H. 196; hann þuklaði á saxi ok vildi þá leggja á Bjarna, Þorst. St. 55; þuklar (þucklar) bróðir járnteininum at eldinum sem hógligast, Mar. 1056; var svá til þuklat (<i>it was handled so</i>) at hvárir-tveggju undu vel við, Fs. 76.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thula"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þula
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n, f. [þylja], <i>a rote,</i> old name for a kind of <i>harp,</i> now used of strings of rhymes running on without strophic division (Dan. <i>ramse</i>), en þá er sú þula var úti, Fas. iii. 206; orta ek eina um jarl þulu, | verðr-at drápa með Dönum verri, Fb. iii. 426; ella mun það þykkja þula | þannig nær sem ek henda mula, Mkv.; Rígs-þula, name of a poem (Edda ii. 496); Þorgrims-þula, Edda i. 480; lesa í þulu og bulu, <i>to read by rote:</i> also used of rhymed or alliterative formulas.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thulr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þulr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., gen. þular, dat. þul, <i>a sayer of saws, a wife-man, a sage</i> (<i>a bard</i>?); this interesting word, the exact technical meaning of which is not known, occurs on a Danish Runic stone—Hruhalds þular á Salhaugum, Thorsen 17: and in old poems, at hárum þul hlæ þú aldregi, opt er gott þat er gamlir kveða, Hm. 135; inn hára þul, Fm. 34; nú skal freista hvárr fleira viti, gestr eða inn gamli þulr, Vþm. 9. <strong>þular-stóll,</strong> m. <i>‘the bard’s-seat,’</i> in which he sat when speaking; mál er at þylja þular-stóli at, Hm. 111; fimbul-þulr, <i>the great wise man,</i> 143; kross hangir fyrir brjósti þul (<i>poet</i>) þessum, Orkn. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thuma"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þuma
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að; þuma e-t upp, <i>to string fish.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thumall"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þumall
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. þumli; [A. S. <i>þûma;</i> O. H. G. <i>dûmo;</i> Engl. <i>thumb;</i> Dutch <i>duim;</i> Swed. <i>tumma;</i> Dan. <i>tomme</i>]:—<i>the thumb,</i> of a glove; í þumlinum.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thumbaldi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þumbaldi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a dull moper:</i> <strong>þumbara-ligr,</strong> adj. <i>moping:</i> <strong>þumbast,</strong> að, <i>to mope.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thumli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þumli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a ‘tom-thumb,’</i> a nickname, Sturl. ii. 153.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thumlungr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þumlungr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>the thumb</i> of a glove; hanzka-þ., Ls. 60, Edda 29.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thumur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          þumur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>holes</i> through which a string is drawn, in fish and blubber hung up to dry, Skýr. 590.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/thund"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
