      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedi-samliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æði-samliga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>furiously.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedi-stormr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æði-stormr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>a furious gale,</i> Barl. 38, Art. 112.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedi-straumr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æði-straumr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a furious current,</i> Art. 66.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedi-vedr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æði-veðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a furious gale,</i> Eg. 195, Ld. 286, Ó. H. 18.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedi-verkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æði-verkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a furious pain,</i> Barl. 52, Bs. i. 340, Gullþ. 9.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedi-vindr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æði-vindr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a furious gale,</i> Barl. 150.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> i. e. <strong>œðr,</strong> adj. [from vaða, óð], <i>fordable;</i> áin var ó-œð, Bs. i. 349; hón (the river Rhine) var eigi œð, ok engi var brú eða farkostr yfir, Karl. 41.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., dat. and acc. æði, pl. æðar, æðir, Barl. 72; sannri lífs æð (dat.), 84; in mod. usage this word is a regular fem. nom. æð, dat. and acc. æð; thus also in old writers; hverja æð (acc.), Pass.; heit lífs-æð, 24. 12; but in plur. æðar, 48. 9, 10: [A. S. <i>âdre;</i> O. H. G. <i>âdara;</i> Germ. <i>ader;</i> Dan. <i>aare</i>; Swed. <i>åder</i>]:—<i>a vein;</i> æðr sú er pulsus heitir, Al. 161; blóð hans var allt ór æðum runnit, Fas. i. 426; æði (dat.) rennandi ok keldu, Barl. 165; Hrafn tók henni æða-blóð í hendi, í æði þeirri er hann kallaði þjótandi, Bs. i. 644; æðarnar, Al. 23, 25; þær æðar, andblásnar æðar, Skálda 169.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedra"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æðra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. [no doubt derived from æðr, f., which word originally meant nerves and veins]:—<i>fear, despondency, despair;</i> verðit vel við ok mælit eigi æðru, Nj. 200; svá at þeir megi eigi á oss finna æðru, Ó. H. 214; þá kemr æðra í brjóst Þorkatli, Fbr. 37. <strong>æðru-orð,</strong> n. <i>a word of fear;</i> in the ancient code of honour a man was never to utter a word of despondency or fear, to do so was thought to be ill-omened; engi maðr skyldi þar æðru-orð mæla eðr kvíða, hvegi úvænt sem þeim hyrfði, Fms. xi. 76; enginn flýði ór sínu rúmi eðr mælti æðru-orð, i. 421; ‘vér munum allir Óðin gista í kveld,’—þatt eitt æðru-orð mælti Hjálmarr, 422; eigi man ek þá lög Jómsvíkinga ef ek kvíði við bana eða mæla ek æðru-orð, eitt sinn skal hverr deyja, Fms. xi. 148.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedrask"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æðrask
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, <i>to falter for fear, lose heart;</i> þó er þat dýr svá, at ek hefi nokkut helzt æðrask við at eiga, Fms. ii. 101; minnr æðraðisk hann at fara úr landi ok sækja eign sína en þú görir nú, 245; þú æðrask mikinn mann en gambrar yfir litlum, Glúm. 332; eigi skyldim vér nú æ. of mjök at leggja til bardaga við Ólaf konung, Fms. x. 346; ok varð þat drjúgara at þeir æðruðusk, viii. 376; en ef vér æðrumk nú nokkut, þá …, Ó. H. 214; kalla ek þann ykkarn ekki at manni vera, er nokkut æðrask í því, at vér takim hann af lífdögum, ef hann ferr í hendr oss, 61.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aedri"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æðri
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "i. e. <strong>œðri,</strong> compar. <i>higher,</i> superl. <strong>œztr,</strong> <i>highest</i> (spelt eozt, Rb. 1812. 51; the mod. spelling is <strong>æðstr</strong>); it has no positive: [this word is the same as the Goth. <i>auhuma, auhumists, h</i> and <i>þ</i> being interchanged; the usages in the Icel. N. T., when compared with the Goth., shew the identity of the words beyond doubt, e. g. æðstu prestar, Matth. xxvi. 59; sá æðsti prestr, 63; þeim æðstu prestum, xxvii. 3; þeir æðstu prestar, 6, 20: with which cp. <i>ahumists gudja</i> in Ulf.: þess árs æðsti prestr, John xviii. 15 (where Ulf. <i>‘ahumists’ weiha</i>)]:—<i>higher, highest:</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> ð, [Germ. <i>üben;</i> Dan. <i>öve</i>], <i>to exercise,</i> quite a mod. word: æfing, f. <i>an exercise.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefa-gi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfa-gi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>æva-gi,</strong> adv. <i>never;</i> knákat ek segja aptr ævagi, þú ert ölðr of heitt, Hým. 32; enn ósviðr maðr kann ævagi síns um máls maga, Hm. 20.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfar-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>ævar-,</strong> a later form for afar, see p. 5, col. 2. bottom:—<i>very, exceedingly;</i> in compds, ævar-ílla, <i>very ill indeed.</i> Fms. i. 150; æfar-íllt, Karl. 404, 529; ævar-vel, <i>very well,</i> Fms. xi. 249, Ísl. ii. 131, Fb. iii. 401; ævar-reiðr, <i>very wroth,</i> Mirm.; ævar-gamall, <i>‘stone-old.’ exceeding old;</i> ævar-langt, Þiðr. 165.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., indecl. and without plur., gen. ævar, N. G. L. ii, is quite exceptional: [Ulf. <i>aiws</i> = αἰών; O. H. G. <i>ewa;</i> Gr. αἰών; Lat. <i>aevum</i>]:—<i>an age, era,</i> and esp. <i>a life-time;</i> hann var konungr yfir Noregi langa æfi, <i>a long time,</i> Fms. i. 1; hann leitaði langa æfi við at drepa hann, Rb. 382; lengi æfi, <i>for a long time,</i> Rd. 291; hélzk þat allt um hans æfi, Eg. 268; þau tíðendi er görðusk um æfi Ólafs konungs ens helga, Ó. H. (pref.); Þorgnýr faðir minn var með Birni konungi langa æfi … stóð um Bjarnar æfi (<i>reign</i>) hans ríki með miklum styrk, 68; á síðasta vetri konungs ævar, N. G. L. ii; á öndurði æfi e-s, Ver. 71; lauk svá hans æfi, Róm. 156; lengi ævi minnar, Fas. i. 542; inn fyrra hluta æfi sinnar, Fs. 3, Fær. 16; alla æfi síðan, Nj. 246; þá er upp leið á æfi Gyðinga … þessa heims ævi, Rb. 392; segðu oss æfi vára ok langlífi, Landn. (Hb.) 77; vil ek at þú segir nökkut frá æfi þinni, Fb. i. 134; ennar fornu æfi, <i>in the old era,</i> Hom. 140; inni fornu æfi, Ver. 59; í inni nýju æfi, <i>in the new era,</i> id.; ef sú æfi stendr nökkura stund, Sks. 347; enginn veit sína æfi fyrr en öll er, a saying, Vídal. ii. 143: the allit. phrase, um aldr ok æfi, <i>for ever and ever,</i> N. G. L. i. 41, and in mod. usage; also, aldr ok um æfi, D. N. iii. 34, 35.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefi-dagar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfi-dagar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. pl. <i>life-days.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefi-langr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfi-langr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>life-long,</i> = æfinligr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefi-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfi-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (<strong>-liga,</strong> adv.), <i>for ever,</i> = æfinligr, Stj. 115, 209, 431.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefi-lok"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfi-lok
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>life’s end, death,</i> Nj. 282, MS. 655 ii. 1, Skíða R. 203; Al. 36, Fms. v. 181.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefi-saga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfi-saga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>a biography,</i> Fms. i. 190, iii. 63, Fær. 63; í æfisögu Noregs konunga, Fms. xi. 211 (v. l.), freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefin-lengd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfin-lengd
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a life’s course,</i> Str. 65.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefin-liga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfin-liga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>for ever,</i> Dan. <i>evindeligen,</i> Fms. i. 140, x. 13, Stj. 64, Gþl. 3, freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefin-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfin-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. (euenligr, Stj. 7), <i>everlasting,</i> Fms. x. 114, Stj. 46, 279; land ok þegna ok æfinligan skatt, Fms. x. 114; chiefly in a secular sense, eilífr being used in a spiritual and eccl. sense.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefin-runar"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfin-rúnar
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl., see æfinn, Rm. 40.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefin-sattr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfin-sáttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>‘ever-agreed,’ for everlasting peace,</i> a technical law term in concluding a peace, D. N. i. 200.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefin-trygdir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfin-trygðir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>an everlasting truce.</i> Grág.; similar to the preceding word.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefin-tyr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfin-týr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., mod. form <strong>æfin-týri;</strong> in old writers it is also used masc., þann æfintýr, Fb. i. 207; einn æfintýr, ii. 136; þessi æ. sem nú var lesinn, Karl. 551: [a for. word, appearing about the end of the 13th century; from late Lat. <i>adventura;</i> Germ. <i>abenteuer;</i> Dan. <i>eventyr;</i> see Dietz]:—<i>an adventure;</i> vita sitt eptir komanda æ., <i>their future life,</i> Stj. 7; þau tíðendi ok æ., 64; auðna ok æ., 202; sumir flýðu fyrir ljóðæsku eða nokkar æfintýr, <i>adventurous exploits,</i> Fas. iii. 3, Pr. 381, Fb. ii. 136.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>ævins,</strong> adj. [= Goth. <i>aiweins</i> = αἰώνιος], <i>everlasting;</i> prefixed in allit. phrases, um aldr ok ævins-daga, <i>life-days,</i> D. N. v. 533; til ævins skiptis, <i>everlasting division,</i> D. N.; aldr-sáttr ok æfin-sáttr. i. 200; aldar trygðar ok æfin-trygðar, Grág.; æfin-rúnar ok aldr-rúnar, <i>life-runes, the mysteries of life,</i> Rm.; æfin-lengd ok ellidómr, <i>life’s length and age,</i> Stj. 65; cp. also æfinligr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "i. e. <strong>œfr,</strong> adj. [afar, of], <i>vehement, angry, chafing;</i> æfr í skapi, Fms. i. 75; ýgr ok æfr, xi. 8; íllr ok æfr, Landn. 235, v. l.; hann görðisk íllr ok æfr við ellina, Eb. 52 new Ed., Fms. iii. 95; æfr ok ærr, iv. 142; æfr maðr (Ed. æfi-maðr), <i>a violent man,</i> Bret.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aefrinn"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æfrinn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj., see ýfrinn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aegi-geisli"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ægi-geisli
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>an awful glance,</i> of the eye, Ad.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aegi-sandr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ægi-sandr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>sea-sand;</i> þótti komit eigi únægra enn ægi-sandr, Ver. 18; fjölgandi sem þann ægisand er eigi fær talt, Stj. 183; sem himinstjörnur eðr ægis-sand, 133: in mod. usage ‘ægisandr’ is the fine sand on the shore of the ocean.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aegir"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ægir
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., thus, not <strong>œgir,</strong> as is shewn both by the spelling of vellums and by ancient rhymes, as <i>ægi</i>r and <i>fræg</i>r in a poem on king Canute: [ægir is an old mythical word, the root of which is not to be sought for in the Norse languages, for it is much older; it may be akin to the Gr. ὠκεανός, both being derived from some Indo-European root; A. S. <i>eagor, the sea;</i> it still survives in provinc. Engl. for the sea-wave or Bore on rivers, ‘have a care, there’s the <i>Eager</i> coming,’ Carlyle’s Heroes, p. 198]:—<i>the sea, ocean, main;</i> hver eru sævar heiti?—heitir marr ‘ægir,’ etc., Edda 100; ægi lægja, <i>to calm the sea,</i> Rm. 40; eldr, veðr, ægi, jörðu, 625. 178; sér hón upp koma öðru sinni jörð ór ægi, Vsp.: <i>gold</i> is ægis bál, eldr, see Lex. Poët.: the word is a favourite with poets, ancient as well as modern, esp. in the ballads and rímur; in prose it only survives in a few phrases and compds, sól gengr í ægi, <i>the sun sets in the sea</i> (cp. ganga til viðar), Fms. ii. 302, v. 169; sól skundar í æginn, Al. 67.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aegis-dyrr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ægis-dyrr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. pl. <i>‘Oceani ostia,’</i> the name of a Dan. river, mod. contr. <i>Eider,</i> Fms. xi. 28, 31, Symb. 15.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aegis-hjalmr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ægis-hjálmr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a helmet of terror;</i> the word is explained under hjálmr (3), q. v.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aegisif"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ægisif
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. a Norse popular name for the Αγία Σοφία in Constantinople, Rb., Symb., being an imitation of the word as spoken by the Greeks of the 11th century; the Norsemen on hearing the word from the mouth of the Greeks seem to have thought of their own heathen goddess Sif.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aegja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ægja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "i. e. <strong>œgja,</strong> ð, [óg-], <i>to scare, frighten,</i> with dat.; sú mær ægði dýrinu með litlum dúki er hón hafði í hendi, Bs. i. 199; ægja e-m píslum, <i>to threaten with tortures,</i> Greg. 38; hón œgði mér af afbrýði, Gkv. 1. 10; þær œgðu mér járnlurki, Hbl. 39.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aeja"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æja
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pres. ær; pret. áði; part. áit or átt; the mod. form is <strong>á,</strong> pres. ái, pret. áði, áð:—<i>to bait, rest;</i> eigi skal maðr æja í engi manns, útlagr verðr hann of þat ef hann ær, Grág. ii. 233; en er hann kom skamt frá ánni, syfjaði hann mjök ok bað hann þá æja þar, Nj. 94; þeir aðu í Kerlingardal, 252; stigu þeir af hestum sínum ok ætluðu at æja, Fms. i. 273; hér munu vér af baki stíga ok æja, Lv. 20; þeir sá einn dag at tíu menn áðu í enginu, … ílla þótti þeim gört at æja í engjum manna, … áðir þú hestum þínum í engjum mínum, Fs. 51, 57; þótti þar mál at æja farar-skjótum sínum, Mar.; æja eykjum sínum í annars manns landi, Jb. 247; einn dag er Illugi áði hesti sínum, Fbr. 48 new Ed.; þeir kröfðu dagverðar ok æja hestum sínum, Eg. 564; þeir láta taka niðr hesta sína ok æja, Ísl. ii. 482; ok er þeir höfðu átt (áit?) um stund, 349.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aela"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "d, [áll], <i>to belch;</i> ælir vatn þar er ‘álar’ falla, <i>water belches,</i> Skálda (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aeli-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æli-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [ala, ól], <i>fit to be brought up,</i> Eb. 116 new Ed.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aeligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [Swed. <i>elak</i>] <i>vile, wretched;</i> sama ælig mér klæði, <i>vile clothes befit me,</i> Fas. i. (in a verse); ælig er sú fórn, Hom. 191 (Ed.); þeir drápn allt þat sem var afleitt eða ælikt (ellkt, v. l.), hrumt eða herfiligt, Stj. 456; mér þinni æligri ambátt. 484.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aell"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æll
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "i. e. <strong>œll,</strong> adj. [ala, ól], <i>fit to be fed</i> or <i>harboured,</i> of an outlaw, Grág. i. 311, ii. 10; ú-æll, ó-æll, of an outlaw <i>that must not be fed.</i> Grág. passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aemta"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æmta
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "i. e. <strong>œmta,</strong> t, = ymta, [Engl. <i>utter</i>], <i>to mutter, utter;</i> jarl æmti því lítt, Fms. ix. 289; kerlingiu œmtir við innar í húsinu … hvat ferr þar nú segir hón, Ísl. ii. 342; þótti honum hann fár við verða ok æmta sér lítt, <i>to utter little,</i> Sturl. iii. 313,; þögðu allir, en er hann sér at enginn æmti honum, Háv. 5 new Ed.; ok æmtir honum hvárki vel né ílla, Finnb. 218.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aepa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æpa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "i. e. <strong>œpa,</strong> t or ð, [óp; Ulf. <i>wopjan;</i> A. S. <i>wepan;</i> Engl. <i>weep</i>, etc.], <i>to cry, scream, shout;</i> Skamkell æpti upp, Nj. 82; bónda-múgrinn æpti ok kallaði, at þeir vildi hann til konungs taka, Fms. i. 21; þá œpta þeir miklu hærra ok kváðusk, Sks. 653 B; æpa at e-m, Eg. 189; æpa her-óp, sigr-óp, 80, Fms. viii. 142, Sturl. iii. 178: <i>to cry</i>, barnið efði (i. e. æpði) á leið fram, Bs. i. 342; úlfi hæra hygg ek þik æpa munu, ef þú hlýtr af hamri högg, Hbl. 47.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aer"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ær
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. ær, dat. and acc. á; pl. ær, gen. á, dat. ám; with the article, ærin, ánni, ána, ærnar, ánna, ánum: older forms with changed vowel occur in ancient vellums, ́, ́na, ́nni, Bs. i. 334. ll. 2, 12, 13; dat. ́um, Grág. ii. 305: [A. S. <i>eowe;</i> Engl. <i>ewe;</i> Lat. <i>ovis;</i> Gr. ὀίς]:—<i>a ewe;</i> ein ær, ærin, Grett. 137, Bs. i. 330, 334; ær ok lamb, N. G. L. i. 59; sá er ́na á, Grág. i. 417, 418; á (acc.) blœsma, 427; lömb undan um, Grág. l. c.; ef dilk-ær eru, ii. 304; ef þeir selja ær til osts, 309, Fms. xi. 149; kýr ok ær, Nj. 236; höfðu ærnar gengit í brott, Fbr. 49; cp. á-sauðr, á-högg, á-bristir.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aer-ligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ær-ligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>honest.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aer-stada"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ær-staða
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u. f. <i>a sheep-walk,</i> B. K. 81.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aera"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æra
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> ð, <strong>eira</strong> in Ld. 204, Fms. vii. 244. Sturl. i. 72, iii. 103, is evidently the same word, <i>ei</i> = <i>æ</i>, and different from eira, <i>to spare:</i> [from ár = <i>an oar</i>]:—<i>to row, pull;</i> æra undan e-m, æra verðr með árum undan dólga fundi, Skálda (in a verse); rétt er at flýja ok undan at æra, Post. (Unger) 242; see eira, p. 123.",
            }
          }
        />
