            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aeti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          æti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aetla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ætla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, often spelt etla. but ætla, Ld. 32 (vellum); in mod. usage it is often sounded <strong>atla:</strong> [a derivative akin to Goth. <i>ahjan</i> = <i>to mind, think,</i> and <i>aha</i> = <i>a mind,</i> as also to Germ. <i>achten,</i> O. H. G. <i>ahton;</i> the Northern languages use none of these words, but only the derivative ætla; an old Germ. <i>ahtilon</i> would answer to Icel. ætla; Scot. <i>ettle</i>.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aetlan"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ætlan
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>ætlun,</strong> f. <i>thought;</i> eptir ætlan, <i>deliberately,</i> Sks. 119 new Ed.; er þat mikil ætlan (<i>a great instinct</i>) skynlaussar skepnu at sjá, 12 new Ed.; hogson ok ætlan, <i>thought and reason,</i> Mar.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aetni"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ætni
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>gluttony,</i> Sks. 540, Hom. 24.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aetr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ætr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [eta, át], <i>eatable,</i> Hkr. ii. 252, Grág. ii. 122, 192, Bárð. 176; ú-ætr, <i>uneatable.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aett"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ætt
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., like sætt (q. v.), the forms vary between átt and ætt; in old writers the latter form is by far the more common; in mod. usage they have been separated, átt meaning <i>a quarter</i> in a local sense, ætt <i>a family:</i> [ætt is akin to Ulf. <i>aihts</i> = τα ὑπάρχοντα; A. S. <i>æhte</i> = <i>property;</i> Early Engl. <i>agte;</i> Germ. <i>acht</i> = <i>patrimony;</i> the root verb is eiga, átti, like mega, máttr; from this original sense are derived both the senses, ætt = <i>a family,</i> and ætt or átt = Scot. <i>‘airt,’ ‘regio caeli;’</i> the etymology of átt from átta (<i>eight</i>), suggested at p. 47, col. 1, is too fanciful.]",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aett-barmr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ætt-barmr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "or <strong>ætt-baðmr,</strong> m. <i>a lineage, stem,</i> Lex. Poët.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aett-balkr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ætt-bálkr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>lineage, family,</i> Fas. i. 387: = frændbálkr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/aett-bogi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ætt-bogi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>lineage,</i> = áttbogi, Fms. i. 287, Bret.",
            }
