        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<i>longest of all,</i> local name of a fiord in the deserts of Greenland, A.A. 306; again discovered in 1870, and called Franz Joseph’s fiord, see Maurer in Augsb. Allgem. Zeit. 29th Oct. 1870.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ollungis"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öllungis
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. (mod. <strong>öldungis,</strong> but in old poets made to rhyme with <i>ll</i>):—<i>altogether, quite;</i> öllungis eigi (cp. Lat. <i>omnino non), not at all,</i> Eluc. 13; öllungis kvittr, Dipl. iv. 11, B. K. 121; drýgja allyngis (sic) hans vilja, Hom. 69; öllyngis ei ok ei, 15; öllungis ílla, <i>altogether ill,</i> Ó. H. (in a verse); öllungis allar, <i>quite all,</i> Bjarn. (in a verse).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/olmusa"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ölmusa
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f., also <strong>almusa,</strong> Hom. passim; [A. S. <i>ælmesse;</i> Engl. <i>alms;</i> Germ. <i>almosen;</i> Dan. <i>almisse;</i> all from Gr. ἐλεημοσύνη]:—<i>an alms, charity,</i> Hom., Stj., K. Á., Bs.; of any charity, thus in the Icel. grammar-school, the allowances are still called ölmusa; ölmusu moli, Stj. 157; ölmusu-gjarn, ölmusu-góðr, <i>charitable,</i> Greg. 75, Bs. i. 332, 356: compds, ölmusu-gæði, <i>charitableness,</i> Hom., Bs.: ölmusu-görð, -gjöf, -gipt, <i>alms-giving,</i> Greg. 75, Grág. i. 163, Blas. 51, Stj., K. Á. 74, D. N. ii. 16: ölmusu-barn, <i>an ‘alms-bairn,’ pauper child,</i> Karl. 400: ölmusu-prestr, <i>a priest pensioned off, ‘emeritus,’</i> Ám. 100: ölmusu-maðr, <i>an almsman, bedesman,</i> Ó. H., K. Á. 78: metaph. of <i>an imbecile person;</i> nenni ek víst eigi at ölmusur sparki í andlit mér, Fs. 31; ölmusur at vexti ok fráleik, 41; gefa mun enn ölmusu-lagi til Húsafells, i. e. <i>even a bedesman would start in such weather as this,</i> Bjarn. 54.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oln"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öln
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>the fore-arm, and</i> hence <i>a cubit, an ell;</i> for this word see alin, p. 13.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oln-bogi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öln-bogi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "usually contracted <strong>ölbogi,</strong> and now sounded <strong>olbogi;</strong> albogi = alnbogi, Ld. 220; almbogi, read alnbogi, Edda 110; [öln and bogi; A. S. <i>elboga;</i> Germ. <i>ellen-bogen;</i> Engl. <i>elbow</i>]:—<i>the elbow;</i> ölbogi, Fms. iv. 383, Ó. H. 176 (ölnboga, Fb. ii. 302, l. c.); hann stendr á knjánum ok ölbogunum, Fms. xi. 64; hann hallaðisk á ölnboga, Str.; upp við ölnboga, Fb. i. 543; höndina fyrir ofan ölnboga, 255; ölboga, 150; olboga, Al. 24, l. 1, passim: a nickname, Orkn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/oln-lidr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öln-liðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "also úlfliðr (q. v.), sounded unliðr, <i>the ‘ell-joint,’</i> i. e. <i>the wrist,</i> see p. 668, col. 2, and Maurer’s Volksagen, 192.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/olr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ölr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> adj. <i>worse for ale, worse for drink;</i> ölr ek varð, varð ek ofr-ölvi, Hm. 13; ölr ertú Loki, Ls. 47, Gm. 51; ölum stilli, Ýt.: allit., eigi veit hvaðan óðr eða ölr kemr at, a saying, Sturl. iii. 183.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/olsadr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ölsaðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
