            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/olvaerliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ölværliga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>cordially, hospitably,</i> Ísl. ii. 348.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ombun"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ömbun
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. (i. e. <strong>öm-bun</strong>), in Norse vellums often spelt <strong>amban,</strong> in mod. usage, <strong>umbun;</strong> [this word is interesting as being undoubtedly in form and sense nearly related to ambátt; Goth. <i>andbahts;</i> A. S. <i>ambeht;</i> Germ. <i>amt</i> (see p. 19); accordingly the etymological sense would be <i>wages, hire</i> given to a servant]:—<i>a payment for service, wages;</i> hinn seksk ok eigi á meðför hans gripar, ef sá hafði í ömbon þann á brott hafðan, of seizing an object in order to pay oneself with it, Grág. ii. 197; þeim skal gjalda makliga ömbun, ok mikit verka-kaup, Fms. i. 215; nú skulu þér taka ömbun verka yðvarra, skortir oss nú eigi föng til at gjalda yðr starf yðvart ok góðvilja, Ld. 12; ef þeir mætti af ömbun erviðis síns slökkva sinn sára hungr, <i>if, from the wages for their work, they might appease their hunger,</i> Fms. i. 222.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ombuna"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ömbuna
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>ambana,</strong> mod. <strong>umbuna,</strong> að, <i>to reward</i> (e-m e-t); alla daga er ek lifi, á ek þér at ambana (ömbuna, v. l.), Fms. vi. 327; þú hefir ömbunat mér íllu gott, <i>thou hast repaid me good by evil,</i> i. 264; láti Guð oss fá þeim umbunat svá at þeir kenni, ix. 499 (ambanat, Fb. iii. 144, l. c.); þá skal Guð ambuna honum, en komi eigi fé fyrir, N. G. L. ii. 91; síðan skal erfingi umbuna honum fyrir starf sitt, Jb. 154; ömbunaði hann þar í móti þrjátigi pakka vaðmáls (<i>paid in turn</i>), Bs. i. 872; þeim skal ek kunna þökk ok ömbuna góðu, er …, Fms. i. 296.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ombunari"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ömbunari
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a rewarder,</i> Karl. 138.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ompull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ömpull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. [from Lat. <i>ampulla</i>], <i>a jug,</i> Pm. 93; see ampli.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ompuls-brot"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ömpuls-brot
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a potsherd,</i> Pm. 93.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/omstr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ömstr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a rick, stack,</i> Edda. ii. 493.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/omun"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ömun
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> f. an obsol. poët. word, <i>voice, sound;</i> see óman or ómun; this word may be akin to önd, cp. Goth. <i>ahma;</i> it is spelt omvn, Skv. 1. 71 (Bugge); omun, Edda i. 544.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/omurligr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ömurligr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>dreary, horrid;</i> í hræðiligu dreka líki ok ömorligu, Niðrst. 1; cp. amra, p. 19.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ond"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önd
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> f., gen. andar, pl. endr and andir, and so in mod. usage; [A. S. <i>ened;</i> Dutch <i>eend;</i> O. H. G. <i>anut;</i> Germ. <i>ente;</i> Dan. <i>and,</i> pl. <i>ænder</i>; Lat. <i>anas, anatis;</i> Gr. νηττα]:—<i>a duck,</i> Edda (Gl.); flaug mikill fjöldi anda (gen. pl.) … eina öndina, Art. 38; endr ok elptr, Karl. 477; vali, álptir, gæss ok andir, Grág. ii. 346, passim; brim-önd, töpp-önd.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ond-faezla"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önd-fæzla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>food for the soul,</i> Hom. 14.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ond-ottr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önd-óttr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [and-, p. 19, col. 2], <i>looking full in the face,</i> an epithet of the eye, <i>fiery;</i> öndótt augu, <i>fiery eyes,</i> Þkv.; öndóttr (not öndótts) inn-máni, Edda, in a verse (Húsd.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ond-vegi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önd-vegi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>önd-ugi,</strong> n. [from and- (<i>opposite</i>) and vegr]:—<i>an ‘opposite-seat,’ high-seat,</i> so called because two seats are placed opposite to one another; in ancient timbered halls the benches were placed longways, running along the walls of the halls (sec bekkr), with the two seats of honour in the middle facing one another; the northern bench facing the sun, was called öndvegi it æðra, <i>the higher</i> or <i>first high-seat,</i> the opposite or southern bench being it úæðra, <i>the lower</i> or <i>second high-seat;</i> the two high-seats were the most honoured places in the hall, and a chief guest used to be placed in the southern high-seat. In England the master and mistress sitting opposite one another at each end of the table may be a remnant of this old Scandinavian custom. The sides of the high-seat were ornamented with uprights (öndugis-súlur) carved with figures, such as a head of Thor or the like; these posts were regarded with religious reverence; many of the settlers of Iceland are said to have taken the high-seat posts with them, and when near Iceland to have thrown them over-board to drift ashore, and where they found them, there they took up their abode. When a man of rank died, the son, after all rites performed, solemnly seated himself in his father’s seat, as a token of succession: in Vd. ch. 23, the sons sat not in the father’s seat before they had avenged his death.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ond-verda"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önd-verða
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>the beginning;</i> fyrir öndverðu heims þessa, Hom. 196.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ond-verdliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önd-verðliga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>early, at the outset.</i> Fas. iii. 356.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ond-verdr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önd-verðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>önd-urðr,</strong> adj. <i>standing face to face;</i> öndurðr horfir þú við í dag—Öndurðir skulu ernir klóask (a saying), Ó. H. 183 (and the verse of Sighvat).",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ondudr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önduðr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. a pr. name, Hornklofi; also of a giant, Edda (Gl.)",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ondugis-holdr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öndugis-höldr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. (Fas. ii. 261), and <strong>öndugis-maðr,</strong> m. (Fagrsk., Eg. 575, Mag. 3), <i>the man sitting in the</i> öndvegi <i>opposed to the lord of the house, the king’s first man,</i> Fagrsk. ch. 219, Fas. iii. 31; in Hom. (St.) ‘architriclinus’, John ii. 9, is rendered by öndvegis-maðr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ondurr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öndurr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. öndri, pl. öndrar = andrar, <i>snow-shoes:</i> whence <strong>öndur-áss,</strong> m. <i>the god of the</i> öndurr, one of the names of <i>the god</i> Ullr, Edda i. 266: <strong>öndur-dís,</strong> f. one of the names of <i>the giantess</i> Skadi; both Ullr and Skadi being represented as great runners on snow-shoes, Edda (Ht.): <strong>öndur-goð</strong> = öndurdís, Haustl.: in poets, Áta öndurr, <i>the sledge of the sea-king</i> Áti, i. e. <i>a ship;</i> Eynefis öndurr, id., Bragi.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ondvegis-sula"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öndvegis-súla
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "u, f. <i>the high-seat post</i> or <i>upright,</i> Landn. 34, 35, 96, 261, Korm. 6, Gísl. 140, cp. Landn. 301.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ondvegis-saeti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öndvegis-sæti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n., Gþl. 252.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ong-vit"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öng-vit
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. <i>a swoon, fainting-fit,</i> Bs. ii. 230; at hann féll í öngvit, en er hann vitkaðisk, Fms. vi. 230, Fbr. 20 new Ed.; ef maðr er lostinn í öngvit, Grág. ii. 16; ok er af henni hóf öngvit, Bjarn. 68 (óvit, Glúm. 368), freq. in mod. usage.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ong-vaerr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öng-værr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>in anguish, distressed;</i> ö. ok auðkumul, Bs. i. 323.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ong-thveiti"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öng-þveiti
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "n. [see þveiti], <i>a ‘narrow place,’ strait;</i> at þú komir aldri síðan í slíkt öngðveiti, Ó. H. 120; verðr hverr fyrir sér at sjá, er menn koma í slíkt öngþveiti, Ld. 264.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ongd"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öngd
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>a strait;</i> öngd ok þröngd, Barl. 102.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ongleiki"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öngleiki
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "a, m. <i>a straitness, narrowness,</i> Post. (Unger) 46.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ongliga"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öngliga
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adv. <i>in straits;</i> vera öngliga staddr, Str. 75.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ongr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öngr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "pron. adj. = eingi, <i>none</i>; see eingi, pp. 120, 121.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ongr-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öngr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [Goth. <i>aggwus;</i> A. S. <i>enge</i> (subst.); Germ. <i>eng;</i> Lat. <i>ang-ustus;</i> cp. Gr. ἄγχω, etc.]:—<i>narrow, strait;</i> aka e-m í öngan krók, <i>to drive one into a corner,</i> Fms. vi. (in a verse, cp. aka ór öngum, see öngur); öngt ok þröngt, Skálda (in a verse); muntú í öngan ormgarð lagiðr, Skv. 3. 57; öngt garðs-hlið ok þröng gata er sú er leiðir til lífs, Barl. 45; halda e-n í öngri gæzlu, Str. 16; öngt í brjósti (cp. Germ. <i>engbrustig),</i> a nickname, Landn.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ongull"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öngull
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m., dat. öngli, [A. S. <i>angel;</i> Engl. <i>angle;</i> Germ. <i>angel;</i> all from Lat. <i>ang-ulus,</i> being from the same root as <i>ang-ustus,</i> öngr, etc.]:—<i>an angle, hook,</i> Hým. 21, Niðrst. 3, 4, Barl. 123, K. Þ. K., and passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ongur"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öngur
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. pl. <i>straits;</i> aldri fyrr kom hann ór þvílíkum öngum, Karl. 196; hann þóttisk ór öngum aka, Bjarn. 52; ór löngum muns öngum, <i>out of long anxiety of mind, anguish,</i> Hallfred: so in the mod. phrase, vera í öngum sínum, <i>to be depressed in mind.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ongva"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öngva
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "and <strong>öngja</strong> or <strong>engja,</strong> d, <i>to straiten, oppress;</i> öngða í allskyns þrautum, Stj. 51; öngðr með úfriði, Str. 14; hón œngvir honum ok hann angrar, 25; takit þessa konu ok látið öngva henni, 34; öngdi þetta ok þröngdi svá mjök orku-efni hennar, Barl. 65; þeir munu svá öngva þér, Flóv. 43.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/ongving"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          öngving
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. = öngd; þína eymd ok öngving, Bs. i. 201.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onn-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= önd, <i>a porch, vestibule,</i> Skm. 31.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onn-3"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önn
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>1.</strong> f. an obsolete word, some part of a sword, <i>the tip</i> or <i>the chape</i> (?), Edda (Gl.); önnar (unnar Cod. wrongly) tunga, <i>the tongue of the</i> önn, i. e. <i>the sword’s blade,</i> Landn. (in a verse); in Hkv. Hjörv. 9 the true reading, we believe, is ‘önn’ er í oddi for ‘ógn;’ hjalt, hugró, önn, egg, valböst all being parts of a sword.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onn-kostr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önn-kostr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "<strong>ann-kostr,</strong> also <strong>önd-kostr,</strong> m., in the phrase, fyrir önd-kost, <i>intentionally, purposely,</i> as a law phrase; hann sigldi skipi sínn á sker fyrir annkost, ok vildi brjóta (andkost, öndkost, v. l.), <i>he ran the ship on shore purposely,</i> Fms. viii. 367; er þó hafa ek fyrir önnkost svá ritið, Skálda 164; ef menn troðask svá mjök at lögréttu fyrir önd-kost (<i>wantonly</i>) eðr göra þar hrang eðr háreysti, Grág. i. 5; spilla fé manna fyrir önnkost ok fyrir illgirni sakar, 131; göra skaða fyrir önd-kost, þá varðar skóggang, 416.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onnungr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önnungr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. <i>a labourer,</i> Edda 107; þat er önnungs verk (<i>household work, farm work</i>) er maðr vinnr hvern dag þat er bóndi vill, K. Þ. K. 136.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onug-legr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önug-legr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>cross, odd, wayward,</i> Fél. x. 175.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onug-lyndi"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önug-lyndi
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f. <i>fretfulness,</i> freq. in mod. usage, but not found in old writers.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onug-lyndr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önug-lyndr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. <i>cross.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onugr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önugr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "adj. [qs. öndugr, i. e. andvígr?] <i>fretful, peevish;</i> þú ert önugr, strákr!",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/onundr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          önundr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "m. (Anundr), qs. An-vindr, a pr. name, Landn. <strong>Önundar-brenna,</strong> Ann., Sturl. i. 197; hence <strong>Önundar-fjörðr,</strong> a local name; <strong>Önundar-firðingr,</strong> Sturl. iii. 58.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-2"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ör
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "f., gen. örvar; dat. öru, Grág. ii. 19, and later ör; pl. örvar, örva, örum; also spelt with <i>f,</i> örfar, etc.: [A. S. <i>aruwe;</i> Engl. <i>arrow;</i> the word may be akin to örr, adj. = <i>the swift</i>]:—<i>an arrow;</i> örina, annarri ör, … ör liggr þar úti, ok er sú af þeirra örum, … örunum, … ör (acc.), Nj. 96, 115, Hkr. i. 241; örvar þrjár, … örvunum (sic), Fas. i. 511, 541, and passim.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/or-3"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          ör-
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "(i. e. <strong>ør-</strong>), a prefixed particle, altered from <i>us-;</i> the <i>s</i> remains in usall = vesall, see p. 699, col. 2; also spelt <i>er-,</i> er-vita, Hkv.; or <i>eyr-,</i> eyr-grynni, Ó. H. 106; evr-lygi, Eg. (in a verse): [Ulf. <i>us-;</i> O. H. G. <i>ur-;</i> when uncompounded, see ór, mod. úr, p. 472; as a prefix to nouns, <strong>ör-</strong> or <strong>ör-,</strong> for which see p. 469, col. 2. Indeed, there is a strong probability that the negative prefix <i>ó-</i> is a contraction, not of <i>un-,</i> but of <i>or-,</i> so that ó-bættr is from or-bættr, ó-verðr from or-verðr, by agglutination of <i>r,</i> whereby the vowel becomes long (as the O. H. G. prefix <i>ar-</i> in A. S. appears <i>â-</i>): this would account for the fact, that in the very oldest and best vellums there is hardly a single instance of <i>ú-</i> for <i>ó-,</i> and this is the sole modern form not only all over Iceland, but also in most popular idioms of Norway and Sweden; a farther proof is that in many words <i>or-,</i> the ancient form, is preserved in a few vellums, especially of the Norse laws, in such rare forms as ör-sekr, ör-bætiligr, ör-vænt, and ó-vænt, where the current form is ó-sekr, etc.; so also, ör-keypis and ó-keypis, ör-grynni and ó-grynni, ör-hóf and ó-hóf. Therefore <i>or-,</i> not <i>un-,</i> is, we believe, the phonetical parent of the later Scandinavian negative prefix <i>ó-</i>. The extensive use of <i>ör-</i> and the utter absence of <i>ú-</i> or <i>un-</i> may be explained by the supposition that, for the sake of uniformity, all words beginning with <i>ör-</i> and <i>un-</i> gradually took the same form; for though in ancient days <i>ör-</i> was more extensively used than it is at present, it can hardly have been the sole form in all words now beginning with <i>ó-</i>]:—ör- is used as denoting a negative, as ör-grynni, <i>a being bottomless;</i> or lack or loss of, as ör-sekr, <i>out of being</i> sekr; ör-verðr.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
