              "__html": "n., or <strong>ör-fjara,</strong> u, f. <i>an out-going, ebbing:</i> <strong>Örfiris-ey</strong> is the pr. name for islands which, at low-water, are joined to the mainland by a reef which is covered at high-water; one such island is near Reykjavik; another at Skard in western Iceland, now called <strong>Öffirs-ey;</strong> so also <strong>Ör-fjara,</strong> u, f. = <i>the island Orfir</i> in the Orkneys, Orkn. 182.",
