          className="link"
          href="/word/ortug"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          örtug
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "also spelt <strong>ertog, ærtog,</strong> [the etymology of the first part of the word is not certain, but it is prob. a compd, qs. ör-togr, the latter part being togr = <i>twenty,</i> prob. so called because twenty ‘penningar’ made an ærtog; ör or ær may be the old name of a small coin, cp. mod. Swed. <i>öre,</i> a small coin worth less than an English farthing; the mod. Norse name ‘ort,’ = a fifth part of a dollar specie, is an abbreviation of örttog]:—the name of <i>an old coin</i> or <i>piece of money,</i> amounting to a third part of an ounce (eyrir) = twenty penningar or pence, N. G. L., D. N. passim; skolu þeir báðir í ertogi (dat.), N. G. L. i. 185; see eyrir.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/orv-ondr"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          örv-öndr
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "= örvhendr, a nickname, Landn. 144.",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          className="link"
          href="/word/orva"
          onClick={[Function]}
          onMouseEnter={[Function]}
          onTouchStart={[Function]}
        >
          örva
        </a>
        <p
          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={
            {
              "__html": "að, [örr, adj.], <i>to exhort;</i> örva ok tendra, Str. 8; the word is very freq. in mod. usage, upp-örva, <i>to exhort, encourage;</i> upp-örvan, <i>exhortation, encouragement.</i>",
            }
          }
        />
      </li>
      <li>
